window.AKK_EASTERN_PALACES_DEVOUT_YET_AMOROUS_CONSORT_CHAPTERS=(window.AKK_EASTERN_PALACES_DEVOUT_YET_AMOROUS_CONSORT_CHAPTERS||[]).concat([{"number":1,"title":"Chapter 1","paragraphs":["In the spring of the nineteenth year of the Pingyuan era, the palace was holding its triennial selection of consorts.","The Crown Prince had been married for six years, yet had few children. This time, four new women were bestowed upon the Eastern Palace.","Shen Yanshui was one of them.","“Shen-jiejie, you’ve been bestowed upon His Highness the Crown Prince!”","Though the voice beside Shen Yanshui had been lowered, it still carried barely suppressed excitement. Shen Yanshui pressed down the disappointment in her heart, along with a trace of confusion.","How had she ended up in the Crown Prince’s Eastern Palace?","Xu Qingle watched her expression and asked hesitantly in a soft voice, “Shen-jiejie, are you... unhappy?”","Shen Yanshui turned to her and smiled, her eyes curving like crescent moons. “No. I’m simply too happy and didn’t know how to react for a moment.”","Forget it. The Crown Prince it was. The imperial edict had already been issued—what else could she do?","In her previous life, the apocalypse had arrived when she was in college.","Fortunately, she had been lucky enough to awaken a wood-element ability.","Even after transmigrating, her wood-element ability had remained with her.","It was just that the power she had once wielded as easily as her own limbs could now only be faintly sensed. Not only was it exceedingly weak, she could not use it at all.","Fortunately, in this life she had been reborn as a young lady of the Duke of Loyalty’s residence in the Great Yong Dynasty. She did not need an ability to get by.","Although she was a daughter born of a concubine, her stepmother was not particularly harsh. The legitimate and illegitimate children of the household were all provided with adequate food, clothing, and necessities.","Thus, she had spent sixteen years lying around peacefully at home, with plenty to eat and drink. Since the world around her was no longer filled with the dangers of the apocalypse, she had gradually let go of her obsession with her ability.","Some time ago, under her stepmother’s arrangements, she had begun meeting potential marriage candidates.","She had been exceptionally obedient and compliant about it.","The Great Yong Dynasty greatly valued lavish dowries.","Her biological father was, at any rate, the duke of a hereditary noble house, while her stepmother was the legitimate daughter of a marquis’s family. Both of them cared deeply about appearances.","They certainly would not shortchange her when it came to her dowry.","Only... she had never expected something to go awry midway.","Three years ago, her elder sister, who had entered the palace, had already become pregnant. Then, news suddenly came that she had miscarried.","The miscarriage had damaged her health, leaving her unable to conceive again.","After the household received the letter her elder sister had sent, it took only a few days for her stepmother to call off the marriage that had been verbally agreed upon for her.","Her stepmother had also summoned her for a private conversation. Her meaning, both explicit and implied, was that Shen Yanshui should enter the palace to help her elder sister compete for the Emperor’s favor and bear him a child. In return, she would enjoy a comfortable life in the future.","Shen Yanshui was naturally unwilling. Who would want to serve an old man? And not just any old man, but the old Emperor, who held the power of life and death over everyone.","But her refusal had been useless.","She did not particularly care.","Who said that entering the palace meant she had to enter the old Emperor’s harem?","So, during the period when she was learning palace etiquette, she had put some effort into finding out about the princes who had reached a suitable age but remained unmarried.","In the end, she had chosen the Fifth Prince.","The Fifth Prince had been blind since birth, making it impossible for him to inherit the throne. He was destined to spend his life as a wealthy prince. No matter which prince eventually ascended the throne, none of them would target the Fifth Prince.","Wealth, good food, security—everything she wanted was guaranteed. It was practically perfect!","During this period, she had made two appearances before Consort Liang.","Judging by Consort Liang’s attitude toward her over the past few days, Shen Yanshui had thought she had succeeded.","She had never expected to end up in the Crown Prince’s Eastern Palace.","Xu Qingle stared blankly for a moment at the faint smile on Shen Yanshui’s face.","Shen Yanshui wore a lotus-colored plain silk, narrow-sleeved top beneath a sky-blue half-sleeved robe. Her hair was arranged in a tassel coiffure. Her skin was as smooth and pale as jade, her brows like spring mountains, and her pair of bright, peach-blossom eyes seemed to brim with feeling. Even when she was not smiling, they were enough to make it difficult for anyone to look away.","Her crow-black lashes were long, thick, and elegantly curved. Her eyes were clear and luminous, as though washed by rain. Even as a woman herself, Xu Qingle could not help feeling her cheeks grow warm and her heart race as she looked at her.","Gazing at Shen Yanshui’s nearly flawless face, she blushed and said softly, “With Shen-jiejie’s beauty, His Highness the Crown Prince will surely value and favor you.”","Shen Yanshui gently squeezed her hand and smiled without replying for a moment.","Her elder sister currently lived in Consort Lan’s Jingfu Palace and was one of Noble Consort Lan’s people.","Noble Consort Lan and the Crown Prince’s birth mother—now Her Majesty the Empress—were mortal enemies.","It was said that after the Empress had fallen seriously ill two years ago, she had never truly recovered.","Even during this selection, the Empress had only appeared at the very beginning.","The rest of the proceedings had been handled jointly by Consorts Xian, Liang, Shu, and De, with Noble Consort Lan taking charge.","The Crown Prince was the Empress’s only son, while Noble Consort Lan’s two sons, the Fourth Prince and the Eighth Prince, had both come of age.","The Fourth Prince was even only a year younger than the Crown Prince.","Shen Yanshui was beginning to wonder whether Noble Consort Lan had deliberately arranged for her to enter the Eastern Palace simply to disgust the Empress and the Crown Prince.","Or perhaps Noble Consort Lan intended to turn her into an informant and pawn later on?","She had no idea. At any rate, no one had secretly approached her so far.","Her elder sister had summoned her to Jingfu Palace twice.","But from what her elder sister had said, both explicitly and implicitly, she merely wished to reassure Shen Yanshui while turning her into a tool for bearing children.","In any case, to anyone watching, she was probably a pawn Noble Consort Lan had placed in the Eastern Palace.","Forget about receiving the Crown Prince’s favor. As long as the Crown Prince did not vent his anger on her—and preferably treated her as though she were invisible—she would be perfectly content.","Shen Yanshui raised her eyes to Xu Qingle and said with a smile, “I’ve heard that the Seventh Prince is known for his filial piety. In the future, you should simply serve Consort Wan together with His Highness the Seventh Prince.”","Xu Qingle’s delicate, lovely face flushed slightly. She nodded earnestly. “Yes. I’ll remember everything Shen-jiejie has told me.”","She had been bestowed upon the Seventh Prince as a secondary consort and would marry him at the end of the year.","“Have all of you young ladies finished packing?” a matron in the Palace of Gathered Elegance asked with a smile. Her voice and manner were noticeably more respectful than usual.","Before today, they had been candidates studying palace etiquette, their fates still uncertain.","But now, some had been eliminated, while others were future imperial princesses by marriage. There were also some who could already be addressed as “Young Lady.”","The imperial edict had been issued. All that remained was for the palace maids and eunuchs to lead them to their respective destinations.","*","“What did you say? Fourth Sister has entered the Eastern Palace?!”","A startled cry rang out from the rear hall of Jingfu Palace.","Lady Shen wore a plain silk robe, and her hair had not yet been arranged. Her originally lovely face was now pale and slightly gaunt. She had been reclining sideways against a cushioned couch, but at those words, she instinctively straightened.","She looked at her personal maid, Xiang Mo, in astonishment. “How could it be the Eastern Palace? Are you certain you didn’t hear incorrectly?”","Xiang Mo wore a maid’s narrow-sleeved, round-collared robe of green patterned fabric. A goose-yellow sash encircled her waist, and a pale-green ribbon tied her hair into twin hanging buns. At that moment, she furrowed her brows, bowed, and answered in a low voice, “In reply to Your Ladyship, this servant made careful inquiries. There is absolutely no mistake. Fourth Miss Shen was indeed bestowed upon the Crown Prince by His Majesty.”","The astonishment on Lady Shen’s face did not fade. Instead, it was joined by even greater pallor. She pressed one thin hand against the small table, gripping it so tightly that her knuckles turned white. As though she had lost her soul, she murmured, “How could it be the Crown Prince...?”","Two months ago, after her miscarriage, she had begun suffering one nightmare after another.","She dreamed that after her miscarriage, she gradually lost the Emperor’s favor.","She dreamed that the Emperor died suddenly.","She dreamed that the Crown Prince unexpectedly contracted an epidemic, beyond the help of medicine and unable to be saved.","In the end, it was the Sixth Prince who ascended the throne...","As a former imperial consort who had long since lost the Emperor’s favor and had no child to rely on, she was ultimately sent to a temple, where she endured half a lifetime beside the green lamps and ancient Buddha.","The legitimate younger sister who had been lazy and useless since childhood, Shen Yanshui, married a newly appointed Presented Scholar and ultimately received the rank of a First-Rank Lady of Imperial Mandate, gaining both honor and prestige.","A month ago, after comparing the events in her dreams with reality and confirming them one by one, she had begun to believe everything in that nightmare.","She had then sent a letter to her mother.","Why had she met such a miserable end in her previous life, while Fourth Sister could so effortlessly obtain wealth, honor, and glory?","Lady Shen’s expression grew uncontrollably ugly, revealing a jealousy of which she herself was unaware.","Lady Shen touched her lower abdomen. No matter what happened in the future, if she could raise a child of her own, it would serve as a safeguard—a way out for her later on.","Only with that reason would Father and Mother send Fourth Sister into the palace.","But she had clearly mentioned it to the Noble Consort, and Her Ladyship had not refused. Why, then, had Fourth Miss Shen ended up entering the Eastern Palace?","She remembered that after the Crown Prince died, the Sixth Prince had not ascended the throne immediately. The Crown Prince still had a legitimate son.","At the time, the court had been filled with calls to establish the Crown Prince’s eldest legitimate son as the Crown Heir, simply because the Crown Prince represented the orthodox line of succession.","But the Crown Prince’s eldest legitimate son had been in poor health. In the end, it was still the Sixth Prince who ascended the throne...","“...Mistress? Mistress?”","Xiang Mo’s face was full of concern.","Seeing her muttering as though possessed, her complexion growing paler by the moment, Xiang Mo hurried forward to support her.","Lady Shen clutched Xiang Mo’s sleeve tightly with one hand. Her chest heaved rapidly as she stared at her and asked in haste, “Do you know which consort selected Fourth Sister?”","Xiang Mo quickly replied, “To answer you, Mistress, it was the Noble Consort.”","Lady Shen’s hand suddenly tightened, and her expression became even more unpleasant.","Seeing this, Xiang Mo could not help frowning worriedly. She comforted her, “Mistress, please don’t worry. The imperial physicians said that as long as you take proper care of yourself, your health will gradually recover. It is not as though you are completely unable to bear children.”","“The child you give birth to yourself will naturally be far better than one born from Fourth Miss Shen. Why place all your hopes on Fourth Sister?”","“I heard that Consort Shu also injured her health after giving birth to the Sixth Prince. After recuperating for several years, did she not go on to give birth to the Seventh Princess? Mistress, your good days are still ahead of you.”","Lady Shen listened to her words, brows knitted as she pondered for a moment. At last, her expression gradually eased.","How could she have forgotten? Consort Shu and the still-unnoticed Sixth Prince were the truly crucial ones.","Besides, Xiang Mo was right. She was not entirely incapable of bearing children; in her dream, it was only after her miscarriage that she spent her days drowning in tears and gradually lost the Emperor’s favor.","She still had plenty of time. She could plan everything slowly.","It was just a pity about Fourth Sister...","After the Crown Prince died, Fourth Sister would probably meet the same fate she had suffered in her previous life, would she not?","Perhaps her fate would be even worse than Lady Shen’s."]},{"number":2,"title":"Chapter 2: Meeting the Crown Princess","paragraphs":["From the Palace of Gathered Elegance to the Eastern Palace’s Palace of Everlasting Celebration, Shen Yanshui walked in the middle of the group, silent all the way.","Among the Crown Prince’s wives and concubines, aside from the Crown Princess, the ranks followed the ancestral system. In descending order, they were Liangdi, Liangyuan, Chenghui, Zhaoxun, and, at the very bottom, Fengyi.","Of the four newcomers, she had been given the rank of Zhaoxun.","Above her were a Liangyuan and a Chenghui, while below her was a Fengyi.","After thinking over the family backgrounds of the other women, she realized that, apart from herself, not one came from a family of military nobles or generals. Their fathers and elder brothers were almost all civil officials.","This did not surprise her. The Great Yong Dynasty’s preference for civil officials over military men was hardly a recent development.","After passing through several covered corridors, they heard the eunuch leading them exchange a few cheerful words with the palace maids at the entrance. Before long, their party was ushered inside.","Looking up, Shen Yanshui saw a main hall five bays wide, flanked by side rooms on either side. The courtyard was paved entirely with gray bricks, their intricate patterns spreading out like rippling water.","At the center of the courtyard stood an artificial mountain assembled from Taihu stones. Its unusual contours were elegant and graceful, while a clear stream trickled melodiously down between the rocks. Several clusters of exotic flowers grew from the crevices, their names unknown to her, though they were blooming beautifully.","“This servant pays his respects to the Crown Princess. May Your Highness enjoy perfect health.”","“Rise.” A warm, gentle voice carrying a hint of laughter rang out.","The Crown Princess wore a pale violet jacket embroidered with winding flowers and edged in gold. Beneath it was a fresh-colored skirt decorated with flowers and strings of pearls. A peony crown adorned her head, along with a jeweled golden hair ornament fitted with hanging pearl strands. Her bearing was dignified and gentle, and she shone with magnificence.","As soon as she finished speaking, Hongling, the senior palace maid beside her, stepped forward with a smile. Dressed in a brown, patterned round-collared robe, she had tied her hair with a gold-dusted, color-fading ribbon adorned with a golden bead. She slipped a small purse into the eunuch’s hand.","“Thank you for your hard work today, Eunuch Zhang.”","Zhang Fu accepted the purse with a broad smile and tucked it into his sleeve. “Your Highness needn’t worry. Everyone admitted to the Eastern Palace has personally received His Majesty’s approval. They are all sure to be fine young women and will certainly not cause Your Highness any trouble. The several young ladies are still waiting outside. What does Your Highness think...?”","The Crown Princess smiled. “Then let them all come in. It is time I became acquainted with my new sisters.”","“Yes, Your Highness.”","Before long, the four women were led into the hall by Matron Zhao. They passed around a huanghuali screen embroidered with landscapes representing the four seasons.","Shen Yanshui quickly raised her eyes to glance at the Crown Princess seated at the front. She was a woman of dignified, gentle, and noble bearing.","The palace maids on either side lifted the pearl-studded brocade curtains. Matron Zhao of the Palace Administration Bureau led the women in one after another. They bent at the waist and paid their respects.","“Greetings to the Crown Princess. May Your Highness enjoy peace and good health.”","Shen Yanshui stood in the middle, her eyes lowered to the tips of her shoes as she followed the others in making a perfectly proper salute.","“Rise, all of you. There is no need for such ceremony.” The Crown Princess looked at the group of striking, radiant newcomers before her, and the flawless smile on her face stiffened for an instant.","Matron Zhao bowed and introduced them one by one. “Your Highness, this is Lady Zhang. Her grandfather is Minister Zhang of the Ministry of Rites.”","Lady Zhang had a quiet, scholarly face. She wore a sandalwood-colored long robe of plain satin, subtly embroidered with silver designs, and a jade hairpin in her hair. At a glance, she looked every inch the dignified and well-bred young lady.","The Crown Princess nodded and asked with a smile, “Then the lady beside her must be Lady Wu, daughter of Minister Wu of the Dali Temple?”","“I had long heard that Miss Wu of the Wu family was a beauty of surpassing grace, possessing the allure of a sinking fish and falling geese. Seeing you today, I find the rumors were not exaggerated. At first glance, you are so beautiful that even I nearly forgot myself.”","At those words, Lady Wu instinctively lifted her chin slightly, the corners of her lips curling upward.","She had a striking and dazzling face, wearing a pomegranate-red skirt patterned with entwined chrysanthemums. A jade hibiscus pendant hung from the sash around her waist, while gold, jade, and agate ornaments adorned her hair. She was radiant and eye-catching.","Having received the Crown Princess’s praise, she grew even more pleased with herself. With an ingratiating smile, she said, “Your Highness is too kind. My beauty is not even one ten-thousandth of the Crown Princess’s.”","Shen Yanshui stood with lowered eyes, her expression meek and proper. She seemed to feel, with perfect clarity, the instant of sudden silence that descended around them.","She could not help sighing inwardly. Lady Wu had probably tried to flatter the wrong person and ended up striking a sore spot.","Lady Wu was indeed beautiful, with bright, flamboyant features that made her a genuine beauty. But as for the Crown Princess’s appearance...","It was not bad, but compared with Lady Wu, it could only be called delicate and refined.","Hearing Lady Wu’s words, no one would take them as praise. They sounded much more like mockery.","The Crown Princess’s lips stiffened for a moment. After looking Lady Wu over, she said, “Lady Wu, did you have honey on your lips today?”","Lady Wu failed to catch the sarcasm. Beaming, she replied, “It is only because Your Highness was born with such natural beauty.”","From the corner of her eye, Shen Yanshui could almost see the Crown Princess’s lips growing rigid.","Matron Zhao gave a light cough and resumed the introductions, though this time she made them much more quickly and succinctly.","Whether the Crown Princess was exhausted from poor health or for some other reason, she did not show any particular favor toward the others.","When Matron Zhao introduced Shen Yanshui, the Crown Princess merely praised her with a sigh, saying that she had a lovely face.","She made no mention of Noble Consort Lan or Shen Yanshui’s elder sister, Lady Shen.","Seeing Lady Wu’s unfriendly gaze upon her, Shen Yanshui smiled at her, not taking it particularly seriously.","At the sight of that smile, Lady Wu immediately frowned in displeasure.","After the introductions, Shen Yanshui learned that the last of the four newcomers, Lady Lin, was the daughter of the magistrate of Xuzhou.","The Crown Princess’s palace maids brought in several cups of tea. Beginning with Lady Zhang, each woman stepped forward to offer tea to the Crown Princess.","When it was Shen Yanshui’s turn, she followed the rules, lowered her eyes, and began to present the tea. At the same time, she felt a gaze descend upon her from above.","After two breaths, the Crown Princess finally lifted the cup and lightly touched it to her lips. Her lowered eyes rested on the face before her.","Shen Yanshui’s beauty was in no way inferior to Lady Wu’s; if anything, it was even more striking. The sight made the Crown Princess deeply uncomfortable.","But when she remembered Shen Yanshui’s connection to Noble Consort Lan, that suffocating feeling eased somewhat.","Besides, the Crown Prince had never been particularly fond of women. Even if Shen Yanshui possessed beauty capable of toppling cities, what difference could it make? She still could not stir up any great waves.","After everyone had finished offering tea, the Crown Princess followed protocol and delivered several solemn admonitions. Then her expression softened, and she said with a smile, “I hope all of you will serve His Highness the Crown Prince wholeheartedly and give him many children as soon as possible.”","“Yes, Your Highness. We will remember your instruction.”","“All right. I have been feeling somewhat unwell these past few days, so I will not keep you here to talk today. I would not want to pass my illness on to you.” The Crown Princess smiled and continued, “Matron, lead the ladies to their respective courtyards so they may settle in.”","Matron Zhou respectfully replied, “Yes, Your Highness.”","*","The place where the Crown Princess lived was called the Hall of Gathered Fragrance, located in the rear hall of the Palace of Everlasting Celebration. The front hall, the Hall of Honored Roots, was where the Crown Prince discussed affairs with the officials of the Eastern Palace. The main hall of the Palace of Everlasting Celebration was where the Crown Prince usually studied and attended to his daily affairs.","Behind the Hall of Gathered Fragrance was a series of rear rooms where the Crown Prince’s consorts lived. Five small courtyards stood side by side across the rear quarters.","Matron Zhou led Shen Yanshui to the one on the far left.","With a smile, she said, “Lady Shen and Lady Liu will be living in Lotus Heart Court from now on. Lady Shen will take the eastern side room, and Lady Liu the western. If you lack anything in your daily provisions, simply send someone to inform us. This old servant will make sure everything is arranged properly for both of you.”","Shen Yanshui turned sideways to return a half-courtesy.","When it came to official ranks, the head matron serving the Crown Princess held a higher status than her, who was only a Seventh-Rank Crown Prince's Lady of Training.","She stepped forward with a warm smile, quickly supporting Matron Zhou's arm as she said, \"Thank you so much for your trouble today, Matron Zhou.\" As she spoke, she handed over a purse she had prepared long in advance.","Matron Zhou did not decline it at all. She accepted it with a smile, all the while saying that Her Ladyship was being too polite.","Seeing this, Lady Liu, who was standing beside her, suddenly slipped the gold-inlaid jade bangle off her wrist and said with a grin, \"I will surely have to rely on your guidance a great deal in the future. Please do not take offense at this small gesture.\"","Matron Zhou still accepted it with a beaming smile. After exchanging a few more polite remarks, she said, \"If the two young mistresses have no further needs, this old servant will take her leave first to report back to Her Highness the Crown Princess.\"","\"Take care, Matron.\"","It was not until Matron Zhou's figure had vanished completely from sight that Shen Yanshui withdrew her gaze, and turned to look at the several palace maids and eunuchs who had been waiting respectfully at the side.","One of the maids, dressed in a blue round-collar robe with a pale yellow sash tied around her waist, stepped forward nimbly at once, curtsied again and greeted her, \"This servant Cuiyun pays her respects to her master. The east side chamber has already been tidied up properly by us. Would Her Ladyship like to go inside first to rest for the noon nap?\"","\"Very well, lead the way,\" Shen Yanshui replied with a clear, bright laugh.","She was in no hurry to tour the small courtyard just yet. She had been walking, standing, and kneeling nonstop all morning, so she wanted to sit down and rest first, and get to know the staff assigned to serve her.","Before walking off, she looked over at Lady Liu and said politely with a smile, \"Please make yourself at home, Lady Liu. I will head in to rest first.\"","Lady Liu was momentarily dazzled by her bright, lovely smile, and unconsciously curtsied back. By the time she came to her senses, she could only catch sight of Shen Yanshui's graceful, swaying figure from behind.","All of her original mood to wander around the courtyard had vanished in an instant. She turned around and walked straight into the west side chamber.","After entering the room, Shen Yanshui glanced around at the furnishings, and found nothing particularly surprising about them. After all, she had lived a life of wealth and luxury for more than ten years.","The several maids and eunuchs behind her watched as their new master lifted her feet and headed straight for the soft couch placed under the window in the eastern warm pavilion.","Once seated, she casually pulled over two soft pillows printed with heavenly fragrance patterns, and leaned back against them. Her movements were so familiar and comfortable as she reclined lazily, as if all the strength had suddenly drained from her body, that the servants were momentarily taken aback.","Even so, their new mistress was still so stunningly beautiful that no one dared to look at her directly.","Shen Yanshui leaned against the soft couch, letting out a soft sigh of relief. She looked at the four maids and two young eunuchs before her and said with a smile, \"All of you, introduce yourselves one by one.\"","Cuiyun, the maid who had stepped forward first, was the first to kneel down. She said respectfully, \"This servant greets Her Ladyship. I am Cuiyun. I entered the palace three years ago, and used to serve in the Imperial Food Bureau.\"","The rest followed her lead, kneeling down and speaking respectfully one after another. \"This servant greets Her Ladyship. I am Liu'er. I entered the palace three years ago, and was assigned to work in the Imperial Laundry Bureau before.\"","\"This servant is Xiuzhu. I entered the palace three years ago, and was in charge of sweeping and cleaning the Imperial Garden.\"","\"This servant is Chun'er. I am fifteen years old, and have only been in the palace for a year. I have been studying palace rules and etiquette under the guidance of matrons all this time.\"","After the four maids kneeling at the front had finished introducing themselves, the two young eunuchs at the back, dressed in crow-blue narrow-sleeved round-collar gowns with side slits and wearing crow-black headscarves, spoke up.","One of them was Little Lu, eighteen years old, with a rather honest and slow-witted look on his face. He used to tend to flowers and plants in the palace of a certain Beauty, but after that Beauty was demoted and sent to the Cold Palace for violating palace rules, he was reassigned back to the Palace Eunuch Service.","The other was Little Fu, sixteen years old. He had a small round face, with two dimples showing when he smiled, and fair, clean features that made him look very delicate and endearing.","\"This servant used to be in the Pavilion of Literary Profundity, in charge of drying and airing books. I can recognize a few characters.\"","Shen Yanshui looked a little surprised when she heard that. There were not many palace maids and eunuchs in the imperial palace who could read.","\"Are any of the rest of you able to read as well?\"","As expected, the chance of finding another such useful talent one after another was very slim. Even so, she was not disappointed. She looked at all of them with her smile unchanged, saying, \"It does not matter if you cannot read. As long as you are willing to learn, that is enough.\"","After all, someone had to take care of all kinds of work, right?","Understanding the implication in her words, all of them could not help feeling overjoyed. \"Thank you for Your Ladyship's great kindness!\"","It was not that they were unwilling to learn to read, but without the explicit permission of the master they served, no one in the palace would teach the palace maids and eunuchs how to read.","And if they wanted to advance to a better position, being able to read was an essential skill.","Seeing their excited and grateful expressions, Shen Yanshui smiled. \"Do not knock your heads and hurt yourselves while kowtowing. Since this is our first meeting, you do not know my temperament very well, so I will make this clear first. I rarely lose my temper, but that does not mean I have no temper at all.\"","\"On a daily basis, all you need to do is to be loyal, fulfill your duties properly, and finish all the tasks assigned to you.\"","\"If any of you wish to seek a different path in the future, you may speak to me frankly. Since we have shared the bond of master and servant, we can part ways amicably. But...\"","As she spoke, her voice grew softer, and she continued slowly with a gentle smile, \"If anyone has improper intentions, tries to play tricks and schemes, and does anything to betray their master...\"","The several maids and eunuchs instantly tensed up, repeatedly saying that they would never dare to do such a thing.","They had not expected that their new mistress, who had seemed all smiles, gentle, and easy to approach without any haughty air from the very beginning, would say such words. It was clear that their master was not as weak and easy to bully as she appeared on the surface.","The imperial palace was a place where people always fawned on those of higher status and stepped on those of lower status. If they wanted to live a good life, they had to climb up the ranks, and that was exactly what they all hoped for.","Following a wise master who could not be fooled was far better than serving a muddleheaded one.","\"Since this servant has chosen to follow Her Ladyship, I will naturally serve Her with all my heart and loyalty, and never have any second thoughts. Please grant us new names, Your Ladyship.\" Cuiyun spoke up first, and the rest followed suit, begging their new master to bestow names upon them.","Shen Yanshui looked at their earnest expressions, motioned for them to rise to their feet, thought for a moment, and then said with a smile, \"In that case, from now on, Cuiyun will be called Chunping, in charge of the tea, snacks, food in the rooms, and the storehouse.","The other three will be named Xia'an, Qiuru, and Dongyi respectively, and they will be responsible for all sorts of matters inside and outside the rooms.","Little Fu will be called Quanfu, in charge of the storehouse keys and all external affairs. Little Lu will be renamed Quanshou, and work under Quanfu's supervision.\"","\"For the time being, all affairs in this courtyard will be managed by Chunping.\"","\"Yes, Your Ladyship,\" all of them replied promptly.","Shen Yanshui looked at them with a soft smile. Peace in the four seasons, peace and good fortune for all — that was the greatest wish she held for herself."]},{"number":3,"title":"Chapter 3: I Wonder Where His Highness Will Be Lodged Tonight","paragraphs":["Shen Yanshui took in every change in the expressions of those present and merely smiled, not taking it to heart.","She was only a Shaoxun of the Crown Prince. Even if she entered the palace, she would not be allowed to bring along the maid who had served her since childhood.","Fortunately, before entering the palace, she had already managed to claw back from her legal mother part of the dowry that had originally been prepared for her.","Even without the Crown Prince’s favor, that fairly substantial sum of money should be enough to ensure she lived comfortably without worrying about food or drink.","After all, there were very few people in this world who could bring themselves to turn down money.","“Chunping, bring me writing materials.”","“Yes.”","Chunping moved swiftly and soon had an entire set of brushes, ink, paper, and inkstone laid out. It was clear that she knew the placement of everything in the room by heart.","Shen Yanshui turned to Quanfu and smiled. “Can you write?”","“Replying to Your Ladyship, I can write a little. It’s just that my handwriting is rather crude, and I fear it may offend your eyes.”","Shen Yanshui felt half her worries ease at once. After having him write a few characters for her to inspect, she realized he had been far too modest. He was well beyond merely being able to read and write.","After questioning him carefully, she learned that Quanfu had acquired his literacy because he had taken an old eunuch who had worked in the Zhaowen Library for over a decade as his adoptive father.","The reason he was now serving in the Eastern Palace was that his adoptive father had fallen ill some time ago. Thinking he might not have much time left, the old eunuch had asked Quanfu what he wanted to do and then called in a favor to have him assigned to work in the Eastern Palace.","Shen Yanshui understood.","She then instructed him to register and inventory everything in the room. Turning to Chunping, she said, “First, follow Quanfu and learn to read. The two of you will manage the storeroom together. From now on, whenever anything enters or leaves the storeroom, both of you must count and verify it, then sign for it.”","She did not expect there to be anything particularly valuable. At present, her most precious possessions were the two thousand taels in banknotes hidden on her person, along with some loose silver for daily expenses.","Still, some rules had to be established from the beginning.","The two of them hurriedly agreed. After Quanfu withdrew, Chunping brought over a cup of hot tea and asked respectfully, “My lady, shall I send someone to the kitchens to bring our meal?”","The wealthy and influential households of the Great Yong Dynasty generally ate three meals a day. The palace kitchens, however, operated according to set hours. One could not simply eat whenever one pleased unless one was willing to pay extra.","Shen Yanshui raised a hand and pushed open the window behind her. Daylight poured in, and the spring sunshine enveloped her, warming her from head to toe and making her feel somewhat languid.","She glanced at the sky outside and realized she was getting hungry. “Go and order the meal. Oh, and have them bring plenty of meat. Something sour and spicy to stimulate the appetite—not anything too bland. If it isn’t included in my allotted provisions, pay for it separately.”","Once she had eaten, she could look around the entire courtyard, take a walk to aid digestion, and then go to sleep. It was a perfect plan.","She was in the middle of imagining it when she noticed Chunping gazing at her with an expression that clearly said she wanted to speak but hesitated.","“What is it?”","Chunping bowed uncertainly. “Replying to Your Ladyship, today is the first day the new consorts have entered the Eastern Palace. If you eat something overly sour and spicy, and His Highness the Crown Prince happens to come by, you might lose some propriety in his presence...”","Not only did the palace maids and eunuchs serving their masters have to keep their clothes neat and ensure they had no unpleasant odors that might offend the noble masters and mistresses, but the consorts and lesser ladies of each palace also had to make sure they carried no strong or disagreeable scents whenever they were required to attend someone.","Shen Yanshui smiled. “There’s no need to worry. Everyone says His Highness the Crown Prince is exceptionally proper and attaches great importance to rules. I have two women ranked above me, after all. It won’t be my turn today.”","Not to mention her relationship with her elder legitimate sister.","She had heard that the Crown Prince’s maternal uncle, the General of Agile Cavalry, had recently clashed repeatedly with the civil officials at court. She guessed the Crown Prince’s mood had been poor lately. It would be best if he did not come.","After hearing this, Chunping thought it made sense and said no more. She went outside to give the orders. However, when instructing Dongyi, she paused to think, then added a few more reminders before finally handing her the money and telling her to collect the meal from the Eastern Palace kitchens together with Quanshou.","*","“Your Highness, it is already the hour of the Monkey. Shall I have the evening meal brought in?”","The cautious yet earnest voice of Zheng Yuande sounded outside the study of the Dunben Hall.","The doors and windows of the study were tightly shut, leaving the room somewhat dim.","A tall man with a straight back and refined, gentle features sat alone behind a rosewood desk, his face expressionless.","He wore a white jade crown and a dark robe with wide sleeves and a round collar, embroidered with subtle silver patterns. A leather belt encircled his waist. His features were scholarly and elegant, yet an aura of noble severity radiated from him, making anyone who looked at him feel intimidated.","“No need.” Cui Yu’s voice was calm as he lowered his eyes to the book before him.","Outside the study, Zheng Yuande was frantic with worry. He stamped his feet in agitation.","“Oh, how can that do, Your Highness? You haven’t eaten properly all day. I beg you, please have at least a little food. What will happen if you make yourself ill from hunger?","“If Her Majesty the Empress finds out, she certainly won’t let this servant off. Your Highness, please take pity on this servant and save me...”","Zheng Yuande’s voice carried a distinctly tearful note, making him sound especially pitiful.","“Too noisy.” Cui Yu furrowed his brows in annoyance.","Zheng Yuande immediately raised his chubby hands to cover his mouth, not daring to say another word.","Yet inwardly, he let out a heavy sigh. He knew His Highness was troubled because of His Majesty’s reprimand of the General of Agile Cavalry, which had ruined his appetite.","But no matter what the matter was, His Highness still had to eat at regular hours. How could this continue?","Just as he was worrying over it, his eyes suddenly lit up. He looked at the person approaching with undisguised anticipation.","“Miss Hongling, what brings you here? Has Her Highness the Crown Princess sent you to invite His Highness to dine with her?”","Hongling gave him a courteous curtsy and smiled. “Greetings, Eunuch Yuande. Her Highness has sent this servant to invite His Highness the Crown Prince to the Xifang Hall for dinner. She has something to discuss with him.”","Upon hearing this, Zheng Yuande smiled so broadly that his teeth nearly disappeared from view. He immediately went into the study to report to His Highness.","In the Xifang Hall, dishes were being arranged in an orderly fashion.","The Crown Princess asked, “Has the rain-before-the-grain Longjing His Highness prefers been brewed?”","“Replying to Your Highness, this servant prepared it some time ago.”","As soon as she finished speaking, the Crown Princess heard the familiar sounds announcing the Crown Prince’s arrival.","First came a series of quick, light footsteps. Only afterward did the steady, unhurried sound of his stride reach them.","The Crown Princess watched the tall, straight figure approaching her, as elegant as green bamboo, his features refined and scholarly. Pressing her lips into a smile, she stepped forward and curtsied.","“Your Highness, I pay my respects.”","Cui Yu’s expression remained tranquil. He raised a hand and gave a token gesture of support. “There is no need for formalities.” His deep, even voice revealed none of his emotions.","Seeing his calm, impassive face, the Crown Princess could not help feeling disappointed.","She naturally took the seat beside him. Cui Yu then turned his head toward her and asked, “Crown Princess, what was it you wished to discuss?”","At his courteous yet distant form of address, the smile on the Crown Princess’s face stiffened almost imperceptibly. It lasted only a moment before she returned to normal.","After three years, she had long since realized that although the Crown Prince possessed exceptionally refined and handsome features, he was truly cold and taciturn by nature.","He was not like this only with her; he treated the other women of the Eastern Palace the same way.","Even so, she had never been able to rid herself of a trace of unwillingness.","He was the Crown Prince, the heir to the empire, but he was also her husband. Why couldn’t he be a little more gentle and considerate with her?","Yet her expression remained composed and gracious. With a smile, she said softly, “There’s no need to hurry. The eunuch in charge of the kitchen told me that Your Highness hasn’t summoned a meal all day, and I was worried about your health. Why don’t you eat something first?”","At that, Cui Yu nodded.","Zheng Yuande, who had been waiting nearby, finally let out a sigh of relief when he saw the Crown Prince pick up his chopsticks.","It wasn’t long, however, before the Crown Prince put down his bowl and chopsticks after eating only a few mouthfuls and half a bowl of chicken congee.","Zheng Yuande: “...”","That wasn’t even enough to count as the two bites His Highness usually ate.","Seeing this, the Crown Princess promptly set down her chopsticks as well. Cui Yu glanced at her. “I had some pastries in the study earlier, so I’m not hungry now. You needn’t worry about me.”","The Crown Princess dabbed at the corner of her mouth and smiled. “Thank you for your consideration, Your Highness. I’m already full as well.”","Cui Yu glanced at her but said nothing more.","After rinsing their mouths, the two of them took their seats on a luohan couch in the eastern warm chamber, with a rosewood tea table between them. The Crown Princess personally brewed a cup of tea. Her fingers were long and slender, and her nails were painted in layers of dazzling crimson.","“This is the pre-Qingming Longjing tea newly delivered by the Imperial Food Bureau this year. Would Your Highness care to try it?”","Cui Yu raised his hand and accepted the cup. After taking a small sip, he said, “Not bad.”","The Crown Princess smiled. “I’m glad Your Highness likes it.”","Just then, Qinghe came to report that the young prince had awakened and was fussing to see the Crown Princess.","The Crown Princess turned toward the Crown Prince and said with a smile, “Quickly, bring Zhang’er here.”","Before long, Qinghe entered with the wet nurse, who was carrying the young prince.","After paying their respects, the wet nurse did not dare raise her head. With the utmost deference, she handed the child to the Crown Princess, who had reached out to take him.","The Crown Princess held the child and chatted merrily as she teased him for the Crown Prince to see.","This was Cui Yu’s only son, as well as his eldest legitimate son, so naturally Cui Yu valued him greatly. At the sight of the child before him, his expression softened unconsciously.","The boy was only a little over two by traditional reckoning, and he had been frail and frequently ill since birth. Even now, one glance was enough to tell that he was thin and not particularly robust.","He still looked as though he had only just awakened, and Cui Yu’s brows instinctively drew together.","After watching him for a while, he asked about the child’s health in recent days.","The Crown Princess handed the child back to the wet nurse, then replied with a loving smile, “Your Highness needn’t worry. With Physician Zhang attending to him, Zhang’er’s health has already improved considerably. He will certainly grow up safe and healthy.”","The slight furrow between Cui Yu’s brows eased.","Seeing this, the Crown Princess smiled again and told him a few amusing stories about the child’s recent antics. However, the Crown Prince merely listened without saying anything further, and the smile at the corners of her lips gradually faltered. Her fingers tightened around the silk handkerchief hidden in her sleeve.","After a moment, she changed the subject. “I specifically invited Your Highness here today to discuss the matter of the palace women newly bestowed by Imperial Father.”","Cui Yu raised his eyes to look at her.","The Crown Princess continued, “All four younger sisters were personally inspected and approved by Imperial Father, and they have now all been settled in their residences.”","“Lady Zhang has been placed in the main hall of Bamboo Fragrance Residence, while Lady Wu has been assigned to the main hall of Begonia Courtyard.”","After saying this, the Crown Princess asked with a smile, “May I ask where Your Highness intends to spend the night?”","Cui Yu set down the teacup in his hand and turned to look at her. His voice was calm and emotionless. “There are four of them, are there not? What of the other two?”","The Crown Princess was slightly taken aback. Looking at his expression, she smiled and replied gently, “The other one, Lady Shen, is the daughter of the Duke of Loyalty and Righteousness. She has been placed together with Lady Liu in the eastern and western side chambers of Lotus Heart Court.”","The Crown Prince suddenly asked, “What does the Crown Princess think of... Lady Shen?”","His abrupt question left the Crown Princess stunned for a moment. Then, without meaning to, she recalled Lady Shen’s beautiful face—one so unforgettable that anyone who saw it would have difficulty looking away.","She frowned instinctively. Had the Crown Prince met Lady Shen? Otherwise, why would he suddenly bring her up?","After a pause, she replied with a smile, “Lady Shen comes from a family of nobility. Her father and brothers are all military men, and she is a daughter born of a concubine, so the rules in her family were inevitably somewhat lax. Although she has learned some proper etiquette since entering the palace, it has only been a short while, and there are still shortcomings in her words and behavior.”","“I was thinking of disciplining her a little before allowing her to attend upon Your Highness.”","Cui Yu’s brows drew together almost imperceptibly. His cold phoenix eyes swept over her. A moment later, he rose calmly and said, “There’s no need. Lady Shen will do.”"]},{"number":4,"title":"Chapter 4: First Encounter","paragraphs":["Zheng Yuande: ...... Doesn't the Crown Princess pay any attention to the recent court affairs at all?","The corners of his mouth twitched a few times as he listened to the Crown Princess chatting and laughing with the Crown Prince as if no one else was around.","The atmosphere had been perfectly pleasant just a moment ago, but the Crown Princess had truly, of her own accord, poured oil straight onto the fire for His Highness.","The General of Agile Cavalry, the Crown Prince's young maternal uncle, had been back in the capital for three months, and during that time, those idle, overfed civil officials would seize any chance they got to submit a memorial accusing him of some offense.","That would have been bad enough on its own.","A few days prior, it was the old man from the Privy Council who had first rudely bumped into the General of Agile Cavalry, then even made outrageous, disrespectful remarks about the General, which led the General to beat him.","But the end result was that the General was impeached by the civil officials and imperial censors, and in the end, His Majesty reprimanded and admonished him, even stripping the General of his post as the military governor of Zhenguo Army!","The Crown Prince had stood up to speak in the General's defense, and for that, he had been reprimanded by His Majesty twice in the past few days.","Right now, the Crown Prince probably could not bear to hear anything about the divide between civil and military officials.","But in the Great Yong Dynasty, the tradition of valuing civil officials over military officials had long been so deeply rooted that it had become second nature to everyone in the court and the commonalty, even ordinary civilians.","If civil and military officials happened to cross paths on the road, even a military officer of higher rank would have to make way for a civil official who was one or two grades lower than them. This had already become an established unwritten rule.","But the Crown Prince and the General of Agile Cavalry were only five years apart in age, and the two had shared a deep, close bond since childhood.","When the Crown Princess heard that the Crown Prince was planning to go to Lady Shen's courtyard, she froze for a split second, and a twinge of jealousy rose unconsciously in her heart.","Yet she still smiled with dignified grace and said, \"Your Highness, Lady Shen does not understand proper etiquette as well as the several talented ladies who come from scholarly families. I am afraid she might end up offending you...\"","The Crown Prince suddenly cut in, \"Does not understand proper etiquette?\" His tone was slightly heavy, the thin, sharp corners of his eyes drooped slightly, and his dark, pitch-black eyes revealed no emotion at all.","The Crown Princess was slightly stunned, and before she could react, she saw that he had already stood up, said that there were still matters to attend to in the front hall, and left.","His expression looked no different from his usual one.","It made her unable to help but wonder... if that glance he had given her just now had only been her imagination.","She rose to curtsy, \"I see Your Highness off, Your Highness.\"","Matron Zhou, who was standing at her side waiting for the others to leave, then whispered, \"Your Highness, this old servant has heard that the entire front court has been in an uproar over the recent incident where the General of Agile Cavalry beat a court official in the street. The Crown Prince is likely in a bad mood because of this matter.\"","The Crown Princess knitted her brows in dissatisfaction. \"Military generals with high merit that overshadow the sovereign are bound to make His Majesty, the Emperor, wary. His Highness's uncle is so undisciplined, does not know how to behave low-key, and keeps causing trouble for His Highness everywhere. Why doesn't the old Duke Fengguo and the old matriarch of the Fengguo Manor discipline him...\"","Matron Zhou sighed and said, \"The old Duke Fengguo now only has the Duke Fengguo, who is disabled in both legs, and this youngest son, who is in good health. He was born when the old Duke was already advanced in age, so it is only natural that he is too reluctant to discipline him strictly.","\"This old servant thinks... perhaps it is because the General of Agile Cavalry has not yet taken a wife and started a family, that he remains so unstable in his actions at his age.\"","The Crown Princess pursed her lips, frowned and thought for a moment, then said, \"What Matron said makes sense. I should speak to the Empress later, and ask her to persuade His Highness's uncle to get married as soon as possible.\"","But as a younger generation, arranging a marriage for an elder would, after all, look rather inappropriate.","She would have to send a message to her own mother, and let her mother find an opportunity to bring it up to the Empress.","Seeing that she still looked deeply troubled, Matron Zhou comforted her, \"Your Highness, there is no need to worry. You already have the little imperial grandson under your protection. No matter which courtyard the Crown Prince visits, no matter which person in the rear palace gains His favor, no one's favor can ever shake your position. We only need to sit back and watch the drama unfold with peace of mind.\"","The Crown Princess knitted her brows, her heart still filled with displeasure, but as the Crown Princess, His Highness currently only had one son and one daughter under his knees, and the imperial descendants were far too few. She could not monopolize the Crown Prince all to herself...","Otherwise, the voices from outside calling her jealous would be enough to drown her out.","Worse still, she had to maintain the demeanor of a virtuous, magnanimous Crown Princess to build an even better reputation for herself.","She could only force the unwillingness in her heart down by telling herself that even when the Crown Prince went to other people's courtyards, he would still keep his usual cold, distant manner, and would never treat anyone with any special favor.","*","The clouds merged like a jade disc, the sunlight faded away, and the night sky was dotted with tiny stars.","Zheng Yuande saw that the time was just about right, so he stepped forward softly and whispered, \"Your Highness, it is almost time to light the palace lanterns. Which courtyard does Your Highness plan to stay for the night tonight?\"","Although the Crown Prince had said in front of the Crown Princess earlier that he was going to Lady Shen's place, he still asked one more cautious question, not daring to make the decision on his own.","Cui Yu frowned slightly, closed the book he was holding, stood up, brushed the dust off his sleeves, and said in a deep, solemn voice, \"Let's go.\"","\"Understood, Your Highness.\" Zheng Yuande quickly lifted the palace lantern and led the way ahead.","*","\"Master, here are the golden crispy chicken, peach blossom pastries, and donkey-hide gelatin silver ear milk drink you asked for.\" Chunping took the food box from Quanshou, quickly walked around the folding screen, and entered the eastern warm pavilion.","Shen Yanshui had long been sitting at the round table waiting eagerly. Now, seeing Chunping walk in, her pair of peach blossom eyes sparkled, almost glowing as they fixed on the food box in her hand.","\"Hurry up and set them all out.\" She had never expected that the diet kitchen in the Eastern Palace could make such delicious food, far better than the food she had eaten in the Xiuzhen Palace back then, and even better than the food the chefs in her father's marquis manor made.","Now that she had tasted such wonderful food, how could she ever go back to the old way?","At Shenshi, around 4 p.m., she had eaten a wonderful late meal, including spicy shrimp and jade thick soup, crispy deep-fried pork, and wine-steamed lamb slices, which had made her feel so happy she almost floated off the ground.","With cooking skills like this, she could stay in the Eastern Palace for a hundred years without ever wanting to leave!","The only drawback was that it cost a little more silver, but other than that, it was absolutely perfect.","It was almost the time of Xu, a little after 8 p.m., the perfect hour for a midnight snack.","In the west side hall opposite, Lady Liu, who had dressed up elaborately and was sitting restlessly, heard the movement from across the courtyard and could not help asking, Yinping, what is going on outside? Could it be that the Crown Prince has arrived?","Deep down, she knew very well that the Crown Prince would most likely not visit her place today, but what if he did?","A tiny sliver of hope lingered in her heart, so much so that she could barely bring herself to take a few bites of her dinner.","Yinping knew very well that if the Crown Prince had arrived, the noise would not be what they had just heard, but she still obeyed her mistress's order to go outside and take a look. She then came back to report, \"Mistress, according to Yinye, the people in the courtyard opposite just sent someone to the diet kitchen to fetch a midnight snack, and it has just been brought in.\"","Lady Liu could not believe her ears. \"A midnight snack?\"","\"How can she even have an appetite for a midnight snack at this hour?\" As she spoke, she curled her lip slightly, thinking to herself that as expected, someone from a military family would have no proper manners and be completely unrefined.","Did she know full well that His Highness would not visit her place tonight? So she had just given up on herself and stopped caring about appearances?","She quickly pushed those thoughts aside, but still could not resist urging her servants to send someone to keep watch outside the courtyard.","*","The moment the Crown Prince stepped onto the corridor in front of the back cover house, the hearts of all the mistresses in every courtyard and room in the rear palace instantly lifted.","Among all of them, Lady Zhang and Lady Wu were the most nervous.","Everyone knew that the Crown Prince was always extremely strict with etiquette and abided by the rules. Logically speaking, his first night after arriving at the rear palace should have been spent in Lady Zhang's courtyard.","Lady Wu, Wu Chenghui, had always been proud of her own beauty, and today, after receiving praise from the Crown Princess, she was at the height of her elation and arrogance, with no intention of thinking otherwise. When she learned that the Crown Prince was heading in the direction of her courtyard, she was instantly filled with both surprise and smug delight. She hurriedly leaned over her dressing mirror to check if there was anything amiss with her face and attire, all the while urging her servants, \"Come, let us go wait for the Crown Prince at the courtyard gate.\"","\"Understood!\" The servants waiting on her were also rarely excited. If their mistress won the Crown Prince's favor tonight, they would gain a fair amount of prestige moving about the Eastern Palace from then on.","But just moments after stepping out, before Lady Wu could even reach the gate, the maid who had been brimming with excitement earlier came hurrying back with a pale, troubled look on her face. Facing her mistress, who was already dressed in ornate, lavish attire, the maid spoke carefully, stammering a little, \"Mistress... the Crown Prince has entered... the adjacent Lotus Heart Courtyard.\"","The bright smile that had been on Lady Wu's face instantly vanished, her expression darkening completely.","*","Shen Yanshui was just savoring a mouthful of sweet, rich donkey-hide gelatin and silver fungus milk beverage when she heard the commotion outside the courtyard. When Chunping came rushing in almost tripping over her own feet to report that the Crown Prince had already arrived at the courtyard entrance, and with the sound of successive greetings of respect rising from every other courtyard, Shen Yanshui nearly choked on her sip of milk.","There was no time to tidy things up. She took a deep breath and hurried to the gate, where she could faintly make out the tall, broad-shouldered, long-legged figure of a man walking toward her at an unhurried pace, surrounded by eunuchs standing bowed on both sides. She did not even have time to lift her head to get a clear look at the newcomer's face before she hurriedly curtsied in greeting.","\"This humble wife Shen greets the Crown Prince. May Your Highness enjoy peace and good health.\" She was uncharacteristically a little nervous.","Her entire attention was fixed on the person standing only two steps away from her. By the glow of the candlelight spilling out from the room, she could even make out the patterns on the dark black leather belt at his waist, as well as the shimmering silver threads woven into his purple robe that caught the light.","Wait, what was the Crown Prince doing here? Hadn't everyone said the Crown Prince was the most strict observer of rules? Why had he come to her courtyard of all places?","Zheng Yuande could not help but think that this Lady Shen really was a free, unconstrained spirit! Not only had she not been waiting at the gate early to welcome the Crown Prince as others did, she had only hurried out to offer her greeting right as His Highness was about to step through the door.","Zheng Yuande glanced at her, and it was obvious she had not even finished dressing properly.","By all proper etiquette, even on days when the Crown Prince was not expected to visit, one should still dress neatly and wait for news of His Highness's arrangements, only extinguishing their lamps to rest once they had confirmed he would not be coming. That was the standard custom in the Eastern Palace.","Cui Yu lowered his eyes and glanced at her.","Shen Yanshui was wearing a narrow-sleeve blouse of pale lotus root pink plain silk, over which she had draped a half-sleeve gown in the color of sky-blue water. Her hair was styled in a tassel bun, tied only with a sky-blue ribbon, all other ornaments having been taken off long ago. She did not wear the heavy, elaborate makeup and lavish jewelry that the other ladies had put on.","She was as fresh as a lotus rising from clear water, unadorned and uncarved, her natural beauty shining through.","\"Rise.\"","Shen Yanshui had kept her head bowed in the greeting posture, and at the sound of his clear, steady voice, she caught a glimpse from the corner of her eye of him lifting his feet and walking past her into the room, the hem of his purple robe brushing lightly against the edge of her skirt.","She still had no idea why the Crown Prince had decided to visit her courtyard tonight, but since he was already here, after the initial shock of being caught completely off guard, she had calmed down a little.","She watched him lift the corner of his robe and settle down on the couch, and that was when she finally got a clear look at his face. Her eyes lit up instantly.","He was as handsome as a jade carving, his features as fine as a painting, his demeanor gentle and refined yet carrying an innate noble majesty. He was even more striking than she had imagined.","Cui Yu suddenly lifted his gaze to look at her. Their eyes met, and Shen Yanshui blinked those naturally charming, bright peach blossom eyes of hers, stepping forward two steps with a sincere smile as she softly explained, \"Your Highness has arrived at just the right moment. The chefs in the Changqing Palace's kitchen make such delicious food, so this humble one prepared a little late-night snack. Would Your Highness care to share it with me?\"","She spoke with a warm smile, saying what was meant to be a polite opening to ease the tension, her heart a little nervous, and a little regretful that she had only taken a few bites of the snack on the table.","Cui Yu turned his gaze to the several plates of food on the table, then noticed the way she had glanced at those dishes no less than several times in just a short moment, her little look of undisguised reluctance and craving.","He had not had any appetite to speak of at first, but seeing that obvious, endearing look on her face, he suddenly nodded in agreement.","Shen Yanshui had only meant to make conversation, to offer a gentle, respectful remark, and never expected him to actually say yes."]},{"number":5,"title":"Chapter 5: An Exploration","paragraphs":["Shen Yanshui looked toward the round-faced, fair and plump eunuch standing behind him. Though he looked to be only in his twenties, he was the chief eunuch, Zheng Yuande.","There was no way she had the nerve to let the Crown Prince eat food she had already eaten.","Seeing this, Zheng Yuande was delighted and hurriedly ordered the kitchens to prepare another late-night meal that would be easy to digest.","The Crown Prince’s requested food arrived far more quickly than anything Shen Yanshui had obtained by spending her own money.","Before long, the dishes were laid out, though they were nowhere near as lavish as she had imagined. Aside from another serving of the food she had previously ordered, there was also a bowl of four-delicacy soup, a bowl of fish soup, and a bowl of chicken congee. Compared with his status, it could even be called simple.","Everything looked light and easy to digest.","She stood properly beside him, serving him food and ladling out the congee. With a smile, she said, “Your Highness, try this chicken congee. I had a bowl during dinner as well. I wonder which chef made it—it was so fragrant.”","Hearing the sincerity and delight in her voice, Cui Yu almost couldn’t help wondering whether the Eastern Palace had changed its head chef and kitchen director today.","But after tasting it, he found that it was no different from usual.","Naturally, nothing that reached his table would be poor in quality. Yet he could not sense the joy and satisfaction toward good food conveyed in her tone.","He said in a low voice, “There’s no need to stand and serve me. Sit down and eat with me.”","The moment he finished speaking, the unmistakable surprise and delight in her eyes caught his attention.","Zheng Yuande watched helplessly as Lady Shen beamed, bowed to thank His Highness, and then plopped herself down securely in her seat—she really sat down.","Shen Yanshui was indeed very happy. After all, the Crown Prince did not seem to have a bad temper, and he had not taken offense at her lack of decorum. Now he was even letting her enjoy a meal for free. How could she not be pleased?","“Mmm—so fragrant and delicious!” The moment Shen Yanshui swallowed a mouthful of fish soup, she couldn’t help widening her eyes slightly at the flavor. With a taste like this, she felt she could eat two more bowls!","Still, good food had to be shared fairly. She couldn’t neglect any of it.","After finishing a little less than half a bowl of fish soup, she had another half bowl of four-delicacy soup. The freshly prepared golden chicken couldn’t go to waste, either. As expected, food made for the Crown Prince was different—she felt even the texture of the chicken was more tender and delicious.","“Mmm!” The instant it entered her mouth, she unconsciously let out the highest praise one could give to a delicacy.","Zheng Yuande’s eyes nearly popped out of his head!","He had never seen a woman like this. The women of Changqing Palace all kept their nerves taut whenever they served His Highness. Who actually ate properly? Didn’t they all take only a couple of bites before claiming to be full?","They were afraid of making a fool of themselves in front of His Highness or leaving him with a bad impression.","He had never seen anyone eat so much—or with such relish—in the Crown Prince’s presence.","Cui Yu was rather surprised as well. He stared at her for quite some time and discovered that she was truly focused on eating.","Her pace was not slow, but her movements were not at all coarse. The satisfied, happy expression between her brows made it seem as though the food in her bowl was even more delicious than everything on the table.","When she ate the four-delicacy soup, he saw that although she finished everything in her bowl, her expression was considerably more subdued.","He lowered his eyes to the four-delicacy soup before him and suddenly felt as though it had lost all its flavor.","After finishing a piece of golden chicken, Shen Yanshui immediately reached for a second. But when she looked up, she saw that the Crown Prince beside her had stopped eating.","She became anxious at once. If he wasn’t going to eat anymore, how was she supposed to continue?","With a concerned, hopeful, and utterly sincere expression, she said, “Why aren’t you eating, Your Highness? This golden chicken is even more delicious than the piece I had earlier. I wonder how it was made—it even has a faint aroma of wine. Your Highness, you should try some too.”","Cui Yu raised his eyes to meet her earnest, expectant gaze. After pausing for a moment, he nodded.","The eunuch serving him, who had been watching his master’s expression closely, immediately picked up a piece of golden chicken and placed it in his bowl.","Seeing him start eating again, Shen Yanshui smiled at once and hurriedly took another piece of the fragrant, golden-brown chicken.","After a while, Shen Yanshui finally ate her fill. Eight-tenths full was just right. She had only just taken a bite of a peach blossom pastry no bigger than her thumb when she looked up and saw the Crown Prince beside her eating with unhurried elegance. Every one of his movements was graceful and pleasing to the eye.","Cui Yu leisurely put down his bowl and chopsticks and picked up a peach blossom pastry.","Seeing that he had eaten quite a bit as well, Shen Yanshui smiled and asked, “Your Highness, would you like to take a walk in the courtyard to aid digestion?”","“Mm.”","Cui Yu did not refuse. He had always exercised restraint, and food was no exception. But somehow, he seemed to have eaten a little too much just now.","Zheng Yuande glanced at the table and smiled broadly, having long since put everything else out of his mind. As long as His Highness was willing to eat properly, the rest did not matter.","After rinsing their mouths and washing their hands, the two of them left the eastern side hall, one following the other with a distance of about half a body between them.","Shen Yanshui looked up at the night sky. The silver moon hung high overhead, and stars glittered brightly. Moonlight spilled across the courtyard paved with bluestone, illuminating the originally dim space.","Just as she was preparing to find some topic of conversation, a deep, slightly low voice suddenly reached her ears.","“What do you usually do at home?”","Shen Yanshui glanced sideways at him. From where she stood, she could clearly see his expression. Both his voice and his manner appeared gentle and calm, yet for some reason, she felt that the Crown Prince was not in a particularly good mood.","She instinctively became more cautious and replied with a smile, “In answer to Your Highness, this concubine is rather foolish. I’ve been a little playful since childhood. Unlike my elder sister, who is skilled in music, chess, calligraphy, and painting, my needlework and embroidery are only passable. Usually, I enjoy fishing, tending flowers, swinging, playing cuju, and playing polo. Most importantly, I love eating all kinds of delicious food.”","The Crown Prince certainly knew all about her background. No matter what, if possible, she should first make it clear that she had nothing to do with her elder sister. Ideally, she would have him believe that she was not one of Noble Consort Lan’s people, nor anyone’s pawn.","She would be spending the rest of her life in the Eastern Palace. If she could improve her quality of life, naturally she ought to do so.","Chunping, following behind them at a respectful distance alongside Zheng Yuande, nearly blacked out twice in succession. Zheng Yuande, meanwhile, was first startled, then even more startled.","Chunping: Mistress, even if we can’t do anything, you can’t say that in front of the Crown Prince!","Zheng Yuande: What a perfect opportunity to be alone with His Highness. Instead of putting on a good showing, she had gone so far as to expose all her shortcomings without the slightest hesitation. He had truly never seen anyone like her...","She could at least have pretended a little! As for needlework and such, even if she herself was no good at it, didn’t she have servants who could do it for her?","How had everything simply tumbled out of her mouth the moment His Highness casually asked a question? Was she not a little dim-witted?","Cui Yu turned back to look at her. Seeing her smiling with her eyes curved into crescents, his brows shifted slightly. He had already realized that she liked to eat, but...","“You know how to play cuju and polo? Did your family hire tutors to teach you?”","Shen Yanshui smiled somewhat sheepishly and said softly, “To answer Your Highness, they weren’t tutors hired by my family. In fact, my parents always taught me that a woman should be chaste, composed, virtuous, and refined. They didn’t like me playing cuju or polo, so the instructors my family hired were all women who taught the qin, chess, calligraphy, painting, flower arranging, tea ceremony, and needlework.”","“I have some interest in playing the qin and painting, so I learned a little of both. As for the rest, I suppose I simply don’t have the talent, so I didn’t force myself to continue.”","As she spoke, her smile grew sincere. She did not seem to think there was anything wrong with not knowing those other skills.","Cui Yu studied the smile on her face and asked with a furrowed brow, “Since your parents forbade it, why did you learn them at all?”","Shen Yanshui tilted her head to look at him and answered with a perfectly natural smile, “Because I like them!”","Then, pressing her lips together in a smile, she added, “Besides, I would never go and tell them that I play cuju and polo. I play in secret. Other than my personal maidservants, no one else knows.”","Cui Yu’s brows lifted slightly. He did not seem to mind that she alternated between calling herself “this wife” and “I.”","The corners of Shen Yanshui’s beautiful, expressive eyes lifted with triumph. Her eyes seemed to reflect scattered stars, dazzling and bright.","She blinked and said, “They were the ones who said it themselves: a woman obeys her husband after marriage. Now that I belong to Your Highness, even if my parents found out, they can’t control me anymore.”","Looking at her lively, spirited face, Cui Yu unconsciously let out a soft laugh. The heavy stone that had long weighed on his heart seemed to loosen slightly.","He only wondered how long a pair of such lively, vibrant eyes would be able to exist in this palace.","His voice suddenly turned somber. “Then why tell me? Aren’t you afraid I might forbid it as well—or dislike it?”","Her heart trembled, and she was startled by the sudden change in his expression. But only for a brief moment. She soon realized that he was deliberately trying to frighten her.","For a moment, Shen Yanshui was at a loss for words. Yet when she considered that the Crown Prince was only about twenty, having just come of age, and saw that even with his face stern and solemn, he remained devastatingly handsome, her mood brightened again.","“Because Your Highness asked,” she murmured. Then, in a small voice, she asked, “Your Highness... do you dislike it?”","Cui Yu paused for a moment before suddenly asking, “If I disliked it, would you stop doing it from now on?”"]},{"number":6,"title":"Chapter 6: His Highness Has Never Been Fond of Women","paragraphs":["Shen Yanshui lowered her head slightly and secretly glanced up at him, saying nothing.","One look at her crystal-clear eyes, in which every thought was laid bare, and Cui Yu could practically read everything on her mind. He couldn’t help finding it amusing.","At last, seeing that his mood seemed to have improved somewhat, Shen Yanshui said earnestly, “Your Highness, playing cuju and polo isn’t merely for amusement. It also helps strengthen the body and makes one less prone to illness. It accomplishes several things at once—what could be better?”","Cui Yu lowered his eyes to her eager expression. This time, he did not try to frighten her again. He smiled and said, “As you say, it is indeed a good thing. There is an open space in the garden of the Palace of Eternal Celebration. If you have nothing to do, you may go there and play.”","Shen Yanshui’s eyes lit up. “Thank you, Your Highness.”","Her voice was filled with such delight that even those who heard it couldn’t help feeling their own spirits lift.","Shen Yanshui was not merely happy because she would now be able to play cuju and polo openly.","It was because, through their brief exchange just now, she had discovered that the Crown Prince was not quite as she had imagined.","Compared with the Crown Prince of the rumors—strictly bound by rules, self-disciplined, respectful of propriety, and dignified to the point of severity—the man before her was indeed imposing and intimidating when expressionless, but he had not held her several lapses in etiquette against her.","Some of those lapses had been unintentional and caught her off guard, while others had come from the cautious little tests she had deliberately made afterward.","Naturally, this kind of Crown Prince pleased her far more than the one in the rumors. At the very least, her days in the Eastern Palace would not be too difficult.","However, the peculiar concern he had shown just now, both in his words and his expression, for cuju and polo suddenly reminded her of some scattered rumors about him from five years ago, before the emperor had formally made him Crown Prince...","In the Great Yong, the appointment of a crown prince followed ancestral custom: if there was a son born to the empress, he was to be made crown prince; if there was no such son, the eldest son would be chosen.","The current emperor, Emperor Pingyuan, had many children, but the empress had only one son among them—the third prince.","Because the third prince had been born with a congenital weakness and had often fallen ill as a child, there had been concerns that he would be unable to shoulder the responsibility of becoming the heir to the empire. Thus, he had not been made crown prince at the time.","It was only after the empress sent the young third prince to be raised for several years at her maternal family’s residence, the Duke Fengguo’s estate, that his health gradually improved.","The Duke Fengguo’s family had been hereditary nobles and military commanders for generations. By the time the third prince was a teenager, after spending several years at their residence, his martial skills had already become quite impressive. At fourteen, during a hunt at the Western Hills, he had outshone all the sons of the noble military families and single-handedly hunted a bear, winning first place.","For a time, his fame was unrivaled.","Yet it was said that because of this, the third prince had instead been harshly reprimanded and punished by Emperor Pingyuan.","As for cuju, polo, and the like, those were merely games he had long since mastered. Otherwise, she would never have dared bring them up so casually.","After he was made Crown Prince at the age of fifteen, however, the Crown Prince spoken of by those around him grew more and more composed and measured with each passing year. Several years had gone by, and she had nearly forgotten those old rumors about him in the capital.","A cool breeze swept past, and Shen Yanshui shivered instinctively.","Cui Yu reached out and took her hand. “It is getting late. Go back and rest.”","Shen Yanshui froze for a moment. Her hand, which had been somewhat chilled, was now completely enclosed in his broad, warm palm. Taking advantage of the situation, she moved closer and pressed herself tightly against his arm. The next moment, she clearly felt his arm tense for an instant, as though on instinct.","She lifted her head and blinked at him as if nothing had happened. “Your Highness, it’s warmer this way.”","Cui Yu: “...”","He raised his eyes and glanced around. Night had already fallen, and they were within his own palace. With the evening dew growing heavier, he ultimately said nothing.","Walking behind them, Zheng Yuande clicked his tongue softly.","So the Crown Prince liked this sort of empty-headed girl?","Could Lady Shen really be one of those fools blessed by sheer luck?","Just look at her background. She was already a source of considerable trouble. Noble Consort Lan and the fourth prince were both eager to pull their Crown Prince down and seize his position for themselves.","Lady Shen’s elder sister had lived in Noble Consort Lan’s Palace of Abundant Blessings ever since entering the palace. Though she was only a minor figure, she was still one of Noble Consort Lan’s people.","Wasn’t this move nothing more than an obvious attempt to disgust the Eastern Palace—a clear effort to plant a pawn there? Yet it had been approved by His Majesty himself, so the Eastern Palace could not do anything to her.","At least for the time being, the Eastern Palace could not show any dissatisfaction openly. Otherwise, Noble Consort Lan’s faction would surely stir up trouble before His Majesty again.","Even so, barring any unexpected turn of events, Lady Shen was destined to spend her entire life without favor, growing old alone.","And yet, the Crown Princess had inadvertently struck a tender spot in the Crown Prince’s heart. The Crown Prince had ignored the courtyards of the two higher-ranking ladies from distinguished families and had instead come to the residence of Lady Shen, the daughter of a noble military family.","If that wasn’t a fool’s good fortune, what was?","Shen Yanshui had no idea that others now regarded her as a fool.","After bathing and changing, she walked around the carved rosewood screen depicting lakes and mountains. To her surprise, she found that the Crown Prince was already lying on the bed with his eyes closed.","She muttered instinctively, “He fell asleep rather quickly.”","According to the rules, she should have bathed and dressed herself early, then waited in exquisite makeup for the Crown Prince’s summons. When it came time to attend him, there was no reason for a mere concubine like her to make the Crown Prince wait.","It was just that tonight had not gone according to plan.","Seeing Chunping’s anxious expression, she waved her hand and dismissed everyone. Zheng Yuande, meanwhile, had withdrawn with great tact as soon as she came out and had ordered people to prepare hot water.","Quanfu, who had been waiting respectfully with his back bent, immediately went downstairs to make the arrangements. Then, smiling obsequiously, he said in a low voice to Zheng Yuande, “Eunuch Zheng, you’ve been working hard all day as well. I’ll wait here, so why don’t you go to the tea room and rest your feet over a cup of hot tea? If His Highness needs anything, I’ll send someone to call you.”","Zheng Yuande cast him a sidelong glance. “You seem fairly quick on the uptake. In that case, this household will go rest for a while. Make sure you all keep your eyes open and be careful.”","Quanshou, who had been standing nearby, immediately bent forward and came over with a broad smile to lead the way.","Only then did Zheng Yuande’s face relax into a smile. He nodded in satisfaction.","There were plenty of people who wanted to rack their brains to curry favor with him in his position. He was not afraid of those who eagerly rushed to flatter him. What he feared were people without sense, whose eyes were fixed only on ingratiating themselves with him while forgetting who their true master was.","In Lady Shen’s residence, the maid named Chunping appeared reasonably steady. That round-faced young eunuch, on the other hand, knew how to handle people and had a sweet tongue. Yet he did not seem like the sort of shortsighted person who cared only about his own interests. Otherwise, the one he had led to the tea room would have been himself.","Inside the room, Shen Yanshui slipped forward in her soft-soled embroidered slippers. She craned her neck to look at him, finding him with his eyes closed, apparently already asleep. Unable to resist, she studied him carefully for a few moments.","His brows and eyes were deep-set, and his lashes were very long. With his eyes closed, they resembled two little fans. Looking at them made her fingertips itch, as though she wanted to reach out and touch them.","She had noticed from the side earlier that the line of his jaw was sharp yet smooth and graceful. She hadn’t expected him to look so handsome even while lying down.","Most importantly, the color and shape of his lips were beautiful too...","Cui Yu was not asleep, he was just resting his eyes in quiet repose. Just as he was about to open them, he keenly caught the sight of her gaze, which had suddenly frozen on his face. Thinking of her status, he held still for a moment.","Then... his brows drew together.","He opened his eyes abruptly, looking right at her pair of eyes that had widened in a flash, his own gaze momentarily confused, even at a loss for words.","\"What were you... doing just now?\"","Shen Yanshui withdrew the finger that had been brushing his eyelid as if nothing had happened, then kicked off her shoes, climbed onto the bed and tucked herself under the covers in one smooth motion.","Cui Yu turned over to face her, his voice slightly low and heavy. \"Speak.\"","Shen Yanshui half-hid her face under the quilt, her voice muffled and halting with obvious embarrassment. \"I thought Your Highness was already asleep, I had no idea you were still awake...\"","With his sharp, dark eyes fixed on her from such close distance, Shen Yanshui began to feel rather pressured. Sure enough, a man was far more pleasant to look at when his eyes were closed.","\"Your Highness, has anyone ever told you that you are exceptionally good-looking?\"","Seeing him frown, she tugged the quilt down a little at once, her tone utterly sincere, her eyes shining bright as she looked at him. \"I mean it truly. Just now I was looking at you, and suddenly thought the Crown Prince is so handsome, every part of you is perfect, even your eyelashes are so thick, long and curly... I have no idea what came over my finger, it seemed to have a mind of its own...\"","\"...\" Cui Yu stared at her pleading, fawning gaze, listening to this unblushing, unreserved compliment that left him stunned for a split second.","As the empress's own son, he had heard endless streams of praise around him growing up, but never anything as straightforward and unmasked as hers.","He was the Crown Prince of Great Yong, every word and action of his was watched by all in the court and beyond. No one ever paid attention to his looks, and even if they did, no one would ever dare say such a thing to his face.","Held by her unhidden, candid gaze, he turned back and lay down.","Just as Shen Yanshui let out a quiet sigh of relief, thinking the matter was over, a tall, strong, lean figure suddenly loomed over her.","Shen Yanshui: \"???\" This is so sudden!","The first time, Shen Yanshui played the part of the shy new consort, making no movements of her own, strictly following the rules the palace matrons had taught her. After all, according to palace regulations, leaving any marks on the Crown Prince's body was a serious offense that harmed his noble person.","When it ended, it had seemed a little... brief. Wait? She froze all at once. That just now... was that a special ability?!","Her heart skipped a beat, but when she tried to sense that faint strange feeling again, it vanished completely without a trace.","Cui Yu noticed that she had drifted off into a trance, and frowned in displeasure...","\"Ah...\" Shen Yanshui yelped out in surprise when his actions caught her off guard, and her thoughts were pulled back entirely to the present.","The second time, she dropped her act halfway, deciding it was time to try something different. After all... this man's skills in bed were really far from ideal.","This was supposed to be something that brought pleasure to both people, and she had no intention of suffering through it all by herself for the rest of her days.","She stretched out her arms, wrapping them softly around his shoulders, and felt his whole body go taut at once. Her palms could clearly feel the defined, firm muscles under his skin.","In the dim moonlight, she could make out the outline of his lean, strong form, not perfectly clear, but the real, solid touch under her hands told her without a doubt that his body was more perfect than any she had ever seen before.","She whispered two soft sentences right by his ear.","Cui Yu: \"...Mm.\"","Hearing his cool, reserved voice, Shen Yanshui had originally planned to take it slow that night, and make gradual adjustments later. After all, even though the palace matrons would instruct young ladies selected for the imperial harem on matters of the bed, it would be rather improper for an unmarried girl to know too much about them.","But to her surprise, he stopped relying entirely on brute force and reckless, clumsy movements right after that, and instead kept his eyes fixed intently on her face.","She responded to him tentatively.","Soon she realized he was carefully watching her reactions, and this small discovery made her feel quite happy.","Judging by Cui Yu's temperament as he had shown so far, he was by and large a rather tolerant man.","Her mind wandered off for a brief moment, only to be pulled apart by his movements, and she sank fully into the moment.","That night, to Cui Yu's own surprise, he called for water to be brought in twice.","For Zheng Yuande, the incident was nothing short of earth-shattering!","His master had never been one to favor sensual pleasures, one round of such activities at most was already the norm. This was the very first time His Highness had called for water twice in one night.","This Lady Shen is truly no ordinary woman!"]},{"number":7,"title":"Chapter 7: Golden-edge Daphne","paragraphs":["Early the next morning, at the first pale glimmer of dawn, Shen Yanshui was still deep in sleep when someone gently roused her.","Her eyes would barely open. Buried beneath the covers, she struggled to pry them open a sliver and saw a faint, hazy light filtering through the bed curtains. In a hoarse, drowsy voice, she asked, “What time is it?”","Chunping answered with a smile, “My lady, it is now three-quarters into the Hour of the Rabbit. It is time to pay our respects to the Crown Princess.”","Shen Yanshui grew a little more alert at that, though her body still did not feel quite well. Thinking of how the Crown Prince had risen at three-quarters into the Hour of the Tiger—just after four in the morning—she could not help but admire him.","Getting up so early every day, attending court, hearing matters of state... Hm?","Wait.","She suddenly jolted upright!","That familiar sensation within her body... could this be... her ability?!","She immediately dismissed everyone from the room, then, almost unable to wait, examined the strange energy that seemed to have suddenly appeared inside her.","It was real. It was not her imagination...","Opening her eyes again, she reached for a branch of half-bloomed peach blossoms from the white porcelain vase on the small table beside her bed and activated her ability.","In mere moments, the buds on the peach branch burst fully into bloom.","Shen Yanshui was overjoyed.","But what was going on? Why had her ability shown no sign of returning for more than ten years, only to suddenly reappear today?","The greatest difference from before was... she had slept with the Crown Prince?","“My lady, it is nearly time. We must not delay any longer,” Chunping reminded her softly from outside.","Shen Yanshui placed the branch back into the vase and called for the attendants to come in.","Whatever the reason, the return of her ability was unquestionably wonderful news.","Xia'an stepped quietly into the inner chamber, bowed, and raised a copper basin of warm water above her head with both hands, waiting for her mistress to rise and wash.","After Shen Yanshui had gotten up and finished washing, she glanced at the brightly colored garments prepared nearby—pomegranate red and begonia pink—and said, “Bring me the lotus-pink one. Put my hair in a small round bun, and the pearl moon crown will do.”","Xia'an, waiting at the side, hesitated for a moment before asking quietly, “My lady, would the lotus-pink one be a little too plain?”","Qiuhe murmured her acknowledgment and began carefully arranging her mistress’s hair and makeup.","Shen Yanshui smiled at Xia'an’s words. “A little plain is exactly right. Do as I said.”","“Yes, my lady,” Xia'an replied.","When it came to clothing and adornment, Shen Yanshui’s preference was simply to remain moderate. She could not dress too plainly or too modestly, lest others take her for timid and easy to bully; but neither could she stand out too much and attract unwanted attention. The fewer troubles she invited, the better.","In Great Yong, married women wore all their hair pinned up in an assortment of styles. The round bun was one of the more common ones.","Common women decorated their buns with ribbons and hairpins, while among noblewomen, ornate floral crowns had become fashionable in recent years. The pearl moon crown was one such style.","The April morning sky was still gray and dim, with a faint chill in the air. Before leaving, Shen Yanshui draped a cloak over her shoulders. The moment she stepped outside, she saw Lady Liu already waiting in the courtyard, dressed rather lightly, her slender figure appearing all the more graceful for it.","“Greetings, Sister Shen.” Lady Liu was dressed rather thinly, her lips trembling slightly from the cold. Seeing Shen Yanshui’s rosy cheeks and radiant complexion, she could not help but feel a touch of envy.","Just looking at Lady Liu made Shen Yanshui feel cold. Although, after gaining her ability, she would likely become impervious to heat and cold, the habits she had formed over so many years were not so easily changed.","“No need for such formality. Lady Liu, you should put on more layers, lest you catch a chill.”","Lady Liu tugged at the corner of her lips in a smile. “Thank you for your concern, Sister Shen, but I am not cold.”","Seeing this, Shen Yanshui said no more. She set out from Lotus Heart Court with Chunping, while Lady Liu was accompanied by a palace maid of her own. The four of them had just left the courtyard when they looked up to see another group of four approaching from the opposite end of the passageway. The two parties happened to meet before Moonlight Gate.","Shen Yanshui was the first to offer a salute, saying with a smile, “Greetings, Lady Zhang.” Lady Liu at her side and Lady Zhao, who stood beside Lady Zhang, likewise curtsied in greeting.","Lady Zhang wore a moon-white cross-collared blouse, paired with a fragrant-consort-pink pleated skirt embroidered with plum blossoms. Over it, she had draped a sky-blue, wide-sleeved open-front robe. Her hair was arranged in a single spiral bun, adorned with a white-jade plum blossom hairpin, a look that suited her refined and scholarly air perfectly.","Only her makeup seemed somewhat heavy; her complexion had been powdered a little too white.","“Lady Shen, please rise.” Lady Zhang smiled at Shen Yanshui’s strikingly beautiful face, though a faint bitterness lingered in her expression.","Though she held the highest rank among the Crown Prince’s new women, he had not visited her chambers the previous night. The thought left a bitter taste in her heart—and made her lose face as well.","For now, she could only console herself that it had been Lady Shen rather than Lady Wu.","At least Lady Shen did not appear to be the sort to be sharp-tongued, competitive, or cruel. Had Lady Wu been the one favored last night, who knew how she might have flaunted it and mocked Lady Zhang today?","After exchanging formal greetings, they said nothing further. After all, they were not yet acquainted.","Shen Yanshui glanced at Lady Zhao, who stood behind Lady Zhang. She had never met her before; then Lady Zhao must have been one of the women already in the Eastern Palace.","They passed through Moonlight Gate and rounded a long covered corridor. The main hall of Fragrant Gathering Hall lay before them. Just as they were about to remove their cloaks, all of them halted in unspoken accord.","Before the steps of the main hall stood an extraordinary tree none of them had ever seen before.","Its branches were covered in silver-white blossoms, bright as snow. The boughs bent low beneath masses of blooms, as if piled with clouds and carved from jade. When the breeze stirred, tiny petals fluttered down in a soft drift, truly resembling spring willow fluff or snow swirling through winter air.","“What... what kind of flower is this? I have never seen anything like it before,” Lady Liu exclaimed softly.","Lady Zhang’s eyes widened slightly as well. “The whole tree is white, as though it had been dusted with snow. What a remarkable sight.”","Shen Yanshui gazed at the April snow before her in equal surprise. Then she quickly noticed several pots of golden-edged winter daphne blooming unusually well beside the steps. Their emerald leaves were rimmed in gold, their purple blossoms clustered thickly together, their fragrance filling the hall.","The others noticed them as well, but before they could look more closely, maids from Fragrant Gathering Hall had already come forward. The group removed their cloaks and was led into the main chamber by a maid serving the Crown Princess.","“Your servant pays her respects to the Crown Princess. May Your Highness enjoy peace and good fortune.”","The Crown Princess wore a wisteria-purple gown with wide sleeves. A shoulder-length crown adorned with hairpins and pearls rested upon her head, lending her a dignified and graceful air. With a warm smile, she looked at the women before her and said, “We are all sisters here, so there is no need for such ceremony. Please, take your seats. Serve the tea.”","“Thank you, Your Highness.”","After the newcomers rose, they exchanged another round of greetings with those who had arrived earlier before finally taking their seats.","Shen Yanshui’s place was toward the back, close to the main hall’s entrance. Holding a cup of hot tea, she looked at the pre-rain Longjing within it and pretended to take a sip. Her lips merely brushed the surface before she stopped. She then wrapped both hands around the cup to warm them.","“One can only have the chance to taste such fine pre-rain Longjing here in Your Highness’s residence. This must be this year’s new tea, mustn’t it?” a clear, ringing voice suddenly called out.","Shen Yanshui raised her eyes and saw a woman dressed in a blue, wide-sleeved jacket. She had a plump, rounded figure, yet wore her hair simply in a round bun. Her face was filled with eager flattery as she addressed the Crown Princess.","The Crown Princess pressed her lips together and replied with an elegant, composed smile, “It was merely some tea bestowed by the Crown Prince. It is nothing particularly valuable. If you like it, you should come sit with me more often.”","“The Crown Prince treats Your Highness so well. I heard that the April Snow and Golden-Edged Daphne outside were both newly presented tributes...”","Listening to the two women exchange pleasantries, Shen Yanshui soon figured out who the speaker was.","Lady Wang. She had a daughter, a little princess who was only a year old, and had once been the Crown Princess’s maid who accompanied her upon marriage.","With an absent-minded glance around the room, Shen Yanshui noticed that every seat was occupied except the one to the Crown Princess’s lower left. That must be the place reserved for Lady Chu, the highest-ranking woman in the Eastern Palace apart from the Crown Princess.","Aside from the Crown Princess, who had given birth to a little imperial grandson, Lady Wang, the Crown Princess’s former maid, was the only woman in the Eastern Palace with a child—a daughter. There were no other offspring.","However, it was said that Lady Chu, who was greatly favored, was now pregnant.","Just as Shen Yanshui was thinking about this, she heard movement outside. The woman’s voice reached them before she herself appeared.","“What fragrance are the Crown Princess and all the younger sisters discussing?”","Shen Yanshui turned her head and saw a strikingly beautiful woman surrounded by everyone else.","The newcomer wore a pomegranate-red gown with wide sleeves and a peony crown studded with pearls. One hand rested on the arm of the nanny beside her as she walked with her heavily pregnant belly. Two palace maids led the way, followed closely by four more nannies.","Shen Yanshui took one look at this display and could not help inwardly clicking her tongue in amazement.","“Your servant pays her respects to the Crown Princess. Please forgive me for being unable to complete the proper ceremony.”","Lady Chu offered only a token curtsy before apologizing with an apologetic expression.","The Crown Princess hurriedly had someone support her and said with gentle reproach, “You are carrying a child, and the imperial physician said that this pregnancy has not been progressing well. I already excused you from paying your respects each morning. You should be resting and taking good care of yourself. Why put yourself through all this?”","Lady Chu pressed her lips into a smile. After taking her seat, she continued with a smile, “Your Highness’s kindness is engraved in my heart. Still, I ought to come and meet all the new younger sisters today. Otherwise, if we happen to meet face-to-face in the future without recognizing one another, would that not be embarrassing?”","With that, she smiled and said, “Oh, right. Your Highness, what were you and the other ladies discussing just now? I could hear how lively it was from all the way over there.”","The Crown Princess smiled. “Nothing much. We were merely talking about some of the flowers and plants outside the hall.”","The corners of Lady Chu’s mouth stiffened for a moment. They had been arranged so conspicuously, as though they were afraid no one would notice them.","She covered her lips and said, “They are indeed rather unusual. But no matter how beautiful the flowers are, how could they compare with the new sisters here? You are all so lovely that even I cannot help feeling inferior.”","Lady Wu instinctively lifted her chin with some pride, while Shen Yanshui and the others hurriedly murmured that she was too kind. Then Lady Chu suddenly changed the subject. Her gaze swept over them, pausing for a moment on Lady Wu’s face, before she smiled and asked, “I wonder which of you is Lady Shen?”","Shen Yanshui rose and lowered her head, offering a respectful curtsy. “This servant pays her respects to Lady Chu.”","Lady Chu cast her a sidelong glance, looking her up and down. Then she smiled carelessly. “You truly are a beauty in the making. No wonder His Highness has taken a liking to you.”","As she spoke, she cast a meaningful glance at Lady Zhang and Lady Wu, who were seated in front of her.","Lady Zhang lowered her head, twisting her handkerchief in both hands without daring to say a word.","Lady Wu, seated only one tea table away from Shen Yanshui, immediately flushed with humiliation and anger. Unable to restrain herself, she turned her head and glared fiercely at Shen Yanshui!","In terms of status, beauty, or talent, she had never thought herself inferior in any way to Shen Yanshui, who had nothing but her looks. So why was Shen Yanshui the one lucky enough to win His Highness’s favor first?","Seeing that Lady Wu was still glaring at her, Shen Yanshui asked with concern, “Sister Wu, what is wrong with your eyes? They are completely red. Are you feeling unwell?”","Lady Wu’s heart lurched, but embarrassment and anger quickly followed. She glared at Shen Yanshui. “What do you mean? Are you saying I’m jealous of you?”","Shen Yanshui glanced at her timidly and pressed her lips together. “Sister Wu, you misunderstand. That was not what I meant. I was only concerned that your eyes might be uncomfortable, so I asked.”","Lady Wu did not believe her. She had seen plenty of women who deliberately acted weak and pitiful like this!","“You—”","The Crown Princess smiled and said, “That is enough. Lady Shen was only showing concern for you.”","Hearing this, Lady Wu felt even more aggrieved and furious. Yet she did not dare to make another scene in front of the Crown Princess, so she could only grit her teeth and swallow her anger.","The Crown Princess turned her gaze toward Lady Shen. Her smile now appeared a little more genuine. After exchanging a few more words and introducing the newcomers to the old residents of the Eastern Palace, she said, “I must go to Kunning Palace shortly to pay my respects to Her Majesty the Empress Dowager. We shall end things here for today. There is no need for you to come for morning greetings every day from now on. Once every five days will suffice.”","“Yes.”","The women rose and curtsied before dispersing. Lady Wu had a breath of anger caught in her throat, but she could only swallow it herself, not daring to cause trouble in front of the Crown Princess.","Lady Chu was the first to leave, accompanied by the same grand retinue as when she had arrived. The others then withdrew in succession according to their rank.","Shen Yanshui slowed her pace, allowing the women of higher rank to go ahead first.","But Lady Wu was determined to have the last word. Pulling a long face, she glared at Shen Yanshui and ground out, “Don’t celebrate too soon. We’ll see how this turns out.”","Shen Yanshui remained composed, smiling as she watched Lady Wu’s retreating back. It was not until they had entered Lianxin Court and returned to their rooms that Chunping lowered her voice and asked, “Mistress, should we have someone keep an eye on Lady Wu?”","Shen Yanshui slipped off her soft-soled embroidered shoes and sat down on the couch. Hearing this, she nodded with a smile. “We can’t be deaf and blind to what goes on in the Eastern Palace, but we must also know where to draw the line. Anyone who personally serves the two little princes must not grow too close to anyone else. Have them keep their distance as much as possible in their daily dealings.”","Chunping bowed. “Yes, Mistress. I understand.”","Shen Yanshui had Qiuru remove the moon-pearl coronet and jade hairpin with its beaded tassels from her head, leaving only two dark-red ribbons to tie up her hair. The weight on her head was instantly much lighter.","She then leaned back comfortably against the couch and began mulling things over, idly fiddling with the verdant bamboo branch on the incense table.","Before yesterday, all of the Crown Prince’s wives and concubines together numbered only seven. Compared with the other princes, whose rear palaces often held twenty or even thirty women, that was not many at all—in fact, it was comparatively few.","Shen Yanshui did not particularly care. Eating well, living comfortably, and enjoying her own quiet little life was what she wanted.","When she had been bestowed upon the Eastern Palace, she had originally assumed that she would have to rely on money to get by from then on. But the Crown Prince had shown her another possibility.","Not wanting to fight tooth and nail merely to win his favor was one thing. But if his favor came her way—and could make her life more comfortable—she would not turn down such an opportunity.","Just then, Quanfu hurried into the room and reported, “Mistress, the Crown Princess has bestowed two pots of golden-edged daphne...”","At that, Shen Yanshui quickly rose and accepted the gift with due respect. As was customary, she slipped the eunuch some silver before sending away the attendants from the Crown Princess’s household. Only afterward did she learn that the Crown Princess had not bestowed gifts on her alone. Several of the more prominent secondary consorts in the rear quarters had received them as well.","The only difference was that some had received fewer pots, while others had received more.","She turned her gaze to the golden-edged daphne blooming luxuriantly beside her.","Its leaves were ringed with gold along the edges and emerald green in the middle. The flowers were tiny, clustered tightly together at the tips of the branches. Their outer petals were pale reddish-purple or pinkish-purple, while the inner petals were milky white.","They looked both elegant and sumptuous, and made a very respectable display in the room.","But Shen Yanshui knew that this flower was also called the “scent-stealing flower,” renowned for its intense fragrance.","If a pregnant woman were to smell it...","Her gaze grew slightly guarded as her fingertips brushed lightly over the clustered purple-red buds.","During pregnancy, a woman’s qi and blood naturally descend to nourish the fetus, leaving the qi in the upper body more prone to weakness.","At first, the flower’s fragrance would make her feel invigorated. But after prolonged exposure, it could cause dizziness and vertigo, making it impossible to sleep at night and leaving one’s rest unsettled, thereby depriving the fetus of nourishment.","With still longer exposure, it could lead to chest tightness, shortness of breath, palpitations, and night sweats...","The only question was whether this had been done deliberately, or whether it was merely an innocent mistake."]},{"number":8,"title":"Chapter 8: Empress","paragraphs":["Shen Yanshui had Quanshou place the two pots of golden-edged daphne in the courtyard, somewhere they could be seen as soon as one entered the gate. It would neither appear neglectful nor cause much inconvenience thereafter.","Unless, of course, someone happened to be particularly sensitive.","“My lady, shall I have breakfast brought in?” Chunping came forward with a smile and bowed as she asked.","Shen Yanshui’s eyes lit up, and she temporarily set the matter aside. “Yes. The dishes you suggested yesterday were all quite good. From now on, add one or two extra dishes to each meal in addition to my regular allowance. I’ll try them all first.”","As a Zhaoxun, her allotted meals were meager—only two meat dishes, two vegetable dishes, a soup, and a serving of fruit per meal. It was hardly enough to fill her stomach.","Although Chunping smiled, she replied in her usual composed manner, “You flatter me, my lady. When I was serving in the Imperial Food Bureau, I happened to hear all sorts of idle talk. I know a little about the specialties of nearly every head chef in the palace kitchens. So long as you enjoy the food, that is all that matters.”","Shen Yanshui smiled and nodded. She then had Qiuru open the cash box and sent someone to order breakfast.","Chunping smiled from the side. “My lady, I’m afraid we won’t need that money today. The servants in this palace are most prone to fawning on the powerful and trampling on the weak. You were just favored by His Highness last night. How could the kitchen staff possibly accept our money now?”","Things turned out exactly as Chunping had predicted. When Dongyi and Quanshou entered carrying two food boxes, their faces were full of unconcealed delight.","Dongyi was young. Though she could not be called flighty, neither was she particularly steady. At once, her joy showed plainly on her face as she said, “My lady, the kitchen staff not only refused to take our money today, they even sent you many extra dishes. One food box couldn’t hold them all.”","Shen Yanshui smiled but did not speak for a moment.","Looking at the two three-tiered, octagonal red sandalwood food boxes in their gaudy mother-of-pearl inlay, Chunping could not help frowning.","“My lady was favored only yesterday, and you are already behaving like this. Others will think that now our mistress has gained His Highness’s favor, she has become arrogant and conceited. They will look down on her.”","Quanshou jumped in fright. Lowering his head, he stammered, “My lady, Quanfu-gege already told me just now. I won’t dare do it again.”","When he had first been reprimanded, he had not taken it entirely to heart. He had even felt a little dissatisfied at being lectured by Quanfu, who was younger than he was.","But Chunping was different. Even before coming to serve Shen Yanshui, she had been more experienced and better connected than any of them. Now she was one of their mistress’s trusted attendants, and her words immediately made him tighten up with fear.","Seeing this, Dongyi’s face turned pale as she dropped to her knees. “Please forgive me, my lady! I—I know I was wrong!”","Shen Yanshui slowly straightened in her seat and looked at the two of them. “Call everyone else in.”","Before long, all the servants had assembled. Shen Yanshui’s expression grew stern.","“Besides what I told you yesterday, there is one more thing I wish to make clear today. My household has no place for arrogant, reckless people.”","“Not to mention that I was only favored for the first time yesterday. No one knows what the future will bring. Even if I were favored for several days, so what? Flowers do not bloom for a hundred days, and no one enjoys good fortune for a thousand. You should understand that better than anyone.”","“Yes, my lady. We will keep it firmly in mind.”","After she finished speaking, everyone’s thoughts naturally varied. Chunping and Quanfu still appeared fairly calm, and even seemed relieved.","After all, acting with restraint was much more reassuring than behaving loudly and ostentatiously.","As for Dongyi, she was still young and had not experienced much of the world. Having spent all this time at the very bottom of the palace hierarchy, she had been unable to control herself when someone suddenly flattered her and had begun to let her pride show.","It was only human nature. Someone who had lived in poverty and been looked down upon for years would likely be unable to resist showing off after suddenly winning the lottery.","Shen Yanshui understood this. In fact, she had anticipated it beforehand. After studying everyone’s reactions, she was reasonably satisfied.","Chunping had worked in the Imperial Food Bureau, a place where she had dealt with all kinds of people. She was experienced, steady, and not easily carried away. Quanfu had received proper guidance; he was clever without lacking tact.","Quanshou was timid, but honest and obedient. After this incident, he should have learned his lesson.","Xia’an and Qiuru were not as steady as Chunping, but for now they seemed dependable enough. Dongyi, however, was the youngest and therefore the most impetuous.","Seeing that Dongyi and Quanshou were trembling uncontrollably, Shen Yanshui did not continue frightening them.","“No matter the circumstances, remember to act cautiously and discreetly whenever you are outside. Do not show off, and do not cause trouble.","“But just because we do not want trouble does not mean we fear it. If anyone bullies you outside, report it to me. I will not let you be mistreated for nothing.”","“Now get up. There is no need to keep kneeling.”","“Yes! Thank you, my lady.”","Hearing her words and sensing her softened tone, Dongyi and Quanshou both breathed a sigh of relief. When they realized that their mistress truly had no intention of punishing them, they hurriedly kowtowed in thanks.","After sending the others away, Shen Yanshui kept Chunping and Quanfu behind. As she ate breakfast, she looked at them with a smile.","“Do you think I made too much of a fuss?”","“We would not dare,” the two of them replied at once, bowing their heads.","Quanfu said respectfully, “A tree that rises above the forest will be battered by the wind. My lady is wise.”","Chunping answered seriously, “It is best to correct them early and make sure they know what may and may not be done. Otherwise, they may cause trouble and resentment for you when they are outside.”","Though palace servants’ lives were worth little more than weeds, even the smallest people could sometimes play a crucial role, in ways no one could imagine. It was always better to make friends than enemies wherever possible.","Hearing this, Shen Yanshui was even more satisfied. She smiled and said, “The kitchen staff saw that I had gained His Highness’s favor and sent an extra dish or two of fresh food. There was nothing wrong with that. But in everything we do, we must keep our judgment. We must not be so easily flattered that we lose all sense of propriety and make ourselves a laughingstock.”","“Yes, my lady. We understand.”","The two bowed and withdrew. Chunping noticed that Dongyi still looked uneasy, so she called her into the room.","Dongyi’s eyes were red, and her voice trembled with tears. “Sister Chunping... I know I was wrong. Yesterday, when I went to collect the food, I bumped into a palace maid and eunuch from the neighboring courtyard. The people in the kitchen made several cutting remarks at me. Then today, after hearing a few pleasant words, I couldn’t stop myself from feeling happy. I really know I was wrong. I won’t dare do it again...”","Chunping had not expected there to be such a reason behind it. Her expression turned serious.","“It is good that you understand your mistake. Our mistress is kind and generous, which is why she did not punish you. From now on, you must act even more steadily and cautiously outside. Other than our own people, no one else is to handle our food at any point. Do you understand?”","Dongyi hurriedly nodded again and again. “I’ll remember it all!”","*","The main hall of Haoyue Study, the residence nearest the Moonlight Gate, was furnished with exquisite luxury. Gold and jade articles could be seen everywhere. Fuguang brocade, which would have been impossible to buy even for a thousand gold pieces outside the palace, had been spread over the daybed as a mattress and made into cushions. Its extravagance was self-evident.","Four pots of golden-edged daphne had been placed far away in the courtyard.","Even with the matrons sent by the Empress keeping watch over her, and imperial physicians coming to check on her health every other day, Lady Chu did not think the Crown Princess would dare to tamper with that potted flower. Still, to err on the side of caution, she had the flower placed far away from her quarters.","\"Master, that Lady Shen...\" a maid at Lady Chu's side suddenly spoke up in a soft voice.","Lady Chu rested her hand gently on her belly, first frowning slightly, then said nonchalantly, \"What's the rush? It's only been a day. Now that there are new concubines in the Eastern Palace, even if it weren't her, there would be others.\"","Among the four new women, Lady Wu was clearly a sharp, overambitious sort. For all her good looks, she was no threat at all.","As for the leading Lady Zhang and Lady Liu, whose petty schemes were written all over her face, Lady Chu did not spare them a single thought.","When it came to that Lady Shen, Lady Chu let out a soft chuckle. \"What a pity...\"","Her personal senior maid stepped forward with a cup of tea, having missed the soft murmur under Lady Chu's breath, and said with a smile, \"The most important thing now is the little imperial grandson in your belly. Once you give birth to a healthy, fine little imperial grandson, your good days are still to come. Even the Empress will surely look at you with new respect then.\"","Lady Chu stroked her belly tenderly, a look of determined triumph on her face. \"Imperial Physician Zhao has already confirmed that the child in my womb is a little imperial grandson, no doubt about it. When my son is born...\"","A look of proud glory came over her as she patted her belly gently. \"My son is bound to be bright and clever. He must strive to do well in the future, and crush that sickly boy into the dirt...\"","*","\"Your Highness, the Empress told us to bring Little Prince to her to see him long ago. We have already declined twice. If we refuse again this time... I am afraid it will make the Empress feel displeased.\"","Inside the Hall of Fragrant Gatherings, Matron Zhou pleaded in a low, earnest voice. \"The imperial physicians also said that the Empress's ailment was brought on by long-term overexertion, and it is not contagious. Little Prince has been in better health lately, so it should be quite safe.\"","But the Crown Princess rejected the idea without the slightest hesitation, frowning and saying, \"The Empress has been ill for ages and has not recovered. She knows full well that Zhang'er has been frail since he was a child, so she should be all the more careful of his health. What if he catches a chill when going out? What if the sickness passes to him?\"","\"Besides, the Empress has long disliked me because I failed to give the Crown Prince a healthy child. Now she has bestowed new concubines on the Eastern Palace, and no doubt she is eagerly looking forward to those women giving birth to heirs for the Crown Prince soon. If that's the case, why bother to trouble my son?\"","Matron Zhou's face fell, and she tried to persuade her again, \"Your Highness...\"","\"Say no more, Matron. That little life in Lady Chu's belly is the apple of the Empress's eye now. It's only been a few months, but the rewards being lavished on Lady Chu flow like water, all to prop that lowly woman up at my expense.\" The Crown Princess said coldly. \"I'd like to see just what that belly of hers can produce.\"","Seeing that the Crown Princess was full of resentment toward the Empress and stubbornly refused to yield, Matron Zhou had no choice but to give up.","...","\"Your subject greets Your Majesty, may Your Majesty live a thousand years in peace and prosperity.\" The Crown Princess stepped into the Palace of Earthly Tranquility, bowed her head, and greeted the Empress respectfully.","Seated at the top was the Empress, dressed in a plain purple informal robe with wide sleeves, no makeup on her face. Even so, one could still tell she had been strikingly beautiful in her youth, though now her face was pale and lined with exhaustion.","The Empress's eyes, which had been full of hope a moment earlier, darkened when she saw the Crown Princess and the retinue behind her.","\"Where is Zhang'er?\"","This was the first time the Empress had not told her to rise immediately. The Crown Princess felt even more certain that the Empress was deliberately making things difficult for her. Her heart filled with rising resentment, and the tone of her voice unconsciously turned stiff.","\"Replying to Your Majesty, the imperial physicians say Zhang'er's illness has not yet healed, so it is not suitable for him to go out, lest he be invaded by cold pathogenic air. Your subject did not bring Zhang'er here, and asks for Your Majesty's forgiveness.\"","Seeing the look of resentment that the Crown Princess could not hide even with her head bowed, the Empress closed her eyes for a moment, then waved her hand to dismiss her, deciding that out of sight was out of mind.","The Crown Princess's face froze slightly. She had come to pay her respects and tend to the Empress during her illness, but she had been sent away only moments after arriving. If word of this got out, her reputation and dignity would be completely ruined.","She forced a stiff smile. \"Your Majesty...\"","The Empress looked at her with a solemn, expressionless face. \"There is a concubine in the Eastern Palace who is with child now. It is your duty to look after her with all your care. You do not need to come here every day to pay me respects for the next few months.\"","At those words, the Crown Princess's face changed slightly, but looking after the heirs of the Eastern Palace was indeed the responsibility of the Crown Princess.","The Crown Princess bowed her head. \"As Your Majesty commands. But while Your Majesty's illness has not healed, and the Crown Prince is busy with government affairs, tending to Your Majesty with care and performing the duties of a daughter-in-law is what my filial piety demands. Otherwise, I would never be able to rest easy.\"","The Empress frowned, and Nanny Fan at her side said with a gentle smile, \"The Empress naturally knows of the Crown Princess's filial piety. But the imperial physicians say Her Majesty's illness requires quiet rest above all, and keeping a cheerful mind is the most important thing.\"","The Crown Princess's expression did not shift, but her hands clenched tightly under her sleeves. That old hag was implying that her visits to pay respects were making the Empress unhappy!","Nanny Fan seemed not to notice her reaction, and continued speaking in the same unhurried, pleasant tone. \"Now that the Crown Prince has very few heirs, the Crown Princess should take good care of her own health, so that she may soon give birth to another child for the Crown Prince.\"","The Empress raised a hand to rub her forehead. \"Nanny Fan is right. From now on, you only need to come to see me once every ten days. You may leave now, Crown Princess.\""]},{"number":9,"title":"Chapter 9: Contradiction","paragraphs":["Only after the Crown Princess had left did Nanny Fan, who attended at the Empress’s side, sigh in displeasure. “Your Majesty, you indulge the Crown Princess far too much.”","At that, the Empress slowly opened her eyes. Frowning, she said regretfully, “Back then, when His Majesty said he wanted to choose a girl from a distinguished family for Yu’er, I thought that since Master Wenchuan was a man of noble character and upright family traditions, his granddaughter—having been taught by him from childhood—would surely be gentle, virtuous, and sensible...”","The Crown Princess’s father, Li Cheng, the Vice Censor-in-Chief, was a man of loyalty and integrity. Her mother came from Duke Wengu’s household. Though the family held no military power, its sons had always entered court through their literary achievements, which was an advantage in itself.","That was why the Empress had chosen her.","“Who could have imagined that the Crown Princess would have such a temperament?”","“The Eastern Palace has always been short of heirs and is already unstable. It is surrounded by wolves and tigers, yet as Crown Princess, instead of thinking about supporting the Crown Prince and securing the Eastern Palace, she keeps her eyes fixed only on the small patch of land that is the inner court.”","“If not for her jealousy, Lady Sun would never have miscarried after I bestowed her upon the Crown Prince, and the Crown Prince would not have become estranged from her!”","“And she actually thinks she is the cleverest person in the world, treating everyone else as fools.” The Empress sneered.","“Your Majesty, please calm down. The Crown Princess does not understand your good intentions. She simply has no blessing to appreciate them.”","The Empress sighed, her voice turning cold. “I only hope she will be clever enough this time.”","If she dared reach out against the Crown Prince’s heirs again, she must not blame the Empress for what followed.","“Your Majesty has bestowed gifts upon Lady Chu several times. In every word, you have both cautioned and reassured her. I imagine the Crown Princess should understand by now.”","Though Nanny Fan said this, she too harbored resentment toward the Crown Princess. If not for the Empress’s kindness—having personally tasted the agony of being separated from her own child and not wishing anyone else to suffer the same—what would have been wrong with taking the Little Prince to Kunning Palace and raising him there?","The Little Prince had been born a year and five months ago—nearly three by nominal reckoning—yet the Empress had only seen him twice. What grandmother in the world was unable to see her own grandson? And yet her mistress had happened to encounter such a narrow-minded woman.","Had the Crown Princess’s mother-in-law been someone other than Her Majesty—one of those high-ranking consorts skilled in underhanded schemes—who knew what sort of torment she would already have endured?","“I hope she truly understands.” The Empress pressed a hand to her brow. “By the way, I was not feeling well some time ago. Yesterday, I noticed that one of the selected candidates originally marked for the Crown Prince had been crossed out, and Noble Consort Lan had selected Lady Shen’s younger sister instead?”","Nanny Fan bowed and replied, “In answer to Your Majesty, that is indeed what happened. Noble Consort Lan deliberately delayed matters and, bypassing you entirely, submitted the list directly to His Majesty.”","The Empress was not surprised. If Noble Consort Lan did not stir up some trouble, she would have found it strange. By selecting the younger sister of Lady Shen—a pawn clearly meant to make the Crown Prince unhappy—it was obvious that Noble Consort Lan had done so deliberately.","But what angered her even more than the disgust she felt was the Emperor’s attitude.","*","After finishing his duties at the hour of Shen, Cui Yu left the Jingzhao Prefecture yamen in his crimson official robes and boarded the Eastern Palace carriage.","In the Great Yong Dynasty, the Crown Prince not only spent his days studying and attending court to hear state affairs; he also served as the Prefect of Jingzhao. It was considered another way of assessing his ability to handle government affairs.","Seated nearby, Zheng Yuande saw that his master’s expression was calm and gave away none of his emotions. He could not help but breathe a sigh of relief.","Having served his master for many years, he could still discern a thing or two. Ever since the General of Agile Cavalry had been reprimanded by His Majesty and stripped of his title as Military Commissioner of the Protecting-State Army, it had been rare to see His Highness in such a peaceful frame of mind.","At court that morning, contrary to Zheng Yuande’s expectations, he had thought His Highness would once again argue with His Majesty and plead for the General of Agile Cavalry, only to be reprimanded by the Emperor. Unexpectedly, His Highness had acted entirely out of character and had not argued on the general’s behalf again.","Cui Yu closed his eyes to rest. Suddenly, he lifted them and said, “If you have something to say, say it.” His voice was clear and steady.","With his round, fair face beaming, Zheng Yuande ingratiatingly replied, “Your Highness truly possesses divine foresight. You can tell that this servant is bursting with questions even with your eyes closed.”","Cui Yu shot him a glance.","Zheng Yuande did not dare put on airs any longer. He chuckled and said, “This servant was worried about Your Highness, but who could have expected His Majesty to praise you in open court? I saw the expressions on the Fourth Prince’s face and those of the other princes when they left the court—not one of them was smiling. It was deeply satisfying.”","Those princes had deliberately come up to needle His Highness after the Emperor reprimanded him. Now that His Highness had received the Emperor’s praise, they were the ones left fuming!","Cui Yu lowered his eyes, his voice deep and unreadable. “Arguing is useless.”","What would winning an argument accomplish?","An emperor would always be wary of a subject whose achievements threatened to overshadow the throne. Whether one was right or wrong no longer mattered.","It was simply that, before this, he had been unable to accept that his maternal uncle had guarded the frontier and fought through bloodshed, only for the military honors he had earned with his life to be stripped away as though they were nothing more than a child’s game.","He felt that it was unfair and unworthy—not only to his maternal uncle, but also to the soldiers who defended Great Yong.","Yet his position as Crown Prince, combined with the military merits his maternal uncle had earned, had already made his father wary of him. If he took a step back, perhaps his father’s suspicion and defenses would ease somewhat, making things safer for his maternal grandfather and uncle.","Since that was the case, there was no need to fight over a momentary victory.","However, as soon as he returned to the Eastern Palace, Cui Yu heard Cao Zhongda, the eunuch in charge of the front halls, quietly report several matters to him. Zheng Yuande’s expression changed slightly. Inwardly, he could not help complaining about the Crown Princess. He truly did not know what she was thinking. How could she dare act one way in public and another in private before the Empress? Her audacity was simply too great.","After hearing the report, Cui Yu’s expression remained unchanged, revealing nothing. Only a trace of coldness appeared in his previously tranquil eyes.","*","“Your Highness, please listen to this old servant’s advice. When we go to pay our respects to the Empress toward the end of the month, let us take the Little Prince with us, all right?” Matron Zhou urged in a low voice, pleading earnestly.","The Crown Princess’s face was grim, and her heart ached even more. “Did you not see how deliberately Her Majesty made things difficult for me today? Every word she spoke implied that the Crown Prince has so few heirs because of me. It is all my fault—that I failed to give His Highness a healthy son!”","Since childhood, she had been the most outstanding among her sisters. The husband she had married was also the most exalted man in the world—the Crown Prince himself. Yet she had given birth to a sickly son, leaving her unable to hold her head high before Her Majesty or anyone else.","Matron Zhou naturally felt distressed for the young mistress she had nursed and raised. But now that the girl was a daughter-in-law of the imperial family, she could no longer allow her to indulge her temper as she pleased.","She consoled her, “Your Highness, please set your mind at ease. The Little Prince is currently the only son under the Crown Prince’s name. No one else can possibly surpass him.”","“If our Little Prince can win the Empress’s affection and favor, it will benefit both us and the Little Prince. Why insist on competing with the Empress over this momentary grievance? If His Highness finds out, the one injured will be the affection between husband and wife.”","The Crown Princess’s expression shifted slightly.","As the two were speaking, familiar sounds came from outside.","The Crown Princess hurriedly straightened her clothes and makeup, then went forward at a brisk pace to greet him and offer her respects.","Cui Yu stopped before her and looked down at her face. Only after a moment did he speak, telling her to rise.","Once they had settled in before the luohan couch, the Crown Princess hurriedly ordered someone to brew a pot of hot tea and presented it to him herself. Her voice was gentle and warm with a smile. “Your Highness, have you just returned from your duties? You have been so busy with state affairs lately, but you must take care of yourself as well. Be sure not to overwork yourself and damage your health.”","Cui Yu lifted his eyes to her gentle smile, his voice slightly deep. “No need.”","The Crown Princess smiled and placed the teacup on a small table nearby. Then she asked with a smile, “Would Your Highness like to have a meal brought in?”","“No need.” After saying this, Cui Yu turned toward Matron Zhou. “Where is Zhang’er?”","At this, the smile on the Crown Princess’s face became even more genuine. She quickly turned and ordered, “Hurry and bring Zhang’er here.”","Matron Zhou was naturally pleased that His Highness the Crown Prince kept their Little Prince in his thoughts. After the wet nurse entered carrying the swaddled infant and paid her respects, she bent forward respectfully and presented the Little Prince to the Crown Prince.","Cui Yu glanced at the child, who still had his eyes closed, then told the wet nurse to carry him away so as not to wake him.","As though asking casually, he said, “I remember the Crown Princess said yesterday that Zhang’er’s health had grown much stronger recently?”","The Crown Princess’s heart tightened. Her fingers unconsciously clenched the handkerchief in her hand. “In reply to Your Highness, the physicians said that although Zhang’er’s health has improved somewhat recently, he still needs to recuperate quietly and cannot be exposed to drafts.”","“Oh? Is that so?” Cui Yu absently rubbed the cool jade ring on his thumb. “As it happens, I summoned the Imperial Physician Director here. Someone, ask Physician Lu to examine Chang’er and make sure he is in good health.”","Zheng Yuande: “Yes, Your Highness.”","The Crown Princess’s expression stiffened slightly, and she hurriedly said, “Your Highness, Zhang’er’s regular physician has always been Physician Zhang. Would it not be better to summon him instead? He is more familiar with Zhang’er’s condition.”","Cui Yu’s voice remained calm. “As the Imperial Physician Director, Physician Lu’s medical skills are naturally no inferior to Physician Zhang’s.”","The Crown Princess’s expression tightened. She lowered her head to conceal it. Every few days, the Crown Prince would ask about the child’s condition, and at first she had not found anything suspicious. But now...","Before long, Zheng Yuande entered with an elderly man whose hair and beard were gray and who wore the official robes of an Imperial Physician Director.","After paying his respects, Imperial Physician Director Lu reported, “In reply to Your Highness and Her Highness, the Little Prince’s health is somewhat weaker than that of ordinary infants his age. However, so long as he is carefully tended, he should be no different from anyone else once he grows up.”","Cui Yu asked, “Can he withstand being moved at present?”","“If curtains are hung around the Little Prince’s palanquin, it will cause no harm.”","“Thank you for your trouble, Imperial Physician Director Lu.”","After Zheng Yuande escorted him out, he had barely stepped back inside when he heard His Highness’s calm, emotionless voice.","“Someone, bring the palanquin.”","The Crown Princess’s heart turned cold and heavy. The Empress must have sent someone to tell His Highness something. Otherwise, why would he have immediately taken action the moment he returned from his duties?","How hateful!","Zheng Yuande smoothly turned around and went back out. He was deeply puzzled by the Crown Princess’s almost blatant disregard for Her Majesty the Empress.","The Empress’s illness was neither a cold nor an infectious disease. It was not contagious in the slightest. Where, then, had the Crown Princess found the courage to challenge Her Majesty’s authority again and again?","Matron Zhou instantly dropped to her knees and kowtowed as she pleaded, “Your Highness, please be magnanimous. Her Highness was simply too concerned about the Little Prince’s health, which was why she did not take him to see Her Majesty the Empress today. When Her Highness returned just now, she even told this old servant that she planned to pay Her Majesty a visit later this month. By then, the Little Prince should have recovered, and Her Highness will take him along so Her Majesty may examine him carefully.”","Cui Yu turned his gaze toward the Crown Princess, his voice turning cold. “Oh? Is that so?”","The Crown Princess’s face was stiff and pale. After a long moment, she finally bit her lip, bent her knees, and lowered her head. “Yes. That was indeed my intention. However, I acted without sufficient consideration and caused Mother Empress needless worry during her illness. I beg Your Highness to forgive me.”","Cui Yu slowly rose to his feet and looked down at her expression and demeanor. After a moment, he said in a low voice, “Mother Empress has devoted herself to making plans for you and me. Zhang’er is the Crown Prince’s legitimate eldest son. Do not disappoint Mother Empress’s painstaking efforts.”","The Crown Princess grew even more resentful at his words.","Making plans? The Empress had only one son, His Highness the Crown Prince. Was it not only natural for her to plan for him? Were her own father and brothers not likewise making arrangements for the Crown Prince in court?","And as for painstaking efforts... A cold laugh rose in her heart. Was he referring to the efforts she had made by repeatedly bestowing gifts upon Lady Chu, heedless of the dignity of the Crown Princess?","Such painstaking efforts were more than she could accept.","Yet no matter what she thought in her heart, she endured the grievance for the moment and kept it from showing on her face.","The disappointment in Cui Yu’s eyes vanished in an instant. His dark eyes were calm and utterly without ripples. He said nothing more, but turned and left."]},{"number":10,"title":"Chapter 10: Vulgar","paragraphs":["It was not until that cold, austere figure had vanished from sight that the Crown Princess finally collapsed onto the couch.","“Your Highness...”","Zheng Yuande stole a glance at his mistress’s expression, inwardly groaning bitterly. What a life they were leading!","His Highness’s mood had only just begun to improve, and now he had to hear about all the troublesome things the Crown Princess had done. Wasn’t it enough that she had already given him so much to worry about?","Cui Yu strode forward with a grave, composed expression. When he looked up, he realized that he had arrived at Lianxin Court. After pausing for only a moment, he walked in.","Shen Yanshui had heard the sudden commotion outside and hurried out to greet him. “Please forgive my lack of ceremony, Your Highness. I hope you won’t take offense.”","Cui Yu saw that she was dressed in nothing more than a simple sky-blue long skirt. She wore no headdress; her dark hair was tied with a gauze ribbon and arranged in a cloud-like coiffure. Her face was bare of powder and rouge, yet her fair cheeks glowed with a healthy flush, full of vitality. Without realizing it, he looked at her a little longer than he should have.","Shen Yanshui raised her eyes and smiled at him, just about to speak, when a light, quick set of footsteps approached. It was Lady Liu.","Though Lady Liu’s clothes were not especially luxurious, they were immaculate. Her makeup was even more exquisite, and a delicate apricot-blossom crown adorned her head, accented with silver-and-jade hair ornaments that chimed softly as she moved. Every word, gesture, smile, and frown seemed to have been measured against the strictest standards of palace etiquette, leaving not the slightest fault to find.","Even Shen Yanshui had to admire her inwardly. Lady Liu certainly had not studied those rules for nothing; she had clearly put considerable effort into them.","Unlike Shen Yanshui, who had few demands of herself and never made things difficult when she could help it—so long as she was neither outstanding nor disgraceful, that was good enough.","This was Lady Liu’s first time seeing the Crown Prince. At a single glance, she could barely control her racing heart and flushed face. Her heart pounded wildly, and she hurriedly lowered her head to conceal her reaction.","She presented the Crown Prince with her most graceful bearing and her most beautiful angle, her voice as gentle as flowing water. “This concubine, Liu, pays her respects to the Crown Prince. May Your Highness enjoy peace and good health. I arrived late—please forgive me, Your Highness.”","Listening to that melodious, lilting little voice, Shen Yanshui had to admit that its tone was rather pleasant.","Cui Yu glanced sideways at her, said, “Rise,” and then turned back to Shen Yanshui, signaling for her to continue.","Lady Liu immediately bit her lip. A sour twinge rose in her heart, and she was filled with regret and frustration.","Shen Yanshui spoke in a bright, cheerful voice. “Your Highness, the weather is fair and pleasant today. I had nothing else to do, so I rearranged the room. Would Your Highness like to go inside and take a look?”","Cui Yu nodded. When he raised his eyes, he noticed that the courtyard, which had previously been somewhat bare, now contained quite a few new additions.","Outside the window of the eastern heated chamber stood a large, lush banana plant with broad green leaves. In front of it, Shen Yanshui had used stones to build a long, winding pond about the height of a table. Its irregular edges followed the natural shapes of the stones, giving it a charmingly rustic appeal.","Shen Yanshui smiled, her eyes curving into crescents. “Although this courtyard is called Lotus Heart Court, I noticed there wasn’t a single place for growing lotuses anywhere around it. So I had the Office of Palace Affairs build this little pond. Not only have we put several fish in it, but we’ve also planted lotus seeds. Before long, we should be able to enjoy the sight of lotuses in full bloom.”","As she spoke, she saw that he showed no sign of impatience and even seemed somewhat interested, so she ushered him into the room with a smile.","She had always been especially fond of spacious, bright apartments with floor-to-ceiling windows. Back at the Earl of Zhongyi’s residence, she had arranged her own bedchamber according to her preferences from the very beginning. Now that she had moved somewhere new, she naturally intended to redecorate it as well.","The moment they entered, the view brightened.","The room’s original furnishings were no different from those of any ordinary chamber. But the heavy screens that had once separated the main hall from the eastern and western heated chambers had disappeared, leaving the space far more open—and much better ventilated.","Just then, a spring breeze swept through, carrying in the faint, fresh scent of grass and trees from outside. Even her stifled mood seemed to ease a little.","The ordinary potted plants that had stood on the narrow-waisted tall stands on either side of the entrance had been replaced with exquisitely woven bamboo baskets, each filled with flowers.","Unlike the extravagant, rare, and costly peonies, peony-like flowers, tuberoses, and begonias commonly used in the other palace chambers, these were simply an assortment of flowers and plants.","There were the most ordinary pink and white primroses, hyacinths, daffodils, and two little flowers whose names he did not know. They were not particularly precious, but they were fresh and elegant all the same, pleasing to the eye.","Incense burned within the room. Its fragrance was gentle and unhurried rather than overpowering, carrying a hint of the fresh scent of sweet orange. He could not help showing a trace of surprise and turned to ask, “What incense are you burning?”","It was not the dragon’s-breath incense, sandalwood, or pinewood scents commonly used in the palace, nor was it like the various floral fragrances favored by women. It seemed to have a faintly invigorating effect as well.","Shen Yanshui replied with a smile, “Your Highness, it’s an incense blend I made myself. I added orange peel and a little mint.”","Seeing her smiling so brightly as she spoke, Cui Yu unconsciously smiled as well. “Acceptable.”","Having received his praise, Shen Yanshui was in a good mood too.","The furnishings in the eastern heated chamber had not changed much from before. It still contained all the necessary furniture, but several soft cushions of various shapes had been added to the couch. The lattice window beside it stood wide open, with a layer of gauzy, fragrant cloud-silk curtains hanging inside that could be drawn from side to side.","At present, the curtains were half open. On the windowsill sat a delicately carved bamboo tube holding two fresh, verdant bamboo sprigs.","At another corner of the open lattice window hung a little wind chime strung with beautiful shells and pearls of various colors. Sunlight spilled across it as a gentle breeze stirred the air, sending the delicate, pleasant chimes tinkling into the room. In an instant, an atmosphere of tranquil serenity arose.","“Not bad.” Cui Yu stepped forward and sat down on the couch. His previously troubled thoughts inexplicably settled, replaced by a faint sense of calm and drowsiness.","Shen Yanshui watched the languid look that had emerged between his brows, staring at him intently for several moments.","As expected, when a man was handsome, even his lazy, relaxed expression looked exceptionally good.","Cui Yu lazily lifted his eyes and glanced at her.","Shen Yanshui blinked at once, her gaze clear and bright, her expression utterly innocent and natural. Then, with her eyes shifting coquettishly, she suddenly turned the tables on him. “Your Highness, why are you looking at me like that? You’re making me blush.”","Cui Yu: “......”","Zheng Yuande, who was waiting nearby: “???”","Although Lady Shen’s delicate, coquettish tone seemed perfectly fitting, there was somehow something a little strange about it.","Cui Yu gazed at her lively expression. He was startled at first, but then, for some inexplicable reason, he suddenly felt like laughing.","And he did let out a soft laugh.","Zheng Yuande was secretly astonished.","He turned his eyes toward the exceptionally beautiful Lady Shen, whose face always seemed to be lit by a cheerful smile, and thought to himself that it was no wonder. Anyone looking at such a pleasing smile would naturally feel a little happier as well.","This Lady Shen... seemed rather extraordinary.","“Gurgle~”","A faint sound suddenly reached both their ears. Cui Yu’s gaze instinctively dropped downward.","Shen Yanshui immediately covered her stomach.","Cui Yu looked up at her, one brow raised. “Hungry?”","Shen Yanshui nodded without hesitation. With a smile pressing at the corners of her lips, she replied, “Your Highness, I’ve been busy all day. It’s just about time for dinner now. Shall we have the meal brought in first?”","Seeing how naturally she changed expressions, Cui Yu raised a brow. Her stomach was growling loudly—something that ought to have been embarrassing—but her manner and tone were so candid that it somehow wasn’t.","“Bring in the meal.”","With the Crown Prince present, dinner was considerably more lavish than when Shen Yanshui ordered food for herself. Most importantly, she could eat as much as she wanted for free!","As a result, the smile never left her face.","The kitchen had prepared such dishes as Boiled Gold and Jade, Red-Silk Boiled Cakes—the noodles kneaded together with shrimp meat, giving them a pinkish hue, with a light yet wonderfully fresh flavor—as well as braised perch, chicken-and-vermicelli soup, three-colored shredded tripe, mutton bones, roasted venison, and several portions of seasonal greens and fruit.","At a glance, everything looked light and delicate. There was not a single chili pepper in sight, nor even the hint of a spicy aroma.","Still, she had never tried the Eastern Palace’s cooking before, so she was full of anticipation and ate with her usual enthusiasm and delight.","She sampled every dish without missing a single one. She even ate quite a lot of the mutton and mutton bones, despite never having been particularly fond of them. The only thing she managed to restrain was the urge to pick up a bone and gnaw on it directly with her hands.","She ate until she was thoroughly satisfied, putting away four hearty bowls of rice in succession. Zheng Yuande, who was serving nearby, was left dumbfounded, while Chunping’s eyes nearly twitched themselves out of their sockets from all the frantic hints she was giving.","Unfortunately, those hints were being sent to a blind woman. Shen Yanshui did not notice them at all—and even if she had, she would never have starved herself for the sake of appearances or dignity.","Cui Yu was naturally surprised as well. People of the time esteemed refined elegance, and women in particular often pursued slender figures as delicate as willow branches swaying in the breeze. As a result, they generally ate very little. Watching them eat had always ruined his appetite, leaving him feeling as though everything he consumed was bland and tasteless.","Lady Shen, on the other hand, could make an ordinary meal seem like a rare delicacy. Her expressions were so vivid and amusing that merely watching her was enough to whet one’s appetite. The only trouble was that... before one knew it, one ended up eating a little more than usual.","Once the two of them had rinsed their mouths and washed their hands, the palace attendants quickly cleared the table.","Taking a walk after a meal to aid digestion was Shen Yanshui’s habit, and today was no exception. But with the two of them together, they ought to find something to talk about. Just as she was racking her brains for a topic, a faint, plaintive melody suddenly drifted into her ears.","She instinctively asked softly, “Where is that qin music coming from?”","There was no need for anyone else to answer. After listening for only a moment, she recognized its source: the courtyard next door.","She had a pretty good idea who it was and could not help smiling.","Catching the smile on her face, Cui Yu glanced at her. “What are you smiling about?”","Shen Yanshui’s eyes curved with amusement. “I was just thinking that taking a walk while listening to this music is rather pleasant.”","Cui Yu said, “Pleasant?”","As if on cue, the melody suddenly changed. A winding, sorrowful quality filled the air, and the space between his brows twitched uncontrollably. He frowned and cast a cold glance at Zheng Yuande.","Zheng Yuande’s plump body immediately moved forward. Reacting with great speed, he turned around and ordered, “Go see who is playing the qin. How dare they disturb His Highness’s ears for no reason?”","An eunuch hurriedly acknowledged the order and rushed out. Before long, the music stopped.","Seeing the glance the Crown Prince had given him, Shen Yanshui could not help feeling a little sheepish. She had not expected the Crown Prince to have such exacting standards when it came to music. She genuinely thought Lady Wu’s playing had sounded quite lovely.","Back when she had been in the Palace of Gathering Elegance, even the palace matron had praised her qin skills.","After their walk, the sky gradually darkened, and the two of them returned to their chambers.","The western side hall opposite them kept a close watch on the Crown Prince’s every move. Seeing them return, Yinping entered the room and reported the matter in a low voice.","Lady Liu closed the window beside the couch with controlled force, her expression unpleasant.","No matter how envious she felt, she had just been given a warning by what had happened earlier. She had naturally heard the commotion from Lady Wu’s chambers next door, separated by only a single wall, but she did not dare do anything.","Hearing the sound of water being summoned from the eastern side hall, she felt a surge of resentment. Secretly gritting her teeth, she thought, “She is relying on nothing but her looks. His Highness is hardly such a shallow man. This freshness will only last a few days. Once the novelty wears off, His Highness will surely recognize my virtues...”","Whether the Crown Prince was shallow or not, Shen Yanshui did not know. But she felt that she certainly was—greedy for both food and beauty.","And there was one more thing she wanted to confirm."]},{"number":11,"title":"Chapter 11: Reward","paragraphs":["Compared with the night before, Shen Yanshui felt that the Crown Prince was proving remarkably quick to learn. As a result, the pleasure they shared—or perhaps the pleasure her body experienced—had grown all the more intense.","After this encounter, she was certain of it: whenever she and the Crown Prince became one, the faint supernatural ability within her would automatically begin circulating. It made her feel as though she were absorbing his yang energy to nourish her yin.","Bah. Judging by the Crown Prince’s condition, it was clearly more like dual cultivation.","The time they spent together seemed to have grown longer, too...","She simply couldn’t understand why this was happening.","Little by little, she began to enjoy it. At first, she had still forced herself to remember the rules and keep her voice down.","But later, all she could remember was the lean, muscular body beneath her, its smooth lines concealing powerful, explosive strength, while hot sweat rolled down...","The next morning, when Shen Yanshui opened her eyes, the person beside her was already gone. She wasn’t surprised. But when she saw the bedding, fresh and completely changed, she remembered the sheets that had been removed the night before—drenched in moisture, marked with patches of varying shades, and covered in all sorts of chaotic traces.","Her waist felt even more sore and weak than it had the previous night. She shifted position, closed her eyes, and gathered her focus. After sensing the supernatural ability within her and skillfully circulating it through her body once, the weariness gradually faded. When she opened her eyes again, she felt refreshed and invigorated.","According to the ranking system of her previous life, she had only just reached the early stage of Rank One.","There were no crystal cores from animals or plants in this world for her to absorb and use to advance. She could only cultivate by drawing upon the faint energy in nature and following the energy-circulation method promoted by the authorities in her previous life. She had no idea how long it would take before she could break through to Rank Two.","Only upon reaching Rank Two would her strength against enemies improve by leaps and bounds.","Otherwise, all she could do was regulate the body and slowly hasten the growth of plants.","“Why has the mistress sat up?”","Chunping came around the screen. Before she had time to be surprised by Shen Yanshui’s posture, she saw the quilt casually wrapped around her mistress. Through the slightly open gap, the marks beneath that fair collarbone were clearly visible, and Chunping’s cheeks flushed faintly.","Shen Yanshui asked about the Crown Prince. After learning that, just as yesterday, he had left at the third quarter of the Hour of the Tiger, she wasn’t surprised. Once she confirmed that the Crown Prince truly held no displeasure toward her laziness in the morning, she simply allowed herself to fall back asleep.","She threw off the quilt and rose. Since she had just circulated her supernatural ability, she did not feel cold.","Although this was not the first time Chunping had seen her, she still couldn’t help flushing and feeling her heart race at the sight of her mistress’s fair, delicate, shapely body.","Especially the peach-colored undergarment before her, which seemed barely able to contain...","Chunping dared not look any longer. She hurriedly and deftly helped her mistress get dressed.","Once everything was in order, she studied Shen Yanshui carefully before saying softly, “Mistress, the size of your undergarments and clothes seems to be a little small. Shall I have Xia’an and the others make you two new outfits?”","Shen Yanshui also glanced at herself in the mirror. The front of her bodice did seem a little tighter than before. The few outfits she currently owned had all been newly made by her birth mother’s embroiderers before she entered the palace, according to her measurements.","“Forget it. I expect the weather will grow warmer soon. We can save the fabric and use it to make summer clothes later.”","The clothing of the Great Yong Dynasty fell somewhere between the styles of the Tang and Song eras of her previous life. There were high-waisted ruqun skirts and waist-high ruqun skirts, as well as beizi jackets, half-sleeved garments, and wide-sleeved outer robes. A single set of spring clothing required quite a lot of fabric.","She received fabric as part of her monthly allotment, but not much. Given her rank, it would not be anything particularly fine, and it was nowhere near as comfortable as what she was wearing now.","As soon as she finished speaking, a commotion came from outside. Xia’an hurried into the inner room, her face full of delight, and whispered, “Mistress, please come out quickly to receive the decree. Her Majesty the Empress has sent gifts!”","Shen Yanshui did not dare delay. Seeing Matron Zhao, a familiar face from the courtyard, she knelt according to protocol and waited to hear the decree. Lady Liu had already knelt down as well.","Matron Zhao discreetly looked Lady Shen over carefully. Only after everyone had gathered did she smile and say, “By Her Majesty the Empress’s oral decree: to Crown Prince Lady Shen, a pair of gold pomegranate-patterned ruyi hairpins, a pair of tortoiseshell bracelets set with gold and jade beads, one bolt of brocade satin, two bolts of cloud satin, and two bolts of plain gauze.”","“To Crown Prince Lady Liu, a pair of jade butterfly hairpins set in gold, a pair of silver ruyi hairpins with pomegranate designs, two bolts of cloud satin, one bolt of blue plain satin, and one bolt of plain gauze.”","Having finished, Matron Zhao looked at the two women with a smile. “May you both conduct yourselves properly, observe your duties, and ease the burdens of His Highness the Crown Prince. May you soon bear branches and leaves for His Highness and extend his line.”","Shen Yanshui kowtowed and offered her thanks. “Thank you for Her Majesty’s gifts. I shall respectfully heed Her Majesty’s instructions.”","Lady Liu naturally kowtowed and gave thanks as well. However, when she heard that Lady Shen had received the additional tortoiseshell bracelet set with gold and jade and the brocade satin, she couldn’t help feeling a pang of jealousy.","The bracelet was one thing, but the brocade satin was an exceptionally fine material. Even the daily allotments of low-ranking consorts like them did not include it.","And yet... as she looked at Lady Shen, whose clothes had always been made from fine materials, her mood grew even more sour.","Without Shen Yanshui needing to say anything, Chunping smiled and slipped a purse into Matron Zhao’s hands. Silver Screen followed immediately after. This was an unspoken rule in the palace.","As someone trusted by Her Majesty the Empress, Matron Zhao naturally did not care about this small amount of silver, but she accepted it with a smile nonetheless.","Shen Yanshui said warmly, “You’ve gone to such trouble, Matron. Why not come inside and have a cup of tea and rest your feet?”","Matron Zhao smiled. “Thank you, Lady Shen, but I’m afraid I must decline. Her Majesty the Empress is waiting for me to report back. This servant will take her leave.”","Shen Yanshui inclined herself in a half-bow and returned the courtesy with a smile. “Then I won’t keep you today. Chunping, see Matron Zhao out.”","“Yes, mistress.”","With a smile on her face, Chunping bowed and said, “Matron, this way, please.”","After Chunping escorted Matron Zhao away, Shen Yanshui looked at the jewelry and bolts of fabric set aside nearby, unable to contain her delight. Afraid she might laugh outright, she exchanged a few words with Lady Liu before turning and returning to the room.","Only after there were no outsiders present did she finally laugh.","Looking at the “silver” that had come to her for free, she sincerely sighed, “Her Majesty the Empress truly has the heart of a bodhisattva. She really is a wonderful person. May Her Majesty enjoy good health and happiness, and live to a hundred years!”","*","“Did she really say that?”","The Empress looked rather surprised.","Matron Zhao, who was reporting in the hall, replied respectfully, “In answer to Your Majesty, that Lady Shen did indeed say those words.”","The Empress had originally been surprised to learn that the Crown Prince had not gone first to Lady Zhang’s residence. She was even more astonished when she discovered that he had spent both nights in a row in Lady Shen’s room.","That was why, taking advantage of the customary distribution of gifts to the palace’s new arrivals, she had deliberately sent Matron Zhao on this trip.","The Empress asked, “What do you think of this Lady Shen, Matron Zhao?”","Matron Zhao replied respectfully, “In answer to Your Majesty, this servant feels that Lady Shen’s temperament is rather unlike that of Lady Shen the Jieyu, despite the two of them being sisters.”","She did not beat around the bush and continued with a smile, “Lady Shen the Jieyu is clearly a high-born noblewoman at first glance. Although she is accomplished in music, chess, calligraphy, and painting, she cannot help being somewhat competitive, proud, and haughty.”","As she spoke, the image of Lady Shen came to mind. No matter the occasion, she always wore a bright smile, as though nothing in the world could trouble her. Lady Shen had also once taught the palace rules to the young women in the Palace of Gathered Elegance, so Matron Zhao knew her to some extent.","“As for Lady Shen, she doesn’t appear to be a complicated or scheming person. Back when she was in the Palace of Gathered Elegance, the thing she cared most about each day was what she would eat and drink. Her temperament is somewhat mild and placid. From what I saw today, Lady Shen is still much the same as before. I couldn’t discern any changes in her.”","The Empress was somewhat surprised. Still, she had considerable faith in Matron Zhao’s judgment of people. Lady Shen was merely the daughter of a concubine from the Loyal Righteous Earl’s manor, and it was hardly strange that her temperament differed from that of her legitimate elder sister.","With that, she let the matter go and paid it no further mind. At the end of the day, she trusted her son more. He was not some fool who would lose his head over a woman; he knew perfectly well what he ought to do and what he ought not.","*","Zheng Yuande waited until the Crown Prince and the two officials had finally finished discussing official matters. Only after the others had withdrawn did he quietly step forward and report, “Your Highness, the Crown Princess’s gifts have also been delivered.”","Cui Yu took a sip of tea to moisten his throat. His long, well-defined fingers rubbed the smooth, delicate surface of the celadon cup in his palm. After a moment, he raised his eyes and ordered, “Open the private treasury and select some things to send to Lady Shen.”","“Ah?” Zheng Yuande froze for an instant. When he caught the glance his master cast in his direction, he hurriedly smiled and said, “Yes, Your Highness. I’ll have someone see to it at once.”","Cui Yu suddenly seemed to think of something. “Wait.”","“Your Highness?”","Cui Yu said, “Choose several bolts of fine fabric as well and send them over.”"]},{"number":12,"title":"Chapter 12: Happily Accepting Them All","paragraphs":["Zheng Yuande obediently acknowledged the order without letting his lips lag, but inwardly, he was rather astonished.","His Highness had never been particularly interested in women. Naturally, he paid even less attention to the secondary consorts in the inner palace. The affairs of court already kept His Highness busy enough; he truly had little time or inclination to concern himself with women.","Moreover, although His Highness was the Crown Prince and possessed the most exalted status, he was neither extravagant nor wasteful in his daily expenditures. In fact, he was quite frugal. As for the secondary consorts in the inner palace, he had always rewarded them according to the rules, with very few additional gifts.","For instance, when Her Majesty the Empress and the Crown Princess bestowed gifts upon a newcomer according to custom, Lady Shen—having only just attended His Highness—would naturally receive somewhat more than the others, both as a sign of favor and as befitted the Crown Princess’s graciousness.","Yet this time, His Highness had not only given additional gifts but had specifically ordered that some fine fabrics be selected...","Zheng Yuande was rather puzzled. Had His Highness forgotten Lady Shen’s identity, or did he simply not care about it at all?","Naturally, Cui Yu could not possibly have forgotten Shen Yanshui’s identity. It was just that...","To him, Shen Yanshui was merely a woman whose temperament and appearance, at present, were not unpleasant and were even somewhat pleasing to the eye.","If any random woman could make him regard the situation as a grave threat, he might as well hand over the position of Crown Prince to someone else.","*","When Shen Yanshui received the Crown Prince’s gifts, she felt that her eyes had practically turned into sparkling stars from smiling so much that day.","One reward after another—there was so much to delight in that it was almost dazzling!","This time, Zheng Yuande had come in person. Seeing Lady Shen looking radiant, her brilliant smile blooming like a flower, even he could not help but stare for a moment. He then greeted her with a beaming smile. “This servant pays his respects to Your Ladyship.”","Shen Yanshui shifted slightly to the side and stepped forward to return half the courtesy with a sincere smile. Only then did she say, “Eunuch Zheng, you are too polite. What brings you here in person?”","Eunuch Zheng answered cheerfully, “This servant has come especially to convey His Highness’s verbal decree.”","This was the third time Shen Yanshui had knelt that day. However, if kneeling once earned her so many wonderful things, she felt that her knees were actually quite sturdy. She could withstand a few more kneelings without any trouble!","As with the previous two rewards, the formalities began with a few official-sounding words of praise. Only then did Eunuch Zheng recite the list of gifts:","“...one pair of jade-inlaid gold ruyi scepters; one set of hair ornaments adorned with red coral and pearls; one bolt of Floating Light silk; one bolt of Soft Mist gauze; one bolt of cicada-wing gauze; one bolt of snow satin; one bolt of scattered-flower damask; two bolts of plain gauze; and two bolts of blue plain satin.”","As Shen Yanshui listened to that long list of exquisite fabrics, she instinctively lifted her eyes to look at Zheng Yuande in astonishment—only to see his plump, fair, round face beaming with a genial smile.","“These were all specially selected for you by His Highness the Crown Prince. Your Ladyship, please rise,” he said.","His Highness had personally instructed him to choose some fine fabrics, so naturally he had not dared cut corners. He had even deliberately selected lightweight, high-quality materials. As for the last few bolts of plain gauze and satin, even if Lady Shen had no use for them, she could always give them to her servants.","Upon hearing this, Shen Yanshui thanked His Highness for the gifts and slowly rose to her feet. She then exchanged a few more sincere pleasantries with him before seeing him off and returning indoors.","Only then did she begin examining the gifts bestowed by the Crown Prince one by one. The snow satin and scattered-flower damask were one thing, but fabrics such as shimmering brocade, soft mist gauze, and cicada-wing silk were not only scarce but exceedingly expensive.","She had never been particularly demanding when it came to clothing. Among the sisters in her family, she had only ever seen her legitimate elder sister wear such costly and beautiful fabrics.","A short while later, Quanfu returned after seeing Zheng Yuande off. Dongyi and Quanshou stood guard outside the door, while Chunping brought over a cup of warm tea.","“My lady, please rest and have some tea.”","Shen Yanshui sat on the daybed and drank more than half the cup. Lost in thought, she lightly tapped the side table with her fingertips. After a long moment, she suddenly raised her eyes and asked, “What gifts did Her Majesty the Empress, the Crown Princess, and the Crown Prince bestow upon the other residences today?”","Quanfu immediately broke into a smile. “In reply to my lady, this servant paid close attention today. Her Majesty the Empress’s gifts to the various ladies of the Eastern Palace were mostly distributed according to their rank and established palace custom. However... the gifts the Crown Princess gave you were two degrees more lavish than those sent to Lady Zhang and Lady Wu. By now, the other courtyards have most likely heard of it as well.”","“But the Crown Prince’s gifts were sent only to our courtyard.”","As soon as Quanfu finished speaking, the expressions of master and servants alike changed.","A flicker of surprise appeared in Shen Yanshui’s eyes. As for the Crown Princess’s gifts, she had already understood the situation from the two remarks Matron Zhou had deliberately made when delivering them.","The Crown Princess wanted to set her up as a target for everyone else—and even expected her to feel grateful for it.","At first, however, the Crown Princess had probably intended to use Lady Wu as that target.","As for the Crown Prince’s gifts, though they suddenly made her look even more like the conspicuous one, what was she supposed to do now that they had arrived? Throw them out?","Of course she would accept them happily!","Qiuru gazed at the room full of exquisite, costly fabrics, gold, silver, and jewels, her face beaming. “His Highness the Crown Prince treats you so well, my lady. He bestowed gifts on you alone. It is clear that His Highness holds you in his heart.”","Shen Yanshui looked at the lavish gifts filling the room and smiled faintly, not taking Qiuru’s words to heart.","Rather than believing that the Crown Prince held her in his heart, she would sooner guess that their nightly activities over the past two evenings had become increasingly harmonious, and that the Crown Prince had been quite pleased—hence these rewards.","“All right, put everything away.”","“Yes, my lady.”","Quanfu led the others in sorting the gifts and placing them in the storeroom. Chunping, however, said with a smile, “This is wonderful. With so much fabric, we can make several more outfits for you, my lady.”","Now that there was more than enough material, Shen Yanshui naturally did not mind having a few more clothes made. “Then make two sets of spring clothes first, and four sets for summer. It is indeed time to prepare summer garments.”","Chunping agreed with a broad smile.","*","The Crown Princess was the first to learn that the Crown Prince had bestowed gifts upon Lady Shen alone, and her expression immediately darkened.","“What does the Crown Prince mean by this?”","Matron Zhou also furrowed her brow. In the past, the matter of distributing gifts among the various courtyards had always been decided by the Crown Princess. The Crown Prince had never intervened before.","“Your Highness, please do not be anxious. Lady Shen’s status is plain for all to see. His Highness the Crown Prince is wise and discerning; he must have his own considerations. Perhaps there is some deeper meaning behind his deliberate bestowal of gifts.”","The Crown Princess’s brows remained faintly furrowed, showing no sign of relaxing. It was all because of Lady Shen’s face—far too striking, far too threatening for her to ignore.","Matron Zhou smiled and soothed her. “Though Lady Shen was blessed with a fine appearance, she is shallow-minded, greedy for food and money. And look at how, after receiving the Crown Prince’s favor for the first time yesterday, she quarreled with Lady Wu and made such a spectacle of her. Even if she has caught His Highness’s eye, it will only be a passing novelty. It cannot last.”","After thinking it over, the Crown Princess’s expression eased somewhat. “By now, I imagine the others have all heard as well. I would like to see whether she can bear the consequences.”","*","The moment Eunuch Zheng, the Crown Prince’s chief personal attendant, entered the rear chambers with the rewards, the rest of the household learned of it before long.","Still, no one was truly foolish. Today, Her Majesty the Empress, the Crown Prince, and the Crown Princess had all bestowed gifts upon them. Whatever they might think in private, they could not make a move now—would that not amount to displaying dissatisfaction with their superiors?","As a result, Shen Yanshui spent several peaceful days without incident. During that time, the Crown Prince did not return to Lotus Heart Court.","Every day, she slept until she woke naturally. After rising and having breakfast, she would practice a set of the Eight Brocades indoors to loosen her body, then stroll through the garden—the place within the entire Eastern Palace with the most flowers and greenery.","At the moment, she sat on a swing in the garden, casually plucking a red apricot blossom bud. In the space of a single breath, as her wrist turned, the bud in her palm had fully bloomed into a pink-white apricot flower. Its petals unfurled, carrying a faint fragrance.","Dongyi smiled in surprise. “Mistress, your eyesight is truly excellent. This servant thought that seemed to be the only apricot blossom in bloom.”","Shen Yanshui looked at the pink-white flower resting quietly in her palm and smiled in excellent spirits. “My luck is rather good. Later, order a few more dishes from the kitchen.”","Her cultivation over the past few days had yielded modest results, but... compared with the effects of “dual cultivation” with the Crown Prince, it still fell far short.","“Yes, Mistress.” Dongyi was delighted at the words. Their mistress had always been generous, especially where food was concerned. Every time, she would order an extra dish, and whatever remained uneaten would be shared among them, allowing them to enjoy meat almost every day.","Not to mention the assorted pastries—her mistress was never stingy with those, either.","The meals provided to palace maids and eunuchs were generally large-pot fare prepared by apprentices. How good could such food possibly be? It was already fortunate if it merely kept them from going hungry.","If they wished to eat better, they had to spend their own silver to have the kitchen prepare something separately. Even then, it was nowhere near as fine as the meals their mistress ate every day.","“It smells so good, so good!” A sudden, somewhat peculiar voice rang out. Dongyi had barely lifted her head when she saw a beautiful little bird, emerald green all over with a touch of orange-red on its forehead, dart past and snatch the pink-white apricot blossom from her mistress’s palm in a flash.","“Ah! That bird—” Dongyi regretted not noticing it sooner and chasing it away. It had nearly startled her mistress.","“It’s nothing.” Shen Yanshui watched the pretty little parrot fly onto an apricot blossom branch and begin pecking eagerly at the petals of the flower she had ripened with her ability. She could not help smiling. Plucking another leaf, she infused it with a trace of her power and laid it in her palm before holding out her hand. “Come here.”","The little parrot had eaten every last petal and even the flower’s center. Hearing her voice, it cocked its head at her. Its tiny, bead-like eyes fixed on the tender leaf in her palm, and it immediately swaggered over on broad little wings. “Like it! I like it!”","Dongyi stared in surprise. “Mistress, this bird can actually speak? Is it... a parrot?”","Shen Yanshui nodded with a smile. “It is.” And clearly one that had been well cared for by someone, though she had no idea who its owner was. “It’s rather adorable.”","“Rather adorable! I’m rather adorable! Greetings to Your Highness, may you enjoy ten thousand blessings and peace! Ten thousand blessings and peace! Food, food! Give me more, give me more!”","Dongyi burst out laughing. “Mistress, this parrot is truly amusing.”","“Amusing, amusing! More, more!”","“You mustn’t eat too much of this.” Smiling, Shen Yanshui stroked the glossy feathers of the little parrot, which was obviously exceptionally well looked after, then gently rubbed its forehead.","The parrot contentedly pressed its forehead against her fingertip. “More, more!”","“Who’s making such a racket up ahead? How utterly lacking in manners.”","“Oh~ Who do we have here? Why, it’s Sister Shen...” Lady Wu approached in a begonia-colored, vine-patterned, fitted three-panel skirt, with a powder-white trimmed short jacket over it. A round fan rested in one hand while the other lay lightly on her maid’s arm, her every step graceful and poised.","Shen Yanshui’s expression remained calm as she bowed. “Greetings, Lady Wu.”","“Sister Shen, you’ve been rather free lately, haven’t you? You come to the garden every day to pass the time. As for me, I’ve been busy attending to His Highness the Crown Prince, and it feels as though I haven’t seen you in ages. Who would have thought we’d happen to meet today? What a very fortunate coincidence.”","She leisurely fanned herself. Only after she had finished speaking did she seem to realize that Shen Yanshui was still bowing. She raised her fan to her lips in exaggerated surprise. “Oh my, Sister, why are you still kneeling there? Get up, get up.”","Shen Yanshui inwardly raised a brow at Lady Wu’s theatrical performance. Such petty attempts to make things difficult for her hardly amounted to anything. So long as no one expected her to put on a performance in return, she could not be bothered to care.","Dongyi’s lips pressed into a tight line, her expression darkening. The moment she rose, she hurried to help her mistress up.","Shen Yanshui said, “Then I shall not disturb you any longer.” She could go back and prepare for dinner now; there was no need to waste time on someone unimportant.","“Wait.” Lady Wu extended her fan to block her path. Chin slightly raised, she looked at Shen Yanshui from the corner of her eye. “Why are you in such a hurry, Sister? You’ll only be going back to an empty room all alone. What fun is that? Why not stay and chat with me?”","Over the past ten days or so, His Highness the Crown Prince had visited the rear quarters only twice in total: once to Lady Zhang’s rooms, and once to hers. Yet two or three days had already passed, and there had been no reward or gift from His Highness, which only made her feel increasingly unsettled."]},{"number":13,"title":"Chapter 13: Birds Fly, People Jump","paragraphs":["\"Oh? What business does Lady Wu have to discuss with me?\" Shen Yanshui's tone was flat, sounding almost perfunctory, yet no one could point to any outright disrespect in her words even if they tried.","Lady Wu's eyebrows pinched together slightly, before she let out a proud cold snort. \"The Dragon Boat Festival is just a few days away. Every year on this occasion, His Majesty and the Empress lead the entire imperial court and the inner palace to the Jinling Pond to watch the dragon boat races. I've heard it's an incredibly lively, spectacular event.\"","She glanced at Shen Yanshui as she spoke, her tone thick with undisguised smugness. \"Every year, the Crown Princess brings two companions with her to the event. Just yesterday, the Crown Princess specifically mentioned this to me. It's such a pity, though—it seems this year, younger sister won't have the good fortune to attend.\"","Shen Yanshui lifted an eyebrow in response, but before she could say a word, a familiar bird cry rang out of nowhere.","\"Shut up, so noisy, so noisy!\"","Lady Wu's face immediately darkened. She pointed furiously at the little creature darting around over her head, daring to scold her out loud. \"Insolent thing!\"","She spun around and snapped at the palace maids and eunuchs waiting at her side. \"You fools! What are you all standing around for? Hurry up and knock this little beast down!\"","\"Help! Help!\" The bird's cry was piercingly loud, sending the whole scene into chaos of flapping wings and panicking people.","\"Little me is so scared! Danger, danger! Fly fast, fly fast!\"","Shen Yanshui: \"......\" The person who raised this little parrot must be a total chatterbox.","She had originally been thinking of helping the little creature out, but seeing how high and fast it was flying, she relaxed. Though this little thing was undeniably a little annoying in its cheekiness.","\"Someone come, someone come! Ugly people are trying to kill the bird! Kill the bird! Save the bird's life! Save the bird's life!\"","Lady Wu was so angry she nearly lost all her poise. \"Use stones! Smash this little beast down!\"","One of the palace maids looked worried, leaning over to whisper in her ear. \"My lady, this parrot clearly belongs to someone of status. If we really injure it...\"","No one who served close to their master in the palace was truly stupid. These little creatures, if they belonged to the right master, were far more valuable than the lives of ordinary palace maids and eunuchs. No one dared to actually lay a heavy hand on it.","Lady Wu barely listened to her personal maid's reminder, but she still frowned tightly, holding back her anger until her chest ached. \"Fine, forget it...\"","Plop. Something warm landed right on her forehead.","Shen Yanshui watched with her own eyes as a small, unmistakably stinky blob of droppings landed right on Lady Wu's forehead. She stared as Lady Wu lifted her hand in bewilderment, and then touched a whole handful of...","\"Ah——!\" The second Lady Wu realized what had landed on her forehead, she broke down and screamed at the top of her lungs.","\"Kill this little beast! Kill it!\" Her face twisted with unbearable disgust, she scrubbed at her forehead frantically with her handkerchief.","\"M-My lady...\" The several maids and eunuchs had never expected such a bizarre coincidence. Faced with their master who had clearly lost her mind in rage, the three of them were flustered for a moment, unsure what to do.","Smack! Lady Wu slapped the palace maid standing in front of her hard across the face. \"What are you all still gawking at?! If you don't kill this little beast today, I'll have the Crown Princess send every last one of you to the Palace Supervisor's Office!\"","Shen Yanshui had just started to frown, about to step in, when the sound of approaching footsteps reached her ears.","\"Who are you sending to the Palace Supervisor's Office?\"","The man who stepped into view wore a dark black informal robe embroidered with subtle silver cloud and thunder patterns, his hair held back by a jade crown, a leather belt cinching his waist. His voice was low and icy, radiating a bone-deep cold that made people want to shrink back the moment they laid eyes on him.","It was none other than the Crown Prince.","In an instant, everyone in the vicinity had knelt to the ground.","\"Little me is scared to death! Scared to death! Your Highness is blessed, Your Highness ten thousand blessings!\" The little parrot landed right on his shoulder, squawking noisily.","Cui Yu frowned instinctively.","Shen Yanshui curtsied in greeting. \"This servant greets Your Highness, may Your Highness be well.\" She wondered if he had just happened to arrive, or if he had been watching from the shadows for a while, and a faint wariness rose in her chest.","She had never expected this cheeky, loudmouthed little parrot to belong to the Crown Prince...","Lady Wu's face flushed bright red then drained of color, then flushed again. A faint dark stain still marked her forehead, ruining her once beguiling, begonia-like beauty and making her look utterly disheveled.","\"Your Highness...\" Tears began to roll down Lady Wu's cheeks like a broken string of pearls, her voice trembling, sounding so pitiable.","But Cui Yu was completely unmoved, not the slightest bit swayed. The look he gave her was nothing short of impatient.","Face burning, Lady Wu bit her lip. \"Your Highness, please forgive me. I had no idea this parrot was yours. It was only because... because...\"","She could not bring herself to admit out loud in front of the Crown Prince that the bird had defecated on her forehead, and she ended up sobbing in frustration. \"Your Highness, I truly did not mean any harm. That bird offended me first, I simply lost my composure for a moment.\"","\"Bad person! Bad person!\" The parrot squawked on.","Cui Yu suddenly frowned, and said coolly, \"Shut up, noisy thing.\"","Shen Yanshui: \"......\" Alright, that explained it. The bird really did learn that line from its master.","This time, the parrot stopped its cheeky squawking, pacing back and forth on his shoulder in silence. It clearly had plenty of practice behaving itself when told off.","Cui Yu glanced at the palace maid kneeling on the ground, one side of her face already swelling up bright red, and his brows twitched slightly.","He had been walking along the corridor outside the Fangyao Garden when he heard his familiar parrot cry \"Help——\" so he had come to investigate. He glanced at Lady Wu's forehead, which she had rubbed raw, then looked away, and said in a deep, steady voice, \"Help your lady back to her quarters.\"","Lady Wu heaved a huge sigh of relief. The Crown Prince had not punished her—he still cared for her!","She could not bear to stay looking like a mess in front of the Crown Prince anyway, so she blinked back her tears, her voice soft and delicate, the kind that was supposed to tug at people's heartstrings. \"Your Highness is most just. This servant takes her leave~\"","But seeing that the Crown Prince was not looking at her at all, she was left with a strange mix of feelings, half relieved that she could leave, half disappointed by his indifference.","Once everyone else had finally left, Cui Yu noticed that Shen Yanshui was still holding her curtsy. He glanced at her, reached out, wrapped his hand around her forearm, and personally helped her to her feet.","His palm met warm skin, separated only by a thin, smooth layer of fabric, and he felt a handful of soft, delicate, almost boneless softness.","Shen Yanshui tilted her head up to look at his face, and smiled. \"Thank you, Your Highness.\" Her voice was clear and melodious.","Shen Yanshui took the chance to wrap her hand around his for a moment, then stepped back with a grin. \"Did Your Highness notice? This is a new dress I made, using the Luminous Brocade that Your Highness bestowed on me. It's the first time I've ever worn such fine material. It's so comfortable and beautiful—don't you think it looks lovely on me?\"","As she spoke, she turned her body slightly to let him get a full look at it.","The moment their palms pressed together, Cui Yu felt a flicker of unfamiliarity. Just as he was about to pull his hand back, he caught sight of the bright, sunny smile on her face. He hesitated for a beat, and in the end, did not move to withdraw his hand at all.","Listening to her voice brimming with pure joy, he looked her over carefully from head to toe. The sun was gentle and bright that day, its soft glow spilling over her figure. The fabric of her dress shimmered with every small movement she made, and the graceful sway of her slender, supple waist as she turned was delicate and stunning. For a split second, his throat felt tight, and his voice dropped a little deeper, \"Yes, it looks good.\"","\"Pretty! So pretty!\" The little parrot suddenly flew from his shoulder and landed right on the pearl hairpin in her hair.","Dongyi's heart jolted with alarm! She was terrified that this parrot would blurt out one of its crude lines in front of their master too — that would be a total disaster!","Cui Yu held out his hand to the parrot with a blank, unamused expression. \"Come here.\"","\"Your Highness, blessings and prosperity! Your Highness, long life and good fortune!\" The little parrot hopped nimbly to another wooden hairpin in her hair instead, its obvious evasive manner both stubborn and cowardly at the same time.","Cui Yu frowned.","Shen Yanshui said, \"Your Highness, let me try to get it, if you would allow.\"","Cui Yu looked down and met her smiling eyes. Seeing that she was not the slightest bit frightened, he gave a low \"mm\" of assent.","Hidden by the sweep of her wide sleeve, Shen Yanshui reached out and plucked another apricot blossom bud. This time, she channeled a smaller amount of her special ability into it, and what settled in her palm in the end was a half-bloomed pink apricot blossom. \"Your Highness, what is its name?\"","Cui Yu paused for a moment, and said nothing right away.","\"I'm Little Jade! I'm Little Jade! Pretty lady, pretty lady, I'm Little Jade!\"","\"Pfft!\" Shen Yanshui could not hold back a laugh. She was amused by the deeply folksy, unrefined name Little Jade, which could not be more mismatched for the grand, regal status of the Crown Prince standing right in front of her. No wonder the man had looked like he would rather say nothing at all just a moment earlier.","Cui Yu: \"...\""]},{"number":14,"title":"Chapter 14: Sturdy","paragraphs":["Little Jade flew to the branches of the apricot tree with a petal in her beak, then immediately lowered her head and began pecking at it furiously!","Shen Yanshui glanced over and found herself smiling. Looking at Cui Yu, who had already recovered his composure, she asked curiously, “Your Highness wasn’t the one who named Little Jade, was he?”","Cui Yu replied, “No.”","The disdain in his eyes was unmistakable, though it was tinged with a hint of helplessness. Judging from the way he had treated Little Jade just now, it was clear enough.","He had allowed Little Jade to hop onto his shoulder without the slightest reaction, looking as though he had long since grown accustomed to it. Either he truly liked birds, or he was fond of the person who had named—or given him—the parrot.","Cui Yu’s brows relaxed slightly. “My maternal uncle gave her to me three years ago. He was the one who named her, too.”","Shen Yanshui’s peach-blossom eyes curved into a smile, and her voice was light, though tinged with surprise. “I never imagined Great General Qi would be such an interesting person.”","She was rather surprised. This seemed to be the first time she had heard him refer to himself as “I.” It appeared that the Crown Prince and his maternal uncle truly were very close.","“Big Nephew! Big Nephew!”","Cui Yu’s brow twitched violently. “Zheng Yuande.”","“Give me some silver to spend! Give me some silver to spend!”","“Oh dear, my little ancestor! Come here, I have something you like to eat...” Zheng Yuande hurriedly rose onto his tiptoes and stretched out his hand, coaxing the little ancestor perched above him.","Shen Yanshui did not dare laugh this time. Pretending she had heard nothing, she cleared her throat and said, “Your Highness, it’s nearly time for the evening meal. Why don’t you return with me and dine together?”","Cui Yu glanced at her slightly curved eyes, nodded, and gave a soft “Mm” before striding away ahead of her.","Watching his unusually swift footsteps, Shen Yanshui could not help but chuckle. She had not expected this man to be capable of embarrassment. His skin was surprisingly thin.","After musing over it for a moment, she followed him.","By the time the two of them returned to Lianxin Court, everyone there had already received word and was waiting at the entrance.","“This servant pays respects to the Crown Prince. May Your Highness enjoy good fortune and peace. This servant pays respects to Our Lady.”","Cui Yu barely glanced at them. He raised a hand and said, “Rise,” completely ignoring the distinctly different voice mixed in among the others’ greetings. Without pausing, he continued straight toward the eastern side hall.","Shen Yanshui noticed that Lady Liu’s eyes had suddenly reddened. Her footsteps faltered for a moment, but she still stopped and helped her up. For a while, she did not know what to say. At a time like this, anything she said would probably sound as though she were showing off.","Lady Liu’s body stiffened slightly. She suppressed the urge to shake Shen Yanshui’s hand away, drew a small breath, and thanked her with a composed smile. “Thank you, Elder Sister. I shall not disturb you and the Crown Prince.”","She turned and returned to the western side hall with the palace servants attending her.","“Close the door!” she said quietly.","The young eunuch behind her hurriedly shut the door tight.","Lady Liu unconsciously twisted the silk handkerchief between both hands. Her eyes held shame, anger, panic, and confusion as she asked in a low voice, “Yinping, why do you think the Crown Prince didn’t even look at me?”","“Could it be... that I’m truly not worthy of catching the Crown Prince’s eye?”","As she spoke, she sat down before the dressing table. Staring at her reflection in the mirror, she absently touched her cheek. She might not be as beautiful as Lady Shen or Lady Wu, but she considered herself no less attractive than Lady Zhang. Why, then, was she the only one the Crown Prince neglected?","When she had first been bestowed upon the Crown Prince, she had been thrilled and expectant, filled with pride and conceit. Yet in the short span of half a month, her heart—once floating in the clouds—had gradually sunk back down.","Yinping said cautiously, “Your appearance is certainly not lacking. Otherwise, you would never have been chosen over so many high-born young ladies by the various esteemed consorts.”","As her mistress’s personal maid, Yinping naturally hoped that Lady Liu would win the Crown Prince’s favor. But Lady Shen’s beauty was simply too overwhelming, making her mistress seem rather dim by comparison.","Lady Liu pressed her lips together, raised a hand, and wiped away the tears on her face. There were still many days ahead. No matter how beautiful a face was, there would surely come a day when the Crown Prince grew tired of looking at it.","* * *","Shen Yanshui had already felt hungry when her ability first broke through.","Now that she was dining with the Crown Prince, not only was the food abundant, but the portions were generous as well. Her chopsticks flew back and forth so energetically that there was no need for anyone else to serve her. This made Cui Yu glance at her several times.","He had known for a long time that she had a considerably larger appetite than ordinary women. Even so, he was still slightly shocked when she finished five bowls of rice and showed no signs of stopping.","Beside her, Chunping’s eyes were practically twitching from the effort of trying to signal her mistress, yet she still failed to stop her mistress from accomplishing the feat of eating five bowls of rice in front of the Crown Prince. In the end, her eyes filled with despair.","Across the table, Zheng Yuande’s mouth had fallen open in astonishment, forming a perfect “O.”","When Shen Yanshui began filling her sixth bowl, she could no longer bear the increasingly astonished looks around her. She looked at Cui Yu with pleading eyes and said softly, “Your Highness, I’m still hungry...”","During the apocalypse, she would not have such a huge appetite whenever she had crystal cores to absorb. But at present, she had none.","She couldn’t possibly keep pretending in front of the Crown Prince just for the sake of appearances, could she?","Wouldn’t that be a loss? Why refuse free food and spend her own silver to buy more?","Although the cooks in the Eastern Palace would not make things difficult for her—in fact, they would sometimes send over a few extra fresh dishes—her appetite was simply too large.","Cui Yu glanced at her and instructed, “Tell the kitchen to prepare a few more dishes. Also, summon an imperial physician from the Imperial Medical Academy.”","Shen Yanshui fell silent. Fine, then.","She gave him a tight-lipped smile. “Thank you, Your Highness.”","After she finished her sixth bowl and set down her chopsticks, Chunping cleared the table at a speed that could only be described as astonishing.","Shen Yanshui was speechless. It seemed she had truly frightened Chunping this time.","She had barely finished a cup of tea when the imperial physician arrived.","“This subject pays respects to the Crown Prince.”","Cui Yu slightly furrowed his brows. “Rise. Examine Lady Shen.”","The imperial physician stood and acknowledged the order.","Shen Yanshui cooperatively extended her wrist. Seeing the Crown Prince’s furrowed brows, the imperial physician could not help but feel his heart tighten. He examined her pulse with even greater care.","Yet after only a short while, the vertical crease between his brows slowly smoothed out, and an expression of surprise even appeared on his face.","At last, he withdrew his hand and bowed. “Reporting to Your Highness, the young lady’s health is perfectly fine. Her pulse is strong, and her qi and blood are abundant. Such a robust and healthy constitution is something this old physician has rarely seen in all his years.”","These days, young ladies all pursued a delicate, willow-like appearance. Most achieved it by starving themselves.","The noble ladies in the palace were even worse. They rarely exercised and had to maintain their figures. After years of this, how healthy could their bodies possibly be?","Shen Yanshui was speechless. “Robust” was really not necessary. Truly.","Cui Yu was slightly surprised by the physician’s words. After examining her carefully, he looked toward the imperial physician and said, “She just ate six bowls of rice.”","The unspoken meaning was clear: Is that really normal?","Shen Yanshui was speechless again. What was wrong with eating six bowls of rice? Was she eating his family’s rice?","Well, she was indeed eating rice from his household.","Imperial Physician Hu smiled. “Your Ladyship has a strong pulse, and naturally a robust appetite as well. I imagine you’re usually quite active, which is why you eat more and digest your food quickly. It won’t have any adverse effect on your health.”","Shen Yanshui hurriedly nodded. “The physician is right. Not only that, I’ve been stronger than most people since I was little, so naturally I eat a little more than they do.”","After the physician left, Cui Yu glanced at her, then turned to Zheng Yuande and instructed, “From now on, if Lady Shen’s daily food and provisions aren’t enough, take what’s needed from my allowance.”","Since she served in his Eastern Palace, he couldn’t very well let her go hungry.","Zheng Yuande glanced at Lady Shen, whose face had instantly lit up with delight. He couldn’t help mulling it over for a moment before respectfully replying, “Yes, Your Highness. This servant will remember.”","Shen Yanshui was genuinely happy now—overjoyed, in fact!","Her eyes sparkled at him as though they were shining with a dazzling “bling, bling,” and in that moment, he seemed especially tall and imposing to her. Especially charming!","She clasped one of his hands in both of hers and said with heartfelt sincerity, “Thank you, Your Highness. You’re truly wonderful!”","This wasn’t just about one or two meals. It was about every meal from now on.","At last, she no longer had to worry about where she would find the money once the two thousand taels of silver ran out.","Her exuberant happiness seemed almost infectious. Without realizing it, the corners of Cui Yu’s lips lifted slightly as well, and for a moment, he forgot the unpleasant events that had taken place at court."]},{"number":15,"title":"Chapter 15: ...Delicate.","paragraphs":["Cui Yu glanced down at the slender, soft, fair hands that were clutching his palm tightly. The moment his fingertips stirred slightly, Shen Yanshui noticed his gaze. She quickly pulled her hands back, smiling brightly and saying, \"Your subject wife got carried away by joy just now and lost my manners. I hope Your Highness will not hold it against me~\"","Cui Yu gently curled his palm into a fist, as if the soft warmth from a moment ago still lingered on both the inside and outside of his hand.","He glanced around the room, then finally turned his eyes back to her and asked, \"What do you usually do on a daily basis?\"","Shen Yanshui did not catch his subtle little gesture. At his question, she proceeded to recount all her daily routines in detail.","To sum it up, she would get up in the morning, have meals, practice Baduanjin twice to stretch her body, (do her cultivation), and wander around the garden, and just like that, the whole morning would be gone.","After that, she would take a siesta, have lunch, read books and listen to storytellers' scripts, tend to the flowers and plants in her courtyard, think about what delicious food to have next, finish her dinner, and the whole afternoon would slip by too. Then she would take a walk to aid digestion, (do her cultivation), and go to bed.","She told him everything truthfully except for the part about cultivation.","And that was the perfect end to her day.","Cui Yu paused for a moment after listening to her account, and said, \"So every day... you are quite 'busy'.\"","Her simple, straightforward description gave off a sense of leisurely coziness, making it feel like she took each day unhurriedly, living her own little life earnestly.","That said, Baduanjin was indeed quite effective in warding off illnesses and keeping fit. If she had practiced it for years, and added activities like cuju and horse polo to that mix, it would hardly be strange that she had such a healthy body.","Shen Yanshui had intentionally mentioned Baduanjin because she knew this form of exercise already existed in the Great Yong Dynasty.","At his words, she pretended to ponder for a moment, then nodded at him seriously, \"Yes, I really am quite busy.\"","Busy cultivating, busy planting flowers and melons, busy sleeping, busy eating good food, and busy enjoying this little life where she had no worries about food or drink, and no one pointing fingers or ordering her around.","All of a sudden, Cui Yu lifted his hand and tapped her forehead with his knuckle, saying in a faint, calm tone, \"I think you are just far too idle.\"","Shen Yanshui covered her forehead with one hand, her tone full of feigned grievance, \"That hurt~\"","The attendants waiting on them inside the room were very observant, and quietly moved far away to give them space.","When Shen Yanshui lowered her hand, Cui Yu saw a small red mark on her originally fair, glossy forehead. He could not help but be slightly stunned for a second. He had not used any force at all, who would have thought her skin was so delicate. Hmm... it was not just her forehead either. It seemed every part of her was always so fragile, that the lightest touch could leave a patch of red...","His gaze deepened for a brief moment, before he pulled his eyes away from her. He casually picked up a book that had been left on the soft couch, his voice lowering slightly, \"What book is this?\" The moment the words left his mouth, a little colorful object slipped out from between the pages.","Cui Yu picked it up, turned to look at her, and said, \"This is... a luck braid? For me?\" His voice sounded perfectly even, giving no hint of what he was thinking.","Shen Yanshui was only stunned for a split second, before she nodded with a perfectly natural expression, \"That's right! The Dragon Boat Festival is in a few days. I wove this specially for Your Highness. This colorful silk braid can ward off evil spirits, and bless you with smooth, safe days. I just never expected you would stumble across it today.\"","She did not mention at all that this had originally been something she had been practicing her weaving on, which was why it was a little wider and larger than usual, as she was still clumsy when she first started.","Chunping, who was standing by the room door, lowered her head even further the moment she heard those words.","Cui Yu eyed the intricately woven concentric-pattern sash before him, crafted from multicolored silk threads and about a finger's width wide. He set it casually on the side table, not seeming to pay it much mind at all.","Shen Yanshui did not take offense. After all, it was just a little trinket she had made as a beginner for fun—how could something so crude catch the eye of a man who had seen countless fine treasures in his life?","The two chatted idly for a while before stepping out to take a stroll to aid digestion. Cui Yu had assumed Shen Yanshui would bring up the trip to Jinling Pool on the Dragon Boat Festival, either directly or subtly, but much to his surprise, she did not mention a single word about it the entire walk.","After they had bathed and changed into fresh robes, all the attendants withdrew, leaving only a single candle by the bedside, its flame flickering gently in the night breeze.","That night, Shen Yanshui was unusually passionate.","Hadn't he called her too idle? Well, here she was, pulling a \"night shift\" even now—though she did not mind this particular shift at all. But how dare he say she had nothing better to do?","Looking at the strong, sturdy form hovering over her, Shen Yanshui did not hold back—there was no need to. She reached out to run her hands over him, and watching the shifting expressions in his eyes, she grew even bolder in her teasing.","Cui Yu's gaze darkened abruptly. The next moment, Shen Yanshui was jolted so hard that her head nearly slammed into the bedpost, only to be tugged back into his arms just in time.","Though she had plenty of stamina, staying in one position for too long grew uncomfortable...","When her head sank once more into the soft propped-up pillow at the head of the bed, her breath came in uneven little gasps. Her voice trembled softly, sounding as if she were pouting in gentle grievance. \"Your Highness, my head hurts from all the bumps...\"","Cui Yu's movements came to a brief halt.","He shifted his hands from where they rested on her body, curling his fingers around her ankles. Shen Yanshui lifted her leg, the rounded tip of her foot pressing lightly against his solid shoulder, her tone laced with faint reproach. \"My back is sore too, from all the rubbing.\"","Cui Yu paused again. His gaze grew heavy, his voice tight, low, and hoarse. \"...Spoiled thing.\"","Before she could say another word, he swept her up into his arms, holding her entire body against his chest.","Startled, Shen Yanshui instinctively wrapped her legs around his lean, powerful waist, her slender, graceful arms clinging tight around his neck.","Cui Yu's breath caught sharply, his face suddenly sinking into the soft, yielding warmth of her skin.","Shen Yanshui: \"...\" Her fair, jade-like cheeks flushed bright red in an instant.","Outside the chamber, Chunping stood rooted to the spot, her face burning bright red as she listened to the faint, muffled rustlings coming from inside the room, punctuated by the occasional soft creaking sound that made her worry for a good long while.","But after a while, the little creaks died away. The room fell almost quiet, yet no one called out for water, which left her quite confused.","Shen Yanshui soon discovered that beneath the Crown Prince's cold, dignified, and gentle exterior, his arm strength was far greater than she had expected. He could carry her while moving so vigorously without showing the slightest sign of strain.","It was a pleasure unlike any other...","The next morning, when Shen Yanshui woke up, the first thing she saw was a strikingly handsome, elegant face, sharp-featured and fair.","She thought for a moment, and then remembered—wasn't today a day off from official duties?","But why was she in his bed? Every time before, after they finished, they would clean up quickly and sleep under their own separate quilts. She had always thought that arrangement was perfect, nothing beat the comfort of having your own quilt to yourself. But now... there was a large, warm hand resting on her chest. No wonder she had felt a heavy weight there all night.","She tried to shift her position, but the moment she moved, Cui Yu opened his eyes.","His palm shifted unconsciously, and a soft, alluring little hum brushed past his ear. That was when Cui Yu finally woke up completely.","Shen Yanshui fixed her pair of peach blossom eyes on him, her tone soft and lingering as she said, \"Your Highness, you were holding my hand far too tight...\" Seeing the faint, unseemly flicker of discomfort cross his face, Shen Yanshui could not help but chuckle inwardly. Before he could utter a single word in response, she added, \"Your Highness, this concubine is feeling a little hungry.\"","Cui Yu calmly and unflappably withdrew his hand as if nothing out of the ordinary had happened. He gave a low grunt of acknowledgement, then lifted the quilt, got out of bed, and walked around the screen to call Zheng Yuande in to attend to him.","Through the faintly translucent screen, Shen Yanshui watched him from behind. The sunlight streaming through the window lattice gilded half of his back, and under the soft pale golden glow, the defined lines of his arms stood out all the more sharply.","As he moved to get dressed, the muscles along his back shifted in smooth, flowing undulations. The only difference was that his otherwise elegant back now bore several faint, thin red marks that looked as if they had been left accidentally by fingernails, lending him a strangely disheveled, alluring charm.","The next moment, he pulled on his white undershirt to cover his body. Only then did Shen Yanshui rise, throw on a loose outer robe, casually tie a sash around her waist, and step forward of her own accord. With a soft, smiling voice, she said, \"Your Highness, allow this concubine to help you dress.\"","Zheng Yuande quickly ducked his head, presented the Crown Prince's outer robe, and stepped a respectful distance away.","Cui Yu lowered his gaze slightly, looking at her half-done attire without saying a word for a moment.","Shen Yanshui's mind raced back to the dressing procedures the nannies had taught her in the Palace of Elegant Virtue, and she followed each step slowly to dress him properly. The leather belt around his waist proved a little tricky to fasten, but she bent over, lowered her head, and eventually managed to tie it neatly, if a little clumsily.","No one rushed her the whole time, which was a relief.","She felt a small swell of satisfaction at the task done. \"There we go,\" she said with a bright smile, and as she lifted her head, she saw the Crown Prince turn his head to stare intently at the bamboo branch on the incense table, as if a full bloom had sprouted right out of the twig.","Cui Yu kept a stern, straight face, only uttering a curt \"Mm\" before he turned and stepped out of the room.","Shen Yanshui watched his departing back, and by chance, her gaze landed on the tips of his ears, which were bright crimson. She paused for a moment in confusion, then suddenly glanced down at her own clothes.","Since she had tied her sash in a rush, the lapels of her robe had fallen loosely open, and she had not even put on her inner chemise beneath it... But thinking back to how he had acted just now, she felt a strange mix of amusement and surprise well up in her chest.","The Crown Prince... could it be that just a glance at that was enough to fluster him so much his ears turned red?","It was not as if his own hands had been anything but unruly earlier, right after they woke up.","Even so, she could not help but think that this version of the Crown Prince, all stony-faced with bright red ears, was unexpectedly quite endearing."]},{"number":16,"title":"Chapter 16: Father and Son of the Heavenly Family","paragraphs":["With the help of Chunping and Xia'an, Shen Yanshui got herself ready in no time. When she walked into the outer room, she saw a line of palace attendants filing in, setting the breakfast spread on the table.","She looked over to Cui Yu, the Crown Prince, who was sitting on the soft couch holding a book, and stepped forward with a smile to pay her respects.","Cui Yu lifted his gaze, as if he had only just noticed her.","The weather that day was lovely, with sunlight streaming into the room early on. Shen Yanshui was wearing a rose-purple soft smoke gauze dress, a white jade crabapple pendant fastened around her slender waist that looked so narrow it could be circled with one hand, with a thin layer of cicada-wing gauze draped over the whole outfit, making her look exceptionally gentle and pretty.","Only her hair and hair ornaments were far too simple.","Cui Yu spoke in a light, calm tone, telling her to rise.","Shen Yanshui noticed that his gaze had lingered on her hair for an extra moment just now, but she did not pay it any mind. Unless she was going out, in her own chambers, she usually only asked Xia'an to twist her hair into a simple bun, securing it with a single hairpin or a hair ribbon, as it was the most comfortable way to wear it.","Of course, this was also her gradual way of testing the limits of what the Crown Prince would allow her to do. So far... the results of her test seemed pretty good.","The two of them began to have their meal. Shen Yanshui was not picky about food at all, so even though all the dishes on the table were originally prepared by the imperial kitchen for the Crown Prince, she ate with great enjoyment.","When Cui Yu set down his silver chopsticks, he saw her glance at him, blink her eyes, and say, \"Your Highness, your concubine hasn't had her fill yet.\"","Cui Yu said gently, \"From now on, when you have meals, you can eat as much as you like. There is no need to hold back on account of me.\"","\"Thank you, Your Highness. You are so kind.\" Shen Yanshui looked at him with bright, sparkling eyes.","After saying that, she served herself another bowl of green vegetable and minced meat porridge and continued to eat.","Though Shen Yanshui ate quite a lot, her manners were not rude or unrefined at all. After all, when a person was as beautiful as she was, every little thing she did was a pleasure to watch.","Seeing how good her appetite was and how happy she looked while eating, Cui Yu let out a soft chuckle, lowered his head to take a sip of tea, then suddenly frowned slightly and put the teacup down.","Zheng Yuande had long since seen through everything. This Lady Shen was truly a simple, silly soul who took every word the Crown Prince said completely seriously.","His Highness had told her to eat freely, and she had really settled in to eat without a second thought, leaving the Crown Prince sitting there waiting for her. It was almost as if tending to His Highness was less important than the two bowls of food in front of her...","Zheng Yuande was left completely speechless.","Still, it was a good thing he had been quick-witted and specifically told the imperial kitchen to make extra portions earlier, otherwise he would have been worried that there would not be enough food left for the Crown Prince to eat.","As for the serving maids Chunping and Xia'an, no matter what complicated thoughts they had in their hearts, none of them dared to say a word. After all, they had tried to gently persuade her before, but... it had not worked at all. In the end, they could only keep a steady, polite smile on their faces.","Shen Yanshui did not keep anyone waiting for long. She finished her meal soon after, and rinsed her mouth.","Cui Yu looked at her and suddenly said, \"In a few days, it will be the Dragon Boat Festival. Would you like to go to Jinming Pool to watch the celebrations?\"","Shen Yanshui was a little surprised, not expecting him to take the initiative to ask her such a question. But right then, her eyes sparkling, she answered without the slightest hesitation, \"This concubine would love to go.\"","Who would not want to go and see all the lively fun?","Zheng Yuande: \"...\" He was now fully certain that this woman was truly a simple one.","Chunping and Xia'an: \"...\"","My lady, even if you really do want to go, you cannot say it so straightforwardly in front of the Crown Prince. You could at least be a little more tactful about it!","Cui Yu nodded at her answer, as if he had not found it unexpected at all. Listening to her speak openly of what she wanted, without using that soft, timid tone to hint and beat around the bush, or take the chance to throw subtle digs at the Crown Princess or other concubines to badmouth them, made the deep, calm light in his eyes soften into a faint, gentle smile. His voice was clear and rich, unhurried as he said, \"I understand.\"","Shen Yanshui curtsied to see him off, and at the same time, she began to look forward to the upcoming Dragon Boat Festival.","Lady Liu watched the Crown Prince leave, his tall, graceful figure receding from sight. She suppressed the sour feeling in her heart, lowered her head, and curtsied to the Lady Shen beside her. \"Sister Shen, I will head back to my chambers first.\"","Shen Yanshui nodded with a smile, pretending not to notice the dark circles under Lady Liu's eyes, and did not say anything extra. There were so many women in the imperial harem. If Lady Liu did not learn to look on the bright side and make an effort to live a better life, she would only end up suffering for it.","Back in her own room, Shen Yanshui picked up the book that was left on the soft couch to continue reading. It was a geographical record of the northern border of the Great Yong Dynasty, filled with the author's accounts of the local customs and conditions there, and she had found it really interesting to read.","\"Eh?\" Shen Yanshui flipped through the pages of the book, then looked all around the soft couch, before lifting her head to ask Chunping, \"Where is my multicolored braided charm?\"","Before Chunping could reply, Xia'an, who was in the middle of ironing clothes, suddenly pressed her lips together and snickered, whispering, \"Your mistress, this servant saw it. The Crown Prince took it with him just now.\"","Shen Yanshui: \"......?\"","*","It was Cui Yu's day off. He did not have to attend court hearings, nor did he have to go to the capital administrative office to handle official duties. But as soon as he arrived at Changqing Palace and before he could even sit down, he turned to give an order. \"I remember that last year, the Southern Ocean tributed a set of hibiscus pink crystal headpieces inlaid with pearls?\"","Zheng Yuande was taken aback for a moment, then replied, \"Your Highness, that is correct. I heard that kind of hibiscus pink crystal is extremely rare and precious.\"","Cui Yu said, \"Deliver that set of headpieces to Lady Shen.\"","Zheng Yuande quickly bowed to acknowledge the order. But before he could step out, he heard His Highness add, \"Also go to the Inner Palace's flower nursery and pick out some well-bloomed flowers and plants.\" He paused for a brief moment, then said in a light tone, \"Have the Palace Attendants Bureau...\"","After Zheng Yuande withdrew, someone came to report that Chen Qian, the Junior Supervisor of the Imperial Household who was an official of the Eastern Palace, was already waiting in the Dunben Hall. Cui Yu's brows drew together slightly.","Chen Qian was just over forty years old, wearing a vermilion official robe with a leather belt fastened around his waist. His features were dignified, and he wore a small goatee. But his expression at the moment was far from pleasant. He was ushered into the Crown Prince's study after his presence was announced.","Chen Qian bowed to pay his respects. \"This subject greets Your Highness, the Crown Prince.\"","Cui Yu said in a calm voice, \"Lord Chen, there is no need for formalities.\"","After Chen Qian straightened up, his brows furrowed into a deep frown. He said in a heavy tone, \"Your Highness, early this morning, His Majesty suddenly issued an order for Marquis Xuanyi to lead forty thousand of the elite Tiger Wing troops under Great General Qi's command. This way, half of the military power has been split off. The Great General has also been ordered to remain at home to rest and recuperate. Your Highness, are we just going to wait for our doom like this?\"","The Duke Fengguo, the maternal family of the Crown Prince, used to hold military power. But ever since the Crown Prince's young uncle Great General Qi rose to prominence on the battlefield, the old duke, who had seemed hale and hearty before, suffered a recurrence of an old injury and could no longer go to the front lines.","Great General Qi was brilliant at fighting wars, but when it came to court politics, he was not as seasoned and experienced as the old duke, so he could not offer much support to the Crown Prince.","After he finished speaking and saw that the Crown Prince did not say a word, he frowned even harder and added, \"Your Highness, word has it that Marquis Xuanyi and Great General Qi have never gotten along, and he is also related by marriage to the He family, the maternal clan of the Fourth Prince. His Majesty is clearly paving the way to elevate the Fourth Prince. We cannot just sit back and do nothing any longer!\"","\"I heard that the arrangements for the Jinming Pool celebrations during the upcoming Dragon Boat Festival have been assigned by His Majesty to the First Prince and the Fourth Prince. We could place some of our men to make some secret moves there...\"","Cui Yu suddenly cut off his next words, his expression turning slightly grim. \"Lord Chen.\"","Chen Qian: \"Your Highness?\"","Cui Yu's brows drew tight. \"I understand Lord Chen's intentions, but the Duanwu Festival gathering at the Golden Bright Pond will draw attention from all across the court and the general public. This matter concerns the imperial family's reputation, so there is no need to discuss it further.\"","In the end, this Lord Chen left with a rigid, stony expression on his face.","Cui Yu's own countenance remained perfectly calm. The matter of military power had long been discussed and planned between him, his maternal grandfather, and his young maternal uncle, so this turn of events was no surprise to him.","His father, the Emperor, was no foolish, incompetent ruler. When Cui Yu was young, he had always looked up to his father as his role model, and he had dreamed of becoming a wise, enlightened sovereign just like him.","Yet, as the Emperor's health faded day by day, and his sons grew older and more capable with each passing day, the Emperor's temperament grew increasingly unpredictable and suspicious.","It was at this exact juncture that foreign tribes from the northern border invaded. Cui Yu's young maternal uncle won instant fame through a decisive battle, and over the following years, he accumulated one brilliant military achievement after another.","As successive reports of victory arrived in the capital from the frontier, Cui Yu gradually noticed a distinct shift in the Emperor's attitude toward him.","Several years on, the original Crown Prince's Household Administration Office had become nothing more than an empty name. The former officials assigned to serve the Eastern Palace had all been dismissed or transferred away. Now, many of the officials holding posts in the Eastern Palace are just like Chen Qian -- good for nothing but show, short-sighted, or eager for quick gains at any cost.","There were a few of them with real talent and ability, but without exception, each of them held multiple concurrent official positions, all serving as the head of a government ministry in the imperial court. Their nominal post as a member of the Eastern Palace's staff was nothing but a meaningless, empty title to them.","It was true that Cui Yu could summon them if he needed something done, but... there was no point in doing so.","They were not the Crown Prince's men. They were the Emperor's men.","Cui Yu's gaze fell on a white jade paperweight at the edge of his desk.","It was one of the birthday gifts the Emperor had personally carved and given to him when he was three years old, the year he began his formal studies. The jade was warm and smooth to the touch, carved with simple, unadorned cloud patterns.","He still remembered the Emperor holding his small hand, guiding him stroke by stroke to write his very first character -- \"yong\", meaning forever.","\"Yu'er, writing is just like being a person. Your brush must be held straight, and your heart must also be straight.\"","Back then, the Emperor's voice had carried a bright, hearty laugh, none of the suspicion and wariness that marked it now. Cui Yu could even recall being too small to reach the desk, so the Emperor had lifted him to sit on his lap, letting him curiously grab the heavy imperial private seal to play with.","The Emperor had not been angry at all, and had simply let him treat the royal seal as a toy, stamping random patterns all over sheets of paper.","Cui Yu slowly closed his eyes, the pad of his index finger unconsciously stroking the smooth edge of the jade paperweight.","Among the sons of heaven, it was far from unheard of for father and son to end up facing each other on the battlefield, fighting a life-and-death struggle.","But... he did not want that to happen between him and his father."]},{"number":17,"title":"Chapter 17: Quite... thoughtful","paragraphs":["Shen Yanshui did not practice the Eight Brocades today. She ordered everyone to leave and began cultivating on her own.","First-rank abilities were extremely weak. Take fire abilities, for example: at the first rank, one could initially produce only a tiny flame. After becoming more proficient, one might be able to launch a fist-sized fireball, but its power and duration were still rather limited.","The same was true of wood abilities. They were generally even weaker than fire abilities. Fortunately, there were no mutated beasts like those in the apocalypse, so being weak was not particularly important.","When her wood ability had been at the first rank, she could only hasten the growth of plants in a small area. In a confrontation, it was practically useless.","All these years, she had never given up exercising her body. It was only that her inexpensive parents had strictly forbidden her from learning martial arts, which had always been a source of regret.","In any case, if she encountered danger, she might not be able to defeat her opponent, but escaping with her life should not be a problem.","She was pondering this when the tips of her ears twitched.","At the same time, the courtyard rang with greetings of varying pitches, along with Zheng Yuande’s voice.","The moment Chunping entered the room, she saw that her mistress had already come out, fully dressed and ready. Chunping could not help but beam with delight. “Mistress, Eunuch Zheng has arrived.”","Shen Yanshui stepped outside and saw the plump, round-faced Zheng Yuande smiling cheerfully at her, along with the long line of people and gifts behind him.","After the two exchanged polite greetings, Zheng Yuande cleared his throat and explained the purpose of his visit. He had indeed come to deliver gifts from the Crown Prince to Lady Shen, but among those gifts was something inconvenient to mention in public—a bed.","Shen Yanshui understood at once. Thinking back, she seemed to have heard the wooden bed creak last night when things had gotten rather intense. She had not expected the Crown Prince to remember such a detail.","Pressing her lips together in a smile, she said, “I suddenly remembered that the paint on the bed in my room has started to peel. I’ll have the Imperial Household Department replace it with a new one later.”","Zheng Yuande let out a sigh of relief. It seemed Lady Shen was not quite as foolish as she appeared.","If the Crown Prince had directly bestowed a bed upon her, what would people say about him once word got out?","Satisfied, he glanced at the items being carried behind him and said, “The Crown Prince heard that you enjoy tending to flowers and plants, Lady Shen, so he specially sent you six pots each of peonies, weeping crabapples, qionghua, and lilacs. There is also some tea for you to sample.”","Shen Yanshui looked at the flowers in full bloom, her eyes curving into delighted crescents. She had not expected the Crown Prince to be so thoughtful with his gifts. As for the tea... Though she did not know why he had suddenly thought to send her tea, anything that came from the Crown Prince was unlikely to be ordinary.","“The flowers bestowed by His Highness are even more beautiful than those in the Imperial Garden. I’ll choose a few to place on my desk later and admire them every day. I certainly won’t fail to appreciate His Highness’s kindness.”","Zheng Yuande chuckled. “I’m glad you like them. If there is nothing else, this servant will take his leave.”","Shen Yanshui exchanged a few more polite words with him before saying, “Take care, Eunuch Zheng.” As usual, she had Quanfu see him out.","Afterward, she first looked over the flowers and plants, then examined the jewelry bestowed by the Crown Prince. A smile spread across her face, and her eyes curved into crescents.","Could it be that the Crown Prince thought... she had no jewelry to wear? Was that why he had given her all these gifts?","Still, this lotus pink crystal was truly beautiful. Even someone like her, who had never cared much for dressing up, found it so lovely that her heart stirred at the sight of it.","“Rain-Season Dragon Well, Silver Needle, Lushan Cloud Mist, Biluochun?” After admiring the jewelry, Shen Yanshui opened each of the white porcelain tea jars, taking a look inside before leaning closer to smell them.","She more or less understood why he had suddenly sent her tea. Perhaps the tea he had drunk at her residence had not suited his taste, so he had remembered to send some of his own here.","Quanfu happened to return after seeing the visitors out and heard her words. He smiled and said, “These are all fine spring teas. Outside the palace, they would probably be worth a fortune.”","Dongyi was astonished. “They’re really that expensive?”","Chunping said, “We must store them carefully, or we’ll end up ruining something so precious.”","Qiuyi’s face was full of smiles, and her eyes were filled with envy. “His Highness is truly good to our mistress.”","Shen Yanshui smiled.","He was indeed very good to her. Although the Crown Prince seemed somewhat aloof, he was not difficult to get along with. He was not overly rigid or formal either, and he was even... rather considerate.","She liked drinking tea as well. She did not have any particular preference, but in this life, she had at least been born into an earl’s household, so she knew the value of fine tea.","With such good tea on hand, she could even make milk tea if she had the opportunity.","However, she felt that if the Crown Prince bestowed gifts upon her two or three more times, she might become the target of everyone’s resentment.","But there was rarely a way to have the best of both worlds. How could one obtain good things without also bearing the risks that came with them?","Thus, she took it all in stride.","“Come, brew me a cup of Biluochun to try. Then go to the kitchen and bring back two plates of pastries.” She gave the order with a beaming smile.","“Yes, Mistress!” Dongyi replied, her face lighting up with delight.","*","The moment Eunuch Zheng left, everyone in the courtyards of the rear quarters learned that the Crown Prince had bestowed more gifts upon Lady Shen.","The flowers and plants were one thing. What shocked everyone was the news that the Crown Prince had even given Lady Shen an entire set of lotus pink crystal jewelry!","Lady Chu’s delicate face darkened, and her expression turned ugly. “That was tribute from the South Seas, an exceptionally rare and precious treasure. His Highness actually gave it to Lady Shen just like that?”","She had once tactfully asked His Highness about it, yet he had refused to give it to her!","The palace maid beside her hurriedly sent the young eunuch who had delivered the news away, then lowered her voice and said, “Please don’t be angry, Mistress. The two matrons are still here.”","Lady Chu took several deep breaths before barely suppressing the resentment and jealousy in her heart. “Forget it. They’re only a few pieces of jewelry. They’re nothing important.”","At present, nothing mattered more than the child in her womb. Once she gave birth to a royal son, there would be plenty of time to settle accounts.","At Begonia Court—","Lady Wu directly smashed the fine celadon cup in her hand after hearing the news.","She said furiously, “That vixen! Who knows what kind of spell she cast on His Highness, or what sort of medicine she gave him!”","Ever since she was young, she had relied on her beautiful face. As long as she wanted something, things generally went smoothly for her.","Yet after entering the Eastern Palace, the beauty she had always taken pride in seemed to have lost its effect. Not only was there now a Lady Shen whose looks were in no way inferior to hers, but that woman also opposed her at every turn.","The Crown Prince was not as attentive and eager toward her as other men had been.","Yesterday, she had even made such a huge fool of herself in front of the Crown Prince!","After returning and looking in the mirror, she had only to remember that she had appeared before His Highness looking like that for her chest to tighten and her breathing to grow labored.","It was all that scheming vixen, Lady Shen’s, fault!","She said indignantly, “Why doesn’t Her Highness the Crown Princess discipline her?! If I were the Crown Princess, I would have dealt with that Lady Shen long ago!”","Her personal maid hurriedly tried to console her, but Lady Wu was clearly in no mood to listen. She continued complaining angrily, occasionally mixing in a few curses and insults.","Living in Begonia Court, Lady Lu, one of the Crown Prince’s long-serving women who occupied the eastern side hall, merely lifted her eyelids when she heard the commotion erupting once again from the main hall. She then continued staring at the begonia blossoms she was embroidering, her gaze gradually growing deeper and more inscrutable...","The palace maid serving beside her heard the disturbance as well. Frowning, she said in a low voice, “I never would have thought Lady Wu had such a temperament. The things we sent her before were probably wasted.”","They had originally planned on befriending the new Lady Wu, thinking that with her beauty, she ought to win the Crown Prince’s favor. If that happened, he would naturally visit Begonia Court more often, making it all the more worthwhile to establish a good relationship with Lady Wu.","But seeing Lady Wu’s disposition now, their plans were likely to come to nothing.","Lady Lu raised her eyes toward the vividly blooming begonias outside the window and said gently, “There’s no need to hurry. Let’s wait a little longer.”","News traveled even faster in Xiefang Hall than it did from the rear quarters. After all, there was no way to conceal the Crown Prince opening his private treasury, and the Crown Princess naturally had people and informants of her own stationed throughout the Eastern Palace.","Matron Zhou had just entered with a bowl of medicinal soup. Taking one look at the Crown Princess’s expression, she knew that Her Highness was in a poor mood.","“Your Highness, please don’t let anger and distress harm you. It’s only a set of jewelry. You must take care of your health.” Matron Zhou was somewhat helpless. The Crown Prince was the heir apparent; it was perfectly ordinary for him to bestow gifts upon his women.","It was simply that, in the past, the Crown Prince had rarely rewarded the women in the rear quarters. Whenever he did give them something, he would usually inform the Crown Princess first and have her present the gifts on his behalf.","The Crown Prince’s attitude should have made them even more vigilant.","Matron Zhou continued, “Your Highness, perhaps the Crown Prince is behaving this way because what happened last time caused him to harbor some resentment toward you. Once a few more days have passed and the Dragon Boat Festival is over, how could His Highness continue holding a grudge against you?” Her words carried an unmistakable implication.","The tension between the Crown Princess’s brows eased slightly, and she instinctively stroked her abdomen.","Matron Zhou went on persuading her. “Your Highness, at most, this is merely a passing novelty for the Crown Prince. Why not go along with his wishes? However you put it, she is no more than a concubine who serves through her beauty. At present, nothing is more important than your health.”","The Crown Princess pressed her lips together. “I understand.”","Although she had long grown accustomed to being “virtuous and accommodating,” that had only been because the Crown Prince had treated everyone more or less equally, without showing any special preference.","But now, she truly needed to win back the Crown Prince’s favor. She could not allow the rift between them to take root."]},{"number":18,"title":"Chapter 18: Sleep, sleep, I'm sleepy.","paragraphs":["Two more days passed. One day, just before the evening meal was served, a messenger was sent by the Crown Princess to invite the Crown Prince to share dinner with her at the Hall of Blossom Gathering.","Cui Yu lifted his head from the stacks of official documents, twisted his stiff neck, and glanced out the window at a sprig of blooming plum blossoms. As if suddenly remembering something, he tossed his brush into the brush holder, stood up, and said, \"Let us go.\"","\"His Imperial Highness the Crown Prince has arrived —\"","\"Greetings to Your Highness the Crown Prince —\" All the servants in the Hall of Blossom Gathering knelt to pay their respects.","The Crown Princess was dressed in a flowing pale purple robe with wide sleeves, her hair adorned with a peony pearl coronet and a golden peony-patterned step sway that glinted with every small movement. Noble, poised, and elegant, she had been waiting respectfully right at the entrance long before he arrived.","When she saw him walking toward her, tall and straight, she greeted him with a soft smile and a curtsy. Cui Yu lifted his hand in a slight gesture to help her rise, then withdrew his hand once she stood.","The two of them stepped into the main hall of the Hall of Blossom Gathering one after the other. Silence during meals and rest was a rule the Crown Princess had been taught to follow since childhood, so as long as Cui Yu did not speak, the dining table remained perfectly quiet, save for the occasional soft clink of chopsticks against bowls.","Cui Yu had a good appetite these days, so he ate heartily at first. But when he noticed that the Crown Princess had only taken two bites before putting down her utensils, her face looking slightly pale and unwell, his brows furrowed. \"Are you feeling unwell, Crown Princess?\"","Though he had been angry with her over an incident some time ago, in the days following his warning, the Crown Princess had conducted herself quite well. He assumed she had learned her lesson and repented of her mistakes.","After all, she was his Crown Princess, and he could not pretend not to notice her obvious discomfort.","Cui Yu asked, \"Has your disharmony of the spleen and stomach not healed yet? Have you summoned the imperial physician to examine you?\" He had noticed her taking medicine occasionally these past days, and had asked once before, which was why he inquired now.","The Crown Princess froze for a moment at his question, then set down her silver chopsticks, a faint, bitter ache rising in her eyes. \"To answer Your Highness, there is nothing serious wrong with my body. My cold is almost fully recovered. It is just that I indulged in too much tea and fruit at noon, so I am not very hungry now. You need not concern yourself with me, Your Highness. Let me attend to you as you eat.\"","Cui Yu glanced at her and said, \"There is no need. You may rest as you like.\"","Even so, the Crown Princess sat by his side, repeatedly placing choice morsels onto his plate, while she herself barely ate a few bites.","Cui Yu had been rather hungry when he arrived, but now his appetite was gone. He only finished one bowl of rice before setting down his chopsticks and bowl. The Crown Princess did not find this strange at all, assuming the Crown Prince must have eaten something else before coming to her hall.","Their conversation inevitably turned to their child, who was still too young, being held and nursed by his wet nurse. After confirming that the child was in good health, Cui Yu nodded in satisfaction. Though the little prince was still not as robust as ordinary children his age, with careful upbringing, he would surely grow stronger and healthier over time.","The Crown Princess chatted on for a while more about the child, before smiling and saying, \"By the way, Your Highness, the Dragon Boat Festival is three days from now. As per usual custom this year, we are to bring two of the younger consorts to the Golden Bright Pond. Have you decided on who the two will be? I was thinking that Lady Zhang —\"","\"Lady Shen shall go with you,\" Cui Yu cut in abruptly.","The Crown Princess's smile froze at the corners for a split second, before she regained her composure and laughed as if nothing was amiss. \"Your Highness is quite right. I had thought that since Lady Zhang holds the highest rank among the new consorts, we might bring her and Lady Chu along. But the Lady Shen you speak of, I have always found her to be a gentle, obedient soul. We shall bring her along as well.\"","Cui Yu nodded. \"She is simple and straightforward by nature. You must look after her well.\"","The Crown Princess's fingers curled tightly inward, her neatly trimmed nails digging deep into the soft flesh of her palms, yet her face remained wreathed in a gentle smile. \"Rest assured, Your Highness. I shall take good care of both of the younger sisters.\"","Cui Yu frowned slightly. \"Lady Chu is with child now. She ought not to go to such crowded, noisy places. Let her stay in the palace and rest peacefully to nurture her pregnancy.\"","The Crown Princess nodded and smiled in agreement, then added in a light, half-joking tone, \"It is just that for the past two years, Sister Chu has joined us every time. If she cannot come this time, I am afraid she will blame me for leaving her behind.\"","Cui Yu's eyes turned cool, his tone steady and unyielding. \"You are the Crown Princess. You hold the authority to assist in managing the affairs of the Eastern Palace. No one else has the right to question your decisions.\"","At his words, the Crown Princess's lips curved into a bright, pleased smile.","That same evening, the Crown Prince went to Lady Chu's quarters. Most of the servants who heard the news in the back suite could not help but feel a flicker of disappointment.","When the news reached the servants in Lotus Heart Courtyard, they exchanged glances with one another. Finally, Chunping stepped forward softly and said, \"Master, the Crown Prince has gone to Bright Moon Retreat.\" As she spoke, she stole a glance at her mistress, her eyes full of quiet worry.","Shen Yanshui lifted her gaze from the book she was reading, looking at Chunping's worried expression, and the rest of the maids who had suddenly become so cautious and tense. She could not help feeling a little amused. Did they really think she was so fragile?","If she could not accept such things, she might as well go off to a nunnery and become a nun. Otherwise, what was the point? Could she ever hope to find a man in this palace who would swear to be devoted only to her, to live a lifetime of perfect fidelity, and stay chaste for no one but her?","She herself could not even guarantee that she would only love one man for her entire life, let alone promise to remain chaste for a single man. No one could tell what the future might bring.","If that was the case, why waste her time pining after such impossible, unrealistic fantasies?","Seeing their anxious faces, she said, a little helplessly, \"What on earth are all of you looking so glum for?\"","Chunping saw that she did not look sad, lost, or angry at all, and felt a little sheepish. \"We were all worried that you would be in a bad mood...\"","Shen Yanshui could not help but ask curiously, \"Back when the Crown Prince visited other courtyards before, why were none of you so worried then?\"","Just looking at their faces, she could easily guess what they were thinking. They assumed that because the Crown Prince had treated her a little differently than the others, she had started to care for him more deeply, and so would grow more and more upset whenever he gave his attention to someone else.","\"Ah, never mind —\" She yawned, her voice soft and drowsy. \"Time for bed. I am sleepy.\""]},{"number":19,"title":"Chapter 19: Cui Yu: \"...glib-tongued.\"","paragraphs":["Shen Yanshui slept wonderfully, without a single dream, until dawn.","When Chunping, Xia’an, and the others attending her helped her rise, they saw her bare, unpowdered face glowing with health, its fair skin flushed with color. Smiles appeared on their faces as well.","While she was having breakfast, Shen Yanshui saw Dongyi hurrying in with a smile. She first offered her respects. “This servant greets Mistress.”","From Dongyi’s expression, Shen Yanshui could tell that she had learned some new news from outside. She asked, “What is it?”","Dongyi’s eyes shone brightly. “A moment ago, this servant heard from the little eunuch guarding Haoyue Residence that Lady Chu won’t be attending the Jinming Lake gathering for the Duanyang Festival this time. On my way back, I already saw quite a few of the young ladies heading to the Crown Princess’s residence.”","“Oh?” Shen Yanshui arched a brow. She was not surprised. Lady Chu did not seem like a foolish woman, and now that she appeared to be seven months pregnant, naturally she would put the child first.","Qiuyi, standing to the side, covered her lips and smiled. “With His Highness’s word, Mistress will certainly be able to go. There’s no need for her to rack her brains trying to curry favor with Her Highness the Crown Princess like the others.”","Dongyi lifted her chin and beamed. “Exactly. Our Mistress is the one His Highness favors.”","Chunping glanced at her, but she merely smiled without saying anything to dampen her spirits. She knew that Dongyi was quite composed in front of outsiders. It was only among their own people that she acted this way.","Not counting today, there were only two days left until the Duanyang Festival. But being able to accompany the Crown Prince and Crown Princess to the Jinming Lake gathering meant more than simply watching the festivities—it was also an excellent opportunity to make an appearance.","The Crown Princess would certainly be seated beside the Empress then, while the people of the Eastern Palace would naturally sit together with her.","If they could make themselves known before the Empress and win Her Majesty’s favor, His Highness the Crown Prince would presumably regard them with greater favor as well.","Not to mention that appearing at such an occasion would bring honor to their parents, sisters, and brothers back home. Their families would value them even more.","Therefore, during this period, while the list of those accompanying them had yet to be announced, everyone who wanted to go was using every means at their disposal.","Now that it had been confirmed Lady Chu would not be attending, their chances of going had clearly increased. Naturally, they became even more eager to curry favor.","Shen Yanshui merely treated it as a bit of gossip. After all, there had never been a shortage of people trying to ingratiate themselves with the Crown Prince and Crown Princess. Dongyi had said that the various residences had been sending the Crown Prince soups, snacks, and all sorts of food without pause.","At first, Chunping and the others had urged her to send something as well. She had indeed sent someone to inquire at the kitchen, but after learning how expensive it was to prepare food that would be served to the Crown Prince, she immediately abandoned the idea.","Besides, considering the Crown Prince’s appetite, he probably couldn’t finish everything anyway. What a waste...","*","It was nearing noon. The sky was clear from horizon to horizon, and the sun shone brightly.","“Godfather, Lady Wu from Haitang Court sent another soup just now. Should I take it in to His Highness?”","Zheng Yuande kicked him in the butt. “You’re foolish, and you truly live up to it. If His Highness had to eat everything people sent over, wouldn’t he be stuffed to death? Besides, you’ve been here for several days now. When have you ever seen His Highness touch any of this?”","Aside from the food the Crown Princess had sent in the past, which the Crown Prince would occasionally sample, he had never touched anything sent by the other women. After inadvertently drinking a bowl of deer-antler soup, His Highness had never again consumed any food sent by another woman.","That day, as was customary, when the Crown Prince finished handling official matters and left the study, she softly reported, “Your Highness, Qiefang Hall, Haitang Court, Zhuxiang Residence, and Lianxin Residence have all sent over soup, fruit, and pastries. Would Your Highness care to try some?”","If the Crown Princess had not sent something today, there would have been no need to ask. The food would simply have gone into his belly later.","“You can have it all.”","Cui Yu flicked his robe aside and tucked its hem into the leather belt around his waist. He was just about to practice his martial arts and loosen up in the courtyard when he suddenly glanced to the side and asked, “What did Lianxin Residence send?”","Zheng Yuande paused for a moment, then quickly understood. Smiling broadly, he reported, “In reply to Your Highness, Lianxin Residence sent a Chinese yam and goji berry soup. This servant has someone keeping it warm over a stove. Would Your Highness like to try it?”","Cui Yu nodded indifferently. “I’ll drink it later.”","After practicing as usual until a thin sheen of sweat covered him, he bathed and changed clothes. Zheng Yuande promptly brought him the soup at just the right temperature.","Cui Yu drank half a bowl and showed no intention of having another. But after meeting with several Eastern Palace officials to discuss matters, he glanced at the sky outside, rose, and ordered, “Go to Lianxin Residence.”","“Yes, Your Highness.”","Before Cui Yu had even stepped onto the corridor leading to the rear chambers, a little eunuch was already peering around near Moonlight Gate. From afar, he spotted the Crown Prince approaching. Delighted, the little eunuch hurried back toward Lianxin Residence.","He nearly collided with Quanshou upon entering.","Quanshou was startled and quickly tightened his hold on the things in his arms. These were grapevines and strawberry plants that Mistress had just obtained from the Directorate of Palace Servants!","“What are you running so fast for?” he asked with a frown.","This was Little Xing, an attendant who served Lady Liu. Usually, he was unfailingly respectful and eager to please the people in their eastern side hall. Why was he being so careless today?","Little Xing hurriedly apologized several times, but he did not even wait for Quanshou to say anything before quickly entering the western side hall.","Quanshou was not the sort to press his advantage. Seeing that Little Xing really was in a hurry, he did not hold it against him.","Dongyi happened to witness the scene. She had just begun to frown when, a moment later, the door opposite opened. Lady Liu emerged, elegantly and meticulously dressed, leaning on the arm of Yinping. Her expression even held a hint of excitement.","Dongyi was somewhat puzzled. It was already nearly time for the evening meal. Where was Lady Liu going at this hour?","She watched as Lady Liu slowly made her way toward the entrance, then scratched her forehead. Since she couldn’t figure it out, she decided not to think about it.","Just then, Quanshou suddenly ran over and said, “The Crown Prince is here!”","Dongyi had only just brightened at the news when she heard Eunuch Zheng’s voice beside the Crown Prince. But in the next instant, she saw Lady Liu nearly throw herself into the Crown Prince’s arms.","Dongyi immediately cursed inwardly: Cunning woman! So that was what Lady Liu had been planning.","“Your Highness?”","Lady Liu wore a light garment made from the fabric bestowed upon her by Her Majesty the Empress. Turning her most beautiful angle toward the Crown Prince, she spoke in a soft, delicate voice, feigning surprise and timidly saying, “This concubine has offended Your Highness. I beg Your Highness’s forgiveness.”","She could not contain her excitement.","Earlier that afternoon, she had learned from the eunuch she had recently spent a great deal of silver bribing that the Crown Prince had been the only one to drink the soup she sent. Ever since then, she had been quietly anticipating this moment.","That was why she had sent Little Xing, who served in her residence, to keep watch and find out what was happening. Even then, she had not been entirely certain that the Crown Prince was coming to Lianxin Residence.","His Highness had finally remembered her. He had truly come to see her at Lianxin Residence.","This time, she had to make him stay.","Cui Yu disliked strangers coming too close to him.","Glancing at the woman who had thrown herself straight into his arms, his voice turned icy cold. \"You have lost all sense of decorum. Tomorrow, the Crown Princess will send a senior palace maid to re-teach you the proper rules of conduct.\"","Lady Liu's face instantly drained of all color. Her slender frame swayed unsteadily, and the gaze she lifted to him was brimming with utter shame, fury, and disbelief.","Then, trembling all over and her face flushed bright red, she begged through tears, \"Your Highness, I know my wrongs now. I beg for Your Highness's mercy and forgiveness. I will never dare to do such a thing again!\"","Cui Yu's expression remained impassive, his voice even colder. \"Two months of confinement.\" With that, he turned on his heel and left, paying her no more heed.","\"Tha- thank you for Your Highness's mercy.\"","Zheng Yuande frowned and waved a hand in slight displeasure. Immediately, a pair of inner eunuchs stepped forward to lead the terrified, pale-faced Lady Liu, who had gone limp with shock, quickly into the side west hall. The entire Lotus Heart Garden fell silent at once.","Such a cheap little trick, and she dared to pull it in front of His Highness the Crown Prince? It was simply laughable. If that sort of thing ever worked, His Highness would never be able to walk a single step unimpeded. There would be hordes of fawning women throwing themselves into his arms every day.","Shen Yanshui had witnessed nearly the entire scene from start to finish, but the situation was clearly not one where it was appropriate for her to step forward. So she had stayed right where she was by the doorway, holding her respectful bow the whole time. After all, she had just seen the consequences play out right in front of her.","From what she had observed of the Crown Prince over the past while, she suspected Lady Liu had deliberately orchestrated the whole incident. If it had truly been an accident, he would never have punished her so severely.","Cui Yu climbed the stone steps, and when he saw Shen Yanshui still half-crouching there, holding her respectful greeting to him perfectly and unwaveringly, the slight displeasure he had been feeling softened into helpless amusement. He chuckled to himself, what a truly earnest, no-nonsense girl she was.","He lifted his hand to give her arm a light, supporting gesture to help her rise, but just as he was about to pull his hand back, his palm was gently wrapped by a soft little hand. His movement froze right there.","Shen Yanshui stood up naturally following the light pressure from his hand, and did not let go of him. She thought his hand was very nice to look at, and she loved the feeling of holding it.","The Crown Prince's hand was large, dry and firm, with long, well-defined knuckles. It was a strikingly handsome hand, the sort you would expect to see on a refined scholar, yet the palm bore a faint layer of calluses, and it always carried a subtle, pleasant scent of ink.","\"Your Highness has such a beautiful hand,\" she said to him with a sincere bright smile, as she met his downward gaze.","Cui Yu: \"... You are such a smooth talker.\" Even so, he did not pull his hand away.","Shen Yanshui murmured quietly under her breath, \"That's not being smooth-tongued, that's giving a sweet compliment.\" She did not believe there was anyone in the world who did not enjoy being praised.","Cui Yu glanced at her, his tone light as he said, \"Silver-tongued, that's what you are.\"","Shen Yanshui: ... She studied his expression carefully, and once she was certain he was in a good mood, she could not help but feel a little amused. She had never expected this man, who always looked so dignified and cold on the outside, to have a little tsundere side to him."]},{"number":20,"title":"Chapter 20: Simply... absurd, absurd","paragraphs":["Shen Yanshui promptly changed the subject. Blinking, she asked with a smile, “Your Highness, are you hungry? Shall I have the servants bring in the meal?”","It wasn’t that Shen Yanshui had nothing else to say to the Crown Prince. First, she truly didn’t know him well enough to think of any profound topics. Second, she was feeling a little hungry herself—and he came by right around mealtimes every time. Wasn’t that a clear sign that he wanted to eat here?","So she felt there was nothing wrong with her question at all.","Wasn’t she simply showing concern for his well-being?","Cui Yu gave a slight nod. “Have the meal brought in.”","As usual, the table was laden with an array of exquisite dishes: meat, vegetables, soup, cold dishes, and fruit. As expected, Cui Yu ended up feeling a little overfull.","Looking at the goji berries floating in the chicken soup before him, he suddenly remembered something and said, “Don’t send me Chinese yam and goji berry soup next time.”","Seeing her look up from her bowl in apparent surprise, he fell silent for a moment. Realizing that his words might have been misunderstood, he added, “If you truly wish to send something, send fruit or the like instead.”","He simply wasn’t very fond of soups and other such watery dishes.","Shen Yanshui: “...”","But she had never sent him any soup at all, had she?","Could he have mistaken a soup sent by someone else for one from her?","She said nothing, but Cui Yu narrowed his eyes slightly at her expression. His voice immediately turned as cold as a gust of winter wind.","“That soup wasn’t sent by you?”","Shen Yanshui didn’t think there was anything wrong with not having sent him soup. After all, she wasn’t the only one who hadn’t sent him any. But still... being caught in such a misunderstanding made her feel inexplicably embarrassed—and a little uneasy.","She even began to wonder whether Lady Liu’s unusually bold actions earlier that day might have something to do with this...","Zheng Yuande’s heart gave a lurch. This was bad!","Who had sent the soup had originally been unimportant. But after the Crown Prince assumed it was from Lady Shen and even told her his preferences, learning that it had not been sent by her meant that the Crown Prince had just embarrassed himself, didn’t it?","Just as he was thinking this, a sharp, icy glance fell upon him. Zheng Yuande was instantly close to tears. His knees went weak, and he was about to plead guilty.","But at that moment, Shen Yanshui suddenly put on an astonished expression and said, “So Your Highness likes fruit? I know of a novel and delicious pastry. I’ll make some myself tomorrow and have someone deliver it to Your Highness for you to try. Would that be all right?”","Cui Yu: “...”","He had felt a faint trace of embarrassment and displeasure earlier, but it could hardly be called anger. More than anything, he felt that his last two remarks had made him look rather foolish.","It was all Zheng Yuande’s fault. The fool couldn’t even explain two simple sentences clearly!","Now that she had offered him a way out, he naturally took it, no longer pressing the matter.","“Mm,” he replied coolly.","Seeing this, Shen Yanshui quietly let out a sigh of relief.","The Crown Prince didn’t seem so difficult to placate after all.","After taking a walk to aid digestion, bathing, and changing clothes, the others withdrew. By then, the faint embarrassment Cui Yu had felt earlier had almost completely faded.","But as the two of them became entangled, he suddenly found himself inexplicably dissatisfied. Clasping her slender, supple waist, he thrust her hips forward with a sharp, forceful motion. Hearing the abrupt change in her voice, he asked hoarsely, “If tomorrow’s fruit doesn’t suit my tastes, what do you intend to do?”","A faint sheen of sweat dampened Shen Yanshui’s temples. Looking into his dark, heavy gaze, she couldn’t help taking a deep breath.","Honestly, why was this man still thinking about that? It was only a bowl of soup, wasn’t it? How could he possibly remember it even at a time like this? Was he looking down on her?","As Shen Yanshui watched the little bean swaying before her eyes, she immediately opened her mouth...","Cui Yu suddenly froze. His body shuddered, then tensed all at once, his sharp eyes growing even wider. “You... How dare you!” he scolded in a low, restrained voice.","The corners of Shen Yanshui’s eyes lifted slightly. His body certainly wasn’t saying the same thing.","And he still had the nerve to call her outrageous.","Was this outrageous? She hadn’t even begun to show him what outrageous really meant.","She decided to let him see for himself.","It was the middle of the night. The wind outside carried a faint chill, but the temperature inside the eastern side chamber of Lianxin Court continued to rise.","Shen Yanshui not only refused to stop, but also made him truly experience what it meant to have a silver tongue and a sharp wit.","Taking advantage of the moment when his self-control faltered, she quietly exerted a little force and, pressed against his taut body, turned and climbed on top.","Cui Yu’s abdomen jolted violently.","He was so shocked that he even forgot to scold her.","This... this was simply too absurd!","Yet when Shen Yanshui saw the astonishment in his eyes, she couldn’t help wanting to laugh.","But she absolutely couldn’t laugh aloud now. Otherwise, this man would surely become embarrassed and furious, and then she would have taken things too far.","Compared with his stubborn mouth, his body was far more honest.","After all, if he truly hadn’t wanted it, she couldn’t have so easily turned them into another position.","Besides, if one was going to work overtime at night, wouldn’t adding a little variety make it even more enjoyable?","It was an experience that stretched him more than any before, and the visual stimulation was something he had never encountered. As a result, Cui Yu surrendered faster than he ever had.","In an instant, his handsome face darkened, then flushed, then darkened again.","Shen Yanshui: “...”","Though she was only momentarily stunned, Cui Yu still noticed.","The next moment, Shen Yanshui felt the world spin before her eyes. She was flipped completely over, ending up on her knees with her back to him...","There was an indescribable eagerness in Shen Yanshui’s heart, but she couldn’t see the dark, somber, turbulent look in Cui Yu’s eyes.","It wasn’t long before she discovered that beneath the refined, gentle exterior this man wore, he was actually more like a ferocious beast...","A man’s pride was truly terrifying.","Cui Yu had never before been so... utterly unrestrained.","Shen Yanshui cried out in bliss. “Wuwuwu... Your Highness... wuwuwu...”","Cui Yu: “...”","He had never seen a woman cry like that in front of him.","When Shen Yanshui noticed the faint look of disdain in his eyes, anger instantly surged through her. Wrapping her arms around his waist, she rubbed her entire tear-dampened face against him!","Cui Yu’s body went rigid in an instant, and his expression changed completely.","Forget it. His body certainly wasn’t lacking for this little bit of her tears now.","“I see you’ve truly grown bold enough to eat the heart of a bear and the gall of a leopard.” Cui Yu reached over from beside her and tugged free a rouge-red undergarment, wiping her face with it somewhat disdainfully.","Shen Yanshui: “...”","Was he deliberately taking revenge on her? It felt as though he had rubbed her skin raw.","Hearing her call out in a soft, slightly hoarse voice that it hurt, Cui Yu paused. He immediately lightened his touch, though his tone remained cold and disdainful. “So delicate.”","With that, he casually tossed aside the small piece of rouge-red fabric in his hand.","Shen Yanshui muttered under her breath, “Has Your Highness never heard that women are made of water? The skin on my face is delicate and tender. How could I possibly compare with rough-skinned, thick-fleshed men like you?”","Cui Yu lifted his eyelids and gave her a sidelong glance, then looked over the disarray covering the bed. She truly was made of water—just the slightest touch, and water came spilling out...","He said nothing, yet Shen Yanshui somehow understood exactly what his gaze meant.","She glanced at the messy bedding, which was frankly too embarrassing to look at, and immediately gritted her teeth as she scrambled off him. “Your Highness had a hand in this too!”","Without even having time to put on her shoes, she ran as quickly as her weakened legs could carry her toward the bathing room, eager to save herself.","As she passed the clothes rack, she did not forget to snatch up one of his outer robes and wrap it around herself, calling for water as she went.","Cui Yu: “...”"]},{"number":21,"title":"Chapter 21: Disposition","paragraphs":["Above the horizon, rosy clouds billowed and surged. Pale golden morning light broke through the layers of cloud, pouring down over the Great Yong imperial palace and enveloping it in a dazzling radiance.","All around the palace, the various residences had long since begun their new day. The courtyards of the Eastern Palace were likewise filled with their own stirrings, but Lotusheart Court remained steeped in silence.","The doors of the western side hall were shut tight, and its occupants had been confined within. The servants attending them had therefore grown even quieter and more cautious.","Chunping could not help glancing at the sky. It was almost past the time for breakfast, yet there was still no sign that the Crown Prince or her mistress intended to rise. She turned to look at Eunuch Zheng, who wore an utterly composed, unruffled expression.","She respectfully asked, “Eunuch Zheng, it’s almost past the time for breakfast. What do you think...?”","Zheng Yuande continued to maintain his calm expression. “Just wait.”","Last night, the Crown Prince and this young mistress had carried on until well into the night. He had already lost count of how many times they had shocked him.","Dark circles had formed beneath his eyes. Since His Highness had not rested, naturally he could not rest either.","And today was a day off from court... If there was still no movement after another quarter of an hour, they truly could not delay any longer. They could not let it upset His Highness’s stomach, after all.","Seeing that he was not in a hurry, Chunping felt reassured as well.","Shen Yanshui had actually been awake for a little while. Her body was soft and languid, however, and she did not feel like moving in the slightest, so she continued lying there with her eyes closed. But after a while, she gradually began to feel hungry...","Cui Yu had also awakened early. Yet for some reason, holding the person in his arms, he found himself unusually reluctant to rise as he normally did. Thinking of the previous night, he felt they had indulged themselves a little too much. In the future, he absolutely could not let things go so far again.","But since it had already happened, there was no need to get up just yet. Thus, he went back to sleep for a while.","When he awoke again, he heard someone calling out beside his ear with a trace of deep grievance, as though summoning his soul.","“Your Highness? Your Highness? Time to get up~”","Shen Yanshui tilted her head slightly and leaned close to his ear, calling to him in a soft voice.","When he finally lifted his eyelids, Shen Yanshui immediately looked at him with a radiant smile.","Thus, the first thing Cui Yu saw upon opening his eyes was her exceptionally bright and dazzling face.","Then, the next moment, a somewhat muffled “Gurgle~ gurgle~” came from beneath the covers.","Cui Yu: “...”","Meeting his gaze, Shen Yanshui said in a perfectly justified little voice, “Last night left me completely exhausted. Aren’t you tired too, Your Highness?”","She possessed an ability, and even she had ended up like this. She refused to believe he was not tired at all. After all, he had been the one to expend more effort.","“Not tired.” Cui Yu’s tone was calm and utterly certain.","Shen Yanshui: “...”","Hah. Men. Even if the sky fell, they would still prop it up with their mouths.","With a sweet smile, she said gently, “I know Your Highness is vigorous and strong, with a robust constitution. Of course you wouldn’t be tired. But it should be nearly the Hour of the Dragon by now. It’s time to get up and eat.”","Cui Yu gave a faint hum.","Seeing this, Shen Yanshui immediately smiled and pulled the bell beside the bed.","Outside, Zheng Yuande had just been making preparations to enter and wake them. When he heard the movement inside, he immediately waved his hand. A procession of eunuchs and palace maids entered the room, carrying the things prepared for washing up.","The two of them each had servants attend to them as they dressed and washed. They were soon properly groomed, and after eating breakfast together, Cui Yu prepared to leave.","Just before departing, however, he suddenly turned his head toward her. Seeing the confusion in her clear eyes, he instructed her in a deep voice, “You will be going to Golden Bright Pool early the day after tomorrow. You must behave yourself that day and be obedient. Do not act recklessly again.”","Shen Yanshui’s eyes gleamed as she looked at him, her smile warm and radiant. “Yes. Thank you, Your Highness!”","Only after Cui Yu had left and she could no longer see him did Shen Yanshui rise and return to her room.","Chunping brought over a cup of warm tea and could not help smiling happily. Although the Crown Prince had previously asked whether her mistress wished to go watch the Dragon Boat Festival festivities at Golden Bright Pool, it had not been set in stone. Only now that the Crown Prince had spoken of it directly could it be considered certain.","It was just that the Crown Prince’s final words before leaving had been rather strange.","Although their mistress seemed somewhat bold in front of the Crown Prince, she was still very proper before the Crown Princess. She had never liked causing trouble, either. As for acting recklessly—her mistress did not seem to have done anything particularly outrageous, did she?","As she was thinking this, Xia’an asked in confusion, “Mistress, what did the Crown Prince mean by those last words?”","The Crown Prince had seemed to be in a good mood during the meal, yet there had been something inexplicably frightening about his tone when he left.","Shen Yanshui smiled but did not answer at once.","On the surface, it sounded as though he was telling her not to be too bold and cause trouble.","But in reality, was the Crown Prince also hinting—or warning her—to keep to her proper place and not get involved with Noble Consort Lan and the others?","Whatever. It was not worth worrying over.","She gave a light laugh and said, “Don’t let your imaginations run wild. Perhaps the Crown Prince simply saw that this is my first time attending such a royal banquet and was worried that I might accidentally cause trouble, so he offered a reminder. As long as we behave honestly and properly, then even if something does happen, it will have nothing to do with us.”","*","Zheng Yuande spent the entire journey back to the Hall of Eternal Celebration with his heart in his throat. The instant he returned and saw His Highness sit down, he dropped to his knees to beg forgiveness. His round, pale, plump cheeks trembled like steamed buns.","With a sob in his voice, he said, “Your Highness, this servant knows he was wrong. Please punish me.”","Cui Yu gave him an expressionless, cold glance. Seeing the dark circles beneath his eyes, he let out a cold snort.","“This time, I will let it pass. But if there is a next time...”","Zheng Yuande immediately took the hint and thanked him. “Thank you, Your Highness! Rest assured, there definitely will not be another time. If there is, this servant will go and receive thirty strokes of the cane!”","Cui Yu’s expression remained calm. “Go and find out who gave Lady Liu the information.”","Zheng Yuande’s heart instantly tightened. He no longer dared to act pitiful or curry favor before his master, and immediately went out to begin the investigation.","He already had a few suspects in mind.","The Eastern Palace appeared relaxed on the surface, but was tightly controlled underneath. He knew exactly what sort of people worked in the Hall of Eternal Celebration.","Since His Highness had never issued any special instructions before, and those few people had behaved well enough, he had not dealt with them. He had never expected that one of them would nearly trip him up!","Zheng Yuande’s heart hardened.","It did not take long before he returned, bent at the waist and treading lightly. Entering the study, he reported cautiously, “Your Highness, this servant has found the culprit. It was one of the Crown Princess’s people. This servant... does not know how she should be dealt with.”","At his words, Cui Yu showed no surprise. Although he had already suspected as much, his expression was still far from pleasant, and his voice turned even colder.","“Was it ordered by the Crown Princess?”","Zheng Yuande’s body trembled. He replied carefully, “It should not have been. The servant confessed everything just now. It was because she had become lovers with one of the palace maids serving in the Crown Princess’s residence and was short of money. In a moment of foolish greed, she accepted money from the Lady and passed along the information in advance.”","What His Highness ate and used—how could such things be casually revealed to outsiders?","Cui Yu’s expression softened somewhat, and he said calmly, “Deal with her according to palace regulations.”","Eunuch Zheng hurriedly acknowledged the order. “Yes, Your Highness.”","“Also, Lady Liu is to be confined to her quarters for half a year.”","Eunuch Zheng respectfully accepted the order, though inwardly he couldn’t help thinking, Serves her right!","Considering that Lady Liu had dared to bribe one of the servants attending the Crown Prince, her punishment was anything but undeserved."]},{"number":22,"title":"Chapter 22: Milk Tea Egg Tarts","paragraphs":["In Lotus Heart Court, Shen Yanshui had just finished a set of Baduanjin exercises and cultivated for a while longer when she saw a lovely little parrot, bright green all over with a spot of orange-yellow on its forehead, flying toward her with obvious familiarity.","“Great beauty! Great beauty!”","Shen Yanshui held out a finger to tease it. “Such a sweet-talker, aren’t you? How come your master didn’t learn even a fraction of your way with words?”","Little Jade pecked lightly at her fingertip with its sharp beak. “Great beauty! Great beauty! This young master is hungry, hungry! Give me something to eat, something to eat!”","Shen Yanshui tapped its little head, then plucked two roses from the vines along the courtyard wall and infused them with a trace of her ability. “Here.”","But she had other things to do today, so she could not spend all her time playing with the bird.","“Come on. Let’s take a look at the main kitchen.”","The Eastern Palace kitchens were not located in Changqing Palace, but in a palace compound next door, separated only by a wall. They were large, spacious, and immaculate—her first impression at a glance.","A plump chief eunuch, round and smiling like the Maitreya Buddha, hurried over. Dressed in the neat uniform of a chief palace attendant, he beamed when he saw mistress and servant at the door.","“Oh my, this must be Lady Shen? This servant greets Lady Shen and pays his respects.”","Shen Yanshui smiled and replied politely, “Chief Steward Tang, there is no need for such ceremony. Please rise. I’ll be troubling you today.”","Chief Steward Tang’s face split into an even broader smile. “Lady Shen wishes to make some pastries for His Highness the Crown Prince. All you needed to do was send word and instruct us. Why come personally to a grimy place like the kitchen? What if your clothes or shoes should be soiled?”","Smiling, Shen Yanshui said, “From what I can see, the kitchen is managed by Chief Steward Tang in excellent order. It is very clean and tidy indeed. I only wonder whether I might hold up the kitchen’s work?”","Her words pleased Chief Steward Tang greatly. With a genial smile, he waved a broad hand. “What are you saying, Lady Shen? It’s only a matter of freeing up one stove. I’ll send two people to assist you and follow your instructions. Would that be acceptable?”","Shen Yanshui thanked him with genuine warmth. “That will be more than enough. Thank you for your trouble, Chief Steward Tang.”","Chief Steward Tang chuckled. “Lady Shen is far too polite.” With that, he immediately ordered two of his apprentices to go and help her.","Shen Yanshui had deliberately worn a short-sleeved, close-fitting top today, making it convenient to work in.","She planned to make egg tarts and milk tea.","In her previous life, she had loved milk tea, egg tarts, and all kinds of small cakes. She had even watched many online tutorials and learned to make them herself.","She had not had any in a very long time. Once the kitchen staff learned how to make them, she would be able to enjoy milk tea and egg tarts whenever she wished!","The most important parts of an egg tart were the custard filling and the flaky puff-pastry shell. The Eastern Palace kitchen had everything needed for both.","Anything they lacked could be made by hand. For molds, she used flower-shaped ones supplied by the kitchen. They were only half the size of modern egg tarts, and looked quite lovely.","As for the final baking, she had previously eaten the baked pastries from the kitchens and asked Dongyi about them. Learning that the Eastern Palace kitchens had an oven capable of baking egg tarts, she had decided to make these.","Otherwise, she could hardly ask the Eastern Palace kitchens to build a usable oven in a single day just so she could bake a few egg tarts, could she?","She began working in the kitchen with calm, orderly efficiency.","At first, the other kitchen staff had been rather restrained, but seeing that Lady Shen seemed even more at ease than they were, they gradually relaxed as well.","This was a relatively quiet time in the Eastern Palace kitchens. Most of the staff had been temporarily sent to the Imperial Kitchen to wrap rice dumplings, and over the past two days, the Eastern Palace kitchens had become much less crowded.","Quite a few people watched in secret, curious.","Chief Steward Tang was curious too. Early that morning, Quanfu from Lotus Heart Court had come to tell him that Lady Shen wished to borrow the kitchen’s oven. Naturally, he had no reason to refuse.","After all, Lady Shen currently held a certain degree of favor with His Highness the Crown Prince.","Had no one noticed that when Lady Shen’s allotted meals proved insufficient, the extra portions were taken from the Crown Prince’s own allowance? Though the Crown Prince had not permitted the matter to be publicized, and few people knew of it.","That fact alone was enough for him to wait upon this young mistress with the utmost care.","Still, he did not hold much hope that Lady Shen could make pastries that were truly delicious. He had even secretly instructed someone to prepare a portion of pastries that the Crown Prince particularly liked. Should they be needed later, it would make for a useful favor, would it not?","Shen Yanshui had no idea that someone had quietly arranged such a safeguard for her. Seeing that the two young eunuchs assigned to assist her neither watched closely to see how she worked nor did anything beyond what she instructed, she quickly understood why.","In these times, every household guarded its recipes and secret techniques closely. They likely thought she was making a Shen family specialty and thus did not dare watch too openly, lest she accuse them of trying to steal her craft.","Shen Yanshui turned and instructed them, “Remember how this is made. That way, you can make it for me in the future.”","The two young eunuchs froze.","Though they were nominally apprentices to the kitchen masters, those masters had many apprentices, and the two of them had not yet earned the qualifications to prepare food or pastries for noble masters. But now Lady Shen was going to teach them how to make pastries?","Their expressions shifted between shock and delight, though they could not help wondering whether they had misheard.","Yet in the next moment, Lady Shen began explaining the process to them, holding nothing back...","The pair immediately perked up and listened with rapt attention.","Seeing this, the others could not help pricking up their ears as well.","After Shen Yanshui finished explaining how to make egg tarts, she continued, “This is the tea I brought. Steep it in boiling water, then strain out the leaves, keeping only the rich, concentrated tea. Start another pot and pour in fresh milk. Simmer it slowly over low heat—do not let it boil over. Once tiny bubbles begin to form around the edges, remove it from the heat. Slowly pour the brewed tea into the milk, stirring as you pour, so that the tea and milk blend together.”","“...Add a little honey or condensed milk to adjust the sweetness, allowing it to balance the fragrance of the milk and tea... Once it is done, strain it once more through fine gauze...”","“Next, take the finest tapioca flour and scald it with boiling water. Knead it into a firm, smooth dough, then pinch it into tiny pearls no bigger than a fingertip.”","“Boil them until they turn translucent throughout and have a pleasing chew. Scoop them out and rinse them once in cool water, then toss lightly with honey to keep them from sticking together. They must be chewy yet tender—neither undercooked nor overboiled.”","“...Choose taro with a soft, floury texture. Peel it and cut it into thick slices, then steam them until they collapse at the slightest poke. Take them out and let them cool slightly before pressing them into a fine, smooth paste with the back of a spoon. There must not be the slightest impurity. Mix in a little milk and honey, stirring until it is dense and velvety, melting on the tongue without a single lump...”","Some listened with rapt attention, but others were unimpressed and found Lady Shen’s ostentatious behavior rather hard to stomach.","Fan Chuan was one of those who looked down on Lady Shen most of all.","He was one of the Crown Princess’s people. His position alone set him apart from the lesser ladies who lived in the rear quarters, and he held himself in high regard. In the kitchens of the Eastern Palace, apart from Tang Hai—that damned fat man—who could faintly overshadow him, he feared no one.","Fan Chuan frowned and curled his lip disdainfully, deeply displeased by Lady Shen’s actions.","Was she not merely relying on the few favors the Crown Prince had bestowed upon her to behave this way?","If every woman who gained a measure of the Crown Prince’s favor acted like her—using the excuse of preparing food for His Highness to come and go from the Eastern Palace kitchens whenever she pleased—would that not utterly ruin the rules?","And if something were to happen to the food intended for the Crown Prince or the Crown Princess, who would bear the responsibility?","That damned fat man Tang Hai was so eager to bow and scrape, yet he could not even tell whom he ought to curry favor with. How laughable.","But then... his eyes shifted, and an idea came to him. He untied the apron at his waist, gave his apprentice a few quiet instructions, and, while no one was paying attention, slipped out of the Eastern Palace kitchens and headed in the direction of Xiefang Hall."]},{"number":23,"title":"Chapter 23: An inexplicable discomfort in my heart","paragraphs":["The Crown Princess was dressed in a dark-purple long robe with wide sleeves, embroidered with peonies and gold scrolling vines, and crowned with a gold-inlaid red-jade peony headdress. At that moment, she sat upright and meticulously composed in a rosewood chair, watching the person standing in the middle of the hall. Her brows drew together slightly.","“Is what you said true?”","Fan Chuan bowed deeply and answered respectfully, “In response to Your Highness, even if this servant had a hundred times the courage, he would never dare deceive you. The Eastern Palace kitchens are in quite an uproar at the moment. Your Highness need only send someone over to investigate and you’ll know.”","“That Lady Shen is, at any rate, the daughter of an official household. How could she truly know how to cook? Isn’t she merely putting on an act to vie for His Highness’s favor? Who knows what a mess she’s made of the kitchens by now.”","At this, the Crown Princess’s brows knitted even more tightly. Though her expression was displeased, she did not speak immediately. She merely waved for Fan Chuan to leave.","Fan Chuan was puzzled, but he did not dare question his mistress’s decision. As he departed, he felt the purse Hongling had given him tucked inside his sleeve. One squeeze of his fingers told him roughly how much it contained, and a satisfied smile spread across his face.","This trip had certainly been worth it!","The Crown Princess’s expression remained displeased. “Whenever Lady Shen comes to pay her respects, she appears obedient enough and never takes the initiative to cause trouble. But she has never been the sort to suffer a loss in silence. It hasn’t even been a month, yet His Highness has already spoiled her into becoming increasingly presumptuous.”","Matron Zhou frowned beside her. “Your Highness is right. Lady Shen is likely hiding wickedness beneath that obedient exterior.”","“Lady Wu may appear ostentatious in her daily conduct, but she has never once managed to show off in front of Lady Shen. On the contrary, she has suffered no small losses at Lady Shen’s hands every time.”","“It seems we were all deceived by her meek and deferential appearance and mistook her for someone docile.”","“Now that she has revealed her true colors, she is no longer anything to fear.” After all, the favored Lady Shen in the palace was her elder sister by birth, and she had always been a thorn in the Crown Prince’s heart.","“If she truly becomes more and more presumptuous now that she has His Highness’s favor, then given His Highness’s temperament, he will soon grow tired of her,” Matron Zhou continued, suddenly lowering her voice. “Moreover, during the Dragon Boat Festival gathering at Golden Bright Lake the day after tomorrow, as long as she and Lady Shen speak privately for a few more words...”","What would the Crown Prince think then?","A flicker passed through the Crown Princess’s eyes.","*","It was noon, and the sky was clear and blue beneath the blazing sun.","Zheng Yuande carefully carried a purplewood, black-lacquered, mother-of-pearl-inlaid, eight-sided box decorated with flowers and birds. He stepped forward and bowed slightly as he reported in a quiet voice, “Your Highness, these are the pastries and drink Lady Shen has just delivered herself. She said that Your Highness must taste the pastries while they’re still warm, as they won’t be as delicious once they cool. This servant didn’t dare delay. Please take a look...”","Under ordinary circumstances, while the Crown Prince was handling official business, Zheng Yuande would never dare interrupt him with food sent by one of the lesser ladies living in the rear quarters. But today, Lady Shen’s matter was clearly different from usual.","After all, he had also been at fault for yesterday’s incident. Naturally, he ought to lend her a hand now.","Cui Yu raised his head from the documents and instinctively pressed his fingers to his brow.","With a smile, Zheng Yuande said, “Your Highness, these pastries and this drink were made personally by Lady Shen using ingredients borrowed from the Eastern Palace kitchens. It’s clear she put great thought into them.”","Cui Yu lifted a brow at that. “Made personally by her?”","Zheng Yuande’s smile instantly widened. He hurriedly affirmed it, then placed the box on a nearby table. He opened the container holding the still-steaming golden pastries, and a rich, enticing fragrance of eggs and milk filled the room.","“Your Highness, please have a taste.”","Cui Yu looked at the golden pastries and picked one up. After taking a bite, his brows rose slightly.","Zheng Yuande watched him nervously. Although he had already tested the food himself, he had no idea whether it would suit His Highness’s taste...","Just as he was thinking this, he saw the Crown Prince eat another, and then a third before finally stopping.","Zheng Yuande immediately put on a broad smile and promptly offered him a clean towel that had just been rinsed.","Cui Yu accepted it and slowly, unhurriedly wiped his fingertips. His tone was indifferent.","“Acceptable.”","Zheng Yuande was even more delighted. Lady Shen truly knew how to please His Highness. Not only had she made something fresh, but His Highness clearly enjoyed it as well.","Cui Yu then glanced at the sweet white porcelain jug nearby. Zheng Yuande quickly poured the Crown Prince a cup, then opened two small porcelain containers and said with a beaming smile, “Your Highness, Lady Shen said this drink is called milk tea. She made it using the tea leaves Your Highness bestowed upon her. She specifically instructed this servant to have Your Highness taste it first and see whether the sweetness is suitable. If it seems too bland, Your Highness may add some of the tapioca pearls and taro paste.”","Cui Yu took a sip. It was smooth and velvety as soon as it entered his mouth, sliding gently down his throat. It was neither bitter nor overly rich, leaving only the full fragrance of milk and tea. The sweetness was just right—sweet without being cloying, mellow and gentle.","He scooped a spoonful each of the tapioca pearls and taro paste into the cup.","The pearls were springy and chewy, carrying a faint sweetness. Mixed with the dense, soft taro paste, they were powdery, sticky, and delicate, melting in his mouth.","By the time he came back to himself, more than half the jug of milk tea had already been emptied.","Only then did he slowly set it down. Suddenly remembering something, he asked in a casual tone, “What sort of food did she send before?”","Yesterday’s incident had merely been an accidental misunderstanding that had cost him a little face. He was not so petty as to hold a grudge over it.","He had never cared about what food any woman sent him. But now that he knew she had been so sincere, he suddenly thought it a pity that the pastries she had made herself, piece by piece, had likely all ended up in Zheng Yuande’s stomach.","“Ah?”","Zheng Yuande froze. He had not expected His Highness to suddenly ask such a question—and it was truly rather difficult to answer...","Cui Yu’s voice deepened. “What is it? Did all the food go into your head instead?”","Zheng Yuande’s plump, fair body trembled in fright. Seeing that His Highness was still staring at him with furrowed brows, he replied awkwardly, “In response to Your Highness, Lady Shen... she... she has never sent any food before.”","After saying this, he wished he could bury his head in his chest. He did not dare look at His Highness’s expression at all.","The study instantly fell so silent that one could hear a pin drop.","Zheng Yuande felt the pressure around the Crown Prince growing heavier and heavier. His legs suddenly went weak, and he dropped to his knees.","After a long moment, Cui Yu cast him a glance and asked in his usual calm voice, “Why are you kneeling?”","Zheng Yuande cautiously raised his head. “...Your Highness?”","That was it? He was no longer angry?","Cui Yu raised a brow. “Do you wish to kneel?”","Seeing his expression and demeanor, Zheng Yuande’s heart immediately relaxed. He scrambled to his feet and hurriedly thanked His Highness.","Still, he remained deeply puzzled inside. His Highness’s moods seemed to be changing faster and faster lately...","Cui Yu noticed the confusion in his eyes but had no intention of explaining.","At first, he had naturally felt uncomfortable upon hearing the answer. Though he did not know where that inexplicable discomfort had come from, he had not thought deeply about it.","Then he suddenly remembered that, in the past, even Lady Shen’s regular allowance had not been enough to feed her. She had needed to spend additional money every day just to supplement it and eat her fill. She was only a concubine-born daughter of her family, so even if she had some private savings, she could not possibly have had much.","Moreover, she was straightforward and sincere by nature. It was only natural that she had not thought of currying favor in this way.","Over the past month or so, of the four newcomers, she alone had done nothing unnecessary. She had never secretly spent money to curry favor with people and make inquiries about the Eastern Palace, nor had she sent anyone to find out about his whereabouts or preferences. Every day, she simply lived her own quiet little life, keeping well within the rules.","That was good.","He turned his gaze toward the sky outside, set aside the documents before him for the time being, and rose to his feet. “Let’s go to Lianxin Court.”","Zheng Yuande hurriedly acknowledged the order, but inwardly grew even more puzzled. Unable to help himself, he scratched the back of his head. Why did he feel that he was becoming less and less able to fathom the Crown Prince’s thoughts?"]},{"number":24,"title":"Chapter 24: So soft and gentle, as if acting cute","paragraphs":["After Shen Yanshui returned to Lotus Heart Court, she had Dongyi distribute the little egg tarts she had specially brought back among Chunping, Quanfu, and the others. She had already eaten in the kitchen, so she kept a cup of milk tea with tapioca pearls and taro paste to drink later.","Looking at the golden pastries and breathing in their sweet, tempting fragrance, everyone smiled and bowed in unison.","“Thank you for the reward, Mistress.”","They were still on duty, however, and none of them were ignorant of proper etiquette. Naturally, they would wait until they took turns going off duty before eating in their own rooms, or warm the tarts in the tea room first.","At ​​‌‌​‌‌​​‌‌​​​​‌​‌‌​​​‌‌​​‌‌‌​​​​‌‌​​​‌‌​​‌‌‌​​​​‌‌​​‌​‌​‌‌​​​‌​​​‌‌​‌​​​‌‌​​​​‌​‌‌​​​‌​​​‌‌‌​​​​​‌‌​​​​​‌‌​​‌​‌​​‌‌​‌​‌​‌‌​​​‌‌​​‌‌​​​​​​‌‌​‌‌​​‌‌​​‌​‌​​‌‌​​​​​‌‌​​​‌‌​​‌‌​​‌​​​‌‌​‌‌​​‌‌​​​‌‌‍any rate, they could not disregard the rules and eat them right in front of their mistress.","Shen Yanshui then had some water brought in and took a bath. Although she had not needed to do everything herself in the kitchen, she had nevertheless picked up some of its mingled odors.","As she sat before the dressing mirror, her gaze fell upon the hibiscus-pink crystal jewelry set beside her, which glittered even more brilliantly beneath the sunlight. Suddenly inspired, she said, “Xia'an, redo my hair and put this set on me.”","Xia'an smiled and stepped forward to acknowledge the order.","After a while, once the styling was complete, Xia'an could not help exclaiming at the sight of her mistress in the mirror, “Mistress, you truly look like a celestial beauty...”","Even though she saw her every day, she was still occasionally stunned by her mistress’s beauty.","Chunping and Qiuru, standing nearby, blushed faintly and hurried to echo her praise. Shen Yanshui was so delighted that her heart bloomed with joy, and she could not help admiring herself thoroughly in the mirror.","What a pity—if cameras had existed, she would absolutely have taken several pictures to keep as mementos.","Only after she had finally admired herself to her heart’s content did Shen Yanshui turn her attention to the things in their hands. Chunping smiled and reported, “Mistress, tomorrow is the Duanyang Festival. We were just preparing to decorate the courtyard, so we can ward off evil and avert calamity for you.”","Shen Yanshui smiled. “You’ve all been very thoughtful.”","Then she looked toward the pile of small items in Qiuru’s arms and casually picked up a brightly colored cloth toy.","“Who made this little tiger?”","Xia'an replied with a smile, “Mistress, Qiuru made it. We never realized before that she was so skilled at making cloth tigers.”","Shen Yanshui praised her without reservation. “It really is beautifully made.” In any case, it was far better than anything Shen Yanshui herself could have made.","During the Duanyang Festival, families often placed tigers around the house to drive away evil and ward off misfortune. Many even dressed their children in tiger robes and tiger hats, making them look like little tigers in the hope of protecting them from evil and keeping them healthy and strong.","Qiuru pressed her lips together shyly. “It’s only a crude little craft. I hardly deserve your praise, Mistress.”","Shen Yanshui smiled. “If it’s well made, then it’s well made. Why shouldn’t you be praised for it?”","As she spoke, she looked down at the little tiger in her hand. It had an impressively fierce expression, though it was also rather adorable. She played with it lovingly for a while before setting it down.","Seeing the things they were holding, and finding herself with nothing else to do, Shen Yanshui decided to find herself a task. She smiled and said, “Bring the ladder over...”","When Cui Yu arrived, he happened to see her holding calamus leaves and mugwort, standing atop a tall ladder and hanging them above the doorway.","“This servant greets Your Highness.”","Qiuru, who had been about to scatter realgar powder at the courtyard gate, was startled when she saw the Crown Prince. She hurriedly dropped to her knees and paid her respects.","The others, hearing this, hastily set down their work and followed suit.","Shen Yanshui naturally turned around as well. A flicker of surprise crossed her face. “Your Highness?” she said, immediately preparing to climb down.","Cui Yu’s heart clenched at the sight. His Adam’s apple bobbed faintly as he said in a low voice, “There’s no need to hurry. Come down slowly.”","Shen Yanshui failed to notice anything amiss and nimbly descended the ladder.","Quanshou, who was still prostrated on the ground, had been hesitating over whether he could get up to receive his mistress before the Crown Prince dismissed them. Then a corner of a dark robe, embroidered with subdued silver patterns of four-clawed pythons, suddenly appeared before his eyes. He immediately lay still, obediently keeping his face pressed to the ground.","Cui Yu reached out and gripped Shen Yanshui’s forearm. Only then did she realize that he seemed to be holding her rather tightly...","Once he saw that she was safely on the ground, Cui Yu’s expression darkened. Turning toward the servants kneeling throughout the courtyard, he said coldly, “What are you all good for? You allowed your mistress to put herself in danger. What use is there in keeping any of you?”","Everyone instantly grew terrified and knocked their heads against the ground, begging forgiveness.","Shen Yanshui had not expected him to lose his temper so violently. She was startled before she came to her senses. Seeing his grim expression, as though his next order would be to punish them all, her heart gave a frightened leap.","But she soon realized that he was angry because he had been worried she might fall, and her composure returned.","If Chunping, Quanfu, and the others were punished merely because she had climbed a ladder, that would be far too unjust.","She tentatively caught hold of a corner of his sleeve, cautiously peeking at his darkened expression as she said in a hesitant, pleading tone, “Please don’t be angry, Your Highness. I was the one who insisted on climbing up there. How could they, as servants, have stopped me?”","Cui Yu cast her a sidelong glance. Only then did he notice that she had changed into a hibiscus-colored, high-waisted silk skirt.","The light fabric, as soft as smoke in the fifth month, carried a delicate hue like a lotus just beginning to bloom, setting off her skin to appear even more luminous and pale.","The high-waisted bodice wrapped snugly around her full breasts, outlining her lush, undulating curves and soft, supple skin.","The hibiscus-pink crystal ornaments in her hair, at her ears, and around her neck radiated a gentle, crystalline glow. The stones were clear as water, shimmering with a faint sheen of sunlight as they sparkled among her cloudlike locks. Their radiance mingled with the hibiscus hue of her dress until it was impossible to tell whether her beauty illuminated the fabric or the jewels lent their glow to her features.","She resembled a water lotus fresh from the stream, its morning dew not yet dry—a sight that made it impossible to look away.","Cui Yu’s eyes shifted faintly, but he continued to keep his face cold and said nothing.","Shen Yanshui secretly hooked her finger around his little finger and gave it a gentle tug. When he still did not react, she grew even bolder and wrapped both arms tightly around one of his.","Then she tipped her chin up and gazed at him imploringly. “Your Highness, I know I was wrong. I shouldn’t have relied on my agility and climbed up and down without regard for the danger.”","However, she changed her tone, a hint of grievance showing on her face. “You know I used to play cuju and polo all the time. I’m very nimble, and I hardly ever fall. Please don’t let it upset you so much that you make yourself ill~”","Her voice was soft and sweet, as though she were acting spoiled. Yet there was an unmistakable note of grievance in it, and the lingering lilt at the end of her words curled like a little hook, burrowing straight into Cui Yu’s ears.","The softness pressed firmly against his arm made his muscles tense unconsciously. He lowered his eyes to look at her, his gaze dark and fathomless. His usually cool voice carried an unfamiliar, low rasp. “You’re quite skilled? Nimble, are you?”","Shen Yanshui met his deep, turbulent gaze and suddenly had the inexplicable feeling that something was not quite right...","Cui Yu stared at her darkly for a long while before turning his eyes toward the servants of Lianxin Court kneeling in the courtyard. His voice was cold as he said, “This time, your mistress pleaded for mercy on your behalf, so I will let it go. But if there is a next time, you needn’t remain at Lianxin Court.”","Chunping, Quanfu, and the others immediately trembled as they kowtowed and thanked him for his mercy.","Shen Yanshui breathed a sigh of relief, but at the same time, she became even more wary.","Just then, she noticed him glance in her direction. His crow-black lashes lowered, concealing his dark eyes. She heard him say coldly, “Come inside with me.”","His voice sounded icy and distant. With that, he turned and walked into the room.","Shen Yanshui: “...”","Something seemed vaguely amiss, but for the moment, she couldn’t put her finger on what.","In the end, she followed him inside.","“Close the door.”","Shen Yanshui paused, then obediently turned around and shut the door.","“Your Highness?” She felt a little uneasy. He sat upright on the couch, his expression blank as he watched her, and she had no idea what he meant to do.","Cui Yu looked at her and said in an even tone, “Come here.”"]},{"number":25,"title":"Chapter 25: Shy and Bashful","paragraphs":["Shen Yanshui walked over lightly. Only when she drew close, under the somewhat dim light, could she clearly make out his expression. Something about him seemed a little strange...","“Your Highness, what’s wrong? Are you feeling unwell?” she asked with concern.","Cui Yu glanced up at her but did not answer for a moment.","He had never expected his body to react simply because she came so close to him. Naturally, he would never say such a thing aloud.","Seeing his cold, expressionless face, Shen Yanshui had initially felt somewhat uneasy. But when her gaze inadvertently swept over a certain place, her mind went blank for a moment.","Shen Yanshui: “...” What happened? Had someone drugged the Crown Prince?","A foolish thought suddenly flashed through her mind. Fortunately, she only thought it and did not say it aloud. After all, this was the Eastern Palace. Who would dare drug the Crown Prince? Did they have a death wish?","In the blink of an eye, she quickly racked her memory and finally realized what was probably going on.","But looking at his cold, impassive face as he sat there in silence, she suddenly felt an irresistible urge to tease him.","With a worried look on her face, she went over and sat down beside him. Resting one hand lightly on his shoulder, she asked gently, “Your Highness, what’s wrong? Are you still angry?”","Before he could answer, Shen Yanshui lightly patted his somewhat tense chest. “Anger is bad for your health. Please don’t be angry, Your Highness. How about I massage your shoulders as an apology?”","When Shen Yanshui saw his ears suddenly turn red, she found it immensely amusing. At that moment, she felt just like a little temptress clinging to him, eager to see how long this Crown Prince—always so serious and aloof by day—could keep enduring it.","Suddenly, her wrist was seized by a large, finely jointed hand. Cui Yu’s gaze was deep and dark.","“An apology?”","Shen Yanshui’s heart jolted. For some inexplicable reason, she felt as if she had suddenly fallen under the dangerous gaze of a ferocious beast.","Before she could respond, the force of his hand pulled her abruptly into his arms, leaving her seated on his lap.","The next moment, she felt it with startling clarity.","Shen Yanshui: “...” That change was a little too fast, wasn’t it?","Cui Yu had never considered himself a gentleman. It was simply that he had never been particularly interested in matters of the bedchamber.","Yet at some point, something seemed to have changed.","Cui Yu raised a hand and pulled at her sash.","Shen Yanshui’s hand shyly slipped through the opening in the hem of his black robes. At the same time, unable to resist the sight of his handsome features, she lowered her eyes and kissed him.","Cui Yu: “...”","The instant their lips touched, Shen Yanshui noticed that his entire body suddenly stiffened. He stopped moving.","Shen Yanshui: “...?”","She looked at him. His brows were slightly furrowed as he lowered his eyes to stare at her, his gaze as black and fathomless as an abyss. She suddenly felt that perhaps she could not continue kissing him...","Uneasily, she drew back a little. Sure enough, being close to the ruler was like sleeping beside a tiger—the ancients had not been wrong!","Her fingers also unconsciously began to slow.","“Your Highness?”","She truly could not tell whether he was refusing her or what he meant. His inexplicable reaction left her completely bewildered.","Cui Yu caught the hand she was preparing to withdraw. “Continue.” His voice was so hoarse that it was almost unrecognizable.","Shen Yanshui: “...”","What was he trying to say? Was he treating her like nothing more than a tool, yet refusing even to kiss her?","For once, she was furious—but in the end, she only dared to be furious for a moment...","Then she suddenly remembered that, the last few times, he had never kissed her on the lips either. Every time, he had started from...","She let out a cold huff inwardly. Hmph. Men!","She ​​‌‌​‌‌​​‌‌​​​​‌​‌‌​​​‌‌​​‌‌‌​​​​‌‌​​​‌‌​​‌‌‌​​​​‌‌​​‌​‌​‌‌​​​‌​​​‌‌​‌​​​‌‌​​​​‌​‌‌​​​‌​​​‌‌‌​​​​​‌‌​​​​​‌‌​​‌​‌​​‌‌​‌​‌​‌‌​​​‌‌​​‌‌​​​​​​‌‌​‌‌​​‌‌​​‌​‌​​‌‌​​​​​‌‌​​​‌‌​​‌‌​​‌​​​‌‌​‌‌​​‌‌​​​‌‌‍couldn’t help grumbling to herself: If you’re so capable, then don’t use your mouth anywhere at all! I haven’t even complained about you, and you’re already finding fault with me?","As if she cared about kissing him!","Shen Yanshui secretly cast a glance at his neatly arranged clothing, then opened her mouth and bit him on the neck. Listening to the change in his voice from its usual cool composure, she began tormenting him with her hands, taking a rather malicious pleasure in getting her revenge...","Then she suddenly felt his entire body stiffen like stone, the muscles in his legs becoming especially taut.","Cui Yu buried his face against her shoulder to regain his composure. After a long while, he put an arm around her slender waist and slowly straightened up.","A fine sheen of sweat covered his forehead, yet the expression on his face had already returned to normal—calm and unruffled as ever. Shen Yanshui secretly curled her lips.","As though by accident, she waved her still-moist hand beneath his eyes and said, with a bashful, troubled air, “Your Highness, what are we to do?”","As she spoke, she cast a pointed glance at the noticeably darker patch spreading across his clothing.","Fortunately, he was wearing dark robes today. Unless one looked closely, it was impossible to notice.","There was a fleeting trace of awkwardness on Cui Yu’s face, though it vanished almost at once. After all, this was the first time they had indulged themselves in broad daylight...","He calmly reached for the teacup. Glancing at her flushed palm, he said without batting an eye, “Rinse it.”","Shen Yanshui: “...”","Fine. At least this counted as the Crown Prince personally attending to her while she washed her hands.","After she had quickly rinsed her hand, she saw him pour another cup of tea over himself with the same smooth, natural efficiency.","The tea immediately soaked into the fabric, leaving his clothes thoroughly damp. The indescribable scent lingering in the air was diluted considerably by the fragrance of the pre-rain Longjing tea.","Shen Yanshui merely gave him a soft snort at this entire cleanup operation and said nothing. She hurriedly slipped down from his lap.","Though, truth be told, her own clothes were hardly in any better condition.","Her cross-collared jacket had somehow become a front-opening garment, while the begonia-red bodice beneath it had long since been pulled far from where it belonged. Her clothes were wrinkled everywhere, and she could hardly bear to look at herself. She felt a pang of distress as well—these garments were made from fine, expensive materials and needed to be carefully tended. Now they had been ruined by him...","Cui Yu looked up and caught the faintly accusing glance in her eyes. Then he looked at her clothes...","Cui Yu: “...”","He turned his head away and coughed lightly before saying in a low voice, “I’ll have some fabric sent to you later.”","Only then did Shen Yanshui finally smile. “Thank you, Your Highness. Please summon Eunuch Zheng to attend to you at once. You mustn’t catch cold. I’ll go inside and change first.”","With that, she swayed gracefully into the inner room.","Cui Yu: “...”","However, he did not immediately summon someone to attend to him. Instead, as though something had suddenly occurred to him, his brows drew together slightly, and he raised a hand to touch his lips without thinking.","He had never kissed anyone on the lips. Yet he knew of such things; he had seen men and women feeding one another with their mouths and tongues. Even a single extra glance had disgusted him, as though it sullied his eyes.","Nor had he ever entertained such a thought.","Cui Yu unconsciously pressed his lips together. Yet that brief sensation just now... seemed not to have repulsed or disgusted him as much as he had imagined it would.","Still, deep down, he instinctively felt that it was somehow unclean.","“Your Highness?” Zheng Yuande’s cautious voice suddenly sounded from outside.","Cui Yu’s voice darkened. “What is it?”","Zheng Yuande promptly replied, “Your Highness, Cao Zhongda has just sent word that Lord Xiao is currently waiting in the front hall.”","Cui Yu frowned. Lowering his eyes and finding that there was nothing obviously amiss, he rose and left the room. Before departing, he turned to the eunuch waiting deferentially to one side and said, “Tell your mistress that I have official business to attend to in the front hall, and will be leaving first.”","He had not intended to leave any particular instruction. But he had originally come here to have lunch with her, and in the end... If he finished and left immediately, it would make it seem as though he had come solely for that purpose.","Quanfu did not dare raise his head. Bowing deeply, he answered respectfully, “Yes.”","But the moment Zheng Yuande caught sight of the disheveled state of the Crown Prince’s clothes, he cried out in alarm, “Oh dear! Your Highness, what happened to your garments? How did you get tea spilled all over yourself?”","Cui Yu frowned. The damp fabric clung tightly to his body, making him uncomfortable, and he was even less inclined to listen to Zheng Yuande’s fussing. “It is nothing. I accidentally spilled some tea just now. Let us go.”","Zheng Yuande repeatedly assented, then hurriedly instructed someone to return and prepare a fresh set of clothes. How could the Crown Prince possibly meet anyone while wearing wet garments?","He could not help grumbling inwardly. What was Lady Shen doing? Did she not know how to attend to His Highness properly? Honestly...","Then he remembered that, before leaving, His Highness had specifically instructed that little eunuch to inform Lady Shen. That was something he had never done before...","Zheng Yuande forcibly swallowed his dissatisfaction. Forget it, forget it. If His Highness himself was not angry, what right did he have to be angry on his behalf?"]},{"number":26,"title":"Chapter 26: Who on earth made up this rumor","paragraphs":["Shen Yanshui did not need Quanfu to pass the message along. She had heard every word clearly from inside her inner chambers, yet she did not rush out immediately. Instead, she changed her clothes at a leisurely pace, taking her time to adjust her attire properly.","A moment later, Chunping stepped in softly to help her finish dressing, though her face could not hide her tense, anxious expression. She had no idea what had transpired between the Crown Prince and her mistress inside the room. All she had seen was the Crown Prince storming in with a dark, heavy look on his face, only to walk out moments later, his whole body splattered with tea, before leaving without a word...","And her mistress had not even come out to bow and see him off properly.","Fretting with worry, she said, \"My lady, about the Crown Prince...\"","Shen Yanshui looked as calm and composed as ever, smiling at her gently. \"It's nothing. Don't worry.\"","Chunping fell silent. Who would not be trembling with fear after seeing the Crown Prince in such a state? Especially since he had come out of their mistress's room looking that way, how could she not be anxious?","Shen Yanshui was actually in a rather good mood. The thought of that man walking off unaware that the teeth mark she had left on him was still there, and that he would have to meet his subordinates like that, made her wonder what kind of expression he would make once he noticed it. Truly, her mood was excellent.","Cui Yu was indeed meeting people right then, and more than one person at that.","But during the entire meeting, the two men before him kept their heads bowed, staring at the ground and not daring to lift their eyes. Frowning in confusion, he asked after they had finished discussing official matters, \"Is there anything else you wish to report?\"","Yu Qinghe immediately bowed deeply. \"Your Highness, there are still some official duties at the Prefectural Magistrate's Office that I must attend to. This official shall take his leave now.\"","Cui Yu nodded to dismiss him, then turned his gaze to Xiao Zhengshan, the commander of the Eastern Palace guards.","Xiao Zhengshan fell silent, watching the man who had been standing right beside him just a moment ago scurry away like a frightened mouse. He gritted his teeth inwardly, that old fox can run faster than anyone else!","\"Speak. What is it?\"","Xiao Zhengshan lifted his eyes slightly, only to catch a glimpse of a faint teeth mark peeking out from under the hem of the Crown Prince's collar. He immediately lowered his head even further, and his sun-tanned face flushed a deep shade of red. How on earth was he supposed to say such a thing to the Crown Prince?","He cursed the fleeing old fox in his heart again.","Cui Yu furrowed his brows. \"Speak.\"","Xiao Zhengshan flinched, and finally, stammering and bright red in the face, he said with his head still lowered, \"Your Highness, your... your appearance is slightly improper. Perhaps you should call Eunuch Zheng in to help you tidy up?\"","Cui Yu's brows shifted. Seeing the odd look on Xiao Zhengshan's face, a bad premonition crept into his mind. He waved his hand to dismiss everyone.","Xiao Zhengshan let out a huge sigh of relief and quickly scurried away.","He could not help but wonder, what bold woman would dare to bite the Crown Prince...","Cui Yu did not call for Zheng Yuande. Instead, he went to the inner chamber of his study alone.","Because of his clothes, he had not allowed any palace attendants to help him change after returning to the Changqing Palace, and had changed his garments all by himself before coming to meet the two men who had been waiting for him.","But when he stood in front of the bronze mirror, his eyes suddenly froze. He tilted his head slightly, pulled down the collar of his robe to expose his neck, and his face instantly turned dark, then flushed bright red, shifting through a whole range of colors...","Finally, his face dark and stormy, he roared, \"Zheng Yuande, get in here this instant!\"","At the sound of that voice, Zheng Yuande's whole plump, pale body trembled in fright. He stumbled and rolled his way into the room.","\"Y-your Highness...\"","In the Changqing Palace, any matter related to the Crown Prince, even the smallest hint of gossip, would be probed and pored over endlessly by everyone.","It was even more so today. In the afternoon, the Crown Prince had gone to the Lotus Heart Courtyard in a fury, and had gone inside the room with Lady Shen for a very long time. He had not even stayed for the noon meal, and had instead emerged from the Lotus Heart Courtyard soaked all over in tea, looking utterly disheveled.","The news had spread not just to the back quarters, but almost the entire Changqing Palace. No one could remember the usually fastidious Crown Prince ever looking so much in disarray before. Everyone was guessing that Lady Shen must have been so spoiled and arrogant that she had offended and enraged the Crown Prince.","This very reasonable-sounding speculation made countless people eagerly wait to see what would happen next.","The Crown Princess frowned, deep in thought. \"This Lady Shen...\"","Matron Zhou smiled. \"Your Highness, I'm afraid we won't even need to wait until tomorrow. Lady Shen will likely have already lost the Crown Prince's favor.\"","A faint smile tugged at the Crown Princess's lips. She was more than happy to see that happen.","When Lady Wu heard the news, her eyes lit up with delight, and she could barely hold back a laugh.","\"She was so arrogant and smug! Now there's a wonderful show to watch! Go, find out more details.\" She even had the audacity to personally go to the palace kitchen to make snacks for the Crown Prince, acting like she was so special!","Even Lady Liu, who was confined to her quarters, felt some of the pent-up frustration in her chest dissipate when she heard the news.","She had only found out after being confined that the Crown Prince had mistakenly thought the bowl of Chinese yam and wolfberry soup she had sent over was from Lady Shen across the courtyard, which was why he had gone to visit her in the first place.","When she learned that, she had been so furious that her head had spun, and she felt like spitting blood.","That soup was hers! And what had happened? It had indeed drawn the Crown Prince's attention, but through a stupid misunderstanding, he had thought Lady Shen had made it. Lady Shen had stolen all the credit, and on top of that, she, Lady Liu, had ended up being confined by the Crown Prince!","She could have torn Lady Shen's heart out with her bare hands.","It was only later, when the Crown Prince had sent a eunuch to reprimand her for snooping on his movements and bribing his personal attendants, that she had broken out in cold sweat, suddenly realizing how much danger she had landed herself in.","She had been completely quiet after that. But now, hearing the news that Lady Shen might be in trouble soon, she was still overjoyed. If she had fallen out of the Crown Prince's favor, why should that woman who had reaped all the benefits of her hard work still be enjoying his grace?","But as they waited and waited... word came that Lady Shen had sent people to the palace kitchen to fetch her noon meal, and was already eating peacefully.","The people who had been waiting eagerly were all confused.","A ​​‌‌​‌‌​​‌‌​​​​‌​‌‌​​​‌‌​​‌‌‌​​​​‌‌​​​‌‌​​‌‌‌​​​​‌‌​​‌​‌​‌‌​​​‌​​​‌‌​‌​​​‌‌​​​​‌​‌‌​​​‌​​​‌‌‌​​​​​‌‌​​​​​‌‌​​‌​‌​​‌‌​‌​‌​‌‌​​​‌‌​​‌‌​​​​​​‌‌​‌‌​​‌‌​​‌​‌​​‌‌​​​​​‌‌​​​‌‌​​‌‌​​‌​​​‌‌​‌‌​​‌‌​​​‌‌‍little later, they heard that Lady Shen had taken her people out to stroll in the palace garden.","They were even more bewildered. Could it be that their guess was wrong?","After a while, news came that the Crown Prince, who had returned to the front hall, had suddenly flown into a rage.","Everyone perked up immediately, their eyes wide.","Shen Yanshui had taken a walk in the garden to aid digestion after her lunch. She had played with the cute, sweet-talking Little Jade for a while before heading back.","On her way back, she ran into Lady Wu by the Moonflower Gate unexpectedly.","Shen Yanshui stopped and curtsied to greet her. \"This servant greets Lady Wu.\"","Lady Wu was wearing a loose, lightweight large-sleeve gown of pale cyan, while her hair was styled in an elaborate, intricate updo dotted all over with glittering pearls and jewels that made her look strikingly elegant and imposing.","Lady Wu rested one hand on the arm of her maid, carrying herself with an air of utmost superiority. She looked at Shen Yanshui and smiled meaningfully.","Then she feigned surprise. \"Sister Shen, please rise. I heard that you personally went to the kitchen to make fruit drinks for the Crown Prince today? I never knew you had such excellent skills! When you have time, do come over to my courtyard more often to keep me company, and let me have a taste of your cooking too.\"","Shen Yanshui smiled, looking slightly shy as she pressed her lips together. \"Sister Wu, you are far too complimentary. I have already given the recipe for that fruit drink to Chief Steward Tang at the kitchen. If you would like to have some, you can just send someone to the kitchen to ask for it any time you wish.\"","With a tone of utter sincerity, she said, \"But if Sister Wu would only have a meal made personally by this little sister, I happen to be completely free right now. If it is convenient at Sister Chu's place, I can go over and make something for you to taste at once.\"","The smile on Lady Wu's face froze for a split second. What was wrong with this woman? Why wasn't she playing by the expected rules?","She was clearly humiliating her! How could this woman still keep a smile on her face?!","Wait a minute...","Her expression shifted sharply. \"Are you mocking me?\"","The very idea of going back to her courtyard to cook for her was ridiculous—her courtyard didn't have a small private kitchen permitted by the Crown Prince! In the entire Eastern Palace, only the Crown Prince, the Crown Princess, and the pregnant Lady Chu had small private kitchens in their residences.","Shen Yanshui looked at her with a perfectly innocent face and said, \"You've misunderstood me, Sister Wu. How would this little sister ever dare to mock you? Every word I said was truly from the bottom of my heart.\"","Lady Wu let out a cold snort, then lifted her chin to look at her with a mocking, smug expression. \"What do you have left to be proud of? You actually dared to splash tea all over the Crown Prince. Even if his Highness is broad-minded and chooses not to hold it against you, the Crown Princess and Her Majesty the Empress will never let you get away with it!\"","Shen Yanshui: \"...\" Who on earth made up such a baseless rumor? It didn't even have a shred of credibility!","Was she so tired of living that she would dare splash tea on the Crown Prince? Thinking back to how that cup of tea had actually ended up in the Crown Prince's presence, she couldn't help curling her lip in disdain. If that man dared to pin the blame on her and get her punished... hmph, she would make sure he regretted it.","As for exactly how she would make him \"regret it\", she would figure that out later.","Seeing that Shen Yanshui had gone silent, apparently shocked, Lady Wu's face lit up with smug satisfaction. She spoke in a lecturing tone, \"Are you scared now? It's good that you know fear. Don't think that just because you have a pretty face and have received a little favor from the Crown Prince, you can ignore all rules of hierarchy and propriety...\"","She was enjoying the sound of her own scolding so much that she failed to notice that the palace maid standing beside her had turned deathly pale and was trembling all over with terror.","Shen Yanshui had heard the familiar footsteps long ago, so she simply bowed her head quietly and listened to the lecture, pretending to notice nothing at all.","Lady Wu hadn't caused her any real, substantial harm so far, but that was only because Shen Yanshui herself was not the meek, yielding type who would let anyone walk all over her. Still, every time they ran into each other, Lady Wu would ramble on and on in front of her. At first, Shen Yanshui had found it somewhat amusing, but now even she was growing tired of it.","Clearly, Lady Wu hadn't learned her lesson from the last time they'd clashed. She'd gotten a tiny bit of gossip and couldn't wait to show off, gloat, and preen in front of her.","Lady Wu had been a little restrained at the start, knowing full well that she'd lost the verbal sparring with Shen Yanshui more than once before. But now that she thought Shen Yanshui had truly angered the Crown Prince and been scared speechless, she grew more and more excited, and her lecturing grew bolder and more unbridled.","\"...As the daughter of a distinguished military clan, it's only natural that this little sister might have poor manners, act a little roughly, and lack proper etiquette. Luckily, the Haitang Garden is right next door to my Lotus Heart Courtyard. I'll have plenty of time to teach you proper rules and decorum, so that you won't make a foolish mistake later and end up dragging the Crown Prince's reputation down with you...\"","\"I never imagined that a lowly Lady Wu would have the authority to lecture and discipline the imperial concubines of this palace.\" Cui Yu spoke in a cold, stern voice as he stepped out from behind the bushes, casting a dispassionate glance at Lady Wu, who had fallen to her knees, her face as white as a sheet."]},{"number":27,"title":"Chapter 27: Don't Tempt Gu.","paragraphs":["“Lord Wu, Minister of the Dali Temple, has certainly raised a fine daughter.”","His voice was calm and even, neither harsh nor mild, yet the sarcasm in it was especially cutting.","Lady Wu was already drenched in cold sweat, so frightened that her mind had gone completely blank. She wanted to speak, to explain herself, but her teeth were chattering so badly that she could not force out a single word.","Only now did she understand that when the Crown Prince was truly angered, the authority surrounding him could weigh down on a person until they could scarcely breathe.","“Y-Your Highness... This concubine was only jealous that Sister Shen had won Your Highness’s favor, and so I lost my sense of propriety. This concubine knows her mistake. I will never dare again. I beg Your Highness to forgive me...”","She wept like a pear blossom in the rain, pitiful enough to stir anyone’s heart.","Listening to her, Shen Yanshui found her irritating, but had to admit that Lady Wu had some presence of mind. She had reduced her offense to nothing more than jealousy and rivalry between women.","And why would she be jealous?","Was it not because she held the Crown Prince in her heart?","Most men would probably fall for that sort of thing.","When a beautiful woman made a small mistake because she cared for you, because she fought with another woman over you—and then looked so pitiful, crying as though her heart had broken—how many men could truly bring themselves to be merciless?","Sure enough, the Crown Prince said in a low voice, “Lady Wu has behaved and spoken without decorum. As punishment, she is to copy the *Instructions for Women* one hundred times and submit it to the Crown Princess for inspection in ten days.”","His tone remained as cold as ever as he ordered Zheng Yuande, “Send someone to inform the Crown Princess.”","Zheng Yuande hurriedly acknowledged the order and immediately sent someone off. Really, the Crown Princess should keep these people in line. How could she leave them unchecked?","They had only been in the Eastern Palace for a month, yet the new arrivals had committed one offense after another. If word got out, what would people say? His Highness was likely mindful of appearances, which was why he had not punished Lady Wu too severely.","Cui Yu’s thoughts were indeed not far from Zheng Yuande’s.","But Shen Yanshui knew nothing of his concerns. She only assumed that he, too, could not bear to be too harsh.","Still, copying the *Instructions for Women* a hundred times in ten days meant writing more than ten thousand characters a day. The handwriting had to be neat, with no mistakes. It was hardly an easy punishment.","Once the matter had been dealt with, Lady Wu still had to thank him profusely for his mercy. Shen Yanshui was standing to one side with her eyes lowered when she suddenly sensed a gaze sweeping over her from head to toe. For some reason, she felt a chill run over her skin.","Cui Yu said coldly, “What are you standing there for? Are you not leaving?”","Shen Yanshui gave the limp, collapsed Lady Wu a slight curtsy before lifting her skirts and following after him.","He was heading toward Lotus Heart Courtyard.","Cui Yu strode ahead with a blank expression, not saying a word. Behind him, the sound of footsteps changed from small, measured steps to quick strides, and then to a light run.","Cui Yu: “...”","He abruptly stopped and turned to stare at her. Shen Yanshui braked sharply, nearly crashing into him. But having learned from Lady Liu’s example, she did not dare throw herself into his arms. She tightened her core and steadied herself firmly in place.","Cui Yu: “...”","His voice was calm and cold. “When you are before me, is your courage not boundless? Yet before others, you turn mute?”","Shen Yanshui’s heart tightened. She stole a glance at him. Seeing the dark, stern look on his face, she hesitated only a moment before honestly murmuring, “This concubine was actually... pretending.”","Cui Yu narrowed his eyes. “Oh?”","Shen ​​‌‌​‌‌​​‌‌​​​​‌​‌‌​​​‌‌​​‌‌‌​​‌​​‌‌​​‌‌​‌‌​​​​‌​​‌‌​‌‌‌​​‌‌‌​​‌​​‌‌​‌​​​‌‌​​​​‌​‌‌​​​‌​​​‌‌‌​​​​​‌‌​​​​​‌‌​​‌​‌​​‌‌​‌​‌​‌‌​​​‌‌​​‌‌​​​​​​‌‌​‌‌​​‌‌​​‌‌​​​‌‌​​​​​​‌‌​‌‌​​​‌‌​‌‌​​‌‌​​‌​‌​‌‌​​​‌‌‍Yanshui noticed the subtle shift in his mood, and inwardly relaxed. As expected, he had seen through her.","She decided that from now on, she should be honest in front of him and stop trying to play tricks with others. After all, he had been Crown Prince for so many years—how could an ordinary person possibly outmaneuver him?","“Lady Wu always likes to make trouble for me. I’m not afraid of her, but she really is rather annoying,” she said, knitting her delicate brows in mild complaint.","Then she glanced at him, her eyes sparkling. Pressing her lips together in a smile, she said, “Just now, I was planning to provoke her a little. Then I happened to see the hem of your robe, so... so I deliberately kept quiet. I wanted Your Highness to suddenly appear and give her a fright.”","Cui Yu cast a glance at her undisguised delight—there was even a touch of gleeful satisfaction in her expression—and gave a cold snort. Though his face remained grim, the faint discomfort in his heart quietly dissipated.","Behind them, Zheng Yuande, who had silently listened to Shen Yanshui speak, could not help widening his eyes.","This Lady Shen truly was so straightforward that even watching her made his heart tremble.","Then again, perhaps this was what people meant by fools having foolish luck. What clever person would enjoy having someone by their side with countless schemes, especially when those schemes were directed at them?","Xia'an, on the other hand, had gone pale. His legs had turned weak and trembled so badly that he nearly could not stand. Just as he was quaking with fear, he heard the Crown Prince turn and enter Lotus Heart Court.","Xia'an let out a fierce sigh of relief. ...That had been far too thrilling.","Shen Yanshui knew that although he still looked expressionless, his mood was no longer as foul as before. She was fairly relaxed as well—until she followed him into the room and the door closed behind them again...","Shen Yanshui’s eyes flew wide open. Looking at his dark, heavy gaze, she stammered, “Y-Your Highness, too much indulgence is bad for one’s health!”","Cui Yu’s already dark expression immediately turned even more forbidding. Raising a hand, he pulled down his sweat-dampened collar and stared at her as he said in a deep voice, “How am I supposed to face anyone tomorrow?”","He had changed into another outfit, but this dark teal robe had a rather high collar and was made of thick fabric—clearly not something suitable for the current season.","When Shen Yanshui saw the rather noticeable bite mark on his neck beneath the lowered collar, she felt somewhat guilty. Still, it was not as though she had failed to consider the consequences. Seeing his expression grow darker by the moment, she said with embarrassment, “It was my fault, but Your Highness need not worry.”","As she spoke, she took his hand and led him around the rosewood four-seasons landscape screen. From a small drawer beside the dressing table, she took out a white porcelain jar of ointment. Opening it, she said, “Your Highness, this is an ointment I often use to reduce bruising and fade marks. It works very well. Use it twice today, and by tomorrow morning there definitely won’t be a trace left.”","Cui Yu lowered his gaze to the white, creamy salve inside and frowned.","Seeing his deeply furrowed brow, Shen Yanshui did not mind whether he doubted the ointment’s effectiveness or suspected there was something wrong with it. She glanced at him, her cheeks faintly flushing, and said, “At noon today, on the couch... didn’t Your Highness notice that the skin on my body looked a little different from last night?” she hinted delicately.","This man was certainly strong. Her skin was fair, and even a slight squeeze would leave a mark. Though every time, after he had left, she would circulate her ability through the meridians in her body, and the marks on her skin would return to normal.","Still, the ointment’s effects had not been exaggerated to him.","The most important herbs in it had all been nurtured with her ability over the past while. For such faint marks on the Crown Prince’s skin—where it had not even been broken—a little ointment would make them disappear quickly.","Cui Yu fell silent for a moment, clearly having thought of something.","“Then let’s try it.”","Shen Yanshui said softly, “Your Highness, this is a secret remedy I happened to acquire from common folk. Shall we summon an imperial physician to inspect it first?”","Cui Yu lifted his eyelids and glanced at her. Expressionless, he said, “I have no face to show anyone like this.”","Shen Yanshui: “...”","Sorry, but seeing his expression, she really wanted to laugh.","And when she thought of how he had already gone around seeing people with that bite mark on him, she found it even more amusing.","But she did not dare tease the tiger again. Keeping a perfectly natural, gentle expression, she applied a little ointment for him, thinking, *I didn’t expect him to be so bold. He’ll use an ointment of unknown origin from me just because I said so.*","Then again, her entire life and fortune were now tied to his. What good would it do her to harm him?","As she applied the medicine, Cui Yu removed his outer robe.","Shen Yanshui: ...All right. No wonder he had deliberately chosen to wear clothes meant for early spring.","Seeing that even his white inner robe was nearly soaked through, she said, “Your Highness, I’ll have someone bring a basin of warm water so you can wipe yourself down.”","When he gave no further instructions, she went out to arrange it.","Knowing how much he cared about appearances, she did not allow anyone else to come in and attend to him. She carried the basin in herself. When she saw that he had already settled onto the couch and was looking at the cloth tiger she had set aside, she approached with a smile.","“Your Highness, take off your clothes. Shall I wipe away your sweat for you?”","Cui Yu gave a quiet hum in reply. Only then did he set down the cloth tiger and raise his arms.","Still smiling, Shen Yanshui stepped forward to tend to him. It was already May, and the weather grew hotter by the day. The sun had not yet set, so naturally the room was rather warm as well. Yet Shen Yanshui did not find it uncomfortable.","That was another advantage of her ability: it made her impervious to heat and cold—at least in this world.","As Shen Yanshui looked at the smooth, powerful lines of his body, she could not help stealing a few extra glances. With a wrung-out cloth, she slowly and unhurriedly wiped him down.","Cui Yu: “...”","The affection in her gaze was far too open and straightforward for him to pretend not to notice.","Suddenly, in a cool, detached voice, he said, “Do not try to seduce me.”","Shen Yanshui: “...?”"]},{"number":28,"title":"Chapter 28: Open the Private Treasury, I Shall Select Personally","paragraphs":["What exactly did she seduce him with? She hadn’t done anything at all. Her hands had stayed perfectly proper—she couldn’t have been any more honest and well-behaved. Wasn’t she even allowed to look at him a couple of times?","After changing into the dry, light clothing Zheng Yuande had sent someone to bring, Cui Yu finally let out a comfortable sigh of relief.","When he turned his gaze, he caught sight of the little cloth tiger, no bigger than his palm. Looking around, he noticed that a remarkably lifelike portrait of Celestial Master Zhang was hanging on the wall of the main hall, directly opposite the entrance.","The palace placed great importance on the Dragon Boat Festival, so naturally there would be decorations. However, the arrangements in the Eastern Palace were all overseen by the Crown Princess. Every year, the main focus was on decorating the Crown Prince’s usual living quarters—the front hall and the Xifang Hall. As for the rear quarters, he had no real impression of them.","Following his gaze, Shen Yanshui smiled. “I heard that portraits of Celestial Master Zhang can guard a home against evil spirits and bless its residents with peace and good health, so I painted one myself.”","Cui Yu looked at her in surprise. “You painted this yourself?”","Shen Yanshui nodded, watching him with a rather pleased expression. “What do you think, Your Highness? Isn’t it pretty decent?” In her previous life, she had majored in fine arts. Although she hadn’t specialized in traditional Chinese painting, she had spent so many years living in Great Yong that her time hadn’t been wasted. She was perfectly capable of using ink wash to paint a realistic figure.","Looking at her lively, spirited little expression of pride, Cui Yu said coolly, “It is lifelike, but overly craftsmanlike. It lacks the character’s spiritual essence.”","Shen Yanshui: “...”","Her painting was indeed not particularly good, but she still thought it was all right. How could he call it overly craftsmanlike?","Not entirely convinced, she muttered under her breath, “Even Little Jade’s mouth is sweeter than yours, Your Highness.”","Seeing the coquettish anger in her shifting eyes, Cui Yu did not take offense at her audacity or her disrespectful comparison of him to a parrot. Instead, he suddenly raised a hand and pinched her moist, rosy lips.","Shen Yanshui: “...?”","Cui Yu lowered his eyes and stared at her soft, pink lips for a long moment. A faint, sweet fragrance of rouge seemed to drift into his breath...","“Your Highness?” Shen Yanshui asked, her eyes full of confusion as she spoke indistinctly.","Cui Yu finally released her and said in an even tone, “Prepare the ink and brush.”","Shen Yanshui’s eyes immediately lit up. She led him to the desk in the small study, eagerly preparing the ink and brush for him. Then she took out a blank scroll, unrolled it, and spread it across the table.","“Your Highness, are you going to paint Celestial Master Zhang too?” she asked curiously. She had never seen him paint before.","Cui Yu gave a soft acknowledgment and dipped his brush in ink.","His brush moved as smoothly as flowing clouds and running water. Though he used only a few strokes, skillfully combining varying shades, dryness, and moisture, he captured the figure’s movement and spirit with extraordinary vividness. The painting seemed to take shape the instant the ink touched the paper.","Before long, Cui Yu set down his brush.","Although Shen Yanshui’s own skill in traditional Chinese painting was only average, she still possessed a basic eye for appreciation.","Her eyes sparkled with adoration. “I never knew Your Highness was so good at painting too! Could you bestow this masterpiece upon me? With Your Highness’s painting of Celestial Master Zhang, it will surely protect our home and keep us all safe, healthy, and sound.”","Cui ​​‌‌​‌‌​​‌‌​​​​‌​‌‌​​​‌‌​​‌‌‌​​‌​​‌‌​​‌‌​‌‌​​​​‌​​‌‌​‌‌‌​​‌‌‌​​‌​​‌‌​‌​​​‌‌​​​​‌​‌‌​​​‌​​​‌‌‌​​​​​‌‌​​​​​‌‌​​‌​‌​​‌‌​‌​‌​‌‌​​​‌‌​​‌‌​​​​​​‌‌​‌‌​​‌‌​​‌‌​​​‌‌​​​​​​‌‌​‌‌​​​‌‌​‌‌​​‌‌​​‌​‌​‌‌​​​‌‌‍Yu glanced at her. He was quite pleased inwardly, but his expression remained calm and unruffled. In a detached tone, he said, “It is merely an ordinary work.”","Shen Yanshui smiled brightly. “Then I’ll take that as Your Highness’s agreement?”","When she saw him give a composed nod, she immediately said happily, “Thank you, Your Highness.”","Before long, once the ink on the front had nearly dried, Shen Yanshui had Quanfu and Quanshou carefully hang it up, replacing the one she had painted.","Earlier, she hadn’t thought much of her own work and had even felt that it was fairly decent. But without comparison, one could never see the difference. Beside the Crown Prince’s painting, hers suddenly seemed rather unimpressive. As he had said, it was lifelike, but the figure lacked spiritual vitality and expressiveness.","She was just about to have someone throw it away when she saw the Crown Prince take it over for a closer look.","Cui Yu lowered his eyes and examined it carefully. After a moment, he said, “It does have its merits.”","Shen Yanshui immediately perked up. She leaned closer, her beautiful, peach-blossom eyes fixed on him in eager anticipation. “See? See?”","Praise me a little more. I love hearing it!","Looking at her beautiful, eager little face, like a cat waiting expectantly for him to praise her, Cui Yu could not help reaching out to stroke her smooth black hair. But all he said was a flat, “Not bad.”","Shen Yanshui: “...”","Would praising her a couple more times make him lose his voice? Sure enough, he was still as miserly with words as ever.","Still, she had been praised, after all, and her mood was quite good.","Cui Yu did not remain in Lianxin Court for long. Seeing that the marks on her neck had faded considerably after the medicine was applied, he finally put his mind at ease. Since it was nearly time for the evening meal, he rose to leave.","“We respectfully see Your Highness off,” Shen Yanshui said.","She didn’t care where he went. If he came to her, she would properly attend to this provider of her food and clothing. If he didn’t, she would simply live her own life.","Before leaving, Cui Yu looked her up and down, his gaze lingering for a moment longer on the hibiscus-pink crystal ornaments in her coiffure. Once he had left Lianxin Court, he instructed, “Open my private treasury. Select some fine, lightweight fabrics suitable for summer, along with various pieces of jewelry, stationery, brushes, ink, and paper, and send them to Lady Shen.”","Zheng Yuande hurriedly acknowledged the order.","Cui Yu frowned. “Forget it. Have Qu Wen bring me the inventory catalogue. I’ll choose them myself.”","She usually wore very little jewelry. Most of what she possessed had been gifts bestowed upon her after entering the Eastern Palace. Since she was only a common-born daughter of the Shen family, her relatives likely had not prepared many such things for her.","As far as he knew, Lady Shen in the palace had presented Consort Shu with a white jade statue of Guanyin worth a fortune just a few days earlier, on the occasion of Consort Shu’s birthday. She was also extremely generous when rewarding servants and the like, to say nothing of her own usual food, clothing, and other expenses.","Zheng Yuande lowered his head to conceal his shock. He did not dare delay and immediately sent someone to deliver the message.","Not long afterward, while Shen Yanshui was having dinner, she received the gifts from the Crown Prince.","Only after seeing off the smiling, courteous Eunuch Zheng did Shen Yanshui gaze brightly at the roomful of silks, satins, gold, silver, and jeweled ornaments. For a moment, she was so delighted that the corners of her mouth were harder to suppress than an AK!","Hmm? There were even two sets of excellent brushes, ink, paper, and inkstones, as well as two painting manuals?","The attendants standing nearby were almost dazzled by the glittering treasure before them. More than that, however, they were delighted! All of this had come from their mistress being favored by the Crown Prince!","Shen Yanshui said with a beaming smile, “Chunping, Quanfu, first record everything Your Highness bestowed and place it in the storeroom.”","She had originally assumed that when the Crown Prince said he would send her a little more fabric, he meant no more than the amount he had sent last time. She had never expected him to send several times as much. If she had all of it made into clothes, she could wear a different outfit every day throughout the summer.","She was not actually so extravagant, though. These fabrics were all excellent; whether kept in storage or used as gifts in the future, they would be useful. She simply could not understand why there were so many pieces of jewelry as well.","A pink tourmaline squirrel-and-grape pendant, with clusters of grapes carved from pink crystal and a lively little squirrel.","A “Begonia in Spring Slumber” hairpin, featuring a slightly drooping begonia carved from pink tourmaline, with pearl tassels swaying gently.","There was a bracelet of eighteen pink tourmaline beads, embellished with pearls and jade. Shen Yanshui counted them: all eighteen pink tourmaline beads were strung together, interspersed with jade knot beads and finished with a guru bead.","A rose-quartz lidded censer with coiling chi-dragon handles was carved entirely from rose quartz, its translucent surface so crystalline it looked like jelly. Under the sunlight, it was simply breathtaking.","A tall-footed porcelain cup with shadow-blue glaze and underglaze red was finished in a blue-white glaze, with splashes of underglaze red scattered across it like pink cherry blossoms drifting through snow.","There was a pink lotus suction cup, a lantern-shaped vase with peach-blossom-cave glaze... and a pastel cup decorated with a three-dimensional lotus relief, its petals fading in soft shades of pink. Every piece was so beautiful that it was impossible to look away.","Shen Yanshui examined them one by one. Each piece made her eyes light up, and she could hardly bear to put any of them down. It was just that... why were they all in shades of pink?"]},{"number":29,"title":"Chapter 29: Competing for Attention and Jealousy","paragraphs":["As gifts and rewards poured into Lotusheart Court like flowing water, the people in the rear quarters were left utterly dumbfounded.","Behind closed doors, their eyes burned red with envy, and they nearly tore several handkerchiefs to shreds.","Could this Lady Shen be a fox spirit reincarnated?!","The Crown Princess had only just received the news when she heard the Crown Prince approaching. She quickly composed her expression and rose to greet him.","After seeing the child and having dinner, the Crown Princess took the initiative to bring up Lady Wu’s matter.","With a slight furrow between her brows, she sighed. “The newcomers who entered the residence this time have repeatedly behaved improperly. It is all because I have failed in my duty to discipline them. I originally thought they were young and needed more guidance. Who would have thought that indulging them would only make them increasingly arrogant and lacking in restraint? This is my fault.”","Cui Yu held his cup and took a small sip without saying a word.","Seeing this, the Crown Princess continued, “I never expected Lady Liu to be so bold as to harbor designs on Your Highness and bribe the attendants serving at Your Highness’s side. From now on, I will discipline her more strictly and make sure she does not dare repeat such a thing.”","Cui Yu’s expression softened slightly. His tone remained calm. “Mm. You have gone to a great deal of trouble, Crown Princess.”","A smile appeared on the Crown Princess’s face as she said gently, “Lady Wu is proud and willful, while Lady Liu is rash and ignorant of proper conduct. I have already sent a matron to instruct them.”","Cui Yu set down his teacup and gave a slight nod.","The Crown Princess glanced at him unobtrusively. Then she suddenly gave a helpless smile and said in the casual tone of someone making conversation, “Speaking of which, it was quite a coincidence. The selection happened to take place when Her Majesty the Empress was unwell and unable to oversee matters personally, so Noble Consort Lan chose these women to enter the residence. Now that I look at them...”","She paused, her voice gentle, as though merely mentioning it in passing. “Aside from Lady Zhang, who is well-read and sensible, and knows how to conduct herself, none of the others has been particularly easy to manage.”","Cui Yu lifted his eyes, his tone even. “The Crown Princess has to manage the affairs of the Eastern Palace every day. If there are matters beyond your capacity, Crown Princess, have Matron Rong assist you from now on.”","The Crown Princess’s expression changed.","Matron Rong was the Crown Prince’s wet nurse. During the first year after the Crown Princess married into the Eastern Palace, that old harpy had constantly interfered in her affairs. Fortunately, because of an old ailment in her hand, Matron Rong had reported it to His Highness in the second year and retired to enjoy her old age in the Eastern Palace.","What did His Highness mean by this?","Was he trying to take away her authority to manage the Eastern Palace?","She pressed her lips together, her expression somewhat strained. Then she lowered her head and said softly, “Matron Rong is enjoying her retirement now. There is no need to trouble her. From now on, I will make sure to discipline them properly and see that they do not break the rules again.”","If that old harpy Matron Rong truly began interfering in the affairs of the Eastern Palace, who knew how the other wives in the family would mock her behind her back? His Highness showed not the slightest consideration for her situation.","Cui Yu’s brows and eyes remained cold and detached, but he did not mention Matron Rong again.","The Crown Princess did not dare probe any further. However, just when she thought His Highness would spend the night with her, the Crown Prince left without even mentioning it. Her heart sank.","Fortunately, he had gone to the front hall rather than the rear quarters.","Seeing that her complexion was not very good, Matron Zhou hurried forward to console her. Her gaze fell upon the Crown Princess’s abdomen, which still showed no obvious signs of pregnancy, and she said with a smile, “Your Highness is not in a convenient condition to attend to His Highness at present. It is just as well that he has gone to the front hall.”","At those words, the tightness in the Crown Princess’s chest eased somewhat.","“Your Highness...”","The Crown Princess looked at her in confusion. “Matron? What is it?”","Matron Zhou was troubled by a lingering concern, and could not help bringing it up again. “Your Highness’s pregnancy is nearly secure now. Would it not be better to inform His Highness and Her Majesty the Empress? The Duanyang Festival is the day after tomorrow. With so many people present, should anyone accidentally jostle Your Highness, it would be disastrous.”","The Crown Princess lifted her chin slightly. “There is no need to worry, Matron. My mother specially sent a female physician to attend me. No one else knows that I am pregnant. Who would dare recklessly collide with me?”","“If someone with ill intentions found out, it might instead cause trouble. Why not give His Highness...and Her Majesty a surprise the day after tomorrow?”","If word were spread in advance, someone might make preparations and plot against her and the child in her womb.","Neither Noble Consort Lan nor Consort De was easy to deal with.","Her mother-in-law was already too preoccupied with her own affairs to help her. Since that was the case, what difference did a day or two make?","Besides, Her Majesty had never liked her. Simply because she had failed to give His Highness a healthy child, the Empress continued to look upon her with displeasure no matter how diligently she attended meals and paid her respects each day.","Yet when Lady Chu became pregnant, Her Majesty had immediately sent an experienced matron from her own side to care for her. When the Crown Princess had been pregnant with Zhang’er, she had received no such attentive care.","How could she not harbor resentment?","Matron Zhou was the person closest to and most trusted by the Crown Princess. Though she still felt somewhat worried after hearing this, she also found the Crown Princess’s reasoning sensible and therefore said no more.","*","Early the next morning, as the rising sun broke through the clouds and cast pale golden rays over the world, Shen Yanshui was already dressed and standing in the main hall of Xiefang Palace to pay her respects to the Crown Princess.","The Crown Princess wore a flowing purple robe with wide sleeves. Her hair was arranged beneath a crystal-glazed mountain-style crown adorned with golden beads. With a warm smile covering her face, she looked at the women before her and said, “Rise. Bring them seats.”","However, when her gaze swept across a certain figure, the smile at the corners of her lips faded slightly.","“Thank you, Crown Princess.”","Only then did everyone slowly take their seats.","Shen Yanshui noticed that, apart from Lady Liu, who had been confined, and Lady Wu, who had been punished with copying the Admonitions for Women, nearly everyone else was present.","There was only one person she had never met before: Lady Sun, who had recently suffered a miscarriage.","Lady Sun was extremely thin, her cheeks sunken. Yet it was clear that she had carefully applied her makeup, perhaps in an effort to appear more spirited. Rouge had even been brushed across her face, making her look somewhat more like a normal person.","Naturally, everyone else was startled as well.","The Crown Princess furrowed her brows with concern. “Why have you become so thin? Have the people serving you been neglecting their duties?”","Lady Sun tugged at the corners of her lips in a smile. “In response to the Crown Princess, I am now able to get out of bed and walk. I have already recovered considerably. I should be fully recovered after some more time. Thank you for your concern, Your Highness.”","The Crown Princess smiled as well and said gently, “That is good, then.”","Lady Wang tactfully changed the subject, and everyone soon stopped paying attention to Lady Sun, who looked unnervingly thin.","The Duanyang Festival fell on the fifth day of the fifth month—tomorrow. Today, the Crown Princess would certainly decide which two women could accompany her, and everyone was secretly filled with anticipation.","A perfectly measured smile rested on Shen Yanshui’s face as she sat properly on a rosewood armchair with a pearwood frame. Noticing that Lady Chu had also come today, which was rare, she could not help casting her a second glance.","Then she listened as the women chatted and joked with the Crown Princess, before reaching for a peach blossom pastry from the small table beside her.","After listening for quite some time, she finally heard the conversation turn to tomorrow’s Duanyang Festival banquet at Golden Bright Pool. Her eyes immediately brightened. She knew the main event had finally arrived.","Sure enough, the Crown Princess said with a smile, “This year, Lady Zhang and Lady Shen will accompany me to the Duanyang Festival banquet at Golden Bright Pool.”","The moment she finished speaking, everyone’s expression changed in its own way.","Some concealed their reactions well and quickly composed themselves, while others made no effort to hide their displeasure.","The Crown Princess’s gaze deepened slightly, though she merely smiled.","Lady Zhang and Lady Shen both rose with smiles and thanked her for the favor.","Though the others were disappointed or displeased, most of them dared not say anything. Lady Shen’s favor was plain for all to see, so it was hardly surprising that she had been chosen to go.","As for Lady Zhang, her rank was high and her family background excellent. In the Eastern Palace, her status was surpassed only by that of the Crown Princess and Lady Chu, so her inclusion was perfectly reasonable.","At that moment, Lady Song, who was two years older than the others, pressed her lips together. Dressed in a pale-blue gown patterned with the character for longevity, she had a delicate, refined appearance, though her features were merely average. With an aggrieved and plaintive expression, she said, “Your Highness, in previous years, it was always Sister Chu and Sister Wang who accompanied you. Their ranks are higher than ours, so naturally they were more qualified than us, but...”","As she spoke, she cast a meaningful glance at Shen Yanshui.","Shen ​​‌‌​‌‌​​‌‌​​​​‌​‌‌​​​‌‌​​‌‌‌​​‌​‌‌​​‌​‌​​‌‌​​‌‌​​‌‌​‌​‌​‌‌​​‌​​​​‌‌​‌​​​‌‌​​​​‌​‌‌​​​‌​​​‌‌‌​​​​​‌‌​​​​​‌‌​​‌​‌​​‌‌​‌​‌​‌‌​​​‌‌​​‌‌​​​​​​‌‌​‌‌​​​‌‌​​​​​​‌‌​​‌‌​​‌‌​​‌‌​‌‌​​‌​‌​​‌‌‌​​​​​‌‌​‌‌​‍Yanshui: “...”","Was Lady Song indirectly targeting her?","Everyone present understood the implication behind Lady Song’s words. For a moment, their gazes turned, openly or covertly, toward Shen Yanshui.","Shen Yanshui kept a smile on her face and acted as though she had noticed nothing. She continued behaving as she pleased. Lady Song had not directly named her, so why should she be foolish enough to jump forward and draw attention to herself?","When Lady Song saw that she received no response—and that Shen Yanshui was still sipping her tea with an easy, smiling air—she grew furious inside.","She tugged at the corners of her mouth and said, “I wonder what Lady Shen thinks?”","Shen Yanshui’s expression did not change. Lowering her eyes with a faint smile, she replied, “I will follow whatever the Crown Princess decides.”","Lady Chu smiled and glanced at the Crown Princess before leaning back slightly to watch the scene unfolding before her. She had known there would be a good show today; otherwise, she would have been too lazy to leave her chambers.","For some reason, she had recently felt terribly dizzy and stifled whenever she stayed indoors for too long. Even the medicine prescribed by the imperial physician had done nothing. Yet after coming outside for a while, she felt much more refreshed.","The Crown Princess glanced at the faint dark circles beneath Lady Chu’s eyes and curled her lips ever so slightly. Before she could speak, Lady Wang, seated to the Crown Princess’s lower right, lifted the round fan in her hand to cover her lips. A meaningful smile tugged at the corners of her mouth as she said softly, “Sister Song, don’t be jealous. Sister Shen earned this honor herself before His Highness. How could Her Highness go against that?”","Lady Song’s face stiffened at once.","Shen Yanshui’s expression remained unchanged, though she turned to glance at Lady Wang, who sat beside the Crown Princess.","She then quickly finished the half-piece of pastry still in her hand and continued smiling politely.","“Your words make me uneasy, Lady Wang.”","Her voice was neither loud nor soft, and her tone was gentle and docile. “I have only been in the Eastern Palace for a short while and am still learning its many rules and formalities. How could I dare claim that I earned any honor before His Highness? It is merely that His Highness has shown me kindness, and Her Highness the Crown Princess is gracious enough to give me this opportunity to pay my respects.”","The fan in Lady Wang’s hand paused, and the smile on her lips faded slightly.","Shen Yanshui’s smile remained, and her tone grew even gentler. “Besides, I believe that His Highness and Her Highness must have had their reasons for deciding who would accompany them. All we need to do is accept the command peacefully and ensure that we do not disappoint their good intentions.”","Lady Wang’s expression changed subtly. With her fan covering her lips, she suddenly found herself at a loss for words.","Lady Chu gave a low laugh. “Sister Shen is quite right.”","The Crown Princess had originally been holding her teacup and watching from the sidelines. At last, she spoke, her tone indifferent. “That will do.”","She glanced at Lady Wang. “Lady Shen is right. The list of those accompanying me was decided after discussion between His Highness and me. Naturally, I have my reasons.”","Lady Wang hurriedly rose and curtsied. “It was my mistake. I spoke out of turn.”","The Crown Princess waved a hand, indicating that she should sit down. She then looked toward Lady Song, her tone softening slightly. “Lady Song, you need not think too much of it. There is still a long road ahead. Whatever is meant to be yours will come to you in time.”","Lady Song’s expression turned awkward, and she dared not say anything more.","Shen Yanshui still wore that gentle, smiling expression, but the way the others looked at her had clearly changed.","Lady Shen truly was not someone easy to deal with... And that made sense. If she had not possessed some ability, how could she have risen above all the other newcomers and become so conspicuous?","The Crown Princess said, “The matter is settled. Tomorrow morning, Lady Zhang and Lady Shen will accompany me to pay our respects to Her Majesty the Empress. The rest of you may leave for today.”","Shen Yanshui lowered her head and followed the others in bowing before taking her leave. She felt that if looks could kill, her body would by now be riddled with blades.","After everyone left Qifang Hall, Lady Chu naturally walked at the very front. Beside Shen Yanshui was Lady Sun, who was so thin that she looked almost skeletal. When Shen Yanshui saw her moving very slowly down the steps, she let her go ahead first.","Lady Sun smiled at her. “My health is poor. I hope I haven’t made a spectacle of myself before you, Sister.”","Seeing her emaciated appearance, Shen Yanshui could not help but speak earnestly. “Sister Sun, you’re still young, and you have a long life ahead of you. From now on, try to eat more nourishing food and take a little walk each day. Your health will gradually improve.”","Lady Sun froze for a moment, apparently not expecting her to say something like that. The smile at the corners of her lips became a little more genuine as she looked at Shen Yanshui and said gently, “Thank you.”","With that, she smiled at her and left with her attendants.","Xia An, who was beside Shen Yanshui, looked puzzled. “Mistress?”","Shen Yanshui let out a soft sigh. “Let’s go back.”","Could one miscarriage really turn a young woman in the prime of her life into someone who looked as though she were on the verge of death?","Shen Yanshui did not understand it. To her, there was nothing in this world more important than one’s own health."]},{"number":30,"title":"Chapter 30: Cui Yu: Don't Let Him Down","paragraphs":["The day seemed to pass especially quickly. Shen Yanshui spent the entire day watching Chunping and the others bustle about, preparing what she would wear for the following day.","The next morning was the fifth day of the fifth month, the Dragon Boat Festival. Dawn was breaking, and the eastern sky was just beginning to brighten.","With several people attending to her, Shen Yanshui took a bath infused with fragrant orchid herbs. According to Chunping, it could dispel toxins and ward off disasters, ensuring that everything went smoothly and safely for her that day.","Once she had finished getting ready, she also ate a little breakfast to settle her stomach.","Quanfu, waiting outside, softly reminded her, “Mistress, it is almost time.”","***","Shen Yanshui brought Chunping with her that day. Chunping was steadier in her dealings and inspired greater confidence. When the mistress and maid arrived at Xiefang Hall, they saw that Lady Zhang had already arrived.","Shen Yanshui gave a slight curtsy and exchanged greetings with her. The two were not familiar with each other, and since Lady Zhang showed no intention of speaking, Shen Yanshui was perfectly content to sit quietly.","Palace attendants brought them tea, fruit, and pastries. Seeing something she had never eaten before, Shen Yanshui picked one up and took a bite.","It was quite tasty.","After eating two small fruits, she felt a little thirsty and calmly drank half a cup of tea.","She had eaten very little at breakfast. Chunping and the others had refused to let her eat more, saying that if she ate too much, she might embarrass herself in front of the nobles, which would hardly be worth the cost.","Shen Yanshui had thought they made sense, so she had endured it after putting just a little food in her stomach.","But in this short while, her stomach had already begun to rebel.","She thought it over. She had no idea what the proceedings would be later. What if she grew so hungry that her stomach rumbled loudly in front of Her Majesty the Empress or the other honored guests? Would that not be even more embarrassing?","After silently agreeing with herself, Shen Yanshui smoothly picked up another small fruit and continued eating, slowly and delicately.","Her actions drew sidelong glances from the maids of Xiefang Hall.","Lady Zhang, who had been observing her in secret, lightly furrowed her willow-shaped brows. A faint trace of disapproval appeared on her face.","Shen ​​‌‌​‌‌​​‌‌​​​​‌​‌‌​​​‌‌​​‌‌‌​​‌​‌‌​​‌​‌​​‌‌​​‌‌​​‌‌​‌​‌​‌‌​​‌​​​​‌‌​‌​​​‌‌​​​​‌​‌‌​​​‌​​​‌‌‌​​​​​‌‌​​​​​‌‌​​‌​‌​​‌‌​‌​‌​‌‌​​​‌‌​​‌‌​​​​​​‌‌​‌‌​​​‌‌​​​​​​‌‌​​‌‌​​‌‌​​‌‌​‌‌​​‌​‌​​‌‌‌​​​​​‌‌​‌‌​‍Yanshui was extremely perceptive. Noticing that Lady Zhang kept glancing at her from time to time, she finally finished an entire plate of small fruits. Then she took a sip of tea, lightly dabbed at the corners of her mouth, and said with a gentle smile, “Sister Zhang, that dress of yours today really brings out your complexion.”","Lady Zhang was wearing a pomegranate-red jacket trimmed with pearls and a three-panel pleated skirt. A peony-and-pearl coronet adorned her head, along with a gold hairpin decorated with curling vines and dangling pearls. Compared with her usual fresh and delicate style, her appearance today was several shades more vivid and striking.","Hearing the compliment, which seemed entirely sincere, Lady Zhang paused for a moment. Then, somewhat self-consciously, she pressed her lips together and looked Shen Yanshui over once more.","A trace of envy rose in her heart, though her face remained courteous as she replied, “You are too kind, Sister Shen. You are the truly beautiful one.”","It was already May, and the weather grew hotter with each passing day. Shen Yanshui had deliberately chosen a light, misty-blue, chest-high ruqun for the occasion. Only the ties at her chest were a water-red shade. The combination of blue and red looked cool without seeming too plain.","Aside from a light lotus coronet made of pink cornelian, she wore only two translucent white jade hairpins in her coiffure. Around her wrist was a bracelet of pink-and-green tourmaline beads adorned with jade and other ornaments, while a matching misty-blue-and-pale-pink ribbon decorated her hair.","She looked like a touch of rouge blooming amid the misty green mountains after rain—an image of effortless beauty, as though both heavy makeup and a light touch suited her equally well. It was impossible not to be drawn to her.","The two women exchanged a few polite remarks. Before long, the Crown Princess emerged in full ceremonial dress.","They hurriedly rose and paid their respects.","The Crown Princess wore the distinctive purple robes of her rank and a seven-tailed phoenix crown. After looking at them both, her gaze settled on Shen Yanshui, and she said with a smile in her eyes, “There is no need for such formality. Rise. We must not keep His Highness waiting.”","After Shen Yanshui rose, she followed quietly behind the other two according to protocol, her heart filled with anticipation for the festivities at Jinming Lake.","Every year, the Jinming Lake gathering was a grand occasion celebrated throughout Shengjing, from the imperial court to the common streets. The lake would be filled not only with imperial relatives, aristocrats, and high officials, but also with ordinary people from the city. The two groups were separated only by Jinming Lake itself.","The most eagerly anticipated and widely discussed event was the dragon boat race. Its teams included various imperial guard units organized by the royal household, as well as teams selected from among the common people. The winning team would be granted an audience with the Emperor and Empress. If the Emperor took a liking to them, rising to prominence overnight was not unheard of.","There had been people who leaped from commoner status to official rank, ordinary imperial guardsmen who rose several levels at once, and competitors who won the favor of the Emperor and Empress and received generous rewards. Such things had all happened before. As a result, the Jinming Lake gathering had grown livelier with every passing year.","Shen Yanshui was lost in anticipation when she suddenly came back to herself and realized that they had already reached the front of Changqing Hall.","The Crown Prince stood there in a deep crimson official robe, a leather belt fastened around his waist and a jade crown atop his head. His figure was straight, his waist slender and legs long. His expression was composed and tranquil, yet the aura surrounding him made it impossible for anyone to overstep their bounds.","As Shen Yanshui bowed with the others to offer their greetings, she could not help stealing a few more glances at him.","Unexpectedly, their eyes met the next moment.","Shen Yanshui: “...”","She had been caught staring.","She blinked, then obediently pretended that she had done nothing at all.","Cui Yu swept his gaze over her. His eyes lingered briefly on the jade hairpins in her hair and the pink-and-green tourmaline bracelet half-hidden around her wrist. A faint smile glimmered in his eyes before he said in his calm voice, “Let us go.”","The Crown Princess led everyone to their feet.","Perhaps because she was worried that they were attending such an occasion for the first time and might make some mistake, bringing disgrace upon the Eastern Palace—or upon her as Crown Princess—the previous afternoon she had sent a matron to Lotusheart Court and Bamboo Fragrance Residence to explain the rules to them.","Thus, Shen Yanshui had a general understanding of the day’s arrangements.","After leaving the Eastern Palace, they would pass through the archery pavilion outside it and cross Jingyun Gate before accompanying the Crown Princess to Kunning Palace to pay their respects to Her Majesty the Empress, just like the families of civil and military officials and the wives of court nobles.","When the appointed time drew near, they would accompany Her Majesty the Empress to Donghua Gate.","The Crown Prince would part ways with them first, going to the Hall of Governmental Affairs to pay his respects to the Emperor. He would then proceed with the Emperor and the civil and military officials to Xuande Gate.","The Divine Martial Imperial Guards would clear the way. The imperial procession would leave through Xuande Gate, cross the main thoroughfare, pass through the inner and outer districts of Shengjing’s imperial city, and finally depart the outer city through Shuntian Gate, leading everyone to the imperial gardens at Jinming Lake.","When the Crown Prince left with his attendants, everyone once again bade him farewell. Shen Yanshui was among them.","Before departing, Cui Yu glanced sideways at her slightly bowed figure. His eyes grew solemn for a moment, but in the end he said nothing.","He hoped she would not disappoint him...","Shen Yanshui, of course, had no idea what he was thinking. She only remembered to follow properly behind the Crown Princess along the way, keeping her eyes lowered and her expression composed. She did not look at anything she ought not to see and spoke whenever she could avoid it, lest she invite trouble upon herself.","Yet when they went before Her Majesty the Empress, she still took advantage of the motion of her formal bow to steal a swift look at the person seated at the head of the hall.","She wore a phoenix crown and a crimson imperial empress’s robe embroidered with dark phoenix patterns. Her bearing was dignified and noble, her expression solemn and composed, and her eyes held a sharpness that made her seem imposing at first glance.","Her face was somewhat thin. Though faint lines had appeared at the corners of her eyes, they did nothing to diminish her overall presence. It was still clear that she was a stunningly beautiful woman.","Shen Yanshui had seen the Empress once before during the selection, but there had been many people present, and she had been standing toward the back of the crowd, quite a distance away. At the time, her goal had been to win Consort Liang’s favor—ideally, to enter the Fifth Prince’s residence—so she had paid little attention to the Empress, who had appeared only briefly.","It was still early, and there was no one else in Kunning Palace yet. After the Crown Princess led the two women forward to pay their respects, the Empress lowered her eyes and swept a glance over the two people behind the Crown Princess. Her voice was fairly gentle.","“There is no need for such ceremony. Rise. Give the Crown Princess a seat.”","After respectfully thanking her, the Crown Princess sat down below the Empress.","Shen Yanshui rose according to protocol and obediently stood behind the Crown Princess. At this distance, she was actually quite close to the Empress—no more than two meters away.","Shen Yanshui keenly noticed that the Empress’s breathing seemed slightly irregular. There was also the faint scent of bitter Chinese medicine clinging to her.","Come to think of it, now that she was closer, Shen Yanshui realized that the Crown Princess also carried a faint medicinal smell.","It was mostly concealed by the fragrance of her rouge and the incense clinging to her clothes, making it difficult for ordinary people to detect.","She had heard that Her Majesty the Empress had been in poor health over the past year. Having overworked herself, she had been taking medicine to recuperate.","The Crown Princess came to pay her respects to the Empress almost every day, so it was only natural that some of the medicinal scent had rubbed off on her.","The moment Shen Yanshui stood up, the Empress’s gaze settled on her face.","So this was Shen, the Lady Shen who had recently become quite favored by Yu, the Empress thought.","It was no wonder Yu had made exceptions for this woman and repeatedly bestowed rewards upon her with such a face.","She glanced at Matron Zhao beside her. Matron Zhao nodded, confirming her guess.","But the Empress said nothing more. She understood her child, and she trusted him.","She knew her son would not lose his head over a little feminine beauty. Thus, she treated the two women equally, asking them only a couple of questions. Seeing how Shen Yanshui kept her eyes lowered and answered with docility, the Empress smiled.","“Very good. You are both obedient and sensible. I hope you will bear more children for the Crown Prince and help continue the imperial line.”","As she spoke, she bestowed a bracelet upon each of Lady Zhang and Shen Yanshui.","Both women blushed shyly, lowered their heads, and murmured their assent.","Shen Yanshui forced her face to redden and pretended to be bashful, sighing inwardly.","Fortunately, she still had some acting skills.","It seemed that the matter of the Crown Prince’s heirs was a deep concern of Her Majesty the Empress. Matron Zhao, who had delivered the Empress’s verbal reward the last time, had said the same thing.","There was something wrong with the Crown Prince’s body.","Although nothing appeared amiss on the surface—in fact, once he took off his clothes, he was even more robust than ordinary men—and his natural endowment in certain areas was quite impressive, there was still... Ahem.","Actually, the first time, he had not lasted very long.","But perhaps because of her wood-element ability, whenever they engaged in intimate nighttime activities, not only did her ability grow stronger, but she also unknowingly regulated and repaired his body. It seemed that the Crown Prince grew stronger each time.","She had gone from being calm and perfectly in control the first time to later being unable to do anything but scramble away—only to find that she could not even crawl away.","Even now, she had not figured out what was behind it all. But since it was not a bad thing, she could not be bothered to investigate further.","As for bearing children... she was not at all fixated on becoming pregnant.","She would simply let nature take its course.","Lady Zhang noticed that the bracelet the Empress had given her was a rare, flawless red agate bangle, one that matched her outfit beautifully.","The one given to Lady Shen, however, was merely an ordinary green jade bracelet. Though it also suited her attire, it was clearly inferior to the red agate bangle in terms of rarity and value.","Lady Zhang could not help feeling even more pleased.","Compared with Lady Shen, this meant that the Empress favored her more.","Shen Yanshui’s peach-blossom eyes curved into a smile, and she sincerely said, “Thank you for the reward, Your Majesty the Empress.” As she spoke, she slipped the bracelet onto her left wrist.","She did not care what the Empress had given anyone else. All she knew was that Her Majesty the Empress was truly a wonderful person. The last time, she had given Shen Yanshui a great many things, and now, merely by coming to pay her respects, she had received another nice bracelet.","Naturally, she was delighted.","The Empress and Nanny Fan fell silent for a moment when they saw how plainly her joy showed on her face, making it clear at a glance that she was not a scheming person.","“Thank you for the reward, Your Majesty the Empress.”","Although Lady Zhang was nervous in the Empress’s presence, she behaved with grace and composure. She did not wish to appear petty or provincial, and managed to maintain her poise.","The Empress watched the two women with a smile, while the Crown Princess also began to speak.","It was only after the two of them started talking that Shen Yanshui sensed something was off.","From their words, it seemed that the relationship between them was not quite as “a mother and daughter-in-law filled with affection” as the rumors claimed.","Before she could think about it any further, Kunning Palace began to grow lively, both inside and out.","The Eastern Palace was neither especially near nor especially far from Kunning Palace, but the Crown Princess had deliberately come early. Quite a few high-ranking consorts from the inner palace would be attending the gathering at Jinming Pool later, and some were practically her elders. Naturally, she could not have those senior women wait for her, a junior.","By now, consorts from the eastern and western palaces who were qualified to attend the gathering at Jinming Pool had begun arriving at Kunning Palace to pay their respects. Noble ladies from outside the imperial family also entered the palace with their younger relatives. The sounds of greetings, kneeling, and formal salutations rang out without pause.","Shen Yanshui remained standing properly behind the Crown Princess, serving as a quiet backdrop while secretly taking in the dazzling procession and pricking up her ears to listen.","Before long, the main hall of Kunning Palace had become bustling with activity. Those seated in the main hall rather than being directed to the side hall or reception room were either imperial relatives and aristocrats or ladies of particularly noble status.","During this time, Shen Yanshui also saw her elder half-sister, Lady Shen, enter behind Noble Consort Lan.","She only glanced at her once. Seeing that the woman looked radiant and beautiful, Shen Yanshui did not pay her any further attention.","She was merely an inconspicuous nobody in the hall. No one would bother noticing a low-ranking concubine of the Eastern Palace, and Shen Yanshui was perfectly happy to remain unnoticed.","She simply kept her head lowered and her ears perked up, listening to the people around her exchange pleasantries with bright smiles while engaging in all sorts of subtle verbal duels.","At first, she found it rather interesting. Some of their words twisted through several layers of implication; unless one thought carefully, it was impossible to figure out what they were really saying.","But after listening for too long, her head began to buzz, and unseen by anyone else, her eyes practically spun with little coils of smoke.","Being one of the people at the very top was no easy task. If this was how life went every day, she wondered how many brain cells would die.","Would it shorten one’s life?","Just as she was beginning to feel bored and wondering when they would finally set out for Jinming Pool, a soft, melodious voice rang out with a smile.","“The woman standing behind the Crown Princess must be Lady Shen of the Crown Prince’s Eastern Palace, mustn’t she? Lady Shen and Lady Shen of this palace are sisters from the same family. From now on, the two of you should be closer. You’re blood relatives, after all—surely you mustn’t grow distant.”","The main hall, which had been filled with laughter and conversation, fell silent at once.","Shen Yanshui raised her eyes and saw the woman seated to the Empress’s lower right—that was to say, directly opposite the Crown Princess.","She was a stunning beauty, with her hair swept into a high coiffure, thick sideburns framing her face, and phoenix eyes beneath willow-shaped brows. Smiling brightly, she was looking straight at Shen Yanshui.","If the beauty’s words had not carried such a sharp barb, Shen Yanshui would have liked listening to that gentle, faintly seductive voice.","The moment Noble Consort Lan finished speaking, Shen Yanshui noticed quite a few covert glances falling upon her.","Everyone with eyes knew that Noble Consort Lan and the Empress were at odds. What was more, most of those present were shrewd and experienced, so no one dared speak rashly.","Over the past six months, Noble Consort Lan’s son, the Fourth Prince, had repeatedly earned the Emperor’s praise. Not long ago, he had even received an appointment in the imperial court and been allowed to participate in state affairs. No one dared offend Noble Consort Lan without careful consideration.","Shen Yanshui lowered her head and inclined herself slightly. With an unchanged expression, she replied gently, “When my sister and I were at home, we were naturally bound by ties of blood. But now that we have both entered the palace, I am merely a lowly lady of the Eastern Palace. I ought to observe the rules of the imperial family first and distinguish rank and order. I would not dare overstep my place.”","Back home, she and this legitimate elder sister had never been close, nor had they shared much affection. Her elder sister had even looked down on her for being lazy, fond of good food and amusements, and unwilling to do anything “proper.”","Closer? Closer to what?","If not for this legitimate elder sister of hers, she might well have had her marriage arranged by now. A whole host of good days ahead of her had been ruined by a single letter from her sister.","If Shen Yanshui had not been so easygoing and able to take things in stride, she might have wanted to kill her elder sister by now."]},{"number":31,"title":"Chapter 31: Her Majesty the Empress is awesome","paragraphs":["“Lady Shen speaks wisely. Once one enters the imperial family, the first thing one must uphold from then on is the imperial family’s rules.” The Empress glanced at Noble Consort Lan and said slowly, “I heard that Lady Shen was personally selected by Noble Consort Lan. It seems Your Consortship has a discerning eye for people—you did not choose wrongly.”","The smile on Noble Consort Lan’s face did not change. “Your Majesty flatters me. Entrusted by His Majesty and Your Majesty, it is only right that I do my utmost.” As she spoke, she turned her gaze toward the docile-looking Shen Yanshui and said with a smile, “Just look—doesn’t Lady Shen have quite a clever little tongue?”","Lady Shen, seated behind her, was somewhat surprised as well. She was four years older than this half-sister of hers, and there was the distinction between legitimate and concubine-born daughters. They had not interacted much in ordinary times.","All she had known was that this younger half-sister, who had become remarkably eye-catching at such a young age, was unlearned and extraordinarily indolent. She had always looked down on her for it.","She had never expected her to be so quick-witted, nor to show the slightest timidity in such an occasion.","It made Lady Shen regard her somewhat more highly. What a pity... she had entered the Crown Prince’s Eastern Palace.","Her gaze shifted to the Crown Princess, who sat before her with a poised and appropriate smile, then finally settled on the Crown Princess’s abdomen, where there was as yet no visible sign. Her eyes darkened slightly.","She remembered that news of the Crown Princess’s pregnancy had been announced only today.","But in her previous life, she had already begun to fall out of the Emperor’s favor and had not gone to Jinming Pool with the others.","She remembered it so clearly because she had later heard that, during the gathering at Jinming Pool, the Crown Princess had suffered a miscarriage by accident.","The Empress had flown into a rage afterward and punished a great many people, shaking the entire palace.","In the end, it was discovered that a maid serving the Fourth Prince’s consort had been responsible. The Fourth Prince consequently lost the Emperor’s favor and was severely punished, while the Eldest Prince, who had been in charge of security for the Jinming Pool gathering, was implicated as well.","It was only after that that the Sixth Prince gradually began to stand out among the many princes.","Shen Yanshui keenly sensed her elder half-sister’s brief glance toward her, but paid it no mind.","Hearing Noble Consort Lan steer past the earlier topic of their “deep sisterly affection” and merely allude to her being “quick-tongued,” Shen Yanshui quietly relaxed. Nor did she care about the faint barb hidden in the consort’s final words.","She merely lowered her eyes, bowed her head, and smiled with her lips pressed together. A faint blush rose on her face, as though she were a little embarrassed by the praise, and she said nothing further.","“Cough, cough.”","In an instant, everyone’s attention turned to the Empress at the head of the gathering, and many voices expressed their concern.","“It is merely an old ailment; there is no cause for worry.” Having said this, the Empress covered her lips and coughed twice more. Her calm yet faintly imposing eyes swept over the crowd as she said unhurriedly with a smile, “It seems to me that the hour is about right. We may continue our idle chatter once we arrive at Jinming Pool, while we enjoy the festivities.”","Everyone rose and bowed. “Yes, Your Majesty.”","★","After leaving Kunning Palace, sedan chairs were already waiting outside. The sky was clear and cloudless, stretching for miles without a trace of haze.","The Empress’s phoenix carriage led the way. The Crown Princess, the high-ranking consorts, and the consorts of the married princes followed behind. Several elderly princess consorts and first-rank titled ladies had also been granted sedan chairs, while the rest proceeded on foot along either side.","Among the crowd, Shen Yanshui caught sight of her stepmother and the younger girls from her household. After a single glance, she withdrew her gaze.","She saw Countess Zhongyi, and Countess Zhongyi naturally saw her as well. At the sight of Shen Yanshui’s face, radiant as a spring blossom, Countess Zhongyi felt her chest tighten with resentment.","This Fourth Miss had apparently been feigning her usual laziness and meekness. The moment an opportunity arose, she had clawed her way into the Eastern Palace. Not only would she be of no help to Hua’er, but she might even drag her down in the future.","“Mother, Fourth Sister is only a Zhaoxun. Is she really qualified to attend the Golden Bright Pool gathering?” the fifth young lady, born of the principal wife, asked softly.","The sixth young lady, whose cheeks still bore a touch of baby fat, watched Shen Yanshui’s retreating figure and said with certainty, “Fourth Sister is so beautiful. His Highness the Crown Prince is sure to like her.”","Countess Zhongyi pressed her lips together and said nothing. She knew full well how lovely her fourth daughter was. She had originally intended to send her into the palace to support Hua’er, yet who would have thought the girl would dare to defy her parents?","Still, what woman in the palace could do without the support of her natal family? Sooner or later, she would come begging at their door.","*","Shen Yanshui had no idea what her stepmother was thinking. Had she known, she would probably have rolled her eyes on the spot.","At the moment, she was quietly walking behind the Crown Princess’s sedan chair. By coincidence, Lady Shen—her elder sister—was walking beside her.","Though perhaps it was not much of a coincidence. By the rules of etiquette, although the Crown Princess belonged to the younger generation, her rank was second only to the Empress’s, even higher than Noble Consort Lan’s. Just as they had been seated in the main hall of Kunming Palace earlier: the Crown Princess sat below the Empress on her left, while Noble Consort Lan sat on her right. The sedan chairs of the other princes’ consorts had been placed behind those of the Four Consorts.","★","At present, the Crown Princess and Noble Consort Lan were following behind the Empress. Naturally, Shen Yanshui and Lady Shen were walking behind their sedan chairs.","“It has been a long time since I last saw you, Fourth Sister. You seem much sharper now, and your tongue has grown far more eloquent,” Lady Shen said with a smile, lowering her voice. After all, Shen Yanshui had even dared to contradict Noble Consort Lan to her face.","Shen Yanshui replied in a soft voice, her smile not reaching her eyes, “I am not even a tenth as clever as Your Ladyship. Otherwise, Your Ladyship would not be seeing me here today.”","Her words were far from polite. She was referring to the letter that had sent her into the palace.","Though she had quickly thought matters through and come to terms with entering the palace, and no longer felt overly angry about it, she had not forgotten that letter.","Besides, no matter what happened today, even if the two of them did not openly trade barbs, they still had to make it clear to onlookers that they were not on good terms.","Of course, there was no need to overdo it. They simply had to display the distant relationship they had always had.","Lady Shen’s expression shifted slightly. In her memory, her fourth sister had almost never talked back to her. Whenever she caught Shen Yanshui neglecting her studies or being lazy and undisciplined, she had rebuked her without mercy, and Shen Yanshui had always meekly accepted it. When had she ever dared to answer back?","For a moment, Lady Shen did not know how to respond.","When she recovered, she felt surprise, then amusement, and... disdain. With a quiet laugh, she said, “It seems Fourth Sister has indeed been living rather well in the Eastern Palace these past days.”","Naturally, many people kept a close eye on the affairs of the Eastern Palace, and scraps of news inevitably leaked out. She knew that her fourth sister had recently won quite a measure of the Crown Prince’s favor, but she had not expected that a little favor, after such a short time, would give her so much confidence that she dared speak to her so bluntly.","Though somewhat displeased, Lady Shen remembered that her letter had indeed turned what had once been her fourth sister’s smooth and promising life into a dead end. In the end, she did not press the matter further. There was even a trace of pity in the way she looked at Shen Yanshui.","Shen Yanshui caught the look in her eyes, her mind full of questions. But seeing that she had quieted down, she did not make a point of finding something else to say.","By the time the Empress led the noblewomen of the inner and outer courts to Xuande Gate, the Emperor and Crown Prince had also arrived with the civil and military officials.","What followed was a round of mutual bows and formal greetings. Shen Yanshui did not even get a proper look at the Emperor before kneeling with the others to kowtow and pay her respects. All she had time to glimpse was the hem of his dark, gold-edged robe embroidered with dragon motifs.","Emperor Pingkang’s voice was far gentler than she had imagined.","“Rise.”","“Thank you, Your Majesty,” everyone replied in unison as they rose.","Once she was on her feet, Shen Yanshui swiftly glanced up and finally saw what Emperor Pingkang looked like.","He wore dark imperial robes and a Tongtian crown. His face was fair and lean, his features well formed, but the looseness of his skin was already evident, making the shadows beneath his eyes particularly noticeable.","He was tall and slender, with a beard along his jaw. A smile rested on his face, giving him an air of both authority and gentleness.","The Divine Martial Imperial Guards cleared the way. The Emperor’s carriage led the procession, followed by the Empress’s phoenix carriage, while the rest proceeded in order of rank.","Before boarding her carriage, Shen Yanshui glanced ahead and saw the Crown Prince mount his horse with swift, practiced ease. He rode beside the imperial carriage as part of its guard, with several princes following close behind.","Once inside her carriage, Shen Yanshui did not look any further. Before long, the carriage beneath her began to move slowly.","All around them rose the cries of the people of Shengjing, kneeling in the streets and shouting blessings of “Long live the Emperor! Long live the Empress!” Through a gap in the carriage curtain, Shen Yanshui gradually caught sight of Shengjing’s bustling streets, overflowing with festive cheer.","Though she had seen such a Shengjing many times before, she could not help but feel sincerely delighted and uplifted by the peace and holiday celebration that filled the city.","They passed through the inner city and then the outer city, eventually arriving at the heavily guarded Jinming Pool.","Jinming Pool was vast. It had been an artificial lake excavated by the founding emperor of Great Yong for naval exercises. Walls surrounded it, with several gates set into them. The northwestern corner served as the inlet, while the main southern entrance was the Lingxing Gate.","From the southern shore to the center of the pool stretched an enormous arched bridge—the Immortal Bridge—several hundred paces long and broad across, its surface lined with fluttering colored banners. Guards in armor, sabers at their waists, stood in neat ranks with their heads held high. Palace maids and eunuchs attended to their respective duties, standing quietly with lowered eyes.","At the bridgehead stood the Baojin Tower, five halls joined together. At the far end of the Immortal Bridge lay the center of the lake, where layered halls and jade-like pavilions rose amid rare flowers and strange stones, exotic birds and precious fowl. Shipyards, docks, warships, and dragon boats were all in place.","Willows dipped their branches into the water, while a haze of grass spread along the embankments.","North of the bridge, near the eastern shore, stood the waterside Linshui Hall, facing north. In previous years, Emperor Pingkang had hosted banquets for his officials there. At present, he had already taken his seat with the civil and military ministers.","Meanwhile, Shen Yanshui followed the Empress and the Crown Princess to the Watermoon Pavilion, not far from Linshui Hall, where they took their seats according to protocol. She let out a quiet breath. At last, they had arrived.","The Empress sat in the center. To her left sat the Crown Princess, the wives of the First, Second, and Fourth Princes, as well as several high-ranking female members of the imperial clan.","Shen Yanshui’s seat had been arranged in the second row, still positioned behind and slightly to one side of the Crown Princess. Beside her, seated closer to the Crown Princess, was Lady Zhang.","Seated on the other side was Secondary Consort Tang from the Eldest Prince’s residence. Apart from exchanging polite greetings at the beginning, the two had not spoken further.","Shen Yanshui was quite satisfied with her seat. It was one of the best viewing spots at Jinming Pool, and with only a single row of people in front of her, nothing obstructed her view.","She turned her gaze toward the eastern bank. In previous years, she had always come with her maidservants to watch the festivities from the temporary awnings erected there.","Sure enough, when she looked over, she saw many commoners already gathered beneath them, their faces bright with smiles and laughter.","A smile rose to her own lips as well.","The palace halls stood lofty and grand, banners snapping in the wind. After the Emperor and Empress each delivered a brief address, palace maids and eunuchs who had long been waiting filed in, carrying assorted rice dumplings and fruits, which they set before the guests on their tables.","Then the drums began to thunder.","The opening water-pageant performance had begun.","There ​​‌‌​‌‌​​‌‌​​​​‌​‌‌​​​‌‌​‌‌​​​​‌​‌‌​​‌​‌​‌‌​​‌​‌​​‌‌‌​​​​​‌‌​​​‌​​‌‌​‌​​​‌‌​​​​‌​‌‌​​​‌​​​‌‌‌​​​​​‌‌​​​​​‌‌​​‌​‌​​‌‌​‌​‌​‌‌​​​‌‌​​‌‌​​​​​​‌‌​‌‌​​​‌‌​​‌​​​‌‌​​‌‌​​‌‌​​‌​​​‌‌​‌‌‌​‌‌​​‌‌​​‌‌​​​‌​‍were countless water spectacles: the annual Dragon Boat Festival naval battle drill; a variety show in which Celestial Master Zhang drove away evil and prayed for disaster relief; dragon boat races; amusing water puppets; the highly entertaining water swings; and the fiercely contested dragon boat bidding races...","Shen Yanshui came to watch every year, yet each year brought no shortage of new delights.","Even she, a modern-born person who could be considered widely experienced, found herself engrossed. Needless to say, for the capital’s common folk—who had far fewer entertainments available—this event, attended by the Emperor and Empress themselves as they celebrated alongside the people, drew immense crowds both inside and outside Jinming Pool every Dragon Boat Festival. It was lively beyond compare.","“This year’s variety performance is quite impressive. Reward them,” the Empress said with a gentle smile.","“Yes, Your Majesty.” At once, a palace maid accepted the rewards with a beaming expression and carried them down.","“As long as Her Majesty the Empress is pleased, I am relieved. I have not failed the trust placed in me by Your Majesty and His Majesty,” Consort De said with a smile from nearby.","Shen Yanshui reached for a small rice dumpling tied with five-colored silk thread. Rather than having Chunping do it, she unwrapped it herself at an unhurried pace. As she watched the water swings in the distance, she also spared a little attention for Consort De.","As far as she knew, Consort De had been born a palace maid. In her youth, her beauty had caught the Emperor’s eye, and fortune had favored her as well. At the time, the imperial harem had either produced no children at all, or the princes who were born had failed to survive. Yet she had given birth to the Eldest Prince and the Second Prince in succession—and both had lived to adulthood.","Thus, despite Consort De’s humble family background, she still held one of the Four Consort positions.","Hearing this, Noble Consort Lan smiled alluringly. “Her Majesty the Empress has been unwell, and Consort De has gone to great lengths for today’s event. I heard that even when a new little imperial grandson was recently born in the Eldest Prince’s household, she had no time to attend to it. Her Majesty truly ought to reward Consort De generously.”","“Could it be that Elder Sister Consort De has so many grandchildren that she no longer finds them precious?” Another teasing, smiling voice chimed in. Beauty Li, whose features were exquisitely lovely, said with a laugh, “Among all of us sisters, Elder Sister Consort De has the least to worry about. The Eldest Prince has only been married for five years, yet he already has five little imperial grandsons and three little imperial granddaughters. It truly makes one terribly envious.”","Before the words had even finished falling, Shen Yanshui keenly sensed the vague, probing gazes around them settling upon the members of the Eastern Palace—especially the Crown Princess.","Shen Yanshui: “...All right. So this round is aimed at the Eastern Palace.”","Sure enough, at an occasion like this, it was impossible to simply sit back and enjoy the show. Still, having long been mentally prepared, she remained quite calm.","Even if the sky came crashing down, the Empress and the Crown Princess were in front of her to hold it up. She was merely a minor Zhaoxun of the Eastern Palace—what was there for her to worry about?","Holding the zongzi she had just unwrapped, she inhaled its fragrant aroma and took a bite. Half of it disappeared in one mouthful. Mm, savory pork filling. It tasted quite good.","Lady Zhang, whose nerves had been wound tight: “...??”","“...?” Secondary Consort Tang could not help but glance sideways, watching Shen Yanshui take a second bite as though she had heard nothing at all...","How could she remain so utterly composed?","And then... Secondary Consort Tang lifted her eyes toward the Crown Princess, whose expression was serene and whose lips still bore a faint smile. A trace of puzzlement arose in her heart.","Under ordinary circumstances, the Crown Princess would surely have been unable to maintain that smile after hearing such remarks.","What was different today? Had she gone somewhere to cultivate inner peace or something?","Secondary Consort Tang was curious.","The smile on Consort De’s face did not change, and her voice remained as gentle as ever. “Your Highness Noble Consort, Sister Beauty Li, please do not tease me. The more children one has, the more debts one owes. Not one of those boys of mine gives me any peace of mind. They are nothing like the Crown Princess, who has raised her child so well. I heard His Majesty say that the little imperial grandson’s health has been improving by the day.”","As she spoke, her brows curved in a smile and her tone became reflective. “We have all been mothers, so we understand the hardships involved. Not only has the Crown Princess managed the Eastern Palace in impeccable order and served the Empress with filial devotion, she has also cared for the little imperial grandson so well that his health continues to improve. She is truly worthy of being Crown Princess—a model for all women who marry into the imperial family. The other sisters-in-law and younger generations should all learn from her.”","Shen Yanshui watched in every direction and listened intently.","On the surface, Consort De’s words seemed to speak up for the Eastern Palace and the Crown Princess. Yet to Shen Yanshui’s ears, that was not entirely the case...","The fact that the Crown Prince had punished two newly arrived concubines of the Eastern Palace within a single month was no great secret. How could Consort De possibly not have heard of it?","And then there was her remark—though subtle—that “not one of those boys gives me peace of mind.” Was that not a jab straight at the Empress’s sore spot?","After all, everyone knew how few heirs the Eastern Palace had.","Not to mention the lavish praise she had heaped upon the Crown Princess afterward, practically drawing hatred toward her.","In just those few sentences, Shen Yanshui had nearly analyzed every word and phrase. It truly was rather mentally exhausting.","The Crown Princess pressed her lips together in a smile, her back unconsciously straightening a little. “Serving Mother Empress with filial devotion and looking after the child are duties I ought to fulfill as her daughter-in-law. I do not deserve Your Ladyship’s praise. The Liangdi of the Eastern Palace is currently with child; in another two or three months, she will likely present His Majesty with another little imperial grandson.”","Shen Yanshui: “...?” No, Crown Princess... was she actually taking that seriously?","The smile on Noble Consort Lan’s face was nearly impossible to contain as she said delightedly, “Oh my, the Crown Princess truly is exceptionally filial! Dignified and virtuous as well. Elder Sister Consort De was absolutely right.”","The Empress glanced at the Crown Princess, then shifted her gaze to the water, where an elaborate water-swing performance was underway. In an even, indifferent tone, she said, “The Fourth Prince has twenty or thirty wives and concubines in his household. If Noble Consort Lan has nothing better to do, she might as well help him manage his domestic affairs. Don’t let trouble break out every other day and make a laughingstock of yourselves.”","Whoa! Shen Yanshui’s eyes instantly widened.","As Noble Consort Lan’s smile gradually faded, an especially loud announcement rang out in Shen Yanshui’s mind—","First Blood!","The next moment, the Empress, whose bearing had become all the more commanding, unhurriedly took a sip of tea. Her phoenix eyes lifted slightly as she said with a faint smile, “A few days ago, I heard that the Second Prince forcibly took a handsome young man back to his residence...”","Consort De’s face turned deathly pale. The kingfisher-feather-and-mother-of-pearl nail guard on her finger nearly snapped!","Hadn’t she ordered the matter dealt with and suppressed immediately? How did the Empress still know about it?","Once again, Shen Yanshui heard in her mind—","Double Kill!","Consort De no longer sounded as composed as before. Earnestly, she said, “Your Majesty, I don’t know where this rumor came from, but it absolutely cannot be trusted. Though the Second Prince is somewhat dissolute, he is not so lacking in restraint as to do such a thing.”","The Empress glanced at her and smiled lightly. “Oh? Is that so?”","Though she said nothing further, that calm, unruffled gaze left Consort De feeling increasingly uncertain. Perhaps the Empress truly did know something...","She promptly and sensibly yielded. “Please rest assured, Your Majesty. The Second Prince has indeed become more and more unruly of late, allowing such rumors to spread and offend Your Majesty’s ears. When I return, I will give him a severe reprimand, make him understand the gravity of his conduct, and teach him a proper lesson.”","Shen Yanshui’s eyes sparkled.","Triple Kill!","Her Majesty the Empress is magnificent!","From where Shen Yanshui sat, she could only see the Empress’s profile. Yet it was precisely that profile that made her suddenly realize that the Crown Prince and the Empress bore a five- or six-tenths resemblance to one another.","At first glance, it might not have been obvious. But from the side, when those naturally sharp phoenix eyes tilted upward ever so slightly, their brows and eyes looked as much as sixty or seventy percent alike.","So handsome!","The Empress happened to glance back and noticed the almost entirely undisguised gaze from behind her. To her surprise, she met a pair of beautiful peach-blossom eyes shining with admiration.","And when she saw who it was, the Empress: “...”"]},{"number":32,"title":"Chapter 32: White, Soft, Plump, and Bulging","paragraphs":["Even Consort De had backed down. Beauty Li, who had spoken up earlier, fell silent the moment the Empress glanced at her, shrinking like a quail and not daring to utter another word.","Yet she could not help feeling puzzled. Had she not heard that Her Majesty the Empress’s health had been worsening these past days?","Otherwise, how could the recent selection of consorts have been entrusted entirely to Noble Consort Lan and the Four Consorts?","Having been rebuked so bluntly, Noble Consort Lan’s smile faded. Her gaze seemed to drift over the Empress, splendidly dressed in regal finery, as though she wished to peer through her carefully made-up face and discern her true complexion.","No one knew better than she did what was wrong with the Empress’s health. During the selection, the Empress ought to have been too ill to hold herself up. How could she now appear so full of vigor, her bearing as commanding as it had been two or three years ago?","Where no one could see, the Empress’s fingernails dug deeply into her palm. She endured the discomfort in her body and continued to sit calmly upon her throne, her expression serene.","As they watched the Empress, so poised and majestic, everyone had their own thoughts. Yet without exception, no one dared make veiled remarks targeting the Eastern Palace again.","The older hands in the palace all knew the Empress’s temperament. Two or three years ago, who would have dared show her the slightest disrespect?","But then the Little Imperial Uncle of the Duke of Feng’s household had become the battle-tested and illustrious Great General Qi, and the political situation at court had shifted.","Over the past year, the Empress had also fallen ill. More importantly, there was His Majesty’s favor... Only then had the balance of power within the palace gradually begun to change.","The Crown Princess sat closest to the Empress. Moreover, she paid her respects to her mother-in-law frequently. Though nothing could be seen from the Empress’s expression, she did not believe that her mother-in-law had truly recovered.","She understood that the Empress was forcing herself to endure her illness rather than show weakness before the others.","But she did not understand why the Empress had been so merciless. Would that not only make Noble Consort Lan and Consort De resent the Eastern Palace even more?","Consort De in particular came from humble origins. The First and Second Princes had virtually no maternal family influence to rely on. Why not win her over and bring her into the Eastern Palace’s camp?","After all, Noble Consort Lan, born into the Chancellor’s household, and her Fourth Prince were their greatest enemies in the Eastern Palace, were they not?","Naturally, Shen Yanshui knew nothing of the Crown Princess’s thoughts—thoughts which, even in her eyes, would have seemed exceedingly naive.","She merely noticed again, with keen perception, that after the Empress looked toward her, the Empress’s breathing seemed to grow even more labored.","This time, she did not hesitate. Secretly, she sent a thread of her supernatural ability into the Empress’s body. Guiding it swiftly through the Empress from head to toe, she then withdrew it.","Her heart sank at once. The Empress’s condition... was not good.","Judging only by her present appearance, no one would have guessed how frail she truly was. The condition of her internal organs was not what it should have been for someone of her age; they had begun to weaken. This went far beyond mere exhaustion from overwork.","For the Empress, the best course now would be to consult the finest physician at once, take medicine, and rest while she recovered.","But given the current situation, the Empress likely could not afford to recuperate in peace. And at such an important public occasion, she could show weakness even less.","Her earlier probe with her supernatural ability had given Shen Yanshui a fairly clear understanding of the situation. There was no single problem with the Empress’s body; rather, for some unknown reason, her entire constitution was gradually deteriorating.","If the root cause could not be found, then her meager ability would not be enough to heal her completely.","Just then, Noble Consort Lan calmly lifted her wine cup, smiling as she said, “Today is the Dragon Boat Festival. This concubine offers a toast to Your Majesty the Empress. Calamus and realgar wine dispels poison and wards off misfortune. May Your Majesty recover soon—and may Your Majesty be merciful and magnanimous enough not to hold this concubine’s past offenses against her.”","Shen Yanshui glanced at Noble Consort Lan, whose smile bloomed as brightly as a flower. Like Consort De, she appeared to be using the toast to humble herself and show weakness, yet Shen Yanshui could not shake the feeling that she was up to no good.","Calamus and realgar wine was warming in nature. It could warm the channels, dispel cold and dampness, clear phlegm, and calm the mind to aid sleep. Ordinarily, even someone somewhat frail would benefit from drinking it. But for the Empress, in her present condition, that might not be the case...","After Noble Consort Lan spoke, she gave a meaningful glance. Beauty Li and Lady Shen, seated beside her, immediately raised their cups with smiles and said respectfully, “This concubine also offers a toast to Your Majesty the Empress. May Your Majesty recover soon, and may you enjoy lasting joy and peace.”","Seeing this, the others also raised their cups in succession and toasted the Empress. “May Your Majesty enjoy peace and good health this Dragon Boat Festival, and lasting joy and peace.”","Shen Yanshui frowned. Noble Consort Lan had backed the Empress into a corner; it seemed she had no choice but to drink.","Sure enough, the Empress calmly lifted her cup with a smile...","With a silent sigh, Shen Yanshui summoned her ability and instantly sent its power into the Empress’s meridians, organs, and limbs.","The moment the wine entered her stomach, Shen Yanshui could clearly sense, through her ability, the tension that seized the Empress’s entire body. Yet to the naked eye, the Empress still wore the same composed smile, without the slightest sign of anything amiss.","The Empress absolutely could not collapse—not on a day like this. Shen Yanshui still hoped to continue living safely and peacefully in the Eastern Palace.","But her ability was still too weak. In order to help the Empress hold on, she had used nearly two-thirds of her power before finally stopping.","She needed to conserve what remained, so that she could ensure her own safety under any circumstances.","At her side, Lady Zhang set down her wine cup and suddenly asked softly, “Sister Shen, are you feeling unwell?”","The change in Shen Yanshui’s complexion was not especially obvious, but she was visibly less spirited, like an eggplant wilted by frost.","Shen Yanshui touched her stomach with one hand and replied with a smile, “Thank you for your concern, Sister Zhang. I’m merely a little hungry.” Hungry enough to eat an entire cow in one sitting.","As she spoke, her hand reached for one of the rice dumplings laid out beside her.","The Empress clenched her wine cup tightly, unable to conceal the astonishment in her heart.","What was going on?","A warm breeze had swept across the pond just moments ago, and it was as though that breeze had blown away the chronic affliction within her. Her body had not felt this light in a very long time. Even her breathing had become much easier, no longer pulling at her internal organs and causing pain.","She could not help lowering her eyes to the wine cup in her hand.","“This wine...”","Noble Consort Lan’s eyes deepened slightly as she put on a look of concern. “What’s wrong with the wine? Is Her Majesty the Empress feeling unwell? Shall we summon the imperial physicians at once to examine her?”","The Crown Princess could not help frowning.","The Empress glanced at Noble Consort Lan. Once she was feeling better, even the face of someone she had previously found hateful seemed far more pleasing to her. For once, a genuine smile appeared on her lips.","“I believe your prayers may have come true, Consort. Just now, I was feeling somewhat unwell, but after drinking this cup of wine, I feel light and refreshed all over.”","Noble Consort Lan: “...”","Could it be that the Empress had truly recovered?","She immediately rejected the thought. Impossible!","Then what, exactly, had gone wrong?","Lady Shen: “...?”","She could not help stealing a glance at the Empress, who looked radiant with health.","In her previous life, the Crown Princess had miscarried. Even after the culprit was eventually identified, the Empress had fallen ill because of it. Less than half a year later, she had passed away.","Lady Shen suspected that it was the Crown Princess’s miscarriage and the resulting damage to her health—which made it difficult for her to conceive again—that had dealt the Empress such a devastating blow, ultimately leaving her bedridden and unable to recover.","She looked toward the Crown Princess again. Seeing no movement from her, she instead caught sight of her younger half-sister eating as though she had been starved for years.","Lady Shen’s brows drew together slightly.","Just as she was praying that no one would notice her half-sister, she heard the brief, mocking giggle of the Fourth Prince’s Secondary Consort.","“Oh my, could it be that Her Highness the Crown Princess didn’t give Lady Shen enough to eat? Heavens above, how did she end up looking so famished?”","Lady Shen: “...”","Not only had she embarrassed the Eastern Palace, she had also brought shame upon the Earl Zhongyi’s household!","Shen Yanshui lifted her eyes. She was elegantly finishing her ninth little zongzi, entirely ignoring the meaningful gazes directed at her from every side. Only after swallowing it did she take an unhurried sip of tea, then turn toward the Empress with an expression of apparent confusion.","Her brows were like spring mountains, and her peach-blossom face now held a hint of bashfulness. In a sincere tone, she said, “I hope I haven’t made a spectacle of myself before Your Majesty. I was just thinking that these zongzi were gifts from His Majesty and Her Majesty. If I left them uneaten, wouldn’t that be wasting their kindness?”","Her cheeks flushed like the rosy clouds of dawn as she continued timidly, “As it happened, I was feeling a little peckish, so I ate a couple more. This is my first time attending such an occasion, and I didn’t understand the rules. I never realized that one wasn’t supposed to eat too many of these zongzi. I hope Your Majesty will be gracious and not punish me.”","The proud, disdainful expression on Secondary Consort Liao’s face changed at once.","The Empress glanced sideways at her, a smile spreading across her face. “Since these zongzi have been bestowed upon you, you may naturally eat as many as you like. An appetite is a blessing. If they are not enough, I have more here.”","As she spoke, she instructed the palace maid attending her to give Shen Yanshui the zongzi on the table beside her.","Someone chimed in with a laugh, “Precisely. These are gifts from His Majesty and Her Majesty the Empress. By eating more, aren’t you simply taking all that good fortune into your belly? These nine-seed zongzi are sure to help Lady Shen conceive a child soon.”","Shen Yanshui froze for a moment before realizing that the “nine-seed zongzi” carried the auspicious implication of praying for children. She could not help feeling rather speechless.","Yet there was nothing she could explain. She merely rose, curtsied, and said with a smile, “Thank you, Your Highness.”","The Crown Princess cast her a sidelong glance, a chill glinting in her eyes.","Having failed to gain any advantage, Secondary Consort Liao was given a fierce glare by Noble Consort Lan. Her face turned pale, and she lowered her head, secretly biting her lip.","That Shen Yanshui was good for nothing but eating—a complete fool—yet she had somehow entered the Crown Prince’s Eastern Palace and even won his favor. What outrageously good luck!","*","“Father Emperor! Is the dragon boat race about to begin?” The ten-year-old Ninth Prince, delicate-featured and still carrying a touch of baby fat in his cheeks, asked excitedly as he looked toward Emperor Pingkang on the throne.","The Eighth Prince, seated beside him, curled his lips in private. Before Emperor Pingkang could answer, he said in a teasing tone, “Little Ninth is right. The dragon boat regatta is about to begin. This is your first time attending, so be sure to watch carefully. Then you can go back and tell the younger princes in the palace all about the excitement.”","The Ninth Prince was born to Beauty Li. Although Beauty Li belonged to Noble Consort Lan’s circle—the mother of the Eighth Prince—the Eighth Prince still could not stand this younger brother, who was so skilled at acting cute and currying favor with their father.","Little Ninth continued to beam. “Eighth Brother is right. In past years, I could only hear about such a grand occasion from the palace maids and eunuchs, catching merely a glimpse of its liveliness through their descriptions. Only under Father Emperor’s rule, in such a peaceful and prosperous age, could an event of this scale be held.”","“Thanks to Father Emperor’s grace, I now have the chance to witness such excitement with my own eyes. I am truly thrilled. My elder brothers must not laugh at me.”","As he spoke, a hint of bashfulness appeared on his still-round, childlike face.","At once, Emperor Pingkang broke into laughter.","When he had finished laughing, he said, “Little Ninth is becoming more and more clever.” With great interest, he began explaining things to him personally.","“The men competing in the dragon boat race are the finest soldiers selected from among the eight upper and middle divisions of the Great Yong Imperial Guard, including the Shenwu Army. Watch carefully, Little Ninth, and guess which team will win the championship. If you guess correctly, I shall reward you handsomely!”","“Thank—” Little Ninth had barely spoken a single word when the Eighth Prince cut him off.","“Father Emperor, you cannot be so partial as to reward only Ninth Brother. The Dragon Martial Army wins almost every year—there is hardly any suspense at all. Since you are asking Ninth Brother to guess, why not change the rules of the contest this year? What does Father Emperor think?”","The Dragon Martial Army had the strictest selection process, and the finest batch of Imperial Guards were said to be gathered there. Thus, they won the championship nearly every year and received the Emperor’s rewards. Only on two rare occasions had another team managed to take the title.","Emperor Pingkang found it rather amusing that Little Eighth, who was usually so unruly, was competing for favor with Little Ninth, who was several years younger. “Then tell me—what sort of change do you have in mind?”","The Eighth Prince grinned shamelessly. “Every year, we simply sit here and watch. After seeing it so many times, it has become rather dull. Why not imitate the ancients and entertain Father Emperor in filial devotion? We sons can each join a different team in the race and see which team, under our leadership, can ultimately seize the championship. That would be far more interesting!”","The moment he finished speaking, the Fourth Prince, who shared the same mother as the Eighth Prince, smiled and said, “What Eighth Brother proposes does sound rather interesting.”","With that, he looked toward the Crown Prince and the First Prince seated above him and asked with a smile, “I only wonder whether His Highness the Crown Prince and Eldest Brother would be willing?”","Cui Yu arched a brow slightly.","The First Prince, whose build was noticeably broader and more powerfully built than that of ordinary men, agreed almost at once. “Why not? So long as it pleases Father Emperor, I am willing to do whatever is required.”","The Second Prince immediately echoed his assent.","Seeing his sons eagerly competing to please him, Emperor Pingkang was naturally in good spirits. He turned to the Crown Prince, who had yet to speak. “What does the Crown Prince think?”","Cui Yu rose to his feet, lowered his gaze, and bowed with clasped hands. His voice was cool and steady. “This son believes Eighth Brother’s proposal is excellent.”","“Good!” Emperor Pingkang laughed heartily. When his laughter subsided, he stroked his handsome beard beneath his chin. “Then today, I shall wait and see.”","Quite a few among the civil and military officials showed surprise.","At this moment, the Second Prince said with a smile, “Father Emperor, to make the competition more entertaining, may we sons freely select men from the various military units and form new teams?”","The Eighth Prince glanced at the Crown Prince and promptly added, “Second Brother is right. Otherwise, whoever leads the Dragon Martial Guard will surely come first. Then whether the rest of us participate or not would make little difference.”","The Vice Censor-in-Chief immediately frowned. Distinctions of rank could not be ignored; it was only proper for the Crown Prince to have the first choice of team. Was the Eighth Prince not deliberately targeting the Crown Prince with these words?","If the Crown Prince lost, would he not be utterly humiliated before the civil and military court officials, as well as the people of the capital?","As the Crown Prince’s father-in-law, his position naturally lay with the Crown Prince. Moreover, the Crown Prince was the legitimate heir of the Empress’s palace, so there was all the more reason for concern.","With a stern expression, he was just about to rise and speak when he caught sight of the old Duke Fengguo, seated at the head of the military officials. The old duke was calmly sipping his wine, seemingly not the least bit worried for the Crown Prince. After only a moment’s thought, the Vice Censor-in-Chief sat back down.","Since even the old Duke Fengguo was not anxious, he might as well wait and see.","Cui Yu lifted his eyes. His expression remained composed, and his tone was equally mild. “Eighth Brother makes a valid point. Since ancient times, rank has its proper distinctions, and age its proper order. But as today is meant to entertain our father in filial devotion, let us set rank aside and proceed according to age. Eldest Brother, please make your selection first.”","Emperor Pingkang was inwardly pleased. Since the palace selection, the Crown Prince had become increasingly sensible. “We shall proceed as the Crown Prince has said.”","The Eighth Prince was immediately choked with frustration. He had not even finished speaking! Yet in the end, Eldest Brother had gained the advantage.","But his father had already spoken, so he could only swallow the rest of his words.","The prospect of having the princes personally lead their teams and compete in the dragon-boat race stirred mixed feelings among the civil and military officials. As for the soldiers and guards who would be taking part, they were variously nervous, excited, exhilarated, flustered, and at a loss.","*","The blazing sun poured down in countless golden rays. Though an occasional breeze swept over the water, Shen Yanshui could see the people beside her beginning to fan themselves with round silk fans.","Just then, the noblewomen and ladies heard some unusual commotion coming from the Waterside Hall. They could not help but turn their eyes in that direction.","The moment they looked, gasps could be heard from time to time.","Shen Yanshui, sharp-eared, caught someone’s astonished exclamation.","“Is that... the Eighth Prince? The Sixth Prince and Seventh Prince? Why have they boarded the dragon boats? And changed into sleeveless tunics?”","“Look—His Highness the Crown Prince and the other princes have changed clothes as well...”","Shen Yanshui had keen eyesight and could already clearly make out the Crown Prince and several princes dressed in sleeveless, open-front vests of different colors, each simply belted at the waist with a sash in a matching shade.","The Crown Prince wore black trimmed in red. It had to be said—it gave him a particularly striking air...","Many soldiers stood nearby, dressed in the same fashion, their figures straight and spirited. They, too, were an arresting sight.","While the ladies were still expressing their surprise, a eunuch arrived from the Waterside Hall to report to the Empress that the princes would each lead a team in the dragon boat race. He further announced, “By His Majesty’s verbal decree, all Your Highnesses and ladies are invited to guess this year’s winner. Whoever guesses correctly shall be richly rewarded by His Majesty.”","Once the eunuch had left, the women immediately broke into hushed, excited chatter. The Empress smiled.","“His Majesty wants us to make our guesses freely. If you guess correctly, I shall have a reward as well. Let this phoenix-head hairpin serve as today’s prize.”","Consort Shu, who had said little until then, spoke with a gentle smile. “Her Majesty is right. This warm white-jade bracelet was bestowed upon me by His Majesty; I shall offer it as a prize today as well.”","As soon as she finished speaking, Noble Consort Lan, the other consorts present, and the elder madams all smilingly contributed some rare trinket of their own. Yet none of them ventured a guess as to which prince would win, leaving such matters to the younger generation.","At the sight of several trays overflowing with dazzling jewelry, Shen Yanshui felt her eyes nearly blinded by the glitter.","As someone from the Eastern Palace, she naturally had to bet on the Crown Prince. Accordingly, she placed the tourmaline bracelet the Crown Prince had bestowed upon her among the stakes.","“Those are top-quality pink tourmalines. Lady Shen is truly willing to put them up as a prize?”","Secondary Consort Liao of the Fourth Prince, seated some distance away, remarked in a faintly mocking tone when she saw what Shen Yanshui had done.","“If it is to be a prize, then naturally one ought to offer something fine,” Shen Yanshui replied with a radiant smile.","Secondary Consort Liao curled her lip disdainfully, though she could not quite suppress her bitterness. Back at the Palace of Cultivated Elegance, Shen Yanshui had possessed no pink tourmalines of such quality. The bracelet must have been a gift from His Highness the Crown Prince.","Then the First Prince’s Consort, seated ahead of them, suddenly turned her eyes toward Shen Yanshui with a smile. “Oh? It seems Lady Shen has great confidence in His Highness the Crown Prince. Do you believe the Crown Prince will certainly claim the prize?”","Shen Yanshui: “...?”","The Crown Princess and Lady Zhang had also wagered on the Crown Prince. Why was she the only one being questioned?","She put on an expression of shy devotion and admiration, then answered bashfully, “In this concubine’s heart, His Highness the Crown Prince has always been accomplished in both letters and martial arts, and no one could be more valiant. Naturally, this concubine believes in His Highness.”","She had seen clearly enough just now. Of all the princes, only the First Prince was somewhat more powerfully built than the Crown Prince. The rest looked like frail scholars who could barely lift a chicken, without even the slightest definition in their arms. They surely could not compare to the Crown Prince.","As for the other contestants, since the princes had chosen their own teams, the outcome would most likely depend on how well these hastily assembled crews worked together.","She still had quite a bit of faith in the Crown Prince. And even if she did not, in a situation like this, she had to uphold his dignity, didn’t she?","The crowd looked at her peach-blossom face, flushed with shy sweetness, and listened to what sounded very much like a declaration of devotion to the Crown Prince. For a moment, no one knew what to say.","The younger ladies, meanwhile, found Lady Shen’s words rather embarrassing to hear in such a setting.","The Eldest Prince’s Consort, whose mind was full of love and romance, found the whole thing unbearably cloying and suddenly lost all interest in continuing the conversation.","But the Crown Princess was somewhat displeased. “Didn’t you also wager on Eldest Brother winning, Sister-in-law?” she said coolly. If those of the Eastern Palace did not bet on the Crown Prince, were they supposed to bet on someone else?","As for the final outcome, she only hoped that even if the Crown Prince failed to win, he would not lose too disgracefully. Otherwise, she would be humiliated along with him—and subjected to the veiled mockery of her fellow sisters-in-law.","“The Crown Princess is right. I spoke out of turn,” the Eldest Prince’s Consort said with a smile, offering a casual reply and arguing no further.","Seeing ​​‌‌​‌‌​​‌‌​​​​‌​‌‌​​​‌‌​‌‌​​​‌​​‌‌​​‌​​​‌‌​​‌​​​​‌‌​‌​‌​​‌‌​​​‌​​‌‌​‌​​​‌‌​​​​‌​‌‌​​​‌​​​‌‌‌​​​​​‌‌​​​​​‌‌​​‌​‌​​‌‌​‌​‌​‌‌​​​‌‌​​‌‌​​​​​​‌‌​‌‌​​​‌‌​‌​​​​‌‌​​‌​​​‌‌‌​​‌​​‌‌​​​​​​‌‌​‌‌‌​​‌‌​​​‌‍this, Shen Yanshui breathed a sigh of relief and turned her eager gaze back toward the Crown Prince’s side.","For some reason, however, Shen Yanshui’s exceedingly lovestruck remark was relayed by a eunuch to the Emperor. At once, the Emperor cast a meaningful look at the Crown Prince, who remained calm and solemn-faced.","The Eighth Prince could not help asking with a grin, “What amusing news has Father Emperor heard? Might Your son be allowed to join in the entertainment as well?”","Emperor Pingkang glanced at the Crown Prince again, a smile curling at his lips. “It is nothing much. I merely heard the Eastern Palace’s Lady Shen say a few words just now, and found them rather amusing. If I remember correctly, Lady Shen is the daughter of Earl Zhongyi’s household? She has a remarkably forthright nature.”","The dignified and stern Earl Zhongyi, seated below, looked somewhat surprised. Rising to his feet, he bowed and said, “Your Majesty overpraises her. She is indeed my daughter.”","Cui Yu’s brow twitched almost imperceptibly. He glanced at Earl Zhongyi, who was modestly accepting the praise, and for some reason felt a faint sense of foreboding.","The Eighth Prince and the other princes: “???”","At Emperor Pingkang’s cheerful gesture, a nearby eunuch proceeded to repeat Shen Yanshui’s words.","Of course, his duty was not solely to relay the words of this Lady of the Eastern Palace. At regular intervals, eunuchs would report every detail of what was happening among the female relatives to the chief eunuch at Emperor Pingkang’s side.","Chief Eunuch Cheng had only mentioned this particular matter because he found it amusing and thought it might entertain the Emperor.","Earl Zhongyi: “...”","In that instant, he was so mortified that he wanted to beat that loose-tongued, unfilial daughter of his to death.","Cui Yu remained composed and expressionless, giving those eager for a spectacle nothing to see.","The Eighth Prince immediately burst out laughing. In a tone that was half teasing, half faintly sarcastic, he said, “I have always heard that His Highness the Crown Prince keeps women at a distance. Who would have thought he could inspire such affection in a young lady? Why not let us brothers witness His Highness’s peerless valor today?”","The others wore varying expressions.","The Sixth Prince smiled as he glanced first at his father, then at the utterly unruffled Crown Prince, his heart sinking slightly.","Recently, the relationship between Father Emperor and the Crown Prince had eased considerably.","The Fourth Prince looked rather disdainful and said nothing.","The Second Prince drawled with a broad grin, “Then that Lady Shen of His Highness the Crown Prince is in for a disappointment. When it comes to letters, we may not be able to beat His Highness, but when it comes to martial prowess, well, that remains to be seen.”","Cui Yu did not argue. He merely replied in an indifferent tone, “We’ll see.”","*","While the women chatted and laughed, the dragon boat race on the other side had already begun.","There were ten teams in all. From the First Prince to the Eighth Prince, seven princes each led a team—the blind Fifth Prince being the only one absent. The remaining three teams were made up of Imperial Guards who had been left over after the others were selected.","The drums thundered, flags snapped in the wind, and oars churned furiously as the lake roiled beneath them.","Cheers from the shore grew louder and louder.","Before long, the ten teams had sorted themselves into their positions. The First Prince’s dragon boat surged into the lead, followed closely by the Fourth Prince’s. The Crown Prince was third, followed by the Sixth Prince, the Eighth Prince, the Second Prince, and finally the Seventh Prince.","Jinming Lake had been expanded many times over by successive emperors. Its winding, elongated shape made it look almost like a natural lake, though its name had never been changed after the founding emperor gave it the name Jinming Lake.","The dragon boat race began from the eastern shore beside the Waterside Hall. The boats had to circle the entire lake before competing for the flag planted high above the water in front of the Waterside Hall.","“His Highness the First Prince really is in the lead!”","“The Fourth Prince and the Crown Prince are fast too!”","Shen Yanshui stared without blinking at the dragon boats speeding closer and closer, until the people aboard them gradually came into clear view.","She suddenly realized that not only the princes, but the Imperial Guards competing in the race were all remarkably good-looking as well.","Their features were handsome and their postures straight and vigorous. Especially beneath the golden sunlight, their arms—damp with either splashed lake water or sweat—strained as they drove the oars through the water. The sight practically radiated raw strength and masculine vitality!","For a moment, she was dazzled by the feast before her eyes. Wherever the dragon boats passed, waves of cheers rose from the nearest shore.","Just as she was secretly admiring the highly pleasing spectacle, she suddenly noticed that the Crown Prince seemed to glance in this direction.","It happened so quickly that she wondered if she had imagined it.","When Cui Yu drew nearest, he quickly spotted the person he had been looking for amid the crowd. But with a single glance, he saw her slender, fair neck craned forward as she watched other men with delight, her brows raised and her eyes smiling.","For some reason, Cui Yu’s mood instantly soured.","Shen Yanshui, however, had long since forgotten that brief glance. After carefully evaluating the view before her, she decided that the Crown Prince still had the best physique.","Not only was the Crown Prince her favorite kind of cool, pale-skinned beauty, but the muscle lines on his arms were also just right—unlike the exaggerated bulk of the First Prince and some of the Imperial Guards. They were perfectly proportioned, pleasing to the eye.","The First Prince did have muscles on his arms, but they were too bulky to be attractive. And he already had a paunch despite his young age. The Crown Prince, on the other hand, had six-pack abs, and they felt wonderful to the touch...","As for the other princes... most of them had the physiques of scrawny chickens, all soft flesh and no muscle—hardly anything worth looking at. Not to mention their faces. Though several of the princes were fairly handsome, standing beside the Crown Prince only made his exceptional looks shine all the more.","Then, from beside her came a soft, faintly envious murmur.","“Lady Shen must be greatly favored by His Highness the Crown Prince in private, mustn’t you?”","Shen Yanshui: “...?”","She glanced sideways at Secondary Consort Tang of the First Prince’s household, who had always seemed somewhat aloof, her expression full of puzzlement.","Secondary Consort Tang first looked at her face, then let her gaze drift downward. Her eyes paused, and the envy in her voice deepened—though this time, it was hard to tell whom exactly she envied.","“His Highness the Crown Prince usually appears so refined and scholarly. Who would have thought he was no less formidable than the commanders of the Imperial Guard? Lady Shen, you are fortunate.” As she spoke, she cast another glance at Shen Yanshui’s pale, soft, generously rounded bosom and added in a low voice, “His Highness the Crown Prince is fortunate as well...”","Shen Yanshui: “............”","This time, there was no way she could pretend not to understand. Though... ahem, in that particular regard, the Crown Prince really was rather impressive."]},{"number":33,"title":"Chapter 33: The Crown Princess Is Pregnant","paragraphs":["Seeing that the dragon boat had rounded the bend and disappeared from sight, Secondary Consort Tang leaned back, took a sip of calamus wine, and said with an indifferent expression, “Why are you looking at me like that? I’m not some untouched young maiden.”","Then, in a soft voice, she added, “Besides, my prince is fairly decent.” Although his build and looks could not compare with the Crown Prince’s, he was still much better than the other princes, who looked as though they had no strength at all.","Shen Yanshui: “............”","Who said the ancients were reserved and restrained?","A procession of palace maids entered, and each table was served with more candied fruits and pastries.","Shen Yanshui had just picked up two pieces to eat when she suddenly heard the Crown Princess retch. She instinctively raised her eyes to look over.","The Empress immediately turned her gaze in that direction. With the Eldest Prince’s Consort at her side, she could not help asking, “What’s the matter with the Crown Princess? Why did she suddenly start retching when she was perfectly fine just now? Could she have eaten something unclean? Or perhaps...”","Consort Shu’s eyes flickered. A moment later, she put on a smile and said with genuine delight, “Could the Crown Princess be... with child?”","Lady Shen glanced at the Crown Princess’s expression and smiled. “It does look that way...” What a pity. It would be gone today.","The Crown Princess covered her mouth and frowned slightly. “I’m not entirely sure myself. I only took a bite of a zongzi filled with fresh meat and felt somewhat unwell...”","The Empress frowned and immediately ordered, “Go and summon the imperial physician.”","The imperial physician arrived very quickly. Everyone’s eyes instantly focused on the Crown Princess, and even Emperor Pingkang sent an attendant over to inquire about the matter.","Shen Yanshui was faintly surprised by how quickly Emperor Pingkang had sent someone over. That fast?","The imperial physician knitted his brows in concentration and soon began taking the Crown Princess’s pulse. Before long, Shen Yanshui saw the tension ease from between his brows. The next moment, he bowed to the Empress and said respectfully with a smile, “Congratulations, Your Majesty. Congratulations, Crown Princess. Her Highness is with child!”","The Empress’s phoenix eyes brightened, and a smile immediately spread across her face. She hurriedly asked, “How many months? Is the Crown Princess in good health? Is the baby in her womb all right?”","The imperial physician replied, “To answer Your Majesty, she is already three months along. The Crown Princess’s health is fairly good. She need only take care not to overexert herself in the coming days. I will prescribe a dose of medicine to prevent miscarriage. She need only take it and rest assured as she nurtures the pregnancy.”","Shen ​​‌‌​‌‌​​‌‌​​​​‌​‌‌​​​‌‌​‌‌​​​‌​​‌‌​​‌​​​‌‌​​‌​​​​‌‌​‌​‌​​‌‌​​​‌​​‌‌​‌​​​‌‌​​​​‌​‌‌​​​‌​​​‌‌‌​​​​​‌‌​​​​​‌‌​​‌​‌​​‌‌​‌​‌​‌‌​​​‌‌​​‌‌​​​​​​‌‌​‌‌​​​‌‌​‌​​​​‌‌​​‌​​​‌‌‌​​‌​​‌‌​​​​​​‌‌​‌‌‌​​‌‌​​​‌‍Yanshui was slightly astonished. Three months already?","The Crown Princess was not carrying her first child, and she had so many matrons attending her. Could she truly have had no idea?","Or had she... deliberately kept it hidden? Had she intentionally chosen this moment to reveal it?","But if she had deliberately chosen this moment, was she not afraid that, amid the crowds and confusion, something might go wrong?","The Empress and the others could naturally think of everything Shen Yanshui could think of—and more besides.","The smile in the Empress’s eyes faded slightly, though it was not obvious on her face. She first rewarded the imperial physician, then sent someone to report the news to Emperor Pingkang.","Before long, Shen Yanshui more or less understood why.","Emperor Pingkang had specifically sent Chief Eunuch Cheng over to deliver an oral decree.","From what Shen Yanshui heard, Emperor Pingkang was overjoyed upon learning that the Crown Princess was with child. Not only had he bestowed numerous rewards upon the Crown Princess, he had even granted every palace servant and guard present a month’s salary. Even the commoners watching around Jinming Lake were to receive a share.","At this, a complicated look crossed the Empress’s eyes for an instant. She then smiled and said to Chief Eunuch Cheng, who had come to deliver the decree, “His Majesty’s compassion knows no bounds. However, the common people are gathered thickly along Jinming Lake. If we were to distribute congratulatory coins on the spot, the crowd would surge and chaos might result, which would instead betray His Majesty’s benevolent intentions.”","Chief Eunuch Cheng’s expression did not change. He remained respectful as he asked, “Then what does Your Majesty suggest?”","The Empress smiled. “I do have an idea. The Dragon Boat Festival is a day for warding off evil and praying for blessings. Why not have people prepare mugwort, sachets, five-colored silk threads, and some zongzi, then distribute them to the common people along Jinming Lake?”","“First, it would suit the festival. Second, it would allow the people to share in the joy of the holiday. Third, mugwort wards off evil, while sachets pray for blessings. This is perfectly suited to the auspicious sign of the Crown Princess’s pregnancy and the imperial family gaining another heir. Letting the people share in this blessing would be far more fitting than scattering coins, would it not?”","After watching Chief Eunuch Cheng acknowledge her words and leave, Shen Yanshui could not help grumbling inwardly.","What was Emperor Pingkang thinking, wanting to scatter money in a place so crowded and lively?","What would happen if a stampede broke out and people were injured or killed?","Fortunately, Her Majesty the Empress had a clear head.","Still... Emperor Pingkang’s attitude toward the Crown Princess’s pregnancy was somewhat beyond her expectations.","Based on the rumors she had heard before, she had always thought that Emperor Pingkang did not much care for the Crown Prince.","Yet now, merely because the Crown Princess was pregnant, he wanted to make such a grand display of his rewards. He truly seemed to value and favor the Crown Prince to some extent.","After the Crown Princess respectfully expressed her gratitude for the imperial favor, her features relaxed considerably, and the corners of her lips kept lifting.","As she listened to the various congratulations and flattering words around her—especially when she saw several of her sisters-in-law forcing smiles as they congratulated her—the smile on the Crown Princess’s face deepened.","Her child was naturally destined to be different.","Moreover, with this news, it would not matter quite so much to her whether the Crown Prince managed to win the race later.","When everyone present heard the emperor’s oral decree, their expressions varied. Some even secretly clenched their handkerchiefs, feeling both sour and jealous at the emperor’s regard for the Eastern Palace and the Crown Prince.","His Majesty had clearly been suppressing the Crown Prince in many ways over the past two years...","Yet outwardly, everyone continued offering their congratulations, and the surroundings remained filled with a festive atmosphere.","Shen Yanshui leisurely ate her fruit, taking in everyone’s expressions. Every now and then, when she saw the look on the Crown Princess’s face as she turned to speak with the Eldest Prince’s Consort, Shen Yanshui could vaguely guess what she was thinking.","Still... she did not quite understand. The child had not even been born yet, and the Crown Princess had already made such a grand spectacle of things. Was she truly not afraid that someone would secretly trip her up?","That said, the faint medicinal scent that had occasionally lingered around the Crown Princess now had a better explanation.","*","“Faster! Faster!” Eighth Prince watched the distance between himself and the Crown Prince grow larger, and his tone became increasingly irritable.","The imperial guards rowing with all their might were driven by his angry urging to exert themselves even harder. Some even abandoned their usual rhythm, while a few, frightened by his shouting, fumbled with their oars. The entire rhythm grew increasingly chaotic.","“Oh? It’s you, Eighth Brother?” Second Prince, who had caught up alongside him, spoke in a teasing, frivolous tone. “You were so eager earlier that your Second Brother thought you had been secretly holding something back, waiting to make a grand entrance. But look at you now... tsk, tsk!”","Eighth Prince’s face instantly flushed with humiliation. “Aren’t you lagging behind too, Second Brother?!”","Second Prince did not care in the slightest. He was merely resting his hands on the oar and was not rowing at all. Raising his brows, he chuckled, “Your Second Brother has no intention of exhausting himself fighting for first place. Besides, someone else is keeping me from coming in last, so there’s no need for me to hurry.”","The Eighth Prince was nearly enraged by his utterly unconcerned, shameless manner. He abruptly turned to look at the Seventh Prince, who was trailing at the very back, and immediately scolded him without mercy.","“Seventh Brother! Did you skip breakfast this morning?”","He could not even beat this useless Second Brother, who spent all his time among women!","Everyone said he was shameless, but in his opinion, Second Brother was clearly the one with the thickest skin!","The Seventh Prince’s expression changed slightly. Even after being rudely shouted at and cursed by the Eighth Prince, who was younger than him, he still said nothing. He glanced forward at the Sixth Prince, then silently continued bringing up the rear.","Seeing his spineless appearance, the Eighth Prince immediately cursed him a few more times, calling him useless!","The Imperial Guards aboard his dragon boat grew increasingly apprehensive. Was the Eighth Prince cursing them, or was he cursing the Seventh Prince behind them?","The Second Prince let out a mocking laugh but said nothing.","Even if the Seventh Prince could overtake them, would he dare?","He narrowed his eyes at the four dragon boats ahead, which were separated by nearly equal distances, and suddenly said, “Row faster.”","At his command, the dragon boat’s speed increased considerably. The Eighth Prince, whose boat was not far away, stared in astonishment.","When the First Prince realized that the Crown Prince’s dragon boat was nearly running neck and neck with his own, his expression grew increasingly tense. The movements of his arms unconsciously quickened.","The Fourth Prince’s expression darkened further. His composure, which he had barely managed to maintain, crumbled when he saw himself falling farther and farther behind. He turned around and sternly berated the rowers, “Are you all nothing but useless freeloaders?!”","As a result, not only did the Fourth Prince fail to achieve the effect he wanted, but the Imperial Guards on his dragon boat also panicked and fumbled their strokes.","He quickly reined in his emotions and suppressed his displeasure before saying in a deep voice, “Even if you can’t win, you must hold on to third place!”","“Oh! Fourth Brother? What a coincidence!” the Second Prince called with a beaming smile, turning his head to greet him.","The Fourth Prince was startled. He had just opened his mouth to speak when someone suddenly dumped an entire bucket of water over his head!","His hair, his eyes, even his mouth were filled with the fishy smell of river water!","“What do you mean by this, Second Imperial Brother?!” The Fourth Prince flew into a rage.","“Ah, ah! It’s all my fault. I’m still not very practiced, and I didn’t expect the water to splash all over Fourth Brother. I’ll apologize to Fourth Brother at once.”","Though he said he was apologizing, just as the Second Prince was about to stand, the dragon’s head somehow veered slightly and rammed straight into the Fourth Prince’s dragon boat!","The Fourth Prince’s boat happened to be following close beside the Crown Prince’s. The dragon’s head was less than three feet from the Crown Prince’s stern.","“Bang!”","“Bang, bang, bang!”","*","“Boom! Boom-boom-boom!”","The drumbeats rolled across the water, suddenly growing more impassioned. Shen Yanshui heard the shouts of the spectators on both banks. She raised her head and gazed into the distance, only to see two dragon boats racing swiftly beneath Xian Bridge.","They were here!","“Ah! It’s the Crown Prince and the First Prince!”","Shen Yanshui’s eyesight was better than most. From the two nearly neck-and-neck dragon boats, she could tell that the Crown Prince’s boat had emerged from beneath the bridge a step ahead.","A short while later, the two boats arrived almost simultaneously in front of the Waterside Hall.","Oars cleaved the waves like ten thousand flying swords; drums split the breakers like a thousand peals of thunder!","Shen Yanshui found herself growing nervous as she watched.","When she saw the Crown Prince seize the golden marker first, its red-and-gold flag streaming proudly in the wind, Shen Yanshui’s smile instantly blossomed.","She had no attention left to spare for whoever came in behind them. Her eyes were fixed entirely on the Crown Prince’s handsome face, flushed slightly from the sun, and on his muscular arms, their lines smooth and powerful.","*","“Congratulations, Your Highness!”","As soon as Cui Yu stepped down from the dragon boat, several people hurried over to congratulate him with broad smiles.","Cui Yu paid them no mind, his expression as calm as ever.","Only after the last of them, the Seventh Prince, had climbed ashore did Emperor Pingyuan laugh heartily and say, “Today, the Crown Prince has won the race, and we have a double blessing to celebrate! What reward would you like?”","The Crown Prince had too few children, which was disadvantageous to the stability of the state and had always been a source of concern to him.","Cui Yu was puzzled. In an even voice, he asked, “A double blessing? What does Father mean?”","Emperor Pingkang’s gaze grew deep, though his tone remained amused. “The Crown Princess is three months pregnant. Did you not know, Crown Prince?”","A faint heaviness settled in Cui Yu’s heart. Then, for the first time, a trace of delight appeared on his usually impassive face.","“Is what Father says true?”","Emperor Pingkang laughed. “How could such happy news be false? Tell me, what reward would you like?”","The other princes, who had already lost the race, felt even worse when they heard that the Crown Princess was pregnant.","As long as the Eastern Palace had no healthy imperial grandson, they still had a chance to contend for that position. But if the Crown Prince had a healthy heir...","The Fourth Prince glared viciously at the Second Prince, who was smiling as though nothing at all had happened.","If the Second Prince had not deliberately rammed his dragon boat, causing him nearly to fall into the water, the Imperial Guards aboard his boat would not have panicked while rescuing him. He would not have lost even to the Sixth Prince in the end!","It was utterly humiliating!","And now the Crown Prince was about to have a legitimate son—one who might very well be healthy...","He suddenly stepped forward and said, “Father, why not withdraw the order for Great General Qi to remain at home and reflect on his mistakes? Great General Qi has risked his life time and again over the past several years and rendered outstanding service to Great Yong. Yet on such a grand occasion, he is unable to attend. Would that not chill the hearts of the soldiers?”","Cui Yu’s gaze turned icy.","Many of the court officials heard the Fourth Prince’s words clearly. Though he appeared to be speaking up for the general, how could he not know that His Majesty was wary of Great General Qi? He was plainly trying to sow discord and provoke the Emperor.","Emperor Pingkang’s gaze deepened. “Oh? Is that also the Crown Prince’s opinion?”","The Crown Prince said solemnly, “Father has already reached a decision on this matter. Father is benevolent. Ordering General Qi to remain at home and reflect on his actions allows him to examine himself, while also showing consideration for the years he has spent campaigning on behalf of the nation. Resting at home and cultivating himself will allow him to serve Father even better in the future. How could I misunderstand Father’s painstaking intentions or harbor resentment toward him?”","The old Duke Fengguo, who had been drinking with his eyes narrowed and looking utterly untroubled, slowly rose to his feet. With tears in his eyes, he bowed respectfully and said gratefully, “His Highness the Crown Prince is absolutely right. Moreover, to be able to serve His Majesty and Great Yong is my son’s good fortune. There are countless soldiers who risk life and limb; my son is merely one among them and not worth mentioning.”","A look of satisfaction appeared on Emperor Pingkang’s face. He saw the Fourth Prince’s intentions perfectly clearly and did not take them to heart. What pleased him was the attitude of the Crown Prince and the old Duke Fengguo.","He wanted to know whether the Crown Prince and the old Duke Fengguo harbored any resentment toward him over his punishment of Qi Mingchuan.","Although the Crown Prince had not deliberately treated coldly the woman of humble noble birth whom the Emperor had bestowed on him after the selection, and had instead shown her considerable favor, appearing as obedient as ever, the Emperor still could not entirely set his mind at ease. The Crown Prince had opposed him several times over Qi Mingchuan, after all.","Now, having heard the Crown Prince’s words, he was finally able to let go of his earlier suspicions. With a satisfied expression and tone, he said, “It is good that the Crown Prince and Minister Qi understand My intentions. Great General Qi has rendered meritorious service to the nation. I naturally will not mistreat a meritorious subject.”","The Crown Prince and the old Duke Fengguo once again offered their thanks.","Only then did Emperor Pingkang turn his gaze toward the Fourth Prince, his expression displeased. “Fourth Son, are you seeking justice for Great General Qi?”","Although he knew perfectly well that the Fourth Prince had been employing a ploy, those words about chilling the hearts of the soldiers—did the Fourth Prince truly think that way as well? Was that why he had blurted them out so readily?","The Fourth Prince’s heart gave a violent jolt, and he was momentarily stunned.","Seeking justice for Qi Mingchuan?","But when he saw the faint anger already rising in his father’s expression, he instantly gathered his wits and said, “This son would not dare! I merely felt that His Highness the Crown Prince and Great General Qi have been close since childhood. As his younger brother, I wished only to help the Crown Prince bear his burdens.”","Cui Yu’s tone remained mild. “You’re relieving my worries? Just now, I thought it was Fourth Prince who had come in first and won the gold token.”","As soon as he finished speaking, Fourth Prince’s face flushed red, then turned green.","“His Highness the Fourth Prince was merely carried away by excitement and lost his sense of propriety. He ought to punish himself with three cups of wine to apologize to His Highness the Crown Prince. Today is a doubly joyous occasion for the Crown Prince, yet he has not even told His Majesty what reward he would like.” He Yixun rose, cupped his hands, and smiled as he tried to smooth things over.","He Yixun was the Vice Chancellor of the court, as well as Fourth Prince’s maternal uncle. He was highly trusted and favored by Emperor Pingyuan.","With him stepping in, Emperor Pingyuan did not pursue the matter any further.","Fourth Prince gratefully took the offered escape route. His face was flushed—whether from anger or humiliation, it was hard to say—and he raised his cup to the Crown Prince, drinking three cups in succession.","The matter was thus put to rest.","*","The women’s side still had no idea what had happened at the Waterside Hall.","Lady Shen smiled at Consort Shu. “The Sixth Prince and Fourth Prince did quite well too.”","Consort Shu smiled. She was not surprised that her son had come in third, but Lady Shen’s attitude lately was truly rather strange...","Noble Consort Lan wore the ugliest expression of all. The Eighth Prince was one thing, but she had never expected her own Fourth Prince to rank behind the Sixth Prince as well!","Consort De was somewhat disappointed that her son had failed to win first place, but she could accept the result. She now began offering her congratulations. “Congratulations, Your Majesty. His Highness the Crown Prince was indeed valiant...”","Shen Yanshui found herself surrounded by compliments for the Empress, the Crown Prince, and the Crown Princess. In high spirits, she continued sipping her wine.","The Empress smiled, her brows and eyes full of warmth. “It was merely a game between brothers. Go and distribute the prizes among everyone.”","Shen Yanshui’s eyes lit up at once!","In the end, not only did she reclaim her original pearl hairpin, she also picked out a heavy yet exquisite gold bracelet, along with two gold-and-jade hairpins.","Hehe, what a profit!","Compared with those beautiful but impractical pieces of jewelry, she much preferred solid gold!","Secondary Consort Tang glanced at her, the corner of her mouth twitching slightly. At last, she said, “Lady Shen is certainly... straightforward.”","Shen Yanshui smiled brightly. “Thank you for the compliment, Your Highness.”","Secondary Consort Tang and Lady Zhang, who had also heard the exchange, were speechless.","Secondary Consort Liao immediately rolled her eyes in disdain. “Vulgar!”","Shen Yanshui smiled until her eyes curved into crescents, treating the remark as nothing more than a fart.","After a while, she rose and left to freshen up. She had drunk a little too much.","Matron Zhou, who served at the Crown Princess’s side, seemed to notice something. She suddenly leaned close and whispered a few words into the Crown Princess’s ear. The Crown Princess glanced sideways at Lady Shen, who had just risen from her seat, and the corners of her lips lifted in a smile.","“Send someone to follow her and see what she’s up to,” she ordered in a low voice.","“Yes.”","*","Shen Yanshui had just finished relieving herself and stepped out of the hall when she saw Lady Shen walking toward her. She was faintly surprised. After giving her a formal salute, she was about to leave, but someone blocked her path.","Shen Yanshui raised her eyes. “What does Lady Shen want?”","Lady Shen glanced around and instructed the palace attendants accompanying her to wait at a distance. She then frowned and looked at Chunping, the maidservant beside Shen Yanshui, who seemed to have no sense of propriety at all.","“Go stand farther away.”","Chunping did not move. She merely raised her eyes slightly toward her own mistress.","Shen Yanshui found Lady Shen’s behavior suddenly rather intriguing.","“If you have something to say, Lady Shen, then say it. If not, I should return. If I stay away too long, the Crown Princess may send someone to look for me, and that would be troublesome.”","Lady Shen frowned unhappily. She stared at the maidservant for a few more moments before turning her gaze back to her fourth younger sister.","“No matter what, we are still sisters of the same family. Do you really think I would deliberately harm you?”","Shen Yanshui lifted her eyelids and gave her a glance. Unhurriedly, she waved the round fan in her hand without saying a word.","Lady Shen’s expression grew even more unpleasant. “You don’t know how to appreciate kindness!” Then she quickly added, “When you go back, you’d better keep your distance from the Crown Princess.”","Otherwise, one careless misstep might implicate her as well.","With that, perhaps because she could not bear to look at Shen Yanshui’s face any longer, she turned and walked away.","Shen Yanshui narrowed her eyes slightly. What did she mean? Why had she told her to keep her distance from the Crown Princess?","Was something about to happen to the Crown Princess? Had Lady Shen learned of it in advance? Was she afraid of being implicated by Shen Yanshui, and so had come specifically to warn her?","Chunping could not help frowning. In a low voice, she said, “Mistress, about this...”","She wanted to ask whether they should inform the Crown Princess. It certainly did not sound like anything good, but then she remembered the relationship between her mistress and Lady Shen. For a moment, she was caught between hesitation and indecision.","Shen Yanshui said softly, “For now, let’s pretend we know nothing.”","Although she only wanted to live peacefully in the Eastern Palace and had no desire to become entangled with Lady Shen, Noble Consort Lan, or any of the others, if she hurried to tell the Crown Princess what had happened, would the Crown Princess really believe her so easily?","Not only did she have no evidence, she was relying entirely on personal speculation. It would be better to wait and see.","Not long after Shen Yanshui returned to her seat, she began paying special attention to everything around the Crown Princess, keeping watch over her movements.","While the women watched the aquatic performance, chatted, and quietly nursed their own schemes, everyone suddenly saw an extravagantly magnificent dragon boat sailing toward the Waterside Hall.","The vessel was more than forty zhang long and four or five zhang wide. Its dragon head and tail fins were inlaid and intricately carved with gold, stone, and jade. It was exquisitely imposing, radiating the dignity and majesty of the imperial family from every angle.","Watching it from afar, Shen Yanshui saw that the three-storied dragon boat was not only fitted with pavilions and terraces, but even contained an artificial garden filled with countless rare flowers and exotic plants. Her eyes widened slightly in amazement.","When she saw the Emperor lead the civil and military officials onto the dragon boat from the Waterside Hall, the vessel was divided among them.","The dragon boat had three levels. The Emperor and Empress led the imperial clan, the senior court officials, and their families onto the top level. Everyone else was assigned to the middle level, while the lowest level was filled entirely with guards, palace maids, and eunuchs, ready to carry out the Emperor and Empress’s orders at any moment.","Shen Yanshui was naturally assigned to the top level.","However, just as she was about to step onto the dragon boat, the vessel’s astonishing splendor captured some of her attention. Then, from the corner of her eye, she suddenly saw Lady Zhang, who was walking beside her, stumble forward!","And walking directly in front of Lady Zhang was the pregnant Crown Princess!","Shen Yanshui reacted with lightning speed, almost instantly reaching out and catching Lady Zhang as she lost her balance and fell forward.","To those behind them, it probably looked as though Lady Zhang had simply stumbled, only to have Lady Shen promptly and steadily catch her by the arm.","Thus, no commotion arose.","But Lady Zhang’s face had gone pale with terror. In the briefest instant, a layer of cold sweat had formed on her forehead. Her legs had gone so weak that she nearly collapsed, and she leaned almost entirely against Shen Yanshui, gripping her arm tightly as she whispered with a trembling voice, “Someone pushed me just now...”","If Lady Shen had not caught her in time, she would have crashed into the Crown Princess. Just imagining the consequences made her body tremble uncontrollably.","“What’s wrong with Lady Zhang? Why does she look so pale?” Secondary Consort Tang asked in surprise and concern.","Hearing this, the Crown Princess turned around and looked over with a slight furrow between her brows. “What happened?”","Lady Zhang’s face turned pale. “I—I...” For a moment, she did not know whether she should say that someone had pushed her.","Lady Shen put on a solemn expression and said with a frown, “Your Highness, Lady Zhang was frightened. Someone pushed her just now, and she nearly fell.”","It was the perfect opportunity to make sure the Crown Princess understood the situation and kept her guard up.","Now that she had given the warning, she would not need to keep dividing her attention afterward and could simply focus on protecting herself.","The moment her words fell, the area around them fell completely silent.","No one could afford to bear the charge of attempting to harm the Crown Princess.","The Crown Princess’s expression darkened. The Empress, who was not far ahead, had also heard her words, and her face suddenly grew grim.","Her voice turned cold. “Lady Shen, is that true?”","Lady Zhang nodded, her face still pale. Trembling, she replied, “Your Majesty, I did not see who pushed me, but the person pushed me from behind.”","The Crown Princess’s displeased gaze immediately fell on the wives of the First, Second, and Fourth Princes, who were standing behind her.","The three princesses-in-law dropped to their knees almost at once. “Your Majesty, please see that we are innocent.”","Their expressions were all somewhat strained, and the others naturally did not dare involve themselves.","The Empress swept an expressionless gaze over the three women and those beside and behind them. Seeing that the Emperor had already turned his attention toward them, she decisively ordered, “The Crown Princess and Lady Zhang are unwell. Send people to escort the Crown Princess to Waterheart Pavilion to rest for the time being.”","“All the matrons and palace maids within ten feet of the Crown Princess are to remain here for questioning. Have them watched.”","Nanny Fan’s expression was stern. She immediately acknowledged the order and efficiently had the palace attendants taken away. Even the Crown Princess’s own people who had been walking behind her were not spared.","The wives of the First, Second, and Fourth Princes went slightly pale and did not dare say a word.","Noble Consort Lan and the other high-ranking consorts had originally intended to say something, but when they saw that even the people from the Eastern Palace beside the Crown Princess had been taken away, they had nothing more to say despite their displeasure.","Chunping was taken away as well. Having been frightened by what had happened, her lips were already pale before she left. Seeing this, Shen Yanshui gave her arm a reassuring pat.","The Crown Princess knitted her brows, feeling somewhat displeased. She had yet to see the Crown Prince. Although she knew that the Empress’s decision was meant to protect both her and the child in her womb, she still felt unwilling to miss the occasion under such circumstances.","Besides, she did not believe that after failing once, the culprit would have the nerve to try to harm her again under the Emperor’s very eyes.","That was what she thought, and it was exactly what she said.","Shen Yanshui: “...”","One could not refuse to eat for fear of choking, but clearly, the Crown Princess currently had no way of ensuring her own safety without fail.","The Empress looked at her with a frown, her voice slightly heavy. “The Crown Princess must put her health first.”","The Crown Princess respectfully lowered her head. With a gentle, grateful smile, she said, “Thank you for your concern, Mother. However, I feel perfectly well and do not have the slightest discomfort.”","Just then, a eunuch serving at the Emperor’s side came over to inquire about the situation.","Seeing that the Crown Princess was stubborn and cared nothing for her own health, the Empress grew even more displeased. Keeping her expression calm, she said to the eunuch, “A minor matter delayed us. Let us go.”","The Crown Princess straightened her back and followed without slowing her steps.","As for Lady Zhang, after hearing the Empress’s words, she quietly breathed a sigh of relief and did not board the dragon boat again.","Everyone else became even more cautious.","Shen Yanshui felt that she had given the warning sufficiently and had put one matter weighing on her mind to rest, so she quickly cast the incident out of her thoughts.","After entering the dragon boat, she discovered that it contained more than a dozen rooms. The largest was naturally the main hall where the Emperor was staying. Next was the Qixu Hall, where the Empress, the women of the imperial clan, and the wives of high-ranking officials were gathered.","A small garden separated the two areas. The lattice windows on either side were open, with only a thin layer of gauze curtains hanging to screen them. Tables, chairs, tea, and refreshments had all been prepared inside, and the space was remarkably broad.","After paying their respects to the Emperor with the Empress, Shen Yanshui saw the Crown Prince standing at the Emperor’s side.","He wore a dark crimson official robe, a leather belt fastened around his waist, and had a calm, composed bearing. His handsome features were gentle and refined.","She had assumed that the Crown Prince would be delighted upon learning that the Crown Princess was pregnant. Yet, judging from his current expression... Perhaps it was only her imagination, but she felt that he did not seem entirely happy.","Still...the Crown Princess’s pregnancy should have been good news for both the Crown Prince and the Eastern Palace. Unable to help herself, she stole another glance at him. His expression remained tranquil, as though nothing could stir him.","The Crown Prince, whose mood was indeed less than pleasant, noticed her gaze and glanced at her.","Shen Yanshui froze for a moment, then gave him a radiant smile.","Cui Yu looked at her bright, peach-blossom smile. Ever since he had learned that the Crown Princess was already three months pregnant, his mood had been faintly gloomy. Yet now, it seemed as though the skies within him had suddenly cleared a little."]},{"number":34,"title":"Chapter 34: Seeing Red, Doubting Trust","paragraphs":["Shen Yanshui did not dare look too closely either. Her gaze swept briefly over the group opposite her, focusing mainly on the several young princes gathered around the Crown Prince. This was the first time she had ever seen so many princes from such close range.","As she was looking around absentmindedly, an elegant and refined face suddenly entered her line of sight.","Shen Yanshui’s eyes halted. She was inwardly startled. Xu Chengwen? What was he doing here?","As a second-rank palace graduate in the imperial examinations, had he caught Emperor Pingkang’s eye? Was that why he was accompanying the imperial retinue?","Curious, she looked at him a few more times. When she noticed him looking back, she politely inclined her head and smiled.","Her former parents had regretted the verbal marriage arrangement they had just made for her. Since the Earl’s Mansion had been in the wrong first, although the matter had not been her choice, she still felt a trace of awkwardness and guilt whenever she saw him.","Fortunately, she had thick skin. The marriage had already been called off, and she quickly set those feelings aside.","She soon shifted her gaze away and followed the Empress into the Qiw u Hall.","Cui Yu watched her turn and leave. From the corner of his eye, he glanced in the direction where she had just stared blankly for a moment. There, he saw Lord Xu—the lecturer at Chongzheng Hall, who had recently won Father Emperor’s favor because of his outstanding poetry and prose—still gazing after her.","Xu Chengwen seemed to sense something and lowered his eyes slightly.","Cui Yu unconsciously knitted his brows.","Then he suddenly remembered how she had looked at the rather handsome Imperial Guards earlier, her expression full of avid interest...","Women rarely had many opportunities to leave their homes, and women in the palace had even fewer. Given her lively and daring nature, it was perfectly normal for her to enjoy watching the excitement. It was just that... he inexplicably felt a little displeased.","*********","After taking her seat, Shen Yanshui began admiring the scenery along both banks of Golden Bright Lake with great interest.","Although this was not her first time seeing it, it was her first time viewing it from aboard a dragon boat. The angle was completely different, lending the scenery a fresh appeal.","Shen Ronghua, however, could not help being startled when she saw Xu Chengwen—the man who should have become her Fourth Sister’s husband.","Indeed, the two had not even formally become engaged. At most, they had met once or twice under the watchful eyes of their servants, so naturally they could not have developed any deep feelings for each other.","But Xu Chengwen would one day rise to become a prime minister. It was truly a pity to miss out on such an excellent future husband. Perhaps... she could suggest this marriage for Fifth Sister instead?","Fifth Sister was her full younger sister, so her status was naturally more distinguished than Fourth Sister’s. Even if the Xu family harbored some resentment because the Earl’s Mansion had broken off the original match, as long as they were willing to marry their legitimate daughter into the Xu family, the Xu family—and Xu Chengwen himself—would only be more pleased.","Besides, in her previous life, Fifth Sister’s husband had treated her poorly. Xu Chengwen, on the other hand, had been famous for his devotion. He had remained wholeheartedly faithful to Fourth Sister. It was said that his inner court was exceptionally quiet: apart from two bedchamber attendants, he did not even have a proper concubine.","Who would not envy such a life?","As everyone exchanged cups, chatted, and admired the scenery, the Crown Princess suddenly said with a smile, “Lady Shen has been watching Lady Shen. Is there something you would like to say? Earlier, Lady Shen even went out of her way to speak with Lady Shen for quite some time. I wonder what the two of you discussed. Why not tell us as well?”","Shen Yanshui was inwardly startled. Someone had actually been eavesdropping when she and her elder sister were talking?","Having been born with memories of a previous life, she had no habit of constantly using her supernatural ability. Her current first-level ability had a range of only a dozen or so meters, scarcely farther than her own hearing, so there was no need to use it unnecessarily.","Moreover, at the time, Imperial Guards, palace maids, eunuchs, and attendants had been moving about all around them. She truly had not noticed anyone deliberately eavesdropping.","But she was certain that within at least several meters of them—the distance at which an ordinary person could hear their conversation—there had been no one.","Just as she was pondering this, Shen Ronghua spoke.","“The Crown Princess is jesting. We merely happened to run into each other while I was going to change clothes, so I casually reminded Fourth Sister to observe the rules and serve the Crown Prince and Crown Princess properly. I never expected that someone so fond of spreading tales would repeat it to the Crown Princess. Truly hateful.”","The Crown Princess sneered inwardly, but her face retained a gentle smile. “Oh? I thought Lady Shen and Lady Shen had been exchanging private words between sisters—something unsuitable for outsiders to hear. I never imagined you were helping me instruct someone from the Eastern Palace.”","Shen Ronghua’s expression stiffened slightly.","The Crown Princess glanced at her rigid face and drawled, “In any case, there is no need for Lady Shen to trouble herself over the people of the Eastern Palace. Besides, Lady Shen has always been very proper. It is Lady Shen who has been worrying needlessly.”","She suspected that the two of them had plotted something.","Otherwise, why had Lady Shen happened to pull Lady Zhang back at such a crucial moment?","Was she trying to win the Crown Princess’s trust? Or did she have a greater scheme in mind—to gain the Empress Dowager’s and the Crown Prince’s favor?","If she had nothing to hide, why could she not speak openly? Why had she instead dismissed the attendants and whispered in secret?","Unfortunately, the people she had sent had failed to hear what the two women had actually discussed.","And because Lady Shen had stepped in to save Lady Zhang earlier, she now had to treat Lady Shen even better. Otherwise, as Crown Princess, she would appear incapable of distinguishing between merit and fault and would lose all dignity.","Seeing that the Crown Princess was no longer pressing the matter, Shen Ronghua smiled and said, “The Crown Princess is right. I have overstepped. I hope the Crown Princess will not take offense.”","Even so, she could not help feeling troubled and uneasy inside.","She had never expected that it would be Fourth Sister who helped the Crown Princess at the critical moment, leaving the Crown Princess unharmed.","But if the Crown Princess had not miscarried, would the events that followed also change?","This deviation from what she had foreseen in her dream left her deeply agitated.","Just as Shen Yanshui was secretly studying her elder sister’s expression and demeanor, she suddenly heard the Empress call her name. She hurriedly rose and saluted.","The Empress looked at her with great warmth. “You may be said to have rendered meritorious service by saving the Crown Princess just now. Those who have merit should be rewarded. Is there anything you would like?”","The Empress had been left with a particularly deep impression of her today. Not only was she beautiful and graceful, but more importantly, she was eloquent. Several attempts had been made to target her, yet she had not suffered a loss even once. Instead, those who had provoked her had only humiliated themselves.","At the critical moment, she had been able to step forward and help. She had also remained calm and composed, explaining everything clearly and logically without the slightest panic. She was clever and courageous. The Empress could not help feeling two more points of fondness for her.","The Crown Princess’s brows drew together slightly. It was one thing for the Empress to reward Lady Shen; after all, Lady Shen had protected her and deserved recognition.","But to indulge Lady Shen to this extent—to let her choose her own reward?","The Crown Princess pressed her lips together.","The others were also faintly surprised by the Empress’s words. They glanced at Lady Shen, realizing that the Empress must be very fond of her.","Shen Ronghua likewise recovered from the Empress’s words and could not help looking at her Fourth Sister with a complicated expression.","Shen Yanshui was a little surprised as well.","But a reward was a reward—why refuse something offered freely?","Besides, she felt she had done nothing to feel guilty about this time. At once, she smiled until her lovely almond-shaped eyes curved into crescents and said in a clear, cheerful voice, “Thank you, Your Majesty. But I honestly don’t know what I want. Whatever Your Majesty chooses to reward me with, I’ll be happy.”","Although the Empress was generous, Shen Yanshui had no intention of pushing her luck. Besides, how could anything personally bestowed by the Empress of the realm be anything but precious?","A trace of surprise flickered through the Empress’s eyes. She recalled how Shen Yanshui had thanked her and accepted the reward without the slightest hesitation. Hearing that bright, melodious voice, brimming with youthful vitality and delight, the Empress’s face unconsciously softened into a smile.","A little farther away, Countess Zhongyi’s heart sank when she heard Shen Yanshui’s words. She hurriedly rose and stepped forward to offer her respects. “Your Majesty, this minister’s wife has failed to properly educate her daughter. I beg Your Majesty to forgive her.”","Her Hua’er had already been implicated and targeted by the Crown Princess earlier. Now she had to come forward and plead for forgiveness on her behalf as well. Countess Zhongyi nearly ground her teeth to pieces.","Shen Yanshui: “...”","She wasn’t stupid. Though her earlier words had indeed been somewhat improper and contrary to the rules governing a proper young lady, she had chosen them after carefully observing the Empress’s expression and the atmosphere of the occasion.","Just as she was thinking this, she secretly raised her eyes to look over—only to meet the Empress’s gaze.","She froze for a moment, then instinctively curved her eyes and gave the Empress a sweet smile.","The Empress was stunned for an instant. Then her expression relaxed, and she smiled kindly. “Lady Shen is still young. She is pure-hearted and forthright. There is no reason to blame her. Countess Zhongyi, please rise.”","In the end, the Empress removed a nine-tailed phoenix hairpin with dangling golden tassels from her own coiffure. Looking at Shen Yanshui’s tender, sweetly smiling face, she said with a smile, “This is something I wear myself. I shall give it to you.”","Shen Yanshui bowed, expressed her thanks, and respectfully accepted it. Yet inwardly, she was somewhat astonished. In a certain sense, a nine-tailed phoenix hairpin represented the Empress’s status and attitude.","It was much like an item bestowed by the Emperor. To a subject, either represented immense honor.","Everyone present was envious—some to the point of jealousy.","The Crown Princess stared at the ornate and exquisite nine-tailed phoenix hairpin with its dangling golden tassels, an ornament only the Empress was qualified to wear, and frowned. She felt that Her Majesty’s reward had gone a little too far.","Even the Crown Princess could only wear a seven-tailed phoenix hairpin according to court regulations...","Fortunately, Lady Shen was not foolish enough to put it on in public. Only then did the Crown Princess shift her gaze away.","Shen Yanshui had no idea what the Crown Princess was thinking. She was in an excellent mood. Today, she had at least made herself known to the Empress. After carefully and properly putting away the phoenix hairpin, she thought that although she could not wear it, it might prove extremely useful someday.","Before long, the Empress told the younger members of the family that they need not remain so formal and could go amuse themselves.","The dragon boat had many different rooms, each equipped with various entertainments. There were games such as shooting at zongzi, pitch-pot, and competing over plants and flowers. There were also rooms where guests could rest. Every so often, the Golden Bright Pool offered different water performances for people to watch, while the bustle and excitement along the banks were equally captivating.","Shen Yanshui was very interested in the garden aboard the dragon boat, which was filled with rare flowers and exotic treasures. Thus, when she saw Secondary Consort Tang rise, she rose as well.","Shen Yanshui did not know what the garden was called, but she noticed that quite a few people had come. Most were in groups of two or three. Some were simply admiring the flowers, while others had selected various plants for elegant or physical contests. She strolled leisurely among the rare and exotic flowers that had been gathered there.","She soon discovered that they truly deserved to be called rare treasures.","Because of her supernatural affinity with plants, she had studied flowers and plants extensively since childhood. She had also taught herself a little rudimentary medicine from medical texts and made some commonly used remedies herself.","Yet she found that quite a number of the plants here were ones she had never seen in Great Yong. Some, however, she recognized from the illustrated encyclopedias of flowers and plants she had deliberately sought out and studied in her previous life, during the apocalypse.","Peonies, Chinese peonies, irises, China roses, roses, wisteria, rambling roses... There were all sorts of common flowers, as well as precious variants in every imaginable color.","But her gaze fell upon a cluster of pink, bell-shaped blossoms only about a centimeter across, swaying in the breeze, as well as the inconspicuous little purple flowers beside them, seemingly used merely as decoration. Her eyes suddenly lit up.","“What is there to see in these flowers?” Secondary Consort Tang asked when she noticed how intently Shen Yanshui was looking at them. She approached at an unhurried pace, though the speed at which she waved her round fan had quickened somewhat. Leaning closer, she saw the pink-and-white bell-shaped flowers she had never encountered before.","An eunuch nearby, who had been keeping watch for the needs of the noble guests, stepped forward and respectfully replied, “In response to Your Highness, these two varieties are newly introduced plants presented by a small Western Regions kingdom. The pink ones are called red willow blossoms, and the purple ones are Anxi fennel.”","Shen Yanshui listened quietly.","So the Apocynum flower was called red willow blossom here, while Anxi fennel was actually cumin blossom.","Apocynum flowers mostly grew along the edges of deserts. Their blossoms were pink or white and had the effects of calming the nerves and lowering blood pressure. They were often used to treat hypertension and neurasthenia.","As for cumin, there was even less need to explain its uses. At the thought of the fragrance of cumin powder sprinkled over barbecued meat, Shen Yanshui nearly began to drool. She had searched for cumin before but had never found any. She had never expected to encounter it here.","If only she had asked the Empress for this as her reward just now!","She was feeling rather regretful when she suddenly remembered that, earlier, the princesses and noble young ladies had seemed to be picking flowers and plants for their contests in this very area...","After hearing the eunuch who tended the plants explain their origins, Secondary Consort Tang nodded. “So they are flowers from the Western Regions. Their appearance is fairly ordinary, but they do smell quite nice.”","As she spoke, she saw Lady Shen of the Eastern Palace reach out, pluck two plants, and dig them up by the roots before stuffing them into a pouch she carried with her.","Secondary Consort Tang: “...?”","Seeing the strange look in her eyes, Shen Yanshui pressed her lips together in a smile. “I find the scent of this Anxi fennel quite pleasant as well, and I like it very much. I thought I would make it into a sachet to carry with me. Please don’t laugh at me, Your Highness.”","The aroma of barbecue... Slurp!","She would force them to grow as soon as she returned!","Looking at her, Secondary Consort Tang found it rather astonishing. They were merely two insignificant flowers—how could they possibly inspire such excitement?","Still, out of kindness, she offered a reminder. “Since these were presented by a small kingdom in the Western Regions, they may be difficult to keep alive unless one specializes in tending flowers and plants.”","Shen Yanshui smiled. “Thank you for reminding me, Your Highness. If you don’t mind, should I be fortunate enough to grow them successfully, I will give you some as well.”","Secondary Consort Tang did not believe she would truly manage to keep them alive, but she did like the scent of the Anxi fennel. Thus, she politely smiled and agreed.","The two were still chatting and laughing when suddenly, a scream nearly split the heavens!","“Ah—there’s a venomous snake!”","“Crash!”","“The Crown Princess!”","“Quick, someone come!”","“Your Highness! Her Highness is bleeding!”","“Hurry and summon the imperial physician!”","In an instant, the atmosphere, which had been filled with cheerful ease, descended into chaos.","The voices were coming from one of the rooms. They sounded somewhat distant, but both Shen Yanshui and Secondary Consort Tang hurried toward the commotion.","By the time Shen Yanshui followed the sound and arrived, she found several layers of people crowded outside the room, standing shoulder to shoulder. Nearly all the wives and female relatives of officials, as well as the guards, were there. Yet the area was unnaturally quiet, making the Crown Princess’s frightened cries of pain and the Empress’s calm questioning of the imperial physician inside the room especially clear.","“How are the Crown Princess and the child in her womb?”","The imperial physician was drenched in cold sweat. In the short span of time since he had arrived, his back was already soaked through. His fingers trembled instinctively as he pressed them against the Crown Princess’s wrist through a handkerchief.","The Crown Princess was unable to suppress the fear and panic in her heart. Her face was deathly pale, and she stared fixedly at the imperial physician, who had already dropped to his knees.","The physician kowtowed and replied in a trembling voice, “R-Reporting to Your Majesty, the Crown Princess was so badly startled that she has suffered a disturbance to her pregnancy. This subject will immediately prepare a prescription to protect the fetus, but...”","The Empress’s expression darkened. “But what?”","“But the Crown Princess has already begun to bleed. This subject... can only do his utmost.” Cold sweat covered the physician’s forehead, and he did not dare raise his head.","“No, no, that’s impossible! I order you to keep the child in my womb safe. If anything happens, even the slightest mishap, I will have your life!” the Crown Princess cried, her face pale and her emotions overwrought. She could not accept such a consequence!","The imperial physician instantly broke into a torrential sweat.","The Empress said grimly, “Help the imperial physician down and prepare the medicine to protect the fetus at once!”","“Yes!”","Someone immediately helped the physician to his feet and escorted him away.","Shen Yanshui’s heart tightened. The Crown Princess’s pregnancy...","She instinctively looked toward Lady Shen, who was standing not far ahead. From the surprise revealed between her brows, Shen Yanshui could tell that this matter likely had little to do with her.","She had not expected the person acting behind the scenes to be so audacious. After failing once, they had actually dared to strike again.","“Greetings, Your Highness the Crown Prince...”","Suddenly, the sound of palace maids and eunuchs kneeling and offering greetings rang out, followed by the greetings of the assembled wives of officials. Shen Yanshui naturally lowered her head as well. From the corner of her eye, she saw a familiar figure stride past with an imperial physician, before quickly entering the room.","The atmosphere inside and outside the room immediately grew even more tense.","Cui Yu’s expression was as dark as water. Without looking at anyone, he went straight inside. The moment he saw the expression on his mother’s face and the Crown Princess’s paper-white complexion, he felt his heart sink despite having been mentally prepared for this.","Shen Yanshui heard the Crown Prince’s voice, cold and heavy as ice, and did not dare relax in the slightest.","The imperial physician whom the Crown Prince had brought reached a conclusion almost identical to that of the first physician. Shen Yanshui tried to discern something from the faces of the high-ranking consorts and imperial princes’ consorts, but all she saw were expressions of concern. She sighed inwardly. As expected, every one of them was an excellent actress.","The physician, who had been observing the Crown Princess’s pulse, suddenly frowned, then relaxed slightly.","Cui Yu’s eyes turned cold, and he immediately asked in a deep voice, “What is it?”","Realizing that the Crown Prince had misunderstood, the physician hurriedly rose to his feet. Trembling with excitement, he said, “Reporting to Your Highness the Crown Prince and Your Majesty the Empress, the fetal heartbeat has grown slightly stronger. It seems Heaven is watching over the child!”","Heavens! His head was finally a little more securely attached to his neck.","At least the situation was no longer deteriorating. When he had taken her pulse earlier, there had been a moment when he could not feel the fetal heartbeat at all... Fortunately, Heaven had not abandoned them and had left the child a thread of hope.","“The medicine is here!”","An imperial physician personally brought the medicine over, and everyone hurriedly made way.","Outside the room, the various people concealed their differing thoughts beneath faces filled with concern.","Hearing the commotion inside, Shen Yanshui also relaxed slightly.","After the Crown Princess finished the medicine, the physician carefully inserted needles into her. Only after two quarters of an hour did he finally raise his sleeve and wipe the cold sweat from his forehead.","He immediately bowed toward the Empress and the Crown Prince, whose expressions were equally cold and solemn, and said, “Reporting to Your Highness the Crown Prince and Your Majesty the Empress, the child in the Crown Princess’s womb has been saved for the time being. However, she has suffered a disturbance to her pregnancy. From now on, the Crown Princess may need to remain bedridden throughout her pregnancy in order to safely give birth to the imperial grandson.”","The breath the Empress had been holding suddenly escaped her. Her legs went weak, and she nearly fell. The palace maid beside her and Cui Yu caught her just in time.","Cui Yu’s brows remained tightly furrowed. “Mother’s health has yet to recover. Help her rest for a while.”","The Empress frowned. “There’s no need...” How could she possibly rest at a time like this?","Cui Yu said, “Mother, rest assured. I am here.”","The Empress looked at the emotions in his eyes, her brows drawing together even more tightly. In a voice so low it was almost inaudible, she asked, “Did you know that the Crown Princess was pregnant...?”","Cui Yu’s voice was low and cold. “I did not.”","The Empress’s heart sank. Her entire body went limp as she leaned back against the chair.","The Crown Princess had actually gone to such lengths to conceal this from Yu’er...","Then again, if Yu’er had known, the Crown Princess would not have appeared here today. For a moment, the Empress was so angry and furious that she almost wanted to laugh.","What on earth was the Crown Princess thinking? What was she trying to do?","***","Once the Crown Princess’s condition had temporarily stabilized, Cui Yu wore a grim expression and immediately had the people involved brought before him. After swiftly interrogating them and clarifying the sequence of events, he sent someone to report to Emperor Pingkang.","Emperor Pingkang was enraged!","Not only because the Crown Princess had nearly miscarried, but also because of the venomous snake that had appeared from nowhere.","A palace maid serving the Crown Princess had been bitten. The venom was fatal upon contact with blood, and she died in less than two breaths.","What if one—or even several—of those deadly snakes had appeared beside him as well?","Emperor Pingkang immediately ordered the dragon boat to dock and instructed the Directorate of Palace Administration to investigate the matter thoroughly.","The First Prince and Fourth Prince, who had been responsible for security during the banquet at Jinming Lake, came forward to accept responsibility. Emperor Pingyuan directly stripped both of them of their positions in court. Noble Consort Lan and Consort De were also implicated and punished with the loss of a year’s salary.","***","When Shen Yanshui returned to the Eastern Palace, Chunping, who had been taken away, still had not come back.","Seeing her return, Quanfu quickly noticed the unusual atmosphere from the change in his mistress’s expression and the banquet at Jinming Lake ending ahead of schedule.","Once the door was closed, Xia'an, who could never keep her questions to herself, immediately asked in a low voice, “Mistress, did something happen at the Xifang Palace?”","Before their mistress returned, the commotion from the Xifang Palace had been so great that even those in the rear rooms had faintly heard it.","This had already left them feeling uneasy. Now that their mistress had returned as well, they finally seemed to have found someone to rely on, and their hearts eased somewhat.","But why hadn’t Sister Chunping returned...?","Seeing the worried, pale, and frightened expressions on everyone’s faces, Shen Yanshui composed herself and said, “The Crown Princess is pregnant and was startled, causing a disturbance to her pregnancy. His Majesty has ordered the Directorate of Palace Administration to investigate thoroughly. The palace will not be peaceful in the days to come, so be more cautious and keep a low profile in everything you do.”","As for Chunping... Recalling what Lady Shen had deliberately said to her earlier, Shen Yanshui unconsciously knitted her brows. After pondering for a moment, she quickly made up her mind.","She could not afford to take any chances.","After receiving their mistress’s instructions, everyone’s expressions turned solemn, and their faces could not help but pale.","Although this matter seemed unrelated to them, so long as Chunping did not return, none of them could truly set their minds at ease.","Shen Yanshui looked at Quanfu and said in a low voice, “Keep watch for when His Highness the Crown Prince returns to the Eastern Palace. Report to me at once when you receive word.”","Quanfu lowered his head anxiously and acknowledged the order.","Three quarters of an hour later, Quanfu returned and reported that His Highness the Crown Prince had gone back to the Eastern Palace, but had proceeded to the Fragrant Garden Hall.","Shen Yanshui nodded, picked up two small rice dumplings, and ate them to calm her nerves.","She had initially thought that the Crown Prince would remain in the Fragrant Garden Hall for quite some time. After all, the Crown Princess had nearly miscarried. Yet before even the time it took to burn a single stick of incense had passed, she learned that His Highness had left the Fragrant Garden Hall and gone to the front hall.","Shen Yanshui was slightly surprised. What had happened? It had only been a few minutes. Could it be that the Crown Princess had felt unwell and gone to rest? Or perhaps...","The lavishly furnished inner chamber of the Fragrant Garden Hall was now filled with the thick, unpleasant smell of medicine.","“Crash!”","A fine celadon vase was violently smashed onto the floor, sending shards of porcelain flying in every direction.","“Your Highness!” Matron Zhou hurried forward and seized her hand. Choking back a sob, she said in a low, panicked voice, “My lady, His Highness the Crown Prince has only just left. What if he heard that noise?”","The Crown Princess’s pale face flushed red, then turned white again. Her hands clenched tightly into the silk sheets beneath her.","She lowered her voice, yet could not suppress the panic in her heart. “Did you see it, Matron? I am the Crown Princess, and I was nearly made to miscarry, yet His Highness... Does His Highness truly regard me as his wife? As his Crown Princess?”","As she spoke, the Crown Princess’s eyes reddened, and a trace of resentment appeared in their depths.","Matron Zhou’s wrinkled face furrowed, but she did not know how to persuade her.","The medicine the Crown Princess had been taking all this time was clearly meant to protect the pregnancy, not to treat a cold. It would not be difficult to investigate the matter thoroughly.","Yet when Matron Zhou saw the expression on the Crown Princess’s face, she ultimately swallowed the words that had reached her lips.","She had watched the Crown Princess grow up. Her mistress had never been able to listen to unpleasant truths. At a time like this, nothing she said would be of any use. The only choice was to indulge her.","“Your Highness, the imperial physician said that you must avoid excessive emotional agitation. It would be harmful both to you and to the child in your womb.” She paused, then continued to comfort her. “His Highness the Crown Prince has always been that way. He treats everyone alike. Surely Your Highness knows this. Why make yourself angry over it?”","Seeing the Crown Princess’s expression relax somewhat, she pressed on.","“Besides, His Highness came straight to the Fragrant Garden Hall to see you after returning from His Majesty. That shows that he still has you in his heart. Your Highness is carrying two lives now, and the child in your womb is the Crown Prince’s legitimate heir. How could His Highness not be worried or concerned?”","The Crown Princess’s anger finally eased a little, and the faint unease in her heart gradually dissipated. Recalling that the Crown Prince had indeed not blamed her, she felt somewhat reassured. He had merely worn his usual cold expression, instructed her to rest and care for the pregnancy, arranged for an imperial physician, and then departed.","Zheng Yuande hurried along behind his master, his steps quick. He stole a glance at the Crown Prince’s cold, gloomy face, and all the fat on his body trembled. He kept wiping the cold sweat from his brow.","He could not help but feel resentful toward the Crown Princess.","That was His Highness’s legitimate son. The Crown Princess had deliberately concealed it from the Crown Prince. Was that not an obvious sign that she did not trust him?","She had even claimed that she had been afraid the pregnancy would not hold and that she would only be giving His Highness false hope—that she had wanted to surprise him.","If that had truly been the case, then perhaps she could be said to be deeply devoted to His Highness.","Unfortunately, the Crown Prince was no fool. Before this, keeping silent might still have been understandable. But they were already about to go to Golden Bright Lake, and she had still not revealed the slightest hint. Yet she still had the audacity to say that she had feared he would worry?","In the depths of his heart, Zheng Yuande very irreverently spat, “Tui!”","Where did she get the nerve? Seriously?!","Back in the study of the Palace of Diligent Governance, Cui Yu’s face was cold as he said in a low voice, “Send word to Assistant Director Wang. Have him deliver any news immediately.”","Zheng Yuande bowed at once and respectfully acknowledged the order.","Assistant Director Wang was one of the most powerful officials in the Directorate of Palace Servants, second only to the two Chief Directors. He was also the Eastern Palace’s man within the Directorate.","***","Shen Yanshui brought Quanfu and Xia’an to the front hall to request an audience with the Crown Prince.","Cao Zhongda, the eunuch in charge of the Eastern Palace’s front hall, wore a solemn expression as well, affected by the oppressive atmosphere in the palace. “Lady Shen, you have come at an unfortunate time. His Highness left the Eastern Palace just moments ago to pay his respects to Her Majesty the Empress at the Palace of Earthly Tranquility. If you have something to say, you may tell this servant. Once His Highness returns, I will certainly relay your words to him.”","Shen Yanshui knitted her brows slightly, then nodded naturally. “Thank you for your kindness, Eunuch Cao. However, I imagine you have many duties to attend to, so I shall not trouble you. I will request an audience with His Highness tomorrow.”","With that, she inclined her head toward him and turned to leave with her attendants.","Cao Zhongda gave a slight bow. He merely lifted his eyes to watch Lady Shen’s departing figure, a thoughtful expression appearing on his face.","After returning to Lotus Heart Court, Shen Yanshui ordered the servants to bring in the meal and ate as usual.","Seeing that their mistress could still calmly eat, everyone else felt more settled as well. At last, they were no longer quite so panicked.","After Shen Yanshui had eaten her fill, she proceeded as usual. This time, however, she did not go outside for a walk to aid digestion. Instead, she strolled slowly around Lotus Heart Court.","When the sky gradually darkened into a deep gray, she bathed, washed up, and lay down to sleep.","***","When Cui Yu returned to the Eastern Palace, his entire body radiating coldness and his face expressionless, he learned what had happened.","Sitting before the writing desk, he thought about what the Empress Dowager had said earlier, as well as the news just delivered by the Directorate of Palace Servants. His sharp brows lifted slightly, and his voice was unnaturally calm.","“Oh?”","Cao Zhongda lowered his head and said nothing, but Zheng Yuande’s heart trembled.","By now, he also knew what had happened to the Crown Princess that day. Even before the poisonous snake appeared, someone had already attempted to harm the Crown Princess and frame Lady Zhang for it. Fortunately, Lady Shen had pulled her away in time, preventing the culprit from succeeding.","Yet according to the palace maid serving the Crown Princess, suspicion had instead fallen upon Lady Shen. Lady Shen and Lady Shen had exchanged a few quiet words in private beforehand, so perhaps the entire incident had been a self-directed performance...","The Fourth Prince was also responsible for the dragon boat’s safety. If this matter had indeed been secretly ordered by Noble Consort Lan and the Fourth Prince, then it would have been exceedingly convenient for them.","And now Lady Shen had actually come to him of her own accord at such a time...","Cui Yu tapped his fingers restlessly against the writing desk for a long while. Then he suddenly rose.","“Go to Lotus Heart Court.”","The night was as deep as water, and all was silent.","The Eastern Palace lay in utter stillness. Yet the moment the sounds belonging exclusively to the Crown Prince reached the corridor outside the rear quarters, everyone’s attention was drawn toward them.","Quite a few people even wondered inwardly whether His Highness the Crown Prince could truly be in the mood to enter the rear quarters today.","Unbeknownst to them, another fine porcelain cup was shattered in the Fragrant Garden Hall.","With the Crown Prince’s arrival, Lotus Heart Court instantly brightened with lamplight. This time, Shen Yanshui had not been slow to react. At her mistress’s instruction, Quanfu went inside to announce His Highness’s arrival the moment the Crown Prince stepped into the corridor of the rear quarters.","Shen Yanshui wore a loose moon-white robe. Her hair was arranged in a simple, casual cloud-knot, secured only by a pink-and-green tourmaline hairpin carved in the shape of auspicious clouds.","The moment she stepped outside and raised her eyes, she saw the Crown Prince approaching in great strides. He was dressed in black trimmed with silver, and his entire person radiated a chilling air.","She hurriedly lowered her head and bowed. “This concubine pays her respects to His Highness the Crown Prince.”","They had already seen from afar that the Crown Prince was in a state entirely unlike his usual self. After the people of Lotus Heart Court knelt in greeting, they did not even dare breathe too loudly.","Cui Yu did not pause. He stepped over the cluster of servants and continued forward until he reached Shen Yanshui. She felt a broad palm gently support her arm, and heard a low voice beside her ear say, “Rise.”","She could not help feeling somewhat relieved.","It seemed that the Directorate of Palace Servants was taking longer to investigate than she had expected.","But hadn’t the Crown Princess previously been sounding out Lady Shen and her as well? Why had she never mentioned it to the Crown Prince?","Judging by the Crown Prince’s manner, he apparently still knew nothing about the private conversation between Lady Shen and herself. Otherwise, his attitude toward her would not still be considered gentle.","She had already prepared for the worst. At most, the Crown Prince would suspect that she had joined forces with Lady Shen, Noble Consort Lan, and the others to plot against the Crown Princess.","Although there was no evidence, even without evidence, it was perfectly ordinary for one or two low-ranking secondary consorts in the Eastern Palace to fall quietly ill and die.","If matters truly came to that, she would have to find a way to fake her death and escape. Those serving her had been assigned by the palace, and they had not served her for long. Given the Crown Prince’s temperament, he likely would not take their lives even if they were implicated.","As for Chunping...","Now that the Crown Prince was willing to seek her out of his own accord, he still trusted her to some degree—at least two or three parts out of ten.","Shen Yanshui rose with the support of his hand. With a respectful expression and a hint of nervousness, she lowered her head and said, “Thank you, Your Highness.”","Cui Yu glanced at her and said in a deep voice, “Come inside. We’ll talk.”","With that, he clasped his hands behind his back and stepped into the room.","Shen Yanshui acknowledged him with a quiet reply and raised a hand to signal that no one should come in to attend them. Once inside, she first served the Crown Prince a cup of warm tea. Then she took two steps back and suddenly knelt, saying solemnly, “Your Highness, this concubine has something to report.”","Zheng Yuande, who had been standing beside the Crown Prince, was startled by her sudden movement. He stole a glance at his master’s expression and hesitated for a moment before quietly withdrawing.","Cui Yu lifted his eyes slightly. His gaze was deep and unreadable. His fingers rubbed the porcelain cup, which held just the right degree of warmth. Only after a moment did he ask in a deep voice, “What is it?”","Shen Yanshui’s bright, limpid peach-blossom eyes, as though washed clean by water, were now filled with unease. Her brows drew together slightly, making anyone who saw her instinctively want to smooth away the worry and sorrow between them.","Cui Yu lowered his eyes and took a sip of tea.","There was an unmistakable note of nervousness in Shen Yanshui’s voice. “Your Highness, it concerns my elder sister, Lady Shen. Today, after the Crown Princess learned that she was with child, Lady Shen saw me and instructed me to keep my distance from the Crown Princess. At the time, I did not know why Lady Shen would say such a thing. I had also spoken somewhat discourteously to her, so after saying that, she simply turned and left.”","“This concubine is foolish. Although I had some vague suspicions in my heart, I had no evidence at all. My status is lowly, and I was frightened and at a loss, not knowing whom I could tell. I could only remain on guard and observe matters myself... If I had told the Crown Princess immediately, perhaps she would not have suffered from disturbed fetal energy. This concubine was at fault. I beg Your Highness to forgive me.”","She did not mention that she had promptly held Lady Zhang back. If nothing had happened to the Crown Princess, that could be counted as a merit.","But ​​‌‌​‌‌​​‌‌​​​​‌​‌‌​​​‌‌​‌‌​​​‌‌​​‌‌‌​​​​​‌‌‌​​​​​‌‌​‌​‌​‌‌​​‌​‌​​‌‌​‌​​​‌‌​​​​‌​‌‌​​​‌​​​‌‌‌​​​​​‌‌​​​​​‌‌​​‌​‌​​‌‌​‌​‌​‌‌​​​‌‌​​‌‌​​​​​​‌‌​‌‌​​​‌‌​‌​‌​​‌‌​‌‌​​‌‌​​​​‌​‌‌​​‌​​​‌‌​​​​‌​‌‌​​‌​‌‍the Crown Princess had ultimately suffered from disturbed fetal energy and had even nearly miscarried. There was no need to bring it up now. Otherwise, it would seem as though she were deliberately claiming credit before the Crown Prince to prove her innocence.","Even though she said nothing, Cui Yu knew what had happened at the time.","As he listened to her account, which matched the testimony submitted by the Directorate of Palace Servants in every detail, without the slightest deception, the crease between his brows slowly eased before he even realized it."]},{"number":35,"title":"Chapter 35: Delectable Beauty","paragraphs":["Cui Yu watched her damp lashes as she lowered her head. He rose and took a step forward, then bent slightly to grasp her arm and help her to her feet. The coldness in his expression had vanished, replaced by a trace of warmth. His deep voice held a gentleness that had not been there before. “I understand. This was not your fault, so there is no need to trouble yourself over it.”","“Thank you for your forgiveness, Your Highness.” Shen Yanshui’s lashes trembled faintly. She raised her eyes to look at him, her brows still slightly furrowed. After biting her lip, she spoke hesitantly, “But there is one more favor I would ask of you...”","Cui Yu took her cool little hand and sat down with her on the soft couch. “What is it?”","Shen Yanshui looked at him, unconsciously curling her fingers around his. In a cautious voice, she said, “It is about Chunping, the lady-in-waiting who was taken away from my side today. I cannot help but worry about her. I do not mean to ask Your Highness to show her favoritism; I was only wondering when the Directorate of Palace Servants will finish questioning her, and when Chunping might return?”","Cui Yu cast her a sidelong glance, his tone calm and composed. “She will be back tomorrow.”","“Really?” Shen Yanshui’s eyes widened at once. A faint mist of tears still shimmered in her beautiful, peach-blossom eyes. Beneath the pale yellow candlelight, her thick, curling lashes seemed dusted with tiny crystals, making her clear eyes appear all the brighter. The surprise, delight, and happiness in her gaze were impossible to miss.","Looking at her, Cui Yu gently brushed his thumb across the dampness at the corner of her eye. His voice was low and clear. “When have I ever lied to you?”","Relieved, Shen Yanshui immediately asked softly, “You have been busy all day, Your Highness. Are you hungry? Would you like to try some egg tarts or peach blossom pastries?” She rose and carried over the two plates of pastries that had been prepared on the round table, setting them on the small table between them on the couch.","Apart from having eaten an early breakfast, Cui Yu had hardly eaten anything that day. The banquet held for the officials at Linshui Hall was not truly intended as a meal, and he had merely eaten a few hurried bites to get by.","Afterward, so much had happened that he had forgotten all about eating and had no appetite whatsoever.","Now, however, he inexplicably felt somewhat hungry. After eating two egg tarts, he said, “It is getting late. Eating too many pastries will make them difficult to digest.” With that, he summoned Zheng Yuande.","Zheng Yuande hurried into the room on tiptoe, taking small, careful steps. “What are Your Highness’s orders?”","“Have the kitchens prepare two simple portions of late-night food, something easy to digest.” Thinking of how hearty her appetite usually was, and how she had encountered all this on her first visit to the Jinming Pool gathering, he knew she must have been preoccupied and had probably not eaten properly all day either.","Shen Yanshui had no idea what he was thinking. Although she truly did have matters weighing on her mind—she had even considered faking her death to escape—she had certainly not eaten any less than usual.","Her supernatural ability had been depleted excessively that day, though. She had eaten roughly her usual portion at dinner, but stopped after becoming only seventy or eighty percent full. That was why she had secretly ordered two plates of pastries to keep herself from getting hungry later.","She had never expected to get a late-night meal while tagging along with the Crown Prince.","At his words, Zheng Yuande immediately looked up in delighted surprise. He nodded repeatedly, unable to resist sneaking two glances at Lady Shen.","Ever since learning that the Crown Princess was with child and had nearly suffered a miscarriage, unsettling the fetus, His Highness had been in a poor mood. When he had arrived earlier, his emotions had been like a violent storm, his entire person steeped in cold severity. Yet now he had actually remembered to eat. Zheng Yuande was overjoyed.","Seeing Zheng Yuande's somewhat comical expression, made all the more so by the flesh on his face and his excitement, Shen Yanshui pressed her lips together in a smile. After watching him briskly hurry out to give instructions, she said, \"Eunuch Zheng cares deeply for Your Highness.\"","Cui Yu said nothing, merely casting her a sidelong glance.","Zheng Yuande had served at his side since childhood; that went without saying. But the maid called Chunping had only been assigned to attend Shen Yanshui after she entered the Eastern Palace.","Yet in barely a month's time, she had gone out of her way to plead with him on behalf of a maid of the humblest status.","He suddenly spoke, asking at an unhurried pace, \"You plead for the maid who serves you now. But if she were disloyal to you, betraying and selling you out as her mistress, what would you do?\"","Shen Yanshui did not know why he had changed the subject so abruptly, but she smiled and replied evenly, \"To be frank with Your Highness, I had long heard of the Judicial Office. While I was still at the Palace of Beautiful Selection, the senior attendants often impressed upon us the formidable reputation of the Judicial Office. It was precisely because of this that I dared to plead with Your Highness on Chunping's behalf.\"","\"The ancients said that loyalty is reverence. The character for loyalty combines heart and sound; to give one's whole heart is to be loyal. Ever since Chunping began serving by my side, she has been diligent and conscientious. She has done no wrong, carried out her duties faithfully, and offered me much useful guidance. That is already loyalty to me.\"","\"I have done what is upright and sat with a clear conscience. There is nothing I cannot say before others.\" Her eyes were full of trust as she looked at him, her voice clear and bright. \"And I believe Your Highness would never allow anyone to falsely accuse me at will. Naturally, I have nothing to hide.\"","Fortunately, after Lady Shen had come to see her, Shen Yanshui had prepared in advance. She had instructed Chunping that should anyone ask about the matter later, she was to answer honestly and had no need to conceal anything deliberately.","Otherwise, Shen Yanshui truly would have had reason to worry that Chunping might be coerced into framing her for one reason or another.","In the apocalypse, she had long witnessed just how far human goodness and evil could go. She had never been sparing in assuming the worst of people.","Yet the Crown Prince's trust in her still surprised her somewhat.","Warmth rose in Cui Yu's heart as he met her gaze.","He turned his hand over and clasped her small one. For a time, he said nothing. Only after a long while did he suddenly look up at her and ask, \"What is your given name?\"","Shen Yanshui: \"...\"","It had been a month. They had even slept together several times, yet he still did not know her name?","Then again, in Great Yong, not every family gave their daughters personal names. More often, they were addressed according to their birth order within the family; after marriage, they simply became so-and-so's wife.","Very well.","Her brows curved, her smile unchanged. Holding his broad palm, she traced words upon it with her fingers as she said with a smile, \"Yanshui. Shen Yanshui.\"","Cui Yu's thin lips parted. \"Yanshui? In the northern frontier, there is a river called Yan, beyond the city of Suyab.\" As he spoke, he caught hold of her restless hand.","She lightly tapped his palm with the tip of her finger, her voice tinged with reproach. “When other people hear my name, they all say it sounds gentle and lovely. Yet Your Highness’s first reaction was to think of a tributary mentioned in a geographical gazetteer?”","Cui Yu lifted his eyes to look at her, his voice cool and even. “Who said that?”","Shen Yanshui: “...”","Was that really the part he chose to focus on?","Under the sharpness of his gaze, Shen Yanshui felt a little sheepish, though her tone remained perfectly natural. “Who else could it be? Naturally, one of my close friends.”","In truth, it had been Xu Chengwen—who had nearly become her fiancé—who had said something along those lines. But there was no need to mention that to the Crown Prince.","Cui Yu turned his gaze away and smoothly changed the subject, his voice faint. “Your father chose that name for you?”","Her slender, pale fingers unconsciously toyed with his long, fair, clearly defined fingers. “It wasn’t my father. According to one of the old nurses in the household, it was my mother who gave me the name.”","When she was three, an old-looking nurse—though in reality, she had been only a little over thirty—had told her the story through her tears.","That was when Shen Yanshui learned that in this world, she too was called Shen Yanshui, the name her late mother had given her.","Cui Yu suddenly said, “Yanshui... perhaps it also carries the meaning of wild geese returning to autumn waters. Perhaps your mother was longing for her family when she gave you that name.” After saying this, he looked at her slightly stunned expression and asked, “You never met any of your mother’s family?”","Shen Yanshui came back to herself and shook her head. “No. My mother passed away not long after giving birth to me. No one from her family has come looking for me all these years. When I was little, I asked my father about it once, and he only said that she had no other family in this world.”","As soon as she finished speaking, a broad, warm palm nearly enveloped her hand. She lifted her eyes to look at him and seemed to detect, beneath his usual calm and impassive expression, a trace of consolation... and perhaps even a hint of pity.","She could not help sighing inwardly. Although the Crown Prince always appeared expressionless and cold, he was not truly an indifferent man.","It was just that... the Crown Princess had suffered a pregnancy scare today. According to the imperial physician, she ought to remain in bed and rest for the remainder of her pregnancy, yet the Crown Prince’s attitude seemed somewhat...","The Crown Princess had concealed her three-month pregnancy until today. Given the dispositions of both the Empress and the Crown Prince, they most likely had not known about it beforehand.","To be deliberately kept in the dark and distrusted by one’s own wife... that could not have been a pleasant feeling.","Still, since this concerned the Crown Prince and Crown Princess, she had no intention of saying anything.","In fact, strictly speaking, discord between the Crown Prince and Crown Princess would be advantageous to her. For a favored concubine like herself, refraining from fanning the flames or turning him against her was already commendable enough.","She returned the clasp of his broad, warm hand and said gently, “Your Highness needn’t grieve on my account. I have Your Highness now, and I am already more than content.”","Looking into her eyes, full of dependence and trust, Cui Yu unconsciously tightened his hold on her soft little hand.","Just then, Zheng Yuande led several young eunuchs into the room, each carrying a food box.","Shen Yanshui looked at the simple yet surprisingly generous late-night meal, and could not help smiling to herself.","It was getting late. The two of them did not speak again while eating their late-night meal. Shen Yanshui could tell that the Crown Prince was genuinely hungry this time. He not only finished an entire bowl of chicken-and-shredded-meat noodles, but also drank two bowls of porridge.","Even though he ate much faster than usual, for some reason, he still appeared unhurried and graceful, a pleasure to watch.","Shen Yanshui ate slowly, taking a bite now and then, while her limpid, alluring peach-blossom eyes kept stealing glances at his exceptionally handsome face.","Then, in the very next moment, she unexpectedly met his seemingly indifferent gaze as he looked over at her.","Cui Yu’s hand paused for an instant. In an even tone, he asked, “Why do you keep looking at me?”","Shen Yanshui blinked. “Haven’t you heard the saying that a beautiful face is enough to satisfy one’s hunger? The late-night meal is so light. With Your Highness’s face to accompany it, I could easily eat two more bowls of porridge.”","Cui Yu cast her a sidelong glance. After a moment, he slowly said, “You’re becoming more and more audacious.”","Zheng Yuande, who was standing nearby to attend to them, was so startled that his eyes, already narrowed by the flesh of his cheeks, flew wide open when Lady Shen actually dared to tease His Highness.","A sharp “How dare you!” was already on the tip of his tongue when his master casually said a few words and left it at that. With considerable difficulty, Zheng Yuande swallowed the rest of his rebuke.","Even so, Zheng Yuande remained utterly astonished.","Was His Highness really reprimanding and warning her? This was clearly indulgence!","Shen Yanshui glanced at his face, which showed no sign of displeasure, then muttered in an “extremely soft” voice, “How was I being bold? I’m terribly timid, you know. Your Highness can’t punish me just because you happen to be too handsome and I looked at you a couple of times and spoke nothing but the truth.”","When she saw his brows twitch, the corner of his mouth quiver slightly, and his face fill with surprise and speechlessness, she could not help finding it amusing.","Cui Yu looked at her mischievous little expression as she tried to suppress her laughter. For some reason, the gloom that had settled deep in his heart eased a little.","He gave a cold snort and assessed her in a rather detached tone. “You have quite a silver tongue.”","Zheng Yuande could only marvel at the sight.","No wonder His Highness liked coming to Lady Shen’s quarters. Just look at her—look at how she had coaxed His Highness into this state!","Shen Yanshui studied his flawless, jade-white, handsome face from close by. Seeing that the gloom between his brows had lessened, she felt that she had played the role of a soothing confidante exceedingly well today.","After they finished their late-night meal, she had the servants clear everything away.","Xia’an and Qiuru came over carrying a copper basin and white cloths, attending to the Crown Prince and Shen Yanshui as they washed their hands.","Through the half-open lattice window, Shen Yanshui glanced at the star-filled night sky outside. Turning back, she asked, “Your Highness, would you like to take a walk and help your food settle?”","Cui Yu looked at her. “No need. It’s late. You should retire early.” With that, he rose to his feet.","Hearing the implication in his words, Shen Yanshui was somewhat surprised, though not entirely so.","If the Crown Princess had suffered from pregnancy pains that very night and the Crown Prince had then stayed in her quarters, rumors might spread the next day that the Crown Prince and Crown Princess were not on good terms—or that the Crown Prince did not respect the Crown Princess.","It would also cause the Crown Princess to regard her as a thorn in her side and a splinter in her flesh in the future—these were all consequences that could easily be foreseen. If the Crown Prince had stayed, it would mean that he himself neither cared nor minded.","If she dared to presume upon this harmless indulgence and favor, and kept prattling on in front of the Crown Prince—","Honestly, what gave her such confidence?","A person’s greatest virtue was knowing her own place.","After seeing him off, Shen Yanshui returned to her room in high spirits and fell straight into bed. She had not eaten much of the late-night snack, and after circulating her ability for a little while, she had digested it completely. It would not affect her sleep in the slightest.","Many ​​‌‌​‌‌​​‌‌​​​​‌​‌‌​​​‌‌​‌‌​​‌​​​​‌‌​​‌​​‌‌​​‌‌​​​‌‌‌​​‌​​‌‌‌​​​​​‌‌​‌​​​‌‌​​​​‌​‌‌​​​‌​​​‌‌‌​​​​​‌‌​​​​​‌‌​​‌​‌​​‌‌​‌​‌​‌‌​​​‌‌​​‌‌​​​​​​‌‌​‌‌​​​‌‌​‌‌​​‌‌​​​‌‌​​‌‌​‌​‌​​‌‌‌​​‌​​‌‌‌​​​​​‌‌​​‌​‍of the women in the rear quarters had still been keeping an eye on the Crown Prince. The moment he left Lianxin Court, they hurried back to their respective mistresses to report the news.","The Crown Prince had gone to Lianxin Court so late at night, called for a late-night snack there, and yet had not stayed the night.","Quite a few people could not help feeling sour at the thought, and they gnashed their teeth in hatred at the vixen in Lianxin Court.","Lady Chu had not retired either. When she heard the news, she inexplicably felt somewhat relieved.","Still, she could not help feeling a little disappointed. She took great pleasure in anything that could make the Crown Princess lose face.","Back when she was still unmarried, she had seen the Crown Princess several times and had already sensed what sort of person lay beneath that dignified, virtuous, and gentle exterior.","The Crown Princess’s grandfather had once been a renowned scholar of Great Yong. She had been raised at her grandparents’ knees from childhood and was said to have been deeply doted on. Only after both grandparents passed away was she taken back to the capital and returned to her parents’ household. Yet she had been extraordinarily fortunate: she was chosen by His Majesty and the Empress and became the Crown Princess in a single bound.","At heart, however, she looked down severely on warriors who acted roughly and rashly. She was exceedingly aloof, held everyone beneath her notice, and thought highly of herself.","Thus, although she appeared extremely filial toward the Empress, she was not truly respectful in her heart toward an Empress who came from a powerful military family of nobles and whose conduct was entirely different from her own.","At the time, Lady Chu had deliberately used Lady Sun’s miscarriage as an opportunity to make a tactful request of the Empress. She had claimed to be frightened and uneasy and asked the Empress to send an experienced matron to look after her. After the Empress agreed, the Crown Princess had immediately become indignant and resentful. She had even come to bear a grudge against the Empress for “treating them differently.”","The Crown Princess was narrow-minded, and even her superficial efforts were poorly executed. She could not help revealing traces of her true feelings whenever she was in the Empress’s presence.","Naturally, Lady Chu’s objective had been achieved.","It would be best if the Empress and even the Crown Prince came to dislike the legitimate son born to the Crown Princess because of her. That way, her own future child would have even more leverage.","What surprised her, however, was that the Crown Princess was pregnant as well—and already three months along—yet not the slightest rumor had gotten out.","Even the Empress and the Crown Prince knew nothing.","At the thought of this, Lady Chu nearly laughed aloud, had she not been mindful of the matron sent by the Empress who was serving in the adjoining room.","This was the Crown Princess digging her own grave. She had brought it upon herself. Lady Chu did not even need to sow discord on her behalf. She refused to believe that the Empress and the Crown Prince would not harbor misgivings about the Crown Princess.","Yet just as she was thinking this, a strange feeling of panic and oppression suddenly rose in her heart again. She felt miserable for quite some time before the symptoms finally eased, though her complexion looked even paler than before.","The elderly matron the Empress had sent to attend her could not help feeling deeply worried at the sight.","Lady Chu's spirits had worsened by the day. The matron had privately wondered whether there might be something unclean about their surroundings, and had even used the excuse of summoning an imperial physician to have everything inspected. Yet nothing had been found; it was said only that such symptoms were common during pregnancy.","Still, she could not shake the feeling that something was amiss...","******","Early the next morning, the sky was overcast, and the air was damp and stifling. Not long after Shen Yanshui had finished breakfast and practiced a set of the Eight Brocades, Chunping was escorted back by a eunuch in the Crown Prince's service.","With a smile, Shen Yanshui said, “Thank you for taking the trouble, young eunuch.” As she spoke, she signaled with her eyes for Quanfu to slip him a purse.","Wang Chun wore a broad smile, but he did not accept the rather substantial purse. Hastily pushing it back, he said with a grin, “It was only a small matter. Your Ladyship is far too kind. Come to think of it, Sister Chunping and I even have rather similar names.”","Surprised inwardly, Shen Yanshui smiled. “Oh? And how should I address you, young eunuch? I have not been in the Eastern Palace long, and I still do not know all those who serve at His Highness's side.”","Wang Chun quickly bowed, his face still fixed in a smile. “This servant does not deserve to be called ‘young eunuch.’ Your Ladyship may simply call this servant Little Chun.”","This opportunity was one he had gone out of his way to secure for himself. Although his godfather was the foremost attendant at the Crown Prince's side—","his godfather had many godsons beneath him, and was even more inclined to promote men from his own hometown.","As for those, like him, who had attached themselves to his patron, his godfather accepted no shortage of gifts, but did not think much of them.","If he wanted to earn greater favor, he would have to find another path. Lady Shen was the opportunity he had chosen, one that might allow him to catch the Crown Prince's eye.","Shen Yanshui nodded with a smile. “So you are Eunuch Wang. It truly is fate that our names are so alike. You have had a tiring journey; would you care to come in for a cup of tea?”","Wang Chun hastily shook his head again and again. With a rueful, crumpled smile, he said, “Your Ladyship, please do not honor this servant so highly. This servant cannot bear it. If my godfather learns of it, he will surely tug this servant's ears and scold him for not knowing the proper rules.”","His godfather?","Following his lead, Shen Yanshui asked whether his godfather was Eunuch Zheng. When he smiled and nodded, she was somewhat surprised, though she exchanged a few more polite words with him.","Wang Chun knew when to stop. Seeing that the mistress and her servants had matters to discuss, how could he linger and make himself unwelcome?","Thus, still smiling broadly, he said, “This servant must return to report to His Highness, so I shall not disturb Your Ladyship any longer. Is there anything Your Ladyship would like this servant to convey to His Highness?”","Smiling, Shen Yanshui replied, “Then I must trouble Eunuch Little Chun to deliver a message to His Highness. Please tell him that I am deeply grateful. Whenever His Highness has the time, I shall personally prepare a table of delicious dishes for him.”","Hearing her address him as “Eunuch Little Chun,” a touch more intimate than usual, Wang Chun felt pleased. He said no more, merely smiling as he assured her, “Rest easy, Your Ladyship. This servant will certainly deliver your message.” With that, he bowed with a smile and took his leave.","After having Quanfu see the visitors out, Shen Yanshui turned to Chunping, whose face was somewhat pale. She swept her gaze over the others, then noticed the eunuch standing before the door of the western room watching them from across the courtyard.","“Let’s go inside and talk first,” she said.","Xia’an and the others who attended her hurried into the room. Quanshou and Dongyi remained outside to stand guard.","The moment they entered, Shen Yanshui had only just seated herself on the cushioned couch when Chunping dropped to her knees and kowtowed. Her grateful voice was tinged with a sob.","“This servant thanks you, Mistress, for saving my life!”","Shen Yanshui quickly rose and helped her up. “It isn’t that serious. Get up. Why is your face so pale?” Her brows knit slightly. “Were you subjected to harsh interrogation?”","The others looked at Chunping as well, their faces full of concern.","Chunping hurriedly shook her head. “In reply to Mistress, they did not use torture on this servant. I said exactly what you instructed me to say. And since you had saved the Crown Princess once to begin with, this servant was not a primary suspect for interrogation. After they questioned me, I was merely held under guard.”","It was only that she had witnessed others being brutally interrogated, while those shrill, miserable screams rang endlessly in her ears...","The furrow between Shen Yanshui’s brows eased slightly.","Xia’an let out a breath of relief. “Thank goodness you’re back, Sister Chunping. We were worried sick!”","The lives of palace servants were worthless. If one died, then one died. She had thought that Chunping, after being taken away, might simply vanish without a sound.","Yet she had never expected their mistress to plead with His Highness the Crown Prince for Chunping’s sake—servants as lowly as they were.","The other palace maids who had been taken away had not yet returned, not even the maids who served at the Crown Princess’s side...","And this was after everything that had happened yesterday. With one careless misstep, even their mistress herself might have incurred the Crown Prince’s wrath.","The others shared Xia’an’s thoughts. For a moment, their hearts surged with fierce gratitude and emotion.","Their mistress kept her word. Though she usually told them to keep a low profile and avoid trouble, if something truly happened, she would not push them out as scapegoats. Nor would she abandon them as disposable pawns simply to protect herself.","After Shen Yanshui took a sip of tea and looked up again, she found several faces with reddened eyes, brimming with tears.","She could not help laughing. “What is all this about?” She had merely adapted her approach according to the Crown Prince’s mood.","Besides, she had not acted entirely for Chunping’s sake. More than anything, she had done it for herself. There was no need for them to be so moved.","Still, seeing how much more united they were than before, she said nothing further.","Chunping quickly chided them, “Crying is forbidden in the palace! Don’t let us bring trouble upon Mistress and make her suffer because of us.”","The others forced their tears back.","Shen Yanshui looked in some surprise at Quanfu, whose eyes too were wet and who seemed unable to hold back his tears. Seeing him flush with embarrassment, she could not help but smile.","“All right, go wash your faces. Chunping, rest for the next couple of days.”","Then she took a gold hairpin from her belongings and handed it to Chunping with a smile.","“Take this. Consider it something to soothe your fright. Later, collect another ten taels of silver from Qiuru.”","She had already received quite a number of rewards, and so she was not stingy when it came to rewarding subordinates who worked diligently, performed their duties conscientiously, and obeyed orders. A gold hairpin was a matter of prestige, but silver was far more practical.","Chunping, however, declined to accept it. She had merely been questioned a few times by people from the Inner Service Office and the Palace Discipline Bureau. She had not rendered her mistress any great service; in the end, it was still her mistress who had rescued her. What right did she have to accept such a reward?","Shen Yanshui raised an eyebrow. “I told you it’s to help you recover from the fright. Take it.”","After all, she believed that for a wage earner, money was the best comfort.","As she spoke, she lifted her hand and directly pinned the gold hairpin into Chunping’s hair. The small ornaments that had once adorned the maid’s bun were now all gone.","Once someone fell into the hands of the Inner Service Office, they would lose a layer of skin even if they had done nothing wrong. That was no exaggeration. Fortunately, the Palace Discipline Bureau, acting on the Empress’s orders, had also participated in the investigation. Otherwise, the situation would have been even harder to say.","Chunping held her breath as she gazed at her mistress’s incomparable beauty from such a close distance. She was terrified that breathing too heavily would allow the foul air in her lungs to defile her mistress, and she held her breath until her cheeks turned bright red.","Afraid of offending her mistress, she hurriedly lowered her eyes. Yet what entered her lowered gaze was a broad expanse of soft, fair skin. Her cheeks grew hot, and in the end, she stared fixedly at the tips of her own shoes.","The others could not help feeling envious when they saw the gold hairpin their mistress had bestowed upon Chunping.","But there was no jealousy. After all, everyone in the palace knew how terrifying the Inner Service Office and the Office of Cautious Punishments were. No one wanted to go through such an ordeal.","If anything, it only strengthened their resolve to work more diligently and loyally for their mistress from then on, and to serve her well.","*","“Your Highness, the senior maid named Chunping who serves Lady Shen has already been sent back to Lianxin Court,” Zheng Yuande said softly, bowing at the waist.","Cui Yu merely answered with an “Mm” without looking up.","Seeing this, Zheng Yuande stood quietly to one side. He clicked his tongue inwardly. It seemed that his godson’s plan was going to fall through this time.","He had quite a few godsons under him, and he had been favorably impressed by Wang Chun, who was fairly clever and quick-witted. Since the boy had found himself a way forward, Zheng Yuande naturally would not stand in his way.","Even without Wang Chun, he had intended to arrange for someone else to keep an eye on the goings-on at Lianxin Court from time to time. That way, if His Highness ever asked about the place, he would not be left completely ignorant.","After a while, Zheng Yuande hurried out and returned with several sheets of paper in hand. In a low voice, he said, “Your Highness, everything has been investigated. The servants in Xiefang Hall who deceived their superiors and endangered their mistress, as well as Physician Zhang, who took the Crown Princess’s daily pulse, have all been taken into custody for the time being.”","Cui Yu skimmed the documents he handed over, his expression growing increasingly grim. “Deal with them all according to palace regulations.”","Then his voice paused briefly before he added coldly, “As for Matron Zhou, who serves the Crown Princess, leave her alone for now.”","If not for the child in the Crown Princess’s womb...","“As for Physician Zhang—he neglected his duties and nearly caused a great disaster. Give him twenty strokes and send him to work in the medicine storehouse for three years. Let him learn properly how to take a pulse and diagnose an illness.”","Zheng Yuande’s heart tightened. He immediately replied, “Yes.”","After the Eastern Palace guards had taken away the several palace maids who usually attended the Crown Princess, along with the physician sent by her family, the Crown Princess's face had gone deathly pale. Matron Zhou, standing beside her, looked no better. Her entire body was trembling uncontrollably, and cold sweat had soaked through her back.","Grand Physician Lu had received the Crown Prince's verbal order and had been waiting in Xifang Hall since early that morning. Seeing the situation, he stepped forward and gently offered a few words of reassurance before immediately inserting several needles to stabilize the pregnancy and calm her mind.","The Crown Princess promptly fell into a deep sleep.","******","After finishing the interrogations and punishments, Zheng Yuande wiped the sweat from his forehead before entering the room to report, “Your Highness, the Li family has submitted a request to enter the palace. Madam Li wishes to come and visit the Crown Princess.”","Madam Li was the Crown Princess's birth mother.","Cui Yu's expression remained cool. “Go and invite Madam Li in.”","About half an hour later, Madam Li was escorted to the main hall of the Eastern Palace.","She was nearly forty, with dignified features and barely concealed worry in her eyes. Seeing the Crown Prince seated at the head of the hall, she gathered her skirts and bowed with perfect propriety. “This humble wife pays her respects to Your Highness.”","Cui Yu stepped forward and made a token gesture of helping her up. “There is no need for such ceremony, Madam.”","Madam Li rose, but the concern in her eyes remained impossible to hide.","Looking at her, Cui Yu said in a calm, steady voice, “The Crown Princess is temporarily out of danger. Imperial Physician Director Lu is keeping watch in the side hall of Xifang Hall. You need not worry excessively, Madam.”","Madam Li immediately expressed her gratitude and offered her thanks, but then she heard the Crown Prince ask, “I hear that the physician serving at the Crown Princess's side was recommended by the Li family?”","Cui Yu's voice was calm and emotionless, giving no indication of what he was thinking.","Madam Li's heart tightened. “In answer to Your Highness, this humble wife did indeed recommend a physician to Her Highness the Crown Princess. May this humble wife venture to ask whether the physician has committed some offense?”","Cui Yu's tone turned faintly cold. “The physician knew that the Crown Princess was with child, yet concealed the matter instead of reporting it...”","He did not finish, but Madam Li could not help feeling a chill in her heart.","The Crown Princess had been pregnant, yet the Crown Prince had not been informed beforehand?","How could the Crown Princess have been so foolish?","Madam Li could no longer remain standing. She bowed and pleaded guilty. “This humble wife failed to educate her daughter properly, was unable to judge people clearly, and recommended the wrong person. I beg Your Highness to forgive me.”","Cui Yu was silent for a moment before ordering someone to help her up. “The Crown Princess's pregnancy is not yet stable. Since you have come, comfort her properly and persuade her to set her mind at ease and rest quietly.”","Madam Li answered respectfully, “This humble wife understands. I will certainly advise and comfort the Crown Princess.”","Cui Yu said nothing more. He instructed Zheng Yuande, “Escort Madam Li to Xifang Hall.”","******","The moment Madam Li stepped into Xifang Hall, she saw her daughter's pale face on the bed.","She came to a halt, and tears immediately began to fall.","Crown Princess Shen was half reclining against the headboard. Hearing the movement, she looked up. When she saw her mother, she first froze, then forced the corners of her lips upward. “Mother...”","Madam Li hurried forward and sat down beside the bed, taking her daughter's hand as tears streamed down her face.","She opened her mouth, wanting to say something, but she was too choked with sobs to speak.","Seeing this, the Crown Princess felt a pang of sorrow as well. She gave Matron Zhou a meaningful look. “Everyone, leave us. This palace would like to speak with Mother.”","Matron Zhou understood. Her legs weak, she led the attendants out of the room and remained outside in the outer hall.","The doors closed, leaving only mother and daughter.","Only then did Madam Li speak, her eyes still red-rimmed. “How are you feeling, Crown Princess? Are you still unwell in any way?”","The Crown Princess shook her head. Her voice was somewhat weak as she said, “Grand Physician Lu has been waiting in the side hall. Mother, please do not worry.”","At those words, Madam Li relaxed slightly. Yet once that breath of relief escaped her, all the words she had held back along the way came spilling out.","Looking at her daughter’s pale face, she could not suppress the regret in her heart. Lowering her voice, she said, “This is all Mother’s fault!”","The Crown Princess froze.","Madam Li clasped her hand, tears falling again. “Mother should never have left you to be raised by your grandfather and grandmother. They loved you, spoiled you, and treasured you as the apple of their eye. Ever since you were little, you had whatever you wanted, and no one ever contradicted you. That is why you grew into such a... such an unruly, arrogant, and unrestrained person.”","The Crown Princess’s expression shifted slightly.","Madam Li frowned as she looked at her. “Hiding your pregnancy for three months—do you realize how serious that is? What do you take the Eastern Palace for? Do you think everyone there is blind? And where does that leave His Highness the Crown Prince?”","“Mother!” the Crown Princess interrupted, her voice stiff.","Seeing the unpleasant look on her daughter’s face, Madam Li’s heart ached. Mindful of her daughter’s condition, she could not bear to continue scolding her. With a sigh, she held her daughter’s hand and softened her tone.","“Never mind. It is too late to say any of this now. Since things have come to this, the most important matter is what you do from here on.”","She looked at her daughter earnestly. “Listen to Mother. From today onward, stop trying to be strong. Take good care of yourself and give birth to the imperial heir safely. Nothing matters more than that. Leave everything else to His Highness the Crown Prince.”","“Mother...”","“Let Mother finish.” Madam Li pressed her hand. “Later, send someone to invite His Highness the Crown Prince here. Apologize to him in person. Do not be stubborn, and do not argue back. Before a man, you must learn when to show weakness...”","Looking at her daughter, she spoke with heartfelt gravity. “You are his wife. Lowering your head before him is no disgrace. Hand over the authority to manage the Eastern Palace and focus solely on resting and caring for your pregnancy.”","The Crown Princess did not look pleased. After a long pause, she said, “I... I know what I am doing.”","“What judgment do you have?” Madam Li cried anxiously. “If you had any sense at all, would you have done something like this?”","The Crown Princess was left speechless. She turned her head away and refused to look at her.","Seeing this, Madam Li suppressed the anger in her heart. She took a deep breath, then patiently coaxed her for some time. At last, when it seemed her daughter had finally taken some of it in, she did not press her further. She sighed, tightening her hold on her daughter’s hand, and softened her voice.","“Enough. Mother will say no more. Think it over carefully yourself.”","After a pause, she added, “Do you know who harmed you?”","The Crown Princess’s brows drew together, her heart filled with resentment. “Who else could it be but someone from Noble Consort Lan’s faction?!”","Madam Li frowned. She had originally wanted to say something more, but seeing her daughter in such a state, she feared upsetting her too greatly and swallowed all her words.","“It may not necessarily have been someone from Noble Consort Lan’s faction. But regardless, neither Her Majesty the Empress, His Highness the Crown Prince, nor our Li family will let you suffer this injustice for nothing. Just focus on nurturing your health and your pregnancy. Do not trouble yourself with anything else.”","The Crown Princess took a deep breath. In the end, she still knew what mattered most at present. Lowering her eyes, she gave a light nod.","The mother and daughter spoke for quite some time. Seeing that it was getting late, Madam Li finally rose, tucked the covers around her daughter, and said softly,","“Mother is leaving now. Remember what I told you.”","The Crown Princess gazed at her mother and, in the end, nodded.","The palace doors opened and closed. The sound of footsteps gradually faded into the distance.","Leaning against the headboard, the Crown Princess stared at the canopy above her bed, unmoving for a long while.","******","Zheng Yuande drew in his slightly slimmer, still-plump body and said quietly, “Your Highness, the palace attendants from Xiefang Hall came to ask whether, if you have some free time, you might go to Xiefang Hall for dinner at the Crown Princess’s invitation.”","Cui Yu instinctively furrowed his brows. “I’m busy.”","The flesh on Zheng Yuande’s body trembled as he nodded repeatedly. “Yes, Your Highness. This servant will send someone to deliver your reply...”","“Wait.”","The crease between Cui Yu’s brows deepened. He asked coldly, “Has Madam Li already left the palace?”","Zheng Yuande nodded. “To answer Your Highness, Madam Li left not long ago. The senior matron who attends to the Crown Princess personally escorted her out of the palace.”","Thinking of the child in the Crown Princess’s womb, Cui Yu remained silent for a long while before finally rising and heading to Xiefang Hall.","Hearing the Crown Prince enter, the Crown Princess felt a quiet sense of relief.","After entering the room, Cui Yu saw the Crown Princess looking pale and struggling to sit up. “There is no need for formalities, Crown Princess. Lie down and rest properly.”","The Crown Princess was helped back down onto the bed. In a gentle voice, she said, “Thank you for Your Highness’s consideration.” As she spoke, her eyes reddened, and she gazed at him through glistening tears. “Your Highness, this wife was in the wrong. I beg you, for the sake of the child in my womb, please do not be angry with me.”","Her voice sounded weak, but her eyes remained fixed intently on him.","Hearing her suddenly yield, Cui Yu studied the expression in her brows and eyes, his gaze growing deeper.","Zheng Yuande was quick to read the situation. He moved a chair to the front of the bed, and Cui Yu sat down. Looking at the Crown Princess’s pale face, he said calmly, “Since the imperial physicians have instructed you to rest and keep your mind at ease, Crown Princess, you should not dwell on anything. Just focus on nurturing the child in peace.”","Hearing the slight warmth in his voice, the Crown Princess felt a dull ache in her heart. Had she... truly been wrong before?","If she had not insisted on winning the Emperor’s favor, if she had not wanted everyone in the imperial harem to witness her glory, this would never have happened...","Yet the Empress valued the child in Lady Chu’s womb so highly. That had always been a thorn in her heart. How could her child possibly be inferior to the child in the womb of a mere Lady Chu?","She had wanted everyone to know that the Emperor valued the child in her womb. No one would be allowed to surpass her child!","But for the moment, what mattered most was winning back the Crown Prince’s favor.","The Crown Princess’s eyes were tinged red as she lowered her voice to a whisper. “I understand. Thank you for Your Highness’s concern.”","She paused, then looked up at the Crown Prince. Her eyes held just the right amount of fragility.","“Your Highness, in my current condition... I fear I am no longer able to manage the Eastern Palace’s affairs. I must trouble Your Highness to ask Matron Rong to take charge of the household affairs for the time being.”","“Matron Rong is His Highness’s wet nurse. She has served in the Eastern Palace for many years and commands deep respect by virtue of her seniority and standing. With her managing the Eastern Palace, there should be no mishaps, and I can devote myself to caring for the child with peace of mind.”","Whenever she mentioned Matron Rong, her tone carried a measure of respect. “I have always held Matron Rong in high regard; I simply did not wish to trouble her under ordinary circumstances. But now that I am of little use, only a venerable and highly respected elder like Matron Rong can keep everyone in the Eastern Palace in line.”","Upon hearing this, Cui Yu glanced at her. “Since the Crown Princess has given this matter such consideration, we shall do as you wish. I will speak to Matron Rong.”","After discussing the important matters, the two of them exchanged a few more words before Cui Yu rose and left.","Only after the Crown Prince’s figure had disappeared did Matron Zhou finally step forward, her face full of concern. “Your Highness, how could you... how could you hand authority over to Matron Rong?” That old woman was the Crown Prince’s wet nurse. If she took charge of the Eastern Palace, wouldn’t she end up ranking above the Crown Princess?","Seeing Matron Zhou’s worried expression, she slowly replied, “My body is inconvenient now, and I cannot manage too many affairs. That is one reason.”","Her tone paused, then she added softly, with pointed meaning, “Second, Lady Chu is nearly due to give birth, is she not?”","Matron Zhou froze.","The Crown Princess lowered her eyes, her voice light and airy. “If she should suffer from inadequate care and something were to happen, it would all be blamed on me as Crown Princess. It would be better to hand this hot potato to someone else and let them worry over it.”","Matron Zhou was stunned for a moment. Then the worry vanished from her face, replaced by a smile. “Your Highness is truly clever! I heard that Lady Chu has been feeling unwell lately, often suffering from palpitations and shortness of breath, and unable to sleep properly. She has even summoned imperial physicians, yet they have found no improvement.” Naturally, Matron Zhou knew the true reason.","She lowered her voice. “If something were to happen during childbirth... then it would be because Matron Rong failed to care for her properly. It would have nothing whatsoever to do with Your Highness.”","The Crown Princess’s gaze deepened. The effect of the gold-edged daphne had been told to her by the physician who served at her side, who had discovered it by chance in the past. It was a rare and precious tribute, and even an ordinary imperial physician who saw the gold-edged daphne in Haoyue Residence would never think to suspect it.","Although she had lost a rather useful physician in the process, she had, through an unexpected twist of fate, completely eliminated a potential source of trouble.","Though there were matrons sent by the Empress Mother to watch over Haoyue Residence, the Crown Princess had lived in the Eastern Palace for many years and had naturally planted her own people in every corner.","They did not need to do anything major. All it took was a little tampering to keep Lady Chu constantly exposed to the daphne’s fragrance, making it difficult for her to sleep peacefully.","Childbirth was a passage through the gates of death for any woman. If Lady Chu were already physically and mentally weakened when the time came... then it would hardly be difficult for something to go wrong.","The Crown Princess could use this opportunity to wash her hands of the matter. She would appear to the Crown Prince to be yielding because of her frailty, while also passing this hot potato off to someone else. That way, even if something happened during Lady Chu’s delivery, no one could blame her."]}]);
